// 元の文章は _tools/base.json と _tools/parts/*.txt にある。
const PASSAGES = [
{"id":"w-0001","page":"words","group":"1〜200","kind":"社内アナウンス","text":"Attention, all staff. As you know, we have a serious backlog of customer orders this month. To deal with it, management has decided to overhaul our entire shipping system. Starting Monday, new scanners will be installed in the warehouse, and the old conveyor belts, which are showing heavy wear and tear, will be replaced. During the work, some areas of the premises will be closed, so please check the notice board each morning. We know the past few weeks have been stressful, and we cannot sustain this pace forever. For that reason, the company will hold a barbecue on Friday evening so that everyone can unwind. Thank you for your hard work, and please see your supervisor if you have any questions.","ja":"従業員の皆さんにお知らせします。ご存じの通り、今月はお客様からの注文が大量にたまっています。これに対処するため、経営陣は出荷システム全体を全面的に見直すことを決めました。月曜日から倉庫に新しいスキャナーが設置され、摩耗がひどくなっている古いコンベヤーベルトは交換されます。作業中は敷地内の一部が閉鎖されますので、毎朝掲示板を確認してください。この数週間が大変だったことは承知しており、このペースをいつまでも続けることはできません。そこで、皆さんにくつろいでもらえるよう、金曜日の夕方に会社でバーベキューを開きます。日頃の努力に感謝します。質問がある場合は上司に聞いてください。","words":[["backlog","words:backlog"],["overhaul","words:overhaul"],["wear and tear","words:wear and tear"],["premises","words:premises"],["sustain","words:sustain"],["unwind","words:unwind"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does the speaker mention?","o":["A shortage of warehouse staff","A drop in monthly sales","A large number of unfilled orders","A late delivery of new scanners"],"a":2,"why":"冒頭の a serious backlog of customer orders（注文が大量にたまっている）が問題。backlog を unfilled orders と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will happen on Monday?","o":["New equipment will be installed.","A company barbecue will be held.","The warehouse will be closed all day.","A new supervisor will start work."],"a":0,"why":"Starting Monday, new scanners will be installed とある。scanners を equipment と言い換えている。バーベキューは金曜日。"},{"q":"What are the listeners asked to do each morning?","o":["Report to their supervisor","Clean the conveyor belts","Sign in at the front desk","Look at the notice board"],"a":3,"why":"please check the notice board each morning とある。check を look at と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0002","page":"words","group":"201〜400","kind":"ニュース","text":"Good evening. This is the business report. After several volatile months, the local economy is showing signs of a resurgence. According to preliminary figures released today, freight traffic through the city's port rose by twelve percent last quarter. Officials say the new rail link has removed a major bottleneck and will facilitate trade with neighboring regions. Small businesses near the port are beginning to prosper, and ridership on the new line is higher than expected. However, the project has not been welcomed by everyone. A plan to raise parking fees downtown has caused a backlash from local shop owners. The city council will discuss the issue at a public meeting next Tuesday. We will have more on that story after the weather.","ja":"こんばんは。ビジネスニュースの時間です。不安定な数か月が続いたあと、地域経済に回復の兆しが見えています。本日発表された暫定の数字によると、市の港を通る貨物の輸送量は前の四半期に12パーセント増えました。当局によれば、新しい鉄道路線が大きな障害を取り除き、近隣地域との取引を促進するとのことです。港の近くの小さな商店は繁盛し始めており、新路線の利用者数も予想を上回っています。しかし、この事業を誰もが歓迎しているわけではありません。中心部の駐車料金を引き上げる計画が、地元の商店主から反発を招いています。市議会は来週火曜日の公開の会合でこの問題を話し合います。この件については、天気予報のあとに詳しくお伝えします。","words":[["volatile","words:volatile"],["resurgence","words:resurgence"],["preliminary","words:preliminary"],["freight","words:freight"],["bottleneck","words:bottleneck"],["facilitate","words:facilitate"],["prosper","words:prosper"],["ridership","words:ridership"],["backlash","words:backlash"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the report mainly about?","o":["A delay in a construction project","Signs of recovery in the local economy","A change in the weather forecast","The closing of the city's port"],"a":1,"why":"the local economy is showing signs of a resurgence が主題。resurgence（復活）を recovery と言い換えている。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what has the new rail link done?","o":["It has raised parking fees.","It has reduced the number of passengers.","It has made trade easier.","It has replaced the port."],"a":2,"why":"has removed a major bottleneck and will facilitate trade とある。facilitate（容易にする）を made easier と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will the listeners most likely hear next?","o":["A weather report","A traffic update","An interview with a shop owner","A sports report"],"a":0,"why":"最後の We will have more on that story after the weather から、次は天気予報だと分かる。"}]},
{"id":"i-0001","page":"idioms","group":"take","kind":"留守番電話","text":"Hi, Maria. This is David from the sales department. I'm calling because I'm taking next week off, and I need someone to take over the Henderson account while I'm away. I know you have already taken on a lot of extra work this month, so I don't want this to take up too much of your time. There is only one meeting, on Wednesday at ten. Please take down the client's requests carefully, because we have to take their budget into account before we send a new price quote. I've left all the files on your desk. If anything is unclear, call my mobile before Friday. Thanks so much, and I'll see you when I get back.","ja":"もしもし、マリアさん。営業部のデイビッドです。来週休みを取るので、不在の間ヘンダーソン社の担当を誰かに引き継いでもらう必要があり、お電話しました。今月すでにたくさんの追加の仕事を引き受けてもらっているのは分かっているので、あまり時間を取らせたくはありません。会議は水曜日の10時に1回あるだけです。新しい見積もりを送る前に先方の予算を考慮に入れなければならないので、お客様の要望を注意深く書き留めてください。資料はすべてあなたの机に置いてあります。不明な点があれば、金曜日までに私の携帯に電話してください。本当にありがとう。戻ったらまた会いましょう。","words":[["taking next week off","idioms:2:take off"],["take over","idioms:2:take over"],["taken on","idioms:2:take on"],["take up","idioms:2:take up"],["take down","idioms:2:take down"],["take their budget into account","idioms:5:take A into B"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the speaker calling?","o":["To cancel a meeting with a client","To ask for a new price quote","To ask a coworker to handle an account","To request some time off"],"a":2,"why":"I need someone to take over the Henderson account（担当を引き継いでほしい）が用件。take over を handle と言い換えている。休みを「願い出て」いるわけではない。"},{"q":"What is scheduled for Wednesday?","o":["A sales training session","A meeting with a client","A department lunch","A phone call with David"],"a":1,"why":"There is only one meeting, on Wednesday at ten とあり、続けて the client's requests を書き留めるよう頼んでいるので、顧客との会議。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say he has done?","o":["Sent an email to the client","Updated the price list","Called Maria's mobile phone","Left some files on Maria's desk"],"a":3,"why":"I've left all the files on your desk とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0002","page":"idioms","group":"come","kind":"会議での発言","text":"Thanks for coming, everyone. Let me start with the new product. The design is coming along well, and it should come out in early spring. However, a problem has come up. Last week, our engineers came up against a safety regulation that we had not expected. While reading the report, I also came across a note saying the testing may cost more than we planned. In the end, it all comes down to time and money. So, here is what I'd like you to do. Please work in small groups this afternoon and come up with at least two ways to reduce the cost. We will meet again at four o'clock to share your ideas. Any questions before we begin?","ja":"皆さん、お集まりいただきありがとうございます。まず新製品の話から始めます。設計は順調に進んでおり、春の早い時期には発売できるはずです。ただ、問題が1つ持ち上がりました。先週、技術者たちが、想定していなかった安全規制にぶつかりました。報告書を読んでいて、試験の費用が計画より高くなるかもしれないという注記も偶然見つけました。結局のところ、すべては時間とお金の問題に行き着きます。そこで、皆さんにお願いがあります。今日の午後は小さなグループに分かれて、費用を減らす方法を少なくとも2つ考え出してください。4時にもう一度集まって、案を共有します。始める前に質問はありますか。","words":[["coming along","idioms:1:come along"],["come out","idioms:1:come out"],["came up against","idioms:4:come up against"],["came across","idioms:3:come across"],["comes down to","idioms:4:come down to"],["come up with","idioms:4:come up with"],["has come up","idioms:1:come up"]],"qs":[{"q":"When is the new product expected to be released?","o":["In early spring","Next week","At four o'clock","At the end of the year"],"a":0,"why":"it should come out in early spring とある。come out（世に出る）を be released と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What problem does the speaker mention?","o":["The design is behind schedule.","An engineer has left the company.","The product failed a safety test.","A regulation was not expected."],"a":3,"why":"came up against a safety regulation that we had not expected（想定外の安全規制にぶつかった）とある。設計は順調（coming along well）で、試験に落ちたとは言っていない。"},{"q":"What are the listeners asked to do this afternoon?","o":["Read a report about testing","Think of ways to cut costs","Meet with the engineers","Prepare a new design"],"a":1,"why":"come up with at least two ways to reduce the cost とある。come up with を think of、reduce を cut と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"n-0001","page":"nouns","group":"人事・採用","kind":"説明会の案内","text":"Welcome to the Riverside job fair. My name is Karen, and I work in human resources at Bright Foods. We currently have five job openings in our sales and delivery teams. If you are interested, please pick up an application form at our booth and return it today with your resume. A cover letter is not required. Our hiring manager will be here until three o'clock, and he can hold a short job interview on the spot. Successful applicants will join a two-week training program next month. We also offer a generous benefits package, including paid vacation from your first year. Our booth is number twelve, next to the main entrance. We look forward to meeting you.","ja":"リバーサイド就職説明会へようこそ。私はカレンと申しまして、ブライト・フーズの人事部で働いています。当社では現在、営業チームと配送チームで5件の求人があります。興味のある方は、当社のブースで応募用紙を受け取り、本日中に履歴書と一緒に提出してください。添え状は必要ありません。採用担当責任者が3時までこちらにおり、その場で短い面接を行うこともできます。採用された方は、来月2週間の研修プログラムに参加していただきます。また、1年目からの有給休暇を含む、充実した福利厚生もご用意しています。当社のブースは12番で、正面入口の隣です。皆さまにお会いできるのを楽しみにしています。","words":[["job fair","nouns:job fair"],["human resources","nouns:human resources"],["job openings","nouns:job opening"],["application form","nouns:application form"],["cover letter","nouns:cover letter"],["hiring manager","nouns:hiring manager"],["job interview","nouns:job interview"],["training program","nouns:training program"],["benefits package","nouns:benefits package"],["paid vacation","nouns:paid vacation"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is the talk most likely taking place?","o":["At a company training session","At a food factory","At a job fair","At a sales meeting"],"a":2,"why":"冒頭の Welcome to the Riverside job fair から、就職説明会の会場だと分かる。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what is NOT required?","o":["A resume","A cover letter","An application form","An interview"],"a":1,"why":"A cover letter is not required とある。応募用紙と履歴書は提出するよう求めている。"},{"q":"What will successful applicants do next month?","o":["Take part in a training program","Take a paid vacation","Visit booth number twelve","Meet the hiring manager"],"a":0,"why":"Successful applicants will join a two-week training program next month とある。join を take part in と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"n-0002","page":"nouns","group":"旅行・交通","kind":"空港アナウンス","text":"Attention, passengers on Sky Air flight 204 to Chicago. Because of a mechanical check, the departure time has been changed to four fifteen. In addition, the boarding gate has been moved from gate nine to gate twenty-two. Please have your boarding pass and passport ready. As this is a full flight, each passenger may bring only one piece of carry-on luggage. If you have a connecting flight in Chicago, please speak to a flight attendant after boarding, and we will do our best to help you. Passengers who would like to wait in the lounge can take the free shuttle bus from the main hall. We apologize for the delay and thank you for your patience.","ja":"スカイエア204便シカゴ行きをご利用のお客様にご案内します。機体の点検のため、出発時刻が4時15分に変更になりました。あわせて、搭乗口が9番ゲートから22番ゲートに変更されています。搭乗券とパスポートをご用意ください。本便は満席のため、機内持ち込み手荷物はお一人様1個までとさせていただきます。シカゴで乗り継ぎ便をご利用のお客様は、ご搭乗後に客室乗務員にお声がけください。できる限りお手伝いいたします。ラウンジでお待ちになりたいお客様は、メインホールから無料の送迎バスをご利用いただけます。遅れが生じましたことをお詫びするとともに、ご理解に感謝いたします。","words":[["departure time","nouns:departure time"],["boarding gate","nouns:boarding gate"],["boarding pass","nouns:boarding pass"],["carry-on luggage","nouns:carry-on luggage"],["connecting flight","nouns:connecting flight"],["flight attendant","nouns:flight attendant"],["shuttle bus","nouns:shuttle bus"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has caused the delay?","o":["Bad weather","A late connecting flight","A crowded lounge","A mechanical check"],"a":3,"why":"Because of a mechanical check, the departure time has been changed とある。"},{"q":"What are the passengers reminded about?","o":["A limit on carry-on luggage","A change in ticket prices","A new passport rule","A meal service on board"],"a":0,"why":"each passenger may bring only one piece of carry-on luggage（持ち込みは1個まで）と伝えている。"},{"q":"Who should speak to a flight attendant?","o":["Passengers who want to use the lounge","Passengers with a connecting flight","Passengers without a boarding pass","Passengers traveling with children"],"a":1,"why":"If you have a connecting flight in Chicago, please speak to a flight attendant とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0003","page":"words","group":"1〜200","kind":"店の広告","text":"Looking for a new look for your home or your wardrobe? Visit Harlow and Finch this weekend for our stupendous spring sale. On the first floor, you will find every kind of garment, from casual shirts to urbane business suits, all in immaculate condition and at half price. On the second floor, our designers can help you furnish an entire apartment in a single afternoon. Worried about the cost? You can pay for any item over three hundred dollars in six monthly installments, with no interest. And if the color you want is sold out, simply place a back-order at the service desk, and we will deliver it free of charge. Harlow and Finch, on Market Street. Doors open at nine.","ja":"ご自宅や服装の雰囲気を変えてみませんか。今週末はハーロウ・アンド・フィンチの、驚きの春のセールへお越しください。1階では、カジュアルなシャツから洗練されたビジネススーツまで、あらゆる衣類が完璧な状態で、しかも半額でそろっています。2階では、当店のデザイナーが、午後のひとときでアパート一軒分の家具をそろえるお手伝いをします。お値段が心配ですか。300ドルを超える商品はどれも、無利子の6回の月払いでお支払いいただけます。ご希望の色が売り切れの場合は、サービスカウンターで取り寄せ注文をしてください。無料でお届けします。ハーロウ・アンド・フィンチはマーケット通りにあります。開店は9時です。","words":[["stupendous","words:stupendous"],["garment","words:garment"],["urbane","words:urbane"],["immaculate","words:immaculate"],["furnish","words:furnish"],["installments","words:installment"],["back-order","words:back-order"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is being advertised?","o":["A furniture repair service","A store's seasonal sale","A new apartment building","A fashion design school"],"a":1,"why":"our stupendous spring sale（驚きの春のセール）と言っており、店の季節のセールの広告だと分かる。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about items over three hundred dollars?","o":["They are sold only on the second floor.","They cannot be returned.","They can be paid for over several months.","They are delivered within a day."],"a":2,"why":"You can pay ... in six monthly installments（6回の月払い）とある。installments を over several months と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What can customers do if a color is sold out?","o":["Order it and have it delivered free","Choose a different item at half price","Come back the following weekend","Ask a designer for advice"],"a":0,"why":"simply place a back-order ... and we will deliver it free of charge（取り寄せ注文をすれば無料で届ける）とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0004","page":"words","group":"1〜200","kind":"ローカルニュース","text":"In local news, the annual harvest festival opened yesterday at the county fairground, but not without problems. The event is famous for the friendly rivalry between the town's two marching bands. This year, however, a raucous crowd gathered near the main stage, and a notorious traffic jam formed on Route Nine. In the ensuing turmoil, several performances were canceled. Residents living nearby made vehement complaints to the organizers, saying the noise was disagreeable and continued past midnight. In response, the festival committee has promised to close the stage by ten o'clock tonight and to add extra parking on the north side. The festival runs through Sunday. Stay tuned for the traffic report.","ja":"地元のニュースです。毎年恒例の収穫祭が昨日、郡の催事場で始まりましたが、問題もありました。この催しは、町の2つのマーチングバンドの間の和やかな競い合いで知られています。しかし今年は、メインステージの近くに騒々しい群衆が集まり、9号線では悪名高い渋滞が発生しました。その後の混乱の中で、いくつかの演奏が中止になりました。近くに住む住民は主催者に激しい苦情を寄せ、騒音が不快で、深夜0時を過ぎても続いたと訴えました。これを受けて祭りの実行委員会は、今夜は10時までにステージを閉めること、北側に臨時の駐車場を設けることを約束しました。祭りは日曜日まで続きます。このあとは交通情報です。","words":[["fairground","words:fairground"],["rivalry","words:rivalry"],["raucous","words:raucous"],["notorious","words:notorious"],["ensuing","words:ensuing"],["turmoil","words:turmoil"],["vehement","words:vehement"],["disagreeable","words:disagreeable"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is the festival being held?","o":["On Route Nine","At a concert hall","In a town square","At a fairground"],"a":3,"why":"opened yesterday at the county fairground（郡の催事場で始まった）とある。9号線は渋滞が起きた場所。"},{"q":"Why did nearby residents complain?","o":["The parking fees were too high.","The noise continued late at night.","The performances were canceled.","The festival was too crowded."],"a":1,"why":"saying the noise was disagreeable and continued past midnight（騒音が不快で深夜を過ぎても続いた）とある。"},{"q":"What has the committee promised to do tonight?","o":["End the stage events earlier","Cancel the marching bands","Close Route Nine","Move the festival to Sunday"],"a":0,"why":"has promised to close the stage by ten o'clock tonight とある。close the stage by ten を end earlier と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0005","page":"words","group":"1〜200","kind":"授賞式での紹介","text":"Good evening, and welcome to the annual business awards. It is my honor to introduce tonight's winner, Dr. Helen Park. During her illustrious career, Dr. Park has built a chain of clinics known for a holistic approach to health care. Her clinics consistently outperform their competitors, yet staff turnover remains remarkably low. She is scrupulous about quality, personally visiting every location twice a year. Dr. Park is also admired for her philanthropic work. Her foundation gave the impetus for our city's free dental program, which now serves two thousand children. The judges' decision this year was unequivocal. Please join me in welcoming Dr. Helen Park to the stage.","ja":"こんばんは。年に一度のビジネス賞の授賞式へようこそ。今夜の受賞者、ヘレン・パーク博士をご紹介できることを光栄に思います。パーク博士は輝かしい経歴の中で、医療への総合的な取り組みで知られる診療所のチェーンを築いてきました。博士の診療所は常に競合を上回る実績を上げていますが、職員の離職率は驚くほど低いままです。博士は品質に細心の注意を払い、年に2回、すべての拠点を自ら訪れています。パーク博士は慈善活動でも尊敬されています。博士の財団が後押しとなって、市の無料歯科プログラムが始まり、今では2,000人の子どもが利用しています。今年の審査員の決定は、迷いのないものでした。どうぞ、ヘレン・パーク博士を拍手でお迎えください。","words":[["illustrious","words:illustrious"],["holistic","words:holistic"],["outperform","words:outperform"],["turnover","words:turnover"],["scrupulous","words:scrupulous"],["philanthropic","words:philanthropic"],["impetus","words:impetus"],["unequivocal","words:unequivocal"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the talk?","o":["To announce a new clinic","To explain a dental program","To introduce an award winner","To ask for donations"],"a":2,"why":"It is my honor to introduce tonight's winner（今夜の受賞者を紹介する）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about Dr. Park's clinics?","o":["Few employees leave them.","They are open twice a year.","They are located in one city.","They treat only children."],"a":0,"why":"staff turnover remains remarkably low（離職率が非常に低い）とある。turnover が低い＝辞める人が少ない、という言い換え。"},{"q":"What did Dr. Park's foundation help to start?","o":["A chain of clinics","A business award","A training course for judges","A free dental program"],"a":3,"why":"Her foundation gave the impetus for our city's free dental program（無料歯科プログラムのきっかけを作った）とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0006","page":"words","group":"1〜200","kind":"ラジオ番組","text":"Welcome back to Science Today. My guest this morning is Professor Alan Reid, who studies how plants grow in cities. Professor Reid grows tomatoes in a small greenhouse on the roof of his office. Many people postulate that sunlight is the main determinant of a good harvest. However, from five years of data, he has been able to deduce that soil temperature matters even more. He reckons that rooftop gardens could supply a tenth of a city's vegetables. Such gardens are already prevalent in northern Europe. After the break, Professor Reid will enunciate, step by step, how you can build one at home. He will even share his recipe for a spicy tomato condiment. Don't go away.","ja":"「サイエンス・トゥデイ」、番組を続けます。今朝のゲストは、都市で植物がどう育つかを研究しているアラン・リード教授です。リード教授は、研究室の屋上にある小さな温室でトマトを育てています。豊作を決める一番の要因は日光だ、と仮定する人は多いです。しかし教授は5年分のデータから、土の温度のほうがさらに重要だと推論することができました。教授は、屋上菜園が都市の野菜の10分の1をまかなえると見ています。こうした菜園は、北ヨーロッパではすでに広く普及しています。休憩のあとは、自宅で菜園を作る方法を、リード教授が一つひとつはっきりと説明してくれます。ピリ辛のトマト調味料のレシピまで教えてくれるそうです。そのままお待ちください。","words":[["greenhouse","words:greenhouse"],["postulate","words:postulate"],["determinant","words:determinant"],["deduce","words:deduce"],["reckons","words:reckon"],["prevalent","words:prevalent"],["enunciate","words:enunciate"],["condiment","words:condiment"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is Professor Reid?","o":["A radio host","A researcher who studies plants","A chef at a restaurant","A city official"],"a":1,"why":"who studies how plants grow in cities（都市で植物がどう育つかを研究している）とある。"},{"q":"According to Professor Reid's data, what matters most for a good harvest?","o":["The amount of sunlight","The size of the greenhouse","The type of tomato","The temperature of the soil"],"a":3,"why":"he has been able to deduce that soil temperature matters even more（土の温度のほうがさらに重要）とある。日光は「多くの人がそう仮定している」だけ。"},{"q":"What will Professor Reid do after the break?","o":["Explain how to build a garden","Travel to northern Europe","Answer questions from listeners","Show photographs of his office"],"a":0,"why":"will enunciate, step by step, how you can build one at home（自宅での作り方を順に説明する）とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0007","page":"words","group":"1〜200","kind":"会議の締めくくり","text":"Before we finish, let me recapitulate the plans for next month's company retreat. We will spend two days at Lake Morton, about ninety minutes from here. The hotel was carefully vetted by our planning team, and it has a large meeting hall and good food. A bus will leave from the front entrance at eight on Friday morning. Please note that the hotel does not dispense medicine, so bring anything you may need. The first afternoon is for team workshops, and the second day is free for hiking or swimming. If you cannot attend, tell Sandra in personnel by Wednesday. That's all for today. Thank you, everyone.","ja":"終わる前に、来月の社員研修合宿の予定をもう一度まとめておきます。ここから90分ほどのモートン湖で2日間過ごします。ホテルは企画チームが綿密に審査したところで、広い会議場があり、食事もおいしいです。バスは金曜日の朝8時に正面入口から出発します。ホテルでは薬を出してもらえませんので、必要なものはご自分でお持ちください。1日目の午後はチームでの研修、2日目はハイキングや水泳など自由行動です。参加できない方は、水曜日までに人事のサンドラに伝えてください。今日は以上です。皆さん、ありがとうございました。","words":[["recapitulate","words:recapitulate"],["retreat","words:retreat (名)"],["vetted","words:vet"],["dispense","words:dispense"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the speaker mainly discussing?","o":["A change in the bus schedule","A new hotel opening","A company trip","A swimming competition"],"a":2,"why":"the plans for next month's company retreat（来月の社員研修合宿の予定）をまとめている。retreat を trip と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are the listeners advised to bring?","o":["Their own medicine","Hiking boots","A meeting agenda","Food for two days"],"a":0,"why":"the hotel does not dispense medicine, so bring anything you may need（ホテルは薬を出さないので必要なものを持参）とある。"},{"q":"Who should contact Sandra?","o":["People who want to go swimming","People who need a hotel room","People who will drive to the lake","People who are unable to attend"],"a":3,"why":"If you cannot attend, tell Sandra in personnel by Wednesday とある。cannot attend を unable to attend と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0008","page":"words","group":"201〜400","kind":"社内アナウンス","text":"This is a message from the IT department. This weekend, we will change the configuration of the payroll system. As a result, all employees must update their passwords straightaway on Monday morning. When you log in, the computer may show a warning about a security certificate. This is normal, so please click the accept button. Next, affix the new blue sticker to the back of your ID card. You will need it to enter the server room. Any deviation from these steps could lock your account. In aggregate, the update should take less than five minutes per person. If you have trouble, call extension four hundred. Thank you for your cooperation.","ja":"IT部門からのお知らせです。今週末、給与システムの設定を変更します。そのため、全従業員は月曜日の朝、すぐにパスワードを更新してください。ログインすると、セキュリティ証明書についての警告が表示されることがあります。これは正常な動作ですので、承認ボタンを押してください。次に、新しい青いシールを社員証の裏に貼ってください。サーバー室に入るときに必要になります。この手順から少しでも外れると、アカウントがロックされるおそれがあります。全部合わせても、更新にかかる時間は1人あたり5分未満のはずです。うまくいかない場合は、内線400番にお電話ください。ご協力ありがとうございます。","words":[["configuration","words:configuration"],["payroll","words:payroll"],["straightaway","words:straightaway"],["certificate","words:certificate"],["affix","words:affix"],["deviation","words:deviation"],["aggregate","words:aggregate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen this weekend?","o":["New ID cards will be issued.","The server room will be closed.","A system will be changed.","Employees will be paid."],"a":2,"why":"we will change the configuration of the payroll system（給与システムの設定を変える）とある。"},{"q":"What must employees do on Monday morning?","o":["Change their passwords","Visit the IT department","Collect a new computer","Sign a certificate"],"a":0,"why":"all employees must update their passwords straightaway on Monday morning とある。update を change と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Why should the listeners call extension four hundred?","o":["To order a blue sticker","To report a problem","To enter the server room","To confirm their attendance"],"a":1,"why":"If you have trouble, call extension four hundred とある。have trouble を a problem と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0009","page":"words","group":"201〜400","kind":"全国ニュース","text":"Now for the national news. After a two-week recess, lawmakers returned to the capital today for a heated parliamentary debate. The main topic was a new media law. Critics say the law amounts to censorship, and it was roundly criticized by several newspapers this morning. Public discontent has been growing since two reporters were detained at a protest last month. The minister of justice promised leniency for the reporters and said they would be released soon. However, he gave only a verbal promise and no written statement. A final vote on the law is expected on Friday. We will bring you live coverage from the capital at six o'clock.","ja":"続いて全国のニュースです。2週間の休会のあと、議員たちは今日、首都に戻り、議会で激しい討論を行いました。主な議題は新しいメディア法です。批判する人々は、この法律は検閲に等しいと述べており、今朝は複数の新聞がこれを厳しく批判しました。先月、抗議活動の場で記者2人が拘束されて以来、国民の不満は高まっています。法務大臣は記者たちに寛大な措置を取ることを約束し、まもなく釈放されると述べました。しかし、大臣が示したのは口頭での約束だけで、書面による声明はありませんでした。法律についての最終的な採決は、金曜日に行われる見通しです。6時に首都から中継でお伝えします。","words":[["recess","words:recess"],["parliamentary","words:parliamentary"],["censorship","words:censorship"],["roundly","words:roundly"],["discontent","words:discontent"],["detained","words:detain"],["leniency","words:leniency"],["verbal","words:verbal"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was the main topic of the debate?","o":["A change in the voting age","A new law about the media","The closing of several newspapers","A two-week holiday"],"a":1,"why":"The main topic was a new media law とある。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what happened last month?","o":["A minister resigned.","A newspaper was sold.","A new law was passed.","Two reporters were held at a protest."],"a":3,"why":"two reporters were detained at a protest last month とある。detained を held と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What is expected to happen on Friday?","o":["A vote will take place.","The reporters will give a speech.","The debate will begin.","A written statement will be released."],"a":0,"why":"A final vote on the law is expected on Friday とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0010","page":"words","group":"201〜400","kind":"美術館の音声ガイド","text":"Welcome to Gallery Four. The captivating photographs in this room were taken in the nineteen thirties. Please read the caption below each picture, which gives the place and the date. For more detail, open your guidebook, where the curator has added an annotation for every image and a footnote listing her sources. The largest photograph shows a village ritual held each spring. Visitors often walk past it absently, but look closely at the faces. The artist wanted to elicit a feeling of both joy and loss. The final picture, of an empty farm, is a cautionary image about the cost of drought. When you are ready, continue to Gallery Five on your left.","ja":"第4展示室へようこそ。この部屋にある心を奪うような写真は、1930年代に撮影されたものです。それぞれの写真の下にある説明文をお読みください。場所と日付が書かれています。さらに詳しく知りたい方は、ガイドブックを開いてください。学芸員がすべての写真に注釈を付け、出典を示す脚注も加えています。一番大きな写真は、毎年春に行われる村の儀式を写したものです。来場者はぼんやりと通り過ぎてしまうことが多いのですが、人々の顔をよくご覧ください。作者は、喜びと喪失の両方の感情を引き出そうとしました。最後の1枚、誰もいない農場の写真は、干ばつの代償を伝える戒めの1枚です。準備ができましたら、左手の第5展示室へお進みください。","words":[["captivating","words:captivating"],["caption","words:caption"],["annotation","words:annotation"],["footnote","words:footnote"],["ritual","words:ritual"],["absently","words:absently"],["elicit","words:elicit"],["cautionary","words:cautionary"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is the talk most likely being heard?","o":["In a photography class","At a village festival","In a museum","On a farm"],"a":2,"why":"Welcome to Gallery Four、the curator（学芸員）などから、美術館・博物館の展示室だと分かる。"},{"q":"What can visitors find in the guidebook?","o":["Notes written by the curator","A map of the village","Prices of the photographs","A list of other galleries"],"a":0,"why":"the curator has added an annotation for every image（学芸員がすべての写真に注釈を付けた）とある。annotation を notes と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are the listeners told to do when they are ready?","o":["Return the guidebook","Go to the next gallery","Take a photograph","Read the final caption"],"a":1,"why":"continue to Gallery Five on your left（左の第5展示室へ進む）とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0011","page":"words","group":"201〜400","kind":"会議での提案","text":"Thanks for joining me, everyone. As you know, our cafe chain will remodel all six locations this summer. To pay for it, I'd like to propose a partnership with Green Leaf, a local start-up that delivers fresh produce. Under the plan, we would source all our vegetables from them, and they would promote our cafes on their website. It is a reciprocal deal, so no money changes hands at first. Later, Green Leaf would earn a five percent commission on catering orders. I know some of you are inclined to stay with our current supplier. However, I believe fresher food will induce customers to visit more often. Let's look at the numbers on the next slide.","ja":"皆さん、お集まりいただきありがとうございます。ご存じの通り、当社のカフェチェーンはこの夏、6店舗すべてを改装します。その費用をまかなうために、新鮮な農産物を配達している地元の新興企業、グリーンリーフとの提携を提案したいと思います。この計画では、当社は野菜をすべて同社から仕入れ、同社は自社のウェブサイトで当社のカフェを宣伝します。お互いに利益のある取り決めなので、最初はお金のやり取りはありません。その後、グリーンリーフはケータリングの注文について5パーセントの手数料を受け取ります。今の仕入先を続けたいと考えている方がいることは承知しています。しかし、より新鮮な食材があれば、お客様がもっと頻繁に来店してくれると私は考えています。次のスライドで数字を見てみましょう。","words":[["remodel","words:remodel"],["start-up","words:start-up"],["source","words:source"],["reciprocal","words:reciprocal"],["commission","words:commission"],["inclined","words:inclined"],["induce","words:induce"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will the cafe chain do this summer?","o":["Open six new locations","Change its menu","Hire a new supplier","Renovate its cafes"],"a":3,"why":"our cafe chain will remodel all six locations this summer とある。remodel を renovate と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What kind of business is Green Leaf?","o":["A company that delivers fresh produce","A website design firm","A catering company","A coffee supplier"],"a":0,"why":"a local start-up that delivers fresh produce（新鮮な農産物を配達する地元の新興企業）とある。"},{"q":"What will the speaker most likely do next?","o":["Visit a cafe","Call the current supplier","Show some figures","Take a short break"],"a":2,"why":"Let's look at the numbers on the next slide とある。numbers を figures と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0012","page":"words","group":"401〜600","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"Turning to the economy. After months in which growth seemed to stagnate, the housing market is finally on the upswing. Sales of new homes rose eight percent in March. Analysts say the rise was triggered by lower interest rates and a scarcity of rental apartments in major cities. However, there are risks. Share prices in the construction sector tumbled yesterday after the government announced plans to curb lending. Some experts warn that the new rules could precipitate another slowdown. Others point to the proliferation of online mortgage companies, which make it easier than ever to borrow. The central bank will publish its own forecast next Thursday. Now, here is Lisa with sports.","ja":"続いて経済です。成長が停滞しているように見えた数か月を経て、住宅市場がようやく上向いています。3月の新築住宅の販売は8パーセント増えました。専門家によると、この増加は、金利の低下と、大都市での賃貸アパートの不足が引き金になったとのことです。しかし、リスクもあります。政府が融資を抑制する計画を発表したことを受け、昨日は建設関連の株価が急落しました。新しい規則が再び景気の減速を引き起こしかねない、と警告する専門家もいます。一方で、オンラインの住宅ローン会社が急増し、これまでになく借りやすくなっている点を指摘する声もあります。中央銀行は来週木曜日に独自の見通しを発表します。では、リサがスポーツをお伝えします。","words":[["stagnate","words:stagnate"],["upswing","words:upswing"],["triggered","words:trigger"],["scarcity","words:scarcity"],["tumbled","words:tumble"],["curb","words:curb (名、動)"],["precipitate","words:precipitate"],["proliferation","words:proliferation"]],"qs":[{"q":"According to the speaker, what rose in March?","o":["Interest rates","Sales of new homes","Rents in major cities","Share prices"],"a":1,"why":"Sales of new homes rose eight percent in March とある。金利は下がった側。"},{"q":"Why did share prices in the construction sector fall?","o":["The government plans to limit lending.","A large company closed.","Interest rates went up.","Fewer homes were built."],"a":0,"why":"tumbled yesterday after the government announced plans to curb lending とある。curb を limit と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will the central bank do next Thursday?","o":["Lower interest rates","Meet with analysts","Open an online service","Release a forecast"],"a":3,"why":"The central bank will publish its own forecast next Thursday とある。publish を release と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0013","page":"words","group":"401〜600","kind":"学会の案内","text":"Good morning, and welcome to the tenth International Design Conference. Let me go over today's schedule. At nine thirty, Professor Ito will open the plenary session in the main hall. She will expound on her theory of color and composition. After lunch, the panel will confer on stage about the future of the industry, with live commentary from our host. Workshops on peripheral topics, such as printing and packaging, will be held in rooms two and three. Please note that the issuance of name badges closes at ten, so collect yours at the front desk now. Finally, every participant will receive a small memento of the conference at the closing ceremony. Enjoy the day.","ja":"おはようございます。第10回国際デザイン会議へようこそ。本日の予定をご案内します。9時30分に、伊藤教授がメインホールで全体会を開会します。教授は、色と構図についての自身の理論を詳しく説明します。昼食後は、パネリストが壇上で業界の将来について協議し、司会者がその場で解説を加えます。印刷や包装といった周辺的なテーマのワークショップは、第2・第3会議室で行います。名札の発行は10時で締め切りますので、今のうちに受付でお受け取りください。最後に、閉会式で参加者全員に会議のささやかな記念品をお渡しします。どうぞ良い一日を。","words":[["plenary","words:plenary"],["expound","words:expound"],["composition","words:composition"],["confer","words:confer"],["commentary","words:commentary"],["peripheral","words:peripheral"],["issuance","words:issuance"],["memento","words:memento"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who most likely is the speaker?","o":["A professor of design","A hotel receptionist","A conference organizer","A printing company employee"],"a":2,"why":"会議の予定を案内し、名札や閉会式について説明しているので、会議の運営側だと分かる。伊藤教授は別の人物。"},{"q":"What will Professor Ito talk about?","o":["Printing and packaging","Color and composition","The history of the conference","The future of the industry"],"a":1,"why":"She will expound on her theory of color and composition とある。業界の将来はパネルの話題。"},{"q":"What are the listeners advised to do now?","o":["Pick up their name badges","Go to room two","Have lunch","Choose a workshop"],"a":0,"why":"the issuance of name badges closes at ten, so collect yours at the front desk now とある。collect を pick up と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0014","page":"words","group":"401〜600","kind":"店の広告","text":"Tech lovers, this one is for you. Circuit World opens its doors this Saturday at the Riverside Mall. Look for the dazzling blue lights and the freestanding sign at the north entrance. Inside, you will find every gadget you can imagine, from smart watches to robot vacuums. To entice early shoppers, the first one hundred customers will receive a free pair of wireless earphones. Our sensational opening offer does not stop there. Bring in an old phone, and our staff will retrieve your photos and contacts for free. We can also outfit your home office with a desk, a monitor, and a printer for under five hundred dollars. Circuit World. Saturday at ten. Don't miss it.","ja":"電子機器が好きな皆さんへのお知らせです。サーキット・ワールドが今週土曜日、リバーサイド・モールにオープンします。北口の、まばゆい青い照明と自立式の看板が目印です。店内には、スマートウォッチからロボット掃除機まで、思いつく限りの機器がそろっています。早めにご来店いただけるよう、先着100名様にワイヤレスイヤホンを無料で差し上げます。驚きのオープン記念はそれだけではありません。古い携帯電話をお持ちいただければ、スタッフが写真と連絡先を無料で取り出します。また、机・モニター・プリンターをそろえて、ご自宅の仕事部屋を500ドル未満で整えることもできます。サーキット・ワールド。土曜日の10時です。お見逃しなく。","words":[["dazzling","words:dazzling"],["freestanding","words:freestanding"],["gadget","words:gadget"],["entice","words:entice"],["sensational","words:sensational"],["retrieve","words:retrieve"],["outfit","words:outfit"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen on Saturday?","o":["A mall will close for repairs.","A phone company will hold a sale.","A new product will be released.","A store will open."],"a":3,"why":"Circuit World opens its doors this Saturday（今週土曜日にオープンする）とある。"},{"q":"What will the first one hundred customers receive?","o":["Free earphones","A discount on a printer","A smart watch","A gift card"],"a":0,"why":"the first one hundred customers will receive a free pair of wireless earphones とある。"},{"q":"What does the store offer to do with an old phone?","o":["Buy it for five hundred dollars","Repair its screen","Recover the data for free","Exchange it for a new one"],"a":2,"why":"our staff will retrieve your photos and contacts for free とある。retrieve photos and contacts を recover the data と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0015","page":"words","group":"401〜600","kind":"部門長の話","text":"Thank you all for coming at short notice. I want to speak frankly about the Atlas project. Last quarter, we were indecisive. We changed the design three times, and the project was relegated to the bottom of our priority list. The customer's verdict was clear: they were disappointed. I am not here to reproach anyone, because the responsibility is mine. From today, things will be different. First, every team will work in alignment with one shared schedule. Second, we will execute the plan exactly as written, with no changes unless I approve them. Third, I will meet the customer every Friday to report our progress. If we work together, we can still deliver by June. Are there any questions?","ja":"急な呼びかけにもかかわらず、お集まりいただきありがとうございます。アトラス計画について率直にお話しします。前の四半期、私たちは優柔不断でした。設計を3回変更し、この計画は優先順位の一番下に追いやられました。お客様の判断は明確で、失望したというものでした。誰かを責めるために集まってもらったのではありません。責任は私にあるからです。今日から、やり方を変えます。第一に、すべてのチームが1つの共通の日程に合わせて動きます。第二に、計画を書かれた通りに実行し、私の承認がない限り変更はしません。第三に、私が毎週金曜日にお客様と会い、進み具合を報告します。力を合わせれば、まだ6月までに納品できます。質問はありますか。","words":[["indecisive","words:indecisive"],["relegated","words:relegate"],["verdict","words:verdict"],["reproach","words:reproach"],["alignment","words:alignment (配置以外)"],["execute","words:execute"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does the speaker mention about last quarter?","o":["The design was changed several times.","A customer canceled an order.","The team missed a Friday meeting.","Several employees left the company."],"a":0,"why":"We changed the design three times とある。three times を several times と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Who does the speaker say is responsible?","o":["The customer","The design team","The speaker","The project's first manager"],"a":2,"why":"I am not here to reproach anyone, because the responsibility is mine（責任は私にある）とある。"},{"q":"What will the speaker do every Friday?","o":["Approve design changes","Meet with the customer","Review the priority list","Hold a team lunch"],"a":1,"why":"I will meet the customer every Friday to report our progress とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0016","page":"words","group":"401〜600","kind":"厨房スタッフへの連絡","text":"Attention, all kitchen staff. During yesterday's inspection, the health officer found traces of dust near the refrigerators. This is baffling, because the area is cleaned every night. For some unaccountable reason, the cleaning record for Tuesday is also missing. To solve the problem, we will deploy an extra cleaning team for the next two weeks. From today, please wipe all counters with disinfectant at the end of each shift, and sign the sheet on the wall when you finish. New bottles are stored in the cabinet under the sink. The officer will return on the fifteenth. Let's make sure everything is perfect by then. Thank you.","ja":"厨房スタッフの皆さんにお知らせします。昨日の検査で、保健所の担当官が冷蔵庫の近くにほこりの跡を見つけました。その場所は毎晩掃除しているので、不可解なことです。また、説明のつかない理由で、火曜日の清掃記録もなくなっています。この問題を解決するため、今後2週間、追加の清掃チームを配置します。今日から、各シフトの終わりにすべての調理台を消毒剤で拭き、終わったら壁の用紙に署名してください。新しいボトルは流しの下の棚に入っています。担当官は15日に再び来ます。それまでに、すべてを完璧な状態にしておきましょう。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["baffling","words:baffling"],["unaccountable","words:unaccountable"],["deploy","words:deploy"],["disinfectant","words:disinfectant"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where do the listeners most likely work?","o":["In a hospital","In a cleaning company","In a kitchen","In a furniture store"],"a":2,"why":"冒頭の Attention, all kitchen staff から、厨房で働く人たちへの連絡だと分かる。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what is missing?","o":["A bottle of disinfectant","A refrigerator part","A set of keys","A cleaning record"],"a":3,"why":"the cleaning record for Tuesday is also missing とある。"},{"q":"What will happen on the fifteenth?","o":["The health officer will come back.","New refrigerators will arrive.","The extra team will leave.","The kitchen will be closed."],"a":0,"why":"The officer will return on the fifteenth とある。return を come back と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0017","page":"words","group":"11/20（金）","kind":"芸能ニュース","text":"And now, entertainment news. The city's new waterfront cinema will be inaugurated this Friday with the film adaptation of the best-selling novel The Lighthouse Keeper. Critics say the movie is faithful to the book, although the sad ending has been changed. The story was filmed on a small Mediterranean island, and the opening scene, shot on an old wooden pier, is especially beautiful. The soundtrack is an eclectic mix of jazz and folk music. The lead roles are played by Anna Costa and James Hall, who will attend the opening on Friday and Saturday, respectively. Tickets went on sale this morning, and interest is not expected to fade off soon. Book early to avoid disappointment.","ja":"続いて芸能ニュースです。市の新しい海沿いの映画館が今週金曜日に開館し、ベストセラー小説『灯台守』の映画化作品で幕を開けます。批評家によると、悲しい結末は変更されているものの、映画は原作に忠実だということです。物語は地中海の小さな島で撮影され、古い木造の桟橋で撮られた冒頭の場面は特に美しいです。音楽は、ジャズとフォークを取り混ぜた多彩な構成です。主演はアンナ・コスタとジェームズ・ホールで、2人はそれぞれ金曜日と土曜日の上映初日に来場します。チケットは今朝発売され、関心はすぐには薄れそうにありません。がっかりしないよう、早めにご予約ください。","words":[["inaugurated","words:inaugurate"],["film adaptation","words:film adaptation"],["faithful","words:faithful"],["Mediterranean","words:Mediterranean"],["pier","words:pier"],["eclectic","words:eclectic"],["respectively","words:respectively"],["fade off","words:fade off"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen this Friday?","o":["A novel will be published.","A new cinema will open.","A music festival will begin.","A film will be shot on an island."],"a":1,"why":"The city's new waterfront cinema will be inaugurated this Friday とある。inaugurated（開館する）を open と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What do critics say about the movie?","o":["It is too long.","Its music is disappointing.","It follows the book closely.","Its opening scene should be cut."],"a":2,"why":"the movie is faithful to the book（原作に忠実）とある。faithful to を follows closely と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are the listeners advised to do?","o":["Buy tickets early","Read the novel first","Arrive on Saturday","Visit the pier"],"a":0,"why":"Book early to avoid disappointment とある。book を buy tickets と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0018","page":"words","group":"11/20（金）","kind":"留守番電話","text":"Hello, Mr. Dawson. This is Rachel from Parkside Properties. I'm pleased to tell you that the owner has accepted your offer, so we have come to an agreement on the office lease. The rent will be only marginally higher than you proposed. There are a few things left to do. First, you must sign the contract in person at our office by Friday. Second, please surrender the keys to your current unit when you move out. Third, our inspector has to certify that the furniture is in good condition. He noticed some damage to the upholstery on two chairs, so I will email you photographs for future reference. Please call me back at your convenience. Thank you.","ja":"ドーソン様、こんにちは。パークサイド不動産のレイチェルです。オーナーがお申し出を受け入れましたので、事務所の賃貸契約について合意に達したことをお知らせします。家賃は、ご提案の額よりわずかに高いだけです。あといくつか手続きが残っています。まず、金曜日までに当社の事務所へ直接お越しいただき、契約書に署名してください。次に、退去の際に、今お使いの部屋の鍵を引き渡してください。そして、家具が良い状態であることを、当社の検査員が証明する必要があります。検査員が椅子2脚の布張りに傷みがあるのに気づきましたので、今後の参考のために写真をメールでお送りします。ご都合のよいときに折り返しお電話ください。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["come to an agreement","words:come to an agreement"],["lease","words:lease"],["marginally","words:marginally"],["in person","words:in person"],["surrender","words:surrender (降伏以外)"],["certify","words:certify"],["upholstery","words:upholstery"],["for future reference","words:for future reference"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the speaker calling?","o":["To cancel an appointment","To ask for a higher rent","To report damage to an office","To say that an offer was accepted"],"a":3,"why":"the owner has accepted your offer（オーナーが申し出を受け入れた）が用件。"},{"q":"What must Mr. Dawson do by Friday?","o":["Sign a contract at the office","Pay the first month's rent","Repair two chairs","Return a phone call"],"a":0,"why":"you must sign the contract in person at our office by Friday とある。"},{"q":"What will the speaker send by email?","o":["A copy of the keys","A list of furniture","Some photographs","A new contract"],"a":2,"why":"I will email you photographs for future reference とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0019","page":"words","group":"11/20（金）","kind":"会議での報告","text":"Let's begin. First, Mr. Tanaka from the planning department cannot join us today because of a prior commitment, so I will present his report. As you know, an errant email last month sent the wrong prices to forty customers. It took some careful maneuvering, but we kept all of them. I can assure you that the error has been fixed, and we now guarantee a reply to every complaint within one day. The new schedule also allows for delays in shipping. Managers, please explain the changes to your subordinates this week. The pressure should ease off by the end of the month, and I am confident we will soon reap the rewards of our hard work.","ja":"始めましょう。まず、企画部の田中さんは先約があって今日は参加できないので、私が代わりに報告します。ご存じの通り、先月、誤って送られたメールのせいで、40社のお客様に間違った価格が届きました。慎重な対応が必要でしたが、すべてのお客様を失わずに済みました。誤りは修正済みであることを私が請け合います。また今後は、すべての苦情に1日以内に返答することを保証します。新しい日程は、配送の遅れも見込んだものになっています。管理職の皆さんは、今週中に部下へ変更点を説明してください。月末までには負担も和らぐはずですし、私たちの努力の成果はまもなく得られると確信しています。","words":[["planning department","words:planning department"],["prior commitment","words:prior commitment"],["errant","words:errant"],["maneuvering","words:maneuver"],["assure","words:guarantee と assure の違い"],["allows for","words:allow for"],["subordinates","words:subordinate"],["ease off","words:ease off"],["reap the rewards of","words:reap the rewards of"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is Mr. Tanaka absent from the meeting?","o":["He is visiting a customer.","He has another appointment.","He is on vacation.","He is feeling unwell."],"a":1,"why":"because of a prior commitment（先約があるため）とある。prior commitment を another appointment と言い換えている。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what happened last month?","o":["Forty customers canceled their orders.","A shipment was delayed.","Incorrect prices were sent to customers.","A manager left the company."],"a":2,"why":"an errant email last month sent the wrong prices to forty customers とある。お客様は1社も失っていない。"},{"q":"What are the managers asked to do this week?","o":["Explain the changes to their staff","Reply to every complaint","Write a new schedule","Meet with Mr. Tanaka"],"a":0,"why":"Managers, please explain the changes to your subordinates this week とある。subordinates を staff と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0020","page":"words","group":"601〜800","kind":"留守番電話","text":"Hello, this is a message for Ms. Nguyen from the Lakeside Medical Society. We are delighted to invite you to our annual symposium, which will convene on May ninth at the Grand Hotel. A short ceremony will precede the first lecture. During the ceremony, we will pay tribute to Dr. Samuel Ortiz for his tireless work in rural clinics, and local children will present him with a garland of flowers. After a busy morning of talks, lunch on the terrace should offer a pleasant respite. Seats are limited, so please RSVP by April twentieth, either by email or by calling this number. We hope to see you there.","ja":"もしもし、レイクサイド医学会からグエン様へのご連絡です。年に一度のシンポジウムにご招待いたします。5月9日にグランドホテルで開かれます。最初の講演の前に、短い式典を行います。式典では、地方の診療所でたゆみない活動を続けてこられたサミュエル・オルティス医師に敬意を表し、地元の子どもたちが花輪を贈ります。講演の続く忙しい午前のあとは、テラスでの昼食が心地よいひと休みになるはずです。席に限りがありますので、4月20日までに、メールまたはこの番号へのお電話で出欠をお知らせください。お会いできるのを楽しみにしております。","words":[["symposium","words:symposium"],["convene","words:convene"],["precede","words:precede"],["tribute","words:tribute"],["tireless","words:tireless"],["garland","words:garland"],["respite","words:respite"],["RSVP","words:RSVP"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the message?","o":["To cancel a lecture","To invite someone to an event","To book a hotel room","To ask for a donation"],"a":1,"why":"We are delighted to invite you to our annual symposium（年次シンポジウムにご招待する）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen during the ceremony?","o":["Lunch will be served.","Children will give a talk.","A new clinic will be opened.","A doctor will be honored."],"a":3,"why":"we will pay tribute to Dr. Samuel Ortiz とある。pay tribute to を be honored と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What is the listener asked to do by April twentieth?","o":["Reply to the invitation","Pay a registration fee","Send flowers","Prepare a lecture"],"a":0,"why":"please RSVP by April twentieth とある。RSVP は「出欠の返事をする」。"}]},
{"id":"w-0021","page":"words","group":"601〜800","kind":"住宅の広告","text":"Is your apartment starting to feel cramped? Then come and see Hilltop Gardens, the city's newest residential tower. Every unit on the upper floors offers a marvelous vista of the bay. More than two hundred families already reside here, and our clientele includes doctors, teachers, and young professionals. Until the end of June, you can make a provisional booking with a deposit of just five hundred dollars, which is fully refundable. And if you introduce a friend, you will both receive one month of free parking through our referral program. Our show apartment is open daily from ten to six. Hilltop Gardens. Come home to something better.","ja":"お住まいのアパートが手狭に感じてきていませんか。それなら、市内で最も新しい住宅タワー、ヒルトップ・ガーデンズをご覧ください。上層階のすべての部屋から、湾の素晴らしい眺めが楽しめます。すでに200を超えるご家族が暮らしており、入居者には医師、教師、若い専門職の方々がいらっしゃいます。6月末までは、わずか500ドルの手付金で仮予約ができ、手付金は全額返金可能です。また、ご友人を紹介していただくと、紹介制度により、お二人とも1か月分の駐車場が無料になります。モデルルームは毎日10時から6時まで開いています。ヒルトップ・ガーデンズ。より良い暮らしへ。","words":[["cramped","words:cramped"],["marvelous","words:marvelous"],["vista","words:vista"],["reside","words:reside"],["clientele","words:clientele"],["provisional","words:provisional"],["deposit","words:deposit (預金以外)"],["referral","words:referral"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is being advertised?","o":["A parking garage","A moving company","An apartment building","A hotel by the bay"],"a":2,"why":"the city's newest residential tower（市内で最も新しい住宅タワー）の広告。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the deposit?","o":["It must be paid in June.","It can be returned.","It includes parking fees.","It is five thousand dollars."],"a":1,"why":"a deposit of just five hundred dollars, which is fully refundable とある。refundable を can be returned と言い換えている。"},{"q":"How can the listeners get free parking?","o":["By visiting the show apartment","By booking before June","By renting an upper floor","By introducing a friend"],"a":3,"why":"if you introduce a friend, you will both receive one month of free parking とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0022","page":"words","group":"601〜800","kind":"経済番組","text":"Good evening, and welcome to Money Matters. Tonight we ask: is a recession coming? Several pundits have warned of an impending slowdown, and one even used the word depression. They point out that the national currency has depreciated by ten percent this year, and that household debt now surpasses the level of two thousand eight. Other experts say these fears are grossly exaggerated. They argue that rising costs pose a smaller risk than before, because families have already cut their discretionary spending. Still, everyone agrees on one thing: the government must act quickly to mitigate the damage to small businesses. After the break, we will hear from the minister of finance. Stay with us.","ja":"こんばんは。「マネー・マターズ」へようこそ。今夜のテーマは「景気後退は来るのか」です。何人かの評論家が、差し迫った景気減速を警告しており、「不況」という言葉を使った人までいます。彼らは、今年に入って自国通貨の価値が10パーセント下がったこと、家計の負債が2008年の水準を上回っていることを指摘しています。一方、こうした懸念は著しく誇張されていると言う専門家もいます。家庭がすでに裁量的な支出を減らしているため、物価上昇がもたらすリスクは以前より小さい、というのがその主張です。それでも、全員が一致している点が1つあります。小規模な事業者への打撃を和らげるために、政府は素早く動かなければならない、ということです。休憩のあとは、財務大臣に話を聞きます。そのままお待ちください。","words":[["pundits","words:pundit"],["impending","words:impending"],["depression","words:depression"],["depreciated","words:depreciate"],["surpasses","words:surpass"],["grossly","words:grossly"],["pose","words:pose"],["discretionary","words:discretionary"],["mitigate","words:mitigate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main topic of the program?","o":["The possibility of an economic downturn","A change in tax rules","The history of the national currency","How to start a small business"],"a":0,"why":"is a recession coming?（景気後退は来るのか）が今夜のテーマ。recession を economic downturn と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What do some experts say about the fears?","o":["They are shared by the government.","They began in two thousand eight.","They are overstated.","They affect only small businesses."],"a":2,"why":"these fears are grossly exaggerated（著しく誇張されている）とある。exaggerated を overstated と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Who will speak after the break?","o":["A small business owner","A government minister","A bank manager","A university professor"],"a":1,"why":"we will hear from the minister of finance とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0023","page":"words","group":"601〜800","kind":"組織変更の説明","text":"Good afternoon. I'd like to explain the reorganization that begins next month. The sales and service departments will merge, and Ms. Clark will serve as interim director until a permanent leader is chosen. A new duty roster will be posted on Monday, and a breakdown of each team's budget will follow by email. I know change is hard. Customer needs will dictate our priorities from now on, not old habits. Our standing meeting on Thursday mornings will continue as usual. We have also enlisted a consultant to help untangle the two computer systems, which currently do not share data. If you have concerns, my door is always open. Thank you for your patience.","ja":"こんにちは。来月から始まる組織再編についてご説明します。営業部とサービス部は統合され、正式な責任者が決まるまで、クラークさんが暫定の部長を務めます。月曜日に新しい勤務当番表を掲示し、各チームの予算の内訳はメールで追ってお知らせします。変化が大変なことは分かっています。これからは、古い習慣ではなく、お客様のニーズが私たちの優先順位を決めます。木曜日の朝の定例会議は、これまで通り続けます。また、今はデータを共有できていない2つのコンピューターシステムの問題を解きほぐすために、コンサルタントの協力を得ました。心配なことがあれば、いつでも私のところへ来てください。ご理解に感謝します。","words":[["reorganization","words:reorganization"],["interim","words:interim"],["roster","words:roster"],["breakdown","words:breakdown"],["dictate","words:dictate"],["standing","words:standing"],["enlisted","words:enlist"],["untangle","words:untangle"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the speaker announcing?","o":["The opening of a new office","A new customer service policy","The hiring of a director","A change in the company's structure"],"a":3,"why":"the reorganization that begins next month（来月からの組織再編）を説明している。"},{"q":"What will be posted on Monday?","o":["A work schedule","A budget report","A list of customers","A meeting agenda"],"a":0,"why":"A new duty roster will be posted on Monday とある。duty roster（勤務当番表）を work schedule と言い換えている。予算の内訳はメールで届く。"},{"q":"Why has a consultant been brought in?","o":["To train the sales staff","To choose a permanent leader","To help combine two computer systems","To reduce the budget"],"a":2,"why":"enlisted a consultant to help untangle the two computer systems, which currently do not share data とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0024","page":"words","group":"601〜800","kind":"大学の初回授業","text":"Welcome to Introduction to Marine Biology. Before we start, please take a copy of the syllabus from the front desk. It lists every lecture and reading for the term. Don't worry, there are not reams of pages to read each week. As the university prospectus explains, this course includes a three-day excursion to the coast in October. The trip is optional, but students who forgo it must write an extra report. A red star next to a date signifies a test. Missing a test without a doctor's note will preclude you from passing, and competition for top grades is stiff. Now, please open your textbooks to chapter one.","ja":"「海洋生物学入門」へようこそ。始める前に、前の机から講義概要を1部取ってください。今学期のすべての講義と課題図書が載っています。ご心配なく、毎週大量のページを読むわけではありません。大学案内にある通り、この授業には10月に海岸への3日間の小旅行が含まれています。参加は自由ですが、参加を見送る学生は追加のレポートを書かなければなりません。日付の横の赤い星印は、試験を意味します。医師の診断書なしに試験を欠席すると合格できなくなりますし、上位の成績をめぐる競争は厳しいです。では、教科書の第1章を開いてください。","words":[["syllabus","words:syllabus"],["reams","words:reams"],["prospectus","words:prospectus"],["excursion","words:excursion"],["forgo","words:forgo"],["signifies","words:signify"],["preclude","words:preclude"],["stiff","words:stiff"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who most likely are the listeners?","o":["Tour guides","University students","Doctors","Bookstore staff"],"a":1,"why":"講義概要、今学期、試験、成績などの話から、大学の授業の受講生だと分かる。"},{"q":"What must students do if they do not go on the trip?","o":["Take an extra test","Pay a fee","Bring a doctor's note","Write an additional report"],"a":3,"why":"students who forgo it must write an extra report とある。forgo（見送る）、extra を additional と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does a red star next to a date indicate?","o":["A test","A holiday","A trip to the coast","A reading assignment"],"a":0,"why":"A red star next to a date signifies a test とある。signifies を indicate と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0025","page":"words","group":"601〜800","kind":"地域ニュース","text":"In regional news, a small earthquake shook the coast early this morning. Its epicenter was located twenty kilometers offshore. No injuries were reported, but the shaking dislodged several roof tiles in the old harbor district. Workshops where local artists craft traditional pottery were also damaged. The city has opened a help desk at the town hall, where residents can reclaim the cost of emergency repairs. Please bring photographs and receipts. Officials have also asked people not to tamper with broken gas pipes or power lines. Instead, call the emergency number and wait for an engineer. The harbor road will remain closed until inspectors finish their work this afternoon.","ja":"地域のニュースです。今朝早く、小さな地震が沿岸部を揺らしました。震源は沖合20キロの地点でした。けが人の報告はありませんが、揺れによって旧港地区で屋根瓦が数枚外れました。地元の作家が伝統的な陶器を丹念に作っている工房にも被害が出ています。市は役場に相談窓口を設け、住民はそこで応急修理の費用の払い戻しを求めることができます。写真と領収書をお持ちください。また当局は、壊れたガス管や電線に勝手に触らないよう呼びかけています。その場合は緊急番号に電話し、技術者の到着を待ってください。港の道路は、今日の午後に検査員の作業が終わるまで閉鎖されたままです。","words":[["epicenter","words:epicenter"],["dislodged","words:dislodge"],["craft","words:craft"],["reclaim","words:reclaim"],["tamper","words:tamper"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened this morning?","o":["A fire broke out at the harbor.","A workshop was opened.","An earthquake occurred.","A road was repaired."],"a":2,"why":"a small earthquake shook the coast early this morning とある。"},{"q":"What should residents bring to the help desk?","o":["Pieces of pottery","Photographs and receipts","Their identification cards","Broken roof tiles"],"a":1,"why":"Please bring photographs and receipts とある。"},{"q":"What are people asked NOT to do?","o":["Call the emergency number","Visit the town hall","Use the harbor road in the evening","Touch damaged pipes or power lines"],"a":3,"why":"not to tamper with broken gas pipes or power lines とある。tamper with を touch と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0026","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）①","kind":"企業ニュース","text":"In business news, the board of directors of Nova Media voted last night to enter into an agreement with the publisher Bright Books. Under the deal, Nova will hold exclusive rights to turn the company's novels into television dramas. The contract sets a precedent, as it is the first of its kind in the country. According to an internal memorandum, lawyers will scrutinize the final details over the next two weeks. Meanwhile, Nova has put its plans for a new sports channel on hold while it studies the viability of the project. Shares in both companies rose slightly this morning. We'll have more business news at the top of the hour.","ja":"ビジネスニュースです。ノヴァ・メディアの取締役会は昨夜、出版社ブライト・ブックスと契約を結ぶことを決議しました。この取り決めにより、ノヴァは同社の小説をテレビドラマ化する独占権を持つことになります。この種の契約は国内で初めてであり、前例を作るものです。社内の連絡メモによると、今後2週間かけて弁護士が最終的な細部を綿密に調べます。一方ノヴァは、新しいスポーツチャンネルの計画について、事業として成り立つかどうかを検討する間、保留にしています。今朝は両社の株価がわずかに上がりました。ビジネスニュースは、次の正時にもお伝えします。","words":[["board of directors","words:board of directors"],["enter into an agreement","words:enter into an agreement"],["exclusive rights","words:exclusive rights"],["precedent","words:precedent"],["memorandum","words:memorandum"],["scrutinize","words:scrutinize"],["put its plans for a new sports channel on hold","words:put A on hold"],["viability","words:viability"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the board of directors decide to do?","o":["Launch a sports channel","Make a deal with a publisher","Sell the company's shares","Hire more lawyers"],"a":1,"why":"voted last night to enter into an agreement with the publisher Bright Books とある。enter into an agreement を make a deal と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will lawyers do over the next two weeks?","o":["Write a memorandum","Meet the board of directors","Examine the details of the contract","Study the sports market"],"a":2,"why":"lawyers will scrutinize the final details とある。scrutinize を examine と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What has Nova Media delayed?","o":["Its plans for a sports channel","The release of a television drama","A meeting with Bright Books","The sale of its novels"],"a":0,"why":"Nova has put its plans for a new sports channel on hold とある。put on hold を delayed と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0027","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）①","kind":"実験室スタッフへの連絡","text":"Attention, all laboratory staff. New safety rules will go into effect on the first of next month. First, all combustible materials must be stored in the metal cabinets at the back of the room. Second, please detach the power cables from the heaters at the end of each day. Third, wear gloves when handling the cleaning liquid, as it can irritate your skin. An engineer will inspect every room next week and will also insulate the pipes near the windows before winter. If you have questions about the new rules, speak to your department head. A full list is posted beside the main door. Thank you for helping us keep the workplace safe.","ja":"実験室スタッフの皆さんにお知らせします。来月1日から、新しい安全規則が施行されます。第一に、可燃性の物質はすべて、部屋の奥にある金属製の棚に保管してください。第二に、毎日の終わりに、暖房器具から電源コードを取り外してください。第三に、洗浄液は肌を刺激することがあるので、扱うときは手袋を着用してください。来週、技術者がすべての部屋を点検し、冬になる前に窓際の配管に断熱材も取り付けます。新しい規則について質問がある場合は、所属の部門長に聞いてください。規則の全文は正面のドアの横に掲示してあります。職場の安全にご協力いただき、ありがとうございます。","words":[["go into effect","words:go into effect"],["combustible","words:combustible"],["detach","words:detach"],["irritate","words:irritate"],["inspect","words:inspect"],["insulate","words:insulate"],["department head","words:department head"]],"qs":[{"q":"When will the new rules begin?","o":["At the end of each day","Next week","Before winter","On the first of next month"],"a":3,"why":"New safety rules will go into effect on the first of next month とある。"},{"q":"Why should staff wear gloves?","o":["The heaters become very hot.","The liquid may harm their skin.","The cabinets have sharp edges.","The pipes are cold."],"a":1,"why":"wear gloves when handling the cleaning liquid, as it can irritate your skin とある。irritate を harm と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Where can the listeners find the full list of rules?","o":["Beside the main door","In the metal cabinets","On the company website","At the engineer's office"],"a":0,"why":"A full list is posted beside the main door とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0028","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）①","kind":"ラジオのグルメ紹介","text":"This week on City Eats, I visited Olive and Stone, a small restaurant that has quickly earned a reputation for its seafood. On weekends, diners flock here from all over the region, and it is easy to see why. I began with an assortment of grilled vegetables, followed by an exquisite fish soup with a hint of lemon. My only complaint is that the iced tea was diluted with too much water. The staff are personable and quick, and the garden, which has a lovely water feature, is perfect for summer evenings. Prices are reasonable, but tables are few, so you should book at least a week ahead. I give it four stars out of five.","ja":"今週の「シティ・イーツ」では、オリーブ・アンド・ストーンを訪ねました。シーフードであっという間に評判を得た小さなレストランです。週末には地域中からお客が押し寄せますが、その理由はすぐに分かります。私はまず焼き野菜の盛り合わせを、続いてほんのりレモンの香りがする絶品の魚のスープをいただきました。唯一の不満は、アイスティーが水で薄まりすぎていたことです。スタッフは感じがよくて手際もよく、すてきな噴水のある庭は夏の夕べにぴったりです。値段は手ごろですが、席数が少ないので、少なくとも1週間前には予約したほうがよいでしょう。評価は5つ星のうち4つです。","words":[["earned a reputation","words:earn a reputation"],["flock","words:flock (動)"],["assortment","words:assortment"],["exquisite","words:exquisite"],["a hint of","words:a hint of"],["diluted","words:dilute"],["personable","words:personable"],["water feature","words:water feature"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the restaurant known for?","o":["Its garden parties","Its low prices","Its seafood","Its iced tea"],"a":2,"why":"has quickly earned a reputation for its seafood とある。"},{"q":"What did the speaker dislike?","o":["The iced tea","The fish soup","The slow service","The noisy garden"],"a":0,"why":"My only complaint is that the iced tea was diluted with too much water とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker recommend?","o":["Visiting on a weekday morning","Ordering the vegetables","Sitting indoors","Making a reservation in advance"],"a":3,"why":"you should book at least a week ahead とある。book ahead を make a reservation in advance と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0029","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）①","kind":"交通情報","text":"This is a travel update for visitors to Pine Island. Because of strong winds, the ferry service has been suspended, and about three hundred tourists are stranded at the port. The winds are expected to subside by early evening. Until then, a free shuttle will run between the port and the visitor center every twenty minutes. Please note that the access road to the lighthouse is closed, and no one may set foot on the north beach. Temperatures will fluctuate sharply tonight, so it would be prudent to carry a warm jacket. Officials are looking into the possibility of an extra ferry tomorrow morning. Listen to this station for further updates.","ja":"パイン島を訪れている皆さんへの交通情報です。強風のためフェリーの運航が見合わせとなり、約300人の観光客が港で足止めされています。風は夕方の早い時間までに収まる見込みです。それまでの間、港とビジターセンターの間を無料の往復バスが20分おきに運行します。灯台への連絡道路は閉鎖されており、北の浜辺には誰も立ち入ることができませんのでご注意ください。今夜は気温が大きく変動しますので、暖かい上着をお持ちになるのが賢明です。当局は、明日の朝に臨時のフェリーを出せるかどうかを調べています。今後の情報は、この放送でお聞きください。","words":[["stranded","words:stranded"],["subside","words:subside"],["shuttle","words:shuttle"],["access road","words:access road"],["set foot on","words:set foot on"],["fluctuate","words:fluctuate"],["prudent","words:prudent"],["looking into","words:look into"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why has the ferry service been suspended?","o":["A ferry needs repairs.","The port is too crowded.","The road is closed.","The winds are strong."],"a":3,"why":"Because of strong winds, the ferry service has been suspended とある。"},{"q":"How often will the shuttle run?","o":["Every ten minutes","Every twenty minutes","Once an hour","Only in the evening"],"a":1,"why":"a free shuttle will run ... every twenty minutes とある。"},{"q":"What are officials considering?","o":["An additional ferry","A new visitor center","A refund for tourists","A road to the north beach"],"a":0,"why":"looking into the possibility of an extra ferry tomorrow morning とある。extra を additional と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0030","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）①","kind":"採用についての連絡","text":"Hello, everyone. I'd like to update you on our search for a new accountant. We placed a classified advertisement last week and have already received thirty applications. Only five candidates are fully qualified, so interviews will begin on Tuesday. Please enter your comments into the shared file after each interview. A short note will suffice. One warning: someone has been impersonating our company online and asking applicants for money, so tell candidates to use only our official website. Also, I know we are all busy, but please do not procrastinate. I will delegate the reference checks to Marcus, and we have decided to outsource the background checks to an agency. Any questions?","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。新しい経理担当者の採用状況をお伝えします。先週、求人広告を出し、すでに30件の応募がありました。条件を完全に満たしている候補者は5人だけなので、面接は火曜日から始めます。面接が終わるたびに、共有ファイルに所見を入力してください。短いメモで十分です。1つ注意があります。何者かがネット上で当社になりすまし、応募者に金銭を要求しています。候補者には、公式ウェブサイトだけを使うよう伝えてください。それから、全員忙しいのは承知していますが、先延ばしにはしないでください。推薦者への確認はマーカスに任せます。また、経歴の調査は代行業者に外部委託することにしました。質問はありますか。","words":[["classified advertisement","words:classified advertisement"],["applications","words:application (申請)"],["qualified","words:qualified"],["enter","words:enter (入力する)"],["suffice","words:suffice"],["impersonating","words:impersonate"],["procrastinate","words:procrastinate"],["delegate","words:delegate"],["outsource","words:outsource"]],"qs":[{"q":"What position is the company trying to fill?","o":["A website designer","A sales manager","An accountant","A receptionist"],"a":2,"why":"our search for a new accountant（新しい経理担当者探し）とある。"},{"q":"What warning does the speaker give?","o":["Someone is pretending to be the company.","The shared file has been deleted.","Too few people have applied.","The interviews may be canceled."],"a":0,"why":"someone has been impersonating our company online とある。impersonating を pretending to be と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Who will check the candidates' references?","o":["An outside agency","The speaker","The new accountant","Marcus"],"a":3,"why":"I will delegate the reference checks to Marcus とある。外部の業者に任せるのは background checks（経歴調査）のほう。"}]},
{"id":"w-0031","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）①","kind":"図書館の催し","text":"Good evening, and thank you for coming to the Westfield Library. Tonight's event is part of our community outreach program. Our guest, the historian Paul Grant, has written a book that chronicles one hundred years of life in this town. The book is made up of letters, photographs, and interviews with local families. Mr. Grant is an observant writer, and his descriptions of the old market will illuminate a period that many of us never knew. He will begin by reading a short excerpt from chapter three. Afterward, there will be time for questions, and copies of the book will be on sale in the lobby. Please welcome Paul Grant.","ja":"こんばんは。ウェストフィールド図書館にお越しいただき、ありがとうございます。今夜の催しは、当館の地域向け活動の一環です。ゲストの歴史家ポール・グラントさんは、この町の100年の暮らしを記録した本を書かれました。この本は、手紙、写真、そして地元のご家族への聞き取りで構成されています。グラントさんは観察力の鋭い書き手で、昔の市場の描写は、私たちの多くが知らない時代を明らかにしてくれるでしょう。最初に、第3章から短い一節を朗読していただきます。そのあと質問の時間を設け、ロビーでは本の販売も行います。それでは、ポール・グラントさんをお迎えください。","words":[["outreach","words:outreach"],["chronicles","words:chronicle"],["is made up of","words:be made up of"],["observant","words:observant"],["illuminate","words:illuminate"],["excerpt","words:excerpt"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is the event taking place?","o":["At a bookstore","At a library","At a town market","At a history museum"],"a":1,"why":"thank you for coming to the Westfield Library とある。"},{"q":"What is Mr. Grant's book about?","o":["The history of the town","Famous markets of the world","How to take photographs","A local family's business"],"a":0,"why":"a book that chronicles one hundred years of life in this town とある。"},{"q":"What will Mr. Grant do first?","o":["Answer questions","Sign copies in the lobby","Read part of his book","Show some photographs"],"a":2,"why":"He will begin by reading a short excerpt from chapter three とある。excerpt を part of his book と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0032","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）①","kind":"不動産会社からの留守番電話","text":"Hi, Mrs. Flores. This is Kevin from Sunrise Real Estate. I'm calling about your house on Maple Street. Our agent visited yesterday to appraise the property, and the news is good. He believes it is worth about ten percent more than you paid. I understand you feel apprehensive about selling, but this is a good time. A new property tax will take effect in January, so many buyers want to finish before then. The paperwork can be a little bureaucratic, but we will handle all of it for you. Also, the furniture store next to our office is holding an end-of-year sale, if you need anything for your new home. Please call me back when you can.","ja":"フローレス様、こんにちは。サンライズ不動産のケビンです。メープル通りのお宅の件でお電話しました。昨日、当社の担当者が物件の査定に伺いましたが、良いお知らせです。担当者は、ご購入時より10パーセントほど高い価値があると見ています。売却に不安を感じていらっしゃるのは分かりますが、今は良い時期です。1月に新しい固定資産税が導入されるため、多くの買い手がそれまでに手続きを終えたがっています。書類の手続きは少々お役所的ですが、すべて当社が代行します。また、当社の隣の家具店が年末セールを開催していますので、新居に必要なものがあればどうぞ。ご都合のよいときに折り返しお電話ください。","words":[["Real Estate","words:real estate"],["appraise","words:appraise"],["apprehensive","words:apprehensive"],["take effect","words:take effect"],["bureaucratic","words:bureaucratic"],["end-of-year sale","words:end-of-year sale"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the speaker calling?","o":["To offer a discount on furniture","To explain a new tax rule","To arrange a visit to a house","To report the value of a house"],"a":3,"why":"担当者が appraise the property（物件を査定）した結果を伝えている。購入時より10パーセント高い価値がある、という報告。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what will happen in January?","o":["A new tax will start.","House prices will fall.","The office will move.","A sale will end."],"a":0,"why":"A new property tax will take effect in January とある。take effect を start と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker offer to do?","o":["Lower the agent's fee","Take care of the paperwork","Buy the furniture","Visit the house again"],"a":1,"why":"we will handle all of it for you（書類はすべて代行する）とある。handle を take care of と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0033","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）②","kind":"市政ニュース","text":"In city news, the council has approved an ambitious plan to rebuild the area around Central Station. The project includes a new overpass for cars and a wide pedestrian crossing in front of the main entrance. The cost is immense, at nearly two hundred million dollars. A similar plan fell through three years ago when a major investor withdrew at the last minute. This time, the mayor is adamant that the work will go ahead. However, the time frame is tight, with construction due to start in March. Until then, the old footbridge will stay closed indefinitely for safety reasons. Drivers are advised to use Park Avenue instead.","ja":"市政のニュースです。市議会は、中央駅周辺を再整備する大掛かりな計画を承認しました。この事業には、自動車用の新しい高架道路と、正面入口前の幅の広い横断歩道が含まれます。費用は莫大で、2億ドル近くにのぼります。3年前にも同様の計画がありましたが、大口の投資家が土壇場で手を引いたため、実現しませんでした。今回、市長は工事を必ず進めると断言しています。ただし期間には余裕がなく、工事は3月に始まる予定です。それまでの間、古い歩道橋は安全上の理由から無期限に閉鎖されたままとなります。車を運転される方は、代わりにパーク大通りをご利用ください。","words":[["ambitious","words:ambitious (大掛かりな)"],["overpass","words:overpass"],["pedestrian crossing","words:pedestrian crossing"],["immense","words:immense"],["fell through","words:fall through"],["at the last minute","words:at the last minute"],["is adamant that","words:be adamant that"],["time frame","words:time frame"],["indefinitely","words:indefinitely"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has the city council approved?","o":["A plan to rebuild a station area","A new bus route","A rise in parking fees","The sale of Central Station"],"a":0,"why":"has approved an ambitious plan to rebuild the area around Central Station とある。"},{"q":"Why did a similar plan fail three years ago?","o":["The mayor opposed it.","An investor pulled out.","Construction costs doubled.","The footbridge was closed."],"a":1,"why":"fell through three years ago when a major investor withdrew at the last minute とある。withdrew を pulled out と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are drivers advised to do?","o":["Wait until March","Park near the main entrance","Use a different road","Cross the old footbridge"],"a":2,"why":"Drivers are advised to use Park Avenue instead とある。"}]},
{"id":"w-0034","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）②","kind":"創立記念のスピーチ","text":"Thank you, and good evening. Tonight we celebrate fifty years of Hartley Tools. Since its inception in a small garage, this company has been guided by one idea, first conceived by our founder, Edward Hartley: make things that last. Edward was a frugal man and a tenacious one. When sales collapsed in the nineteen eighties, he turned the business around in just two years. His daughter, a true disciple of his methods, led us into Asia. Today, I am proud to stand here as his lineal descendant. But we must not let our thinking fossilize. Young engineers now look to us for new ideas, and we will not disappoint them. Please raise your glasses.","ja":"ありがとうございます。皆さん、こんばんは。今夜はハートレー・ツールズの50周年を祝います。小さなガレージでの創業以来、この会社は1つの考えに導かれてきました。創業者エドワード・ハートレーが最初に思い描いた、「長く使えるものを作る」という考えです。エドワードは倹約家で、粘り強い人でした。1980年代に売上が急落したとき、彼はわずか2年で事業を立て直しました。彼のやり方を忠実に受け継いだ娘が、当社をアジアへと導きました。そして今日、私は彼の直系の子孫として、ここに立てることを誇りに思います。しかし、私たちは考え方を時代遅れにしてはなりません。若い技術者たちは今、新しい発想を求めて私たちに目を向けています。その期待を裏切ることはありません。どうぞグラスをお上げください。","words":[["inception","words:inception"],["conceived","words:conceive"],["frugal","words:frugal"],["tenacious","words:tenacious"],["turned the business around","words:turn around"],["disciple","words:disciple"],["lineal","words:lineal"],["fossilize","words:fossilize"],["look to","words:look to"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is being celebrated?","o":["The opening of a factory in Asia","The founder's birthday","The launch of a new tool","A company's anniversary"],"a":3,"why":"Tonight we celebrate fifty years of Hartley Tools（50周年を祝う）とある。"},{"q":"What did the founder do in the nineteen eighties?","o":["He moved the company to a garage.","He retired from the business.","He rescued the company.","He hired young engineers."],"a":2,"why":"he turned the business around in just two years（2年で事業を立て直した）とある。turn around を rescue と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are the listeners asked to do at the end?","o":["Make a toast","Visit the factory","Share their ideas","Meet the founder's daughter"],"a":0,"why":"Please raise your glasses（グラスを上げてください）は乾杯の呼びかけ。make a toast と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0035","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）②","kind":"店の自動音声案内","text":"Thank you for calling QuickPrint and Post. Our hours of operation are eight to seven, Monday through Saturday. Please note that we will be closed this Thursday in observance of the national holiday. If you are sending a parcel overseas, bring a photo ID so that we can validate your customs form. Our self-service copiers are available all day, and we keep the work area spotless for your comfort. Free refreshments are offered to customers who are waiting for large print orders. To check the status of an order, press one. To reach out to our sales team about a company account, press two. We appreciate your business and look forward to serving you.","ja":"クイックプリント・アンド・ポストにお電話いただき、ありがとうございます。営業時間は、月曜日から土曜日の8時から7時までです。今週木曜日は祝日のため休業いたしますので、ご注意ください。海外へ小包を送る場合は、税関の書類を確認できるよう、写真付きの身分証明書をお持ちください。セルフサービスのコピー機は終日ご利用いただけ、作業スペースは快適にお使いいただけるよう、いつも汚れひとつない状態に保っています。大量の印刷をお待ちのお客様には、無料でお飲み物をご用意しています。ご注文の状況を確認するには1を、法人のお取引について営業担当に連絡するには2を押してください。日頃のご愛顧に感謝し、ご利用をお待ちしております。","words":[["hours of operation","words:hours of operation"],["observance","words:observance"],["parcel","words:parcel"],["validate","words:validate"],["copiers","words:copier"],["spotless","words:spotless"],["refreshments","words:refreshment"],["reach out to","words:reach out to"],["your business","words:business (顧客)"]],"qs":[{"q":"When will the store be closed?","o":["On Monday","On Thursday","On Saturday","On Sunday only"],"a":1,"why":"we will be closed this Thursday in observance of the national holiday とある。"},{"q":"What should customers bring to send a parcel overseas?","o":["A customs stamp","A printed order form","A company account number","A photo ID"],"a":3,"why":"If you are sending a parcel overseas, bring a photo ID とある。"},{"q":"Why would a caller press two?","o":["To check on an order","To hear the opening hours","To discuss a company account","To report a broken copier"],"a":2,"why":"To reach out to our sales team about a company account, press two とある。注文の状況確認は1。"}]},
{"id":"w-0036","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）②","kind":"年度の振り返り","text":"Let's review the results for the fiscal year. Overall, sales rose four percent, but there are concerns. Our overreliance on two large customers is risky, as they account for half of our income. To drum up new business, the marketing team will attend six trade shows this spring. I would like to single out Priya's team for praise. They handled a very demanding client expertly and saved the contract. On costs, we found that several monthly reports are redundant, so we will stop producing them. Finally, please send me any pertinent figures by Friday so that I can finish the annual report. That's everything from me. Let's take a ten-minute break.","ja":"今年度の業績を振り返りましょう。全体では売上が4パーセント伸びましたが、懸念もあります。大口の顧客2社に頼りすぎているのは危険です。この2社で収入の半分を占めているからです。新しい取引先を開拓するため、マーケティングチームはこの春、6つの見本市に出展します。ここで、プリヤのチームを特に取り上げて称えたいと思います。要求の非常に厳しい顧客に巧みに対応し、契約を守ってくれました。経費については、月次の報告書のいくつかが重複していて不要だと分かったので、作成をやめます。最後に、年次報告書を仕上げられるよう、関連する数字があれば金曜日までに私へ送ってください。私からは以上です。10分間休憩しましょう。","words":[["fiscal","words:fiscal"],["overreliance","words:overreliance"],["drum up","words:drum up"],["single out","words:single out"],["demanding","words:demanding"],["expertly","words:expertly"],["redundant","words:redundant"],["pertinent","words:pertinent"]],"qs":[{"q":"What concern does the speaker mention?","o":["Sales fell by four percent.","The company depends too much on two customers.","The trade shows were canceled.","The annual report is late."],"a":1,"why":"Our overreliance on two large customers is risky とある。overreliance を depends too much と言い換えている。売上は4パーセント「増えた」。"},{"q":"Why does the speaker praise Priya's team?","o":["They dealt well with a difficult client.","They wrote the monthly reports.","They attended six trade shows.","They reduced the company's costs."],"a":0,"why":"They handled a very demanding client expertly とある。demanding を difficult、handled expertly を dealt well と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are the listeners asked to do by Friday?","o":["Stop producing reports","Take a ten-minute break","Contact new customers","Send relevant figures"],"a":3,"why":"please send me any pertinent figures by Friday とある。pertinent を relevant と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"w-0037","page":"words","group":"11/23（月）②","kind":"番組のお知らせ","text":"Here is a reminder about tonight's programs. At eight o'clock, we will air a special documentary to mark the vernal equinox, the first day of spring. It follows farmers in three countries as they prepare their fields. At nine, our consumer show looks at a food company that knowingly sold products past their expiration date. The reporter describes how a guard motioned for her to leave when she arrived with a camera. After that, stay tuned for the late news and weather. Finally, a note for our listeners: our telephone lines will be closed tomorrow morning for repairs, so please contact us by email instead. Thank you for listening.","ja":"今夜の番組のお知らせです。8時からは、春の最初の日である春分にちなんだ特別ドキュメンタリーを放送します。3つの国の農家が畑の準備をする様子を追った作品です。9時からの消費者向け番組では、賞味期限を過ぎた商品を、そうと知りながら販売していた食品会社を取り上げます。記者は、カメラを持って訪ねたところ、警備員から身ぶりで立ち去るよう合図されたときの様子を語ります。そのあとは、深夜のニュースと天気予報をお届けします。最後に、リスナーの皆さんへのお願いです。明日の午前中は修理のため電話回線が使えませんので、ご連絡はメールでお願いします。お聞きいただき、ありがとうございます。","words":[["air","words:air (動／名・空気以外)"],["vernal","words:vernal"],["knowingly","words:knowingly"],["motioned","words:motion (動)"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will be broadcast at eight o'clock?","o":["The late news","A consumer show","A documentary about farmers","A weather report"],"a":2,"why":"At eight o'clock, we will air a special documentary ... It follows farmers in three countries とある。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what did the food company do?","o":["It sold products that were too old.","It closed three farms.","It refused to pay a reporter.","It changed its expiration dates."],"a":0,"why":"knowingly sold products past their expiration date（期限を過ぎた商品をそうと知りながら売った）とある。"},{"q":"How should the listeners contact the station tomorrow morning?","o":["By telephone","By email","By letter","In person"],"a":1,"why":"our telephone lines will be closed tomorrow morning ... so please contact us by email instead とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0003","page":"nouns","group":"人事・採用","kind":"新入職員への説明","text":"Good morning, and welcome to your orientation session at Riverside Hospital. I'm Dana from the administration office. In front of you is the employee handbook. Please read it carefully, especially the section on the dress code. All new staff have a three-month probation period. During that time, you will not be assigned to the night shift. Each work shift lasts eight hours, including a one-hour break. Remember to fill out your time sheet every Friday and send it to the payroll department, or your pay may be late. This afternoon, there will be a training session on the patient record system in room four. Now, let me show you around the building.","ja":"おはようございます。リバーサイド病院の新人説明会へようこそ。私は事務局のデイナです。皆さんの前にあるのが従業員手引書です。特に服装規定の部分をよく読んでください。新しい職員には全員、3か月の試用期間があります。その間は夜勤に入ることはありません。1回の勤務シフトは、1時間の休憩を含めて8時間です。毎週金曜日に勤務時間記録表を記入して、給与課へ送るのを忘れないでください。忘れると、給与の支払いが遅れることがあります。今日の午後は、第4会議室で患者記録システムの研修会があります。それでは、建物の中をご案内します。","words":[["orientation session","nouns:orientation session"],["employee handbook","nouns:employee handbook"],["dress code","nouns:dress code"],["probation period","nouns:probation period"],["night shift","nouns:night shift"],["work shift","nouns:work shift"],["time sheet","nouns:time sheet"],["payroll department","nouns:payroll department"],["training session","nouns:training session"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who most likely are the listeners?","o":["Hospital patients","New employees","Visiting doctors","Job applicants"],"a":1,"why":"welcome to your orientation session、All new staff などから、新しく入った職員だと分かる。"},{"q":"What may happen if a time sheet is not submitted?","o":["The employee will work the night shift.","The probation period will be extended.","The employee's pay may be delayed.","The training will be repeated."],"a":2,"why":"send it to the payroll department, or your pay may be late とある。late を delayed と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will the speaker do next?","o":["Hand out uniforms","Start a training session","Collect the time sheets","Give a tour of the building"],"a":3,"why":"Now, let me show you around the building とある。show around を give a tour と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"n-0004","page":"nouns","group":"人事・採用","kind":"待遇変更の発表","text":"I have some news from the board about next year's compensation package. First, every full-time employee will receive a three percent pay raise in April. A further salary increase will depend on your annual performance review. The performance evaluation form has been simplified, and your manager will explain it this week. Second, our employee benefits are improving. Paid sick leave will rise from ten days to fifteen, and maternity leave will be extended to six months. Finally, the company will now match your contributions to the retirement plan, up to five percent of your salary. Full details will be emailed tomorrow. If anything is unclear, please ask at the meeting on Thursday.","ja":"来年の報酬制度について、取締役会からのお知らせがあります。まず、正社員は全員、4月に3パーセントの昇給があります。それ以上の昇給は、年に一度の勤務評定によって決まります。業績評価の用紙は簡単なものに変わりましたので、今週中に上司から説明があります。次に、福利厚生が良くなります。有給の病気休暇は10日から15日に増え、産休は6か月に延長されます。最後に、退職金制度への皆さんの積立に対して、会社が給与の5パーセントを上限に同額を上乗せします。詳細は明日メールでお送りします。不明な点があれば、木曜日の会議で質問してください。","words":[["compensation package","nouns:compensation package"],["pay raise","nouns:pay raise"],["salary increase","nouns:salary increase"],["performance review","nouns:performance review"],["performance evaluation","nouns:performance evaluation"],["employee benefits","nouns:employee benefits"],["sick leave","nouns:sick leave"],["maternity leave","nouns:maternity leave"],["retirement plan","nouns:retirement plan"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will full-time employees receive in April?","o":["A pay raise","A new evaluation form","Extra vacation days","A retirement bonus"],"a":0,"why":"every full-time employee will receive a three percent pay raise in April とある。"},{"q":"How is paid sick leave changing?","o":["It will be cut to ten days.","It will last six months.","It will depend on performance.","It will increase to fifteen days."],"a":3,"why":"Paid sick leave will rise from ten days to fifteen とある。6か月は産休の話。"},{"q":"When will the full details be sent?","o":["This week","Tomorrow","On Thursday","In April"],"a":1,"why":"Full details will be emailed tomorrow とある。木曜日は会議の日。"}]},
{"id":"n-0005","page":"nouns","group":"人事・採用","kind":"人事部からの連絡","text":"Before we finish, two quick items from the personnel department. First, staff turnover in the call center is still too high. Exit interviews show that people leave because they see no chance of career advancement. So, we have rewritten the job description for team leaders and will promote from inside the company. For outside hiring, every job applicant must now provide a reference letter before we make a job offer. Second, as you know, Mr. Gomez is leaving us after thirty years. His retirement party will be held next Friday at five in the cafeteria. Please sign the card at reception by Wednesday. That's all. Thanks, everyone.","ja":"終わる前に、人事部から2点だけ連絡します。1つ目です。コールセンターの離職率が、依然として高すぎます。退職時の面談によると、昇進の見込みがないと感じて辞める人が多いようです。そこで、チームリーダーの職務内容説明書を書き直し、社内から昇進させることにしました。外部からの採用については、今後、採用通知を出す前に、すべての応募者に推薦状を提出してもらいます。2つ目です。ご存じの通り、ゴメスさんが30年の勤務を終えて退職されます。退職パーティーは来週金曜日の5時に、社員食堂で開きます。水曜日までに、受付にあるカードに署名してください。以上です。皆さん、ありがとうございました。","words":[["personnel department","nouns:personnel department"],["staff turnover","nouns:staff turnover"],["career advancement","nouns:career advancement"],["job description","nouns:job description"],["job applicant","nouns:job applicant"],["reference letter","nouns:reference letter"],["job offer","nouns:job offer"],["retirement party","nouns:retirement party"]],"qs":[{"q":"According to the speaker, why do people leave the call center?","o":["The pay is too low.","The hours are too long.","They see no chance of promotion.","They dislike their team leaders."],"a":2,"why":"they see no chance of career advancement とある。career advancement を promotion と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What must job applicants now provide?","o":["A reference letter","A job description","A signed card","A medical certificate"],"a":0,"why":"every job applicant must now provide a reference letter とある。"},{"q":"What are the listeners asked to do by Wednesday?","o":["Attend an interview","Sign a card","Book the cafeteria","Meet Mr. Gomez"],"a":1,"why":"Please sign the card at reception by Wednesday とある。パーティーは来週金曜日。"}]},
{"id":"n-0006","page":"nouns","group":"会議・オフィス","kind":"留守番電話","text":"Hi, Tom. It's Julia. I'm calling about tomorrow. The weekly staff meeting has been moved to conference room B because the board meeting is using the large room all morning. I've emailed you the meeting agenda. Could you take the meeting minutes this time? Also, please bring your progress report on the website project. The client asked for a status update, and we have a conference call with them at three. They may ask for a deadline extension, so we should agree on an action plan before the call. I'll be at my desk until six if you want to talk. Thanks, Tom. See you tomorrow.","ja":"もしもし、トム。ジュリアです。明日の件で電話しました。午前中いっぱい取締役会議が大きな部屋を使うので、週1回のスタッフ会議は会議室Bに変更になりました。会議の議題はメールで送ってあります。今回は議事録を取ってもらえますか。それから、ウェブサイトの案件の進捗報告書を持ってきてください。お客様から進捗状況の報告を求められていて、3時に先方との電話会議があります。締め切りの延長を求められるかもしれないので、電話の前に行動計画を固めておきましょう。話したいことがあれば、6時までは席にいます。よろしくね、トム。ではまた明日。","words":[["staff meeting","nouns:staff meeting"],["conference room","nouns:conference room"],["board meeting","nouns:board meeting"],["meeting agenda","nouns:meeting agenda"],["meeting minutes","nouns:meeting minutes"],["progress report","nouns:progress report"],["status update","nouns:status update"],["conference call","nouns:conference call"],["deadline extension","nouns:deadline extension"],["action plan","nouns:action plan"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why has the staff meeting been moved?","o":["The agenda was changed.","Julia will be out of the office.","The client asked for a new time.","Another meeting is using the large room."],"a":3,"why":"because the board meeting is using the large room all morning とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker ask Tom to do?","o":["Take the meeting minutes","Book a conference room","Email the agenda","Cancel a phone call"],"a":0,"why":"Could you take the meeting minutes this time? とある。議題をメールしたのは話し手のほう。"},{"q":"What will happen at three o'clock?","o":["A board meeting will start.","A website will be launched.","There will be a call with a client.","Julia will leave the office."],"a":2,"why":"we have a conference call with them at three とある。them は the client。"}]},
{"id":"n-0007","page":"nouns","group":"会議・オフィス","kind":"営業会議の案内","text":"Welcome to our annual sales conference. Here is the plan for today. Our keynote speaker, Dr. Lena Fischer, will give her keynote address at ten in the main hall. It will be followed by a panel discussion with three regional managers and a short question-and-answer session. Please write your questions on the cards at the front desk. During lunch, feel free to exchange a business card or two with colleagues from other branches. Photos from today will appear in next month's company newsletter. Finally, a reminder: this year's company retreat will take place in September, and the sign-up sheet for the summer company outing is on the table by the door.","ja":"年に一度の営業会議へようこそ。本日の予定をご案内します。基調講演者のレナ・フィッシャー博士が、10時にメインホールで基調講演を行います。続いて、地域担当マネージャー3人による公開討論と、短い質疑応答があります。質問は、受付にあるカードに書いてください。昼食の間は、ほかの支店の同僚とぜひ名刺を交換してください。今日の写真は、来月の社内報に載ります。最後にお知らせです。今年の社員研修合宿は9月に行います。また、夏の社員旅行の申込用紙は、ドアのそばのテーブルに置いてあります。","words":[["keynote speaker","nouns:keynote speaker"],["keynote address","nouns:keynote address"],["panel discussion","nouns:panel discussion"],["question-and-answer session","nouns:question-and-answer session"],["front desk","nouns:front desk"],["business card","nouns:business card"],["company newsletter","nouns:company newsletter"],["company retreat","nouns:company retreat"],["company outing","nouns:company outing"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen at ten o'clock?","o":["Lunch will be served.","A speech will be given.","Photos will be taken.","A retreat will begin."],"a":1,"why":"Dr. Lena Fischer, will give her keynote address at ten とある。keynote address を speech と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Where should the listeners write their questions?","o":["On the sign-up sheet","In the company newsletter","On their business cards","On cards at the front desk"],"a":3,"why":"Please write your questions on the cards at the front desk とある。"},{"q":"What is on the table by the door?","o":["A sign-up sheet for an outing","A list of regional managers","A copy of the newsletter","A box of business cards"],"a":0,"why":"the sign-up sheet for the summer company outing is on the table by the door とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0008","page":"nouns","group":"会議・オフィス","kind":"総務からの連絡","text":"A few reminders from the office manager. First, office supplies such as pens and paper are now kept in the supply cabinet next to the break room, not in the supply room on the second floor. Larger office equipment, including the new printer, must be booked at the reception desk. Second, the old filing cabinet in the hallway will be removed on Friday, so please take your documents out. Third, if you go on a business trip, submit your expense report within five days. Travel expenses over two hundred dollars need a manager's signature. Finally, our business hours over the holiday are posted on the bulletin board. Thank you.","ja":"総務からいくつかお知らせです。1つ目。ペンや紙などの事務用品は、2階の備品室ではなく、休憩室の隣の備品棚に置くことになりました。新しいプリンターなど大きめのオフィス機器は、受付で予約が必要です。2つ目。廊下にある古い書類整理棚を金曜日に撤去しますので、書類を取り出しておいてください。3つ目。出張に行った場合は、5日以内に経費報告書を提出してください。200ドルを超える出張旅費には、上司の署名が必要です。最後に、休暇期間中の営業時間は掲示板に貼ってあります。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["office supplies","nouns:office supplies"],["supply cabinet","nouns:supply cabinet"],["break room","nouns:break room"],["supply room","nouns:supply room"],["office equipment","nouns:office equipment"],["reception desk","nouns:reception desk"],["filing cabinet","nouns:filing cabinet"],["business trip","nouns:business trip"],["expense report","nouns:expense report"],["Travel expenses","nouns:travel expenses"],["business hours","nouns:business hours"],["bulletin board","nouns:bulletin board"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where are pens and paper kept now?","o":["In the supply room on the second floor","At the reception desk","In a cabinet next to the break room","In the hallway"],"a":2,"why":"are now kept in the supply cabinet next to the break room, not in the supply room とある。"},{"q":"What will happen on Friday?","o":["A filing cabinet will be removed.","A new printer will arrive.","The office will close for the holiday.","Expense reports will be collected."],"a":0,"why":"the old filing cabinet in the hallway will be removed on Friday とある。"},{"q":"What requires a manager's signature?","o":["Booking the printer","Travel expenses over two hundred dollars","Taking documents out of the cabinet","Changes to business hours"],"a":1,"why":"Travel expenses over two hundred dollars need a manager's signature とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0009","page":"nouns","group":"経営・会社","kind":"企業ニュース","text":"In business news, Delta Foods has named Maria Santos as its new chief executive officer. Ms. Santos, who is currently vice president of marketing, will take over in July. She joined the parent company, Delta Group, fifteen years ago at a small branch office before moving to the head office in Chicago. Analysts expect her to focus on merger and acquisition deals in Asia. Last year, Delta formed a joint venture with a Japanese snack maker, and its market share in the region has doubled. The company's growth rate, however, slowed to two percent last quarter. Ms. Santos will speak to reporters tomorrow morning.","ja":"ビジネスニュースです。デルタ・フーズは、マリア・サントス氏を新しい最高経営責任者に指名しました。現在マーケティング担当の副社長を務めるサントス氏は、7月に就任します。サントス氏は15年前、親会社のデルタ・グループに小さな支店で入社し、その後シカゴの本社に移りました。専門家は、サントス氏がアジアでの合併・買収に力を入れると見ています。デルタは昨年、日本の菓子メーカーと合弁事業を立ち上げ、同地域での市場占有率は2倍になりました。ただし、同社の成長率は前の四半期に2パーセントまで鈍化しています。サントス氏は明日の朝、記者団の質問に答える予定です。","words":[["chief executive officer","nouns:chief executive officer"],["vice president","nouns:vice president"],["parent company","nouns:parent company"],["branch office","nouns:branch office"],["head office","nouns:head office"],["merger and acquisition","nouns:merger and acquisition"],["joint venture","nouns:joint venture"],["market share","nouns:market share"],["growth rate","nouns:growth rate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What position will Ms. Santos take in July?","o":["Vice president of marketing","Head of the Asian branch","Manager of a joint venture","Chief executive officer"],"a":3,"why":"has named Maria Santos as its new chief executive officer ... will take over in July とある。副社長は現在の役職。"},{"q":"Where did Ms. Santos first work for the company?","o":["At a branch office","At the head office in Chicago","At a snack maker in Japan","At a marketing agency"],"a":0,"why":"She joined ... fifteen years ago at a small branch office before moving to the head office とある。"},{"q":"What will Ms. Santos do tomorrow morning?","o":["Travel to Asia","Sign a merger agreement","Speak to reporters","Visit a branch office"],"a":2,"why":"Ms. Santos will speak to reporters tomorrow morning とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0010","page":"nouns","group":"経営・会社","kind":"予算についての会議","text":"Thank you for staying late. As you know, each board member received our budget proposal last week. Unfortunately, they have asked for a ten percent budget cut. Because of these budget constraints, we must delay the new warehouse. The cost estimate from the builder was simply too high. Instead, I suggest a smaller cost reduction plan. We could close the storage site on Elm Street and rent space when we need it. Before we decide, the risk management team will carry out a feasibility study, which should take three weeks. I'd like each of you to send me your ideas by Monday. Let's meet again next Wednesday.","ja":"遅くまで残っていただき、ありがとうございます。ご存じの通り、先週、役員全員に予算案を配りました。残念ながら、役員からは10パーセントの予算削減を求められました。この予算の制約のため、新しい倉庫の建設は延期せざるを得ません。建設業者からの費用見積もりが、とにかく高すぎました。その代わりに、もう少し小規模な経費削減の計画を提案します。エルム通りの保管施設を閉めて、必要なときだけ場所を借りることもできます。決める前に、リスク管理チームが実現可能性の調査を行います。3週間ほどかかる見込みです。皆さんは、月曜日までにそれぞれの案を私に送ってください。来週の水曜日にもう一度集まりましょう。","words":[["board member","nouns:board member"],["budget proposal","nouns:budget proposal"],["budget cut","nouns:budget cut"],["budget constraints","nouns:budget constraints"],["cost estimate","nouns:cost estimate"],["cost reduction","nouns:cost reduction"],["risk management","nouns:risk management"],["feasibility study","nouns:feasibility study"]],"qs":[{"q":"What have the board members asked for?","o":["A larger warehouse","A reduction in the budget","A new builder","A meeting on Monday"],"a":1,"why":"they have asked for a ten percent budget cut とある。budget cut を a reduction in the budget と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will be delayed?","o":["The feasibility study","The closing of a storage site","The construction of a warehouse","The next board meeting"],"a":2,"why":"we must delay the new warehouse とある。"},{"q":"What are the listeners asked to do by Monday?","o":["Send their ideas","Visit Elm Street","Sign the budget proposal","Contact the builder"],"a":0,"why":"I'd like each of you to send me your ideas by Monday とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0011","page":"nouns","group":"経営・会社","kind":"銀行の説明会","text":"Good afternoon. My name is Alan Brooks, and I am the branch manager of First City Bank. Today I'll explain how to apply for a small business loan. First, you need a clear business plan. It should begin with a short mission statement and include market research on your customers. Show that you understand the current market trend in your industry. If you have a business partner, both of you must sign the forms. We are especially interested in companies planning business expansion into nearby towns. Applications take about four weeks to review. Please take a brochure from the table, and I will be happy to answer your questions.","ja":"こんにちは。ファースト・シティ銀行の支店長、アラン・ブルックスです。今日は、小規模事業者向け融資の申し込み方法をご説明します。まず、明確な事業計画が必要です。短い企業理念から始め、顧客についての市場調査を盛り込んでください。ご自身の業界の、現在の市場動向を理解していることを示しましょう。共同経営者がいる場合は、お二人とも書類に署名していただきます。当行は特に、近隣の町への事業拡大を計画している会社に関心を持っています。申請の審査には4週間ほどかかります。テーブルのパンフレットをお取りください。ご質問には喜んでお答えします。","words":[["branch manager","nouns:branch manager"],["business plan","nouns:business plan"],["mission statement","nouns:mission statement"],["market research","nouns:market research"],["market trend","nouns:market trend"],["business partner","nouns:business partner"],["business expansion","nouns:business expansion"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the speaker?","o":["A small business owner","A market researcher","A university lecturer","A bank manager"],"a":3,"why":"I am the branch manager of First City Bank とある。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what should a business plan begin with?","o":["A list of partners","A mission statement","A loan amount","A map of nearby towns"],"a":1,"why":"It should begin with a short mission statement とある。"},{"q":"How long does it take to review an application?","o":["About four weeks","About four days","About two months","About one year"],"a":0,"why":"Applications take about four weeks to review とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0012","page":"nouns","group":"会計・金融","kind":"銀行の自動音声案内","text":"Thank you for calling Harbor Bank. Please listen carefully, as our menu has changed. To hear your account balance, press one. To order a paper bank statement for your checking account or savings account, press two. For today's interest rate on home loans and the exchange rate for major currencies, press three. To check the status of a loan application or to ask for a higher credit limit on your card, press four. If you would like to open a new bank account, please visit any branch with two forms of identification. Our offices are open from nine to four on weekdays. To speak with a representative, please stay on the line.","ja":"ハーバー銀行にお電話いただき、ありがとうございます。メニューが変わりましたので、よくお聞きください。口座残高の確認は1を押してください。当座預金口座または普通預金口座の、紙の取引明細書のご請求は2を押してください。本日の住宅ローンの金利と、主要通貨の為替レートは3を押してください。融資申込の状況の確認、またはカードの利用限度額の引き上げのご相談は4を押してください。新しく銀行口座を開設される場合は、身分証明書を2種類お持ちのうえ、お近くの支店へお越しください。窓口は平日の9時から4時までです。担当者とお話しになる場合は、そのままお待ちください。","words":[["account balance","nouns:account balance"],["bank statement","nouns:bank statement"],["checking account","nouns:checking account"],["savings account","nouns:savings account"],["interest rate","nouns:interest rate"],["exchange rate","nouns:exchange rate"],["loan application","nouns:loan application"],["credit limit","nouns:credit limit"],["bank account","nouns:bank account"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should a caller press to hear an account balance?","o":["One","Two","Three","Four"],"a":0,"why":"To hear your account balance, press one とある。"},{"q":"What information is available by pressing three?","o":["The status of a loan","The location of branches","Interest and exchange rates","The opening hours"],"a":2,"why":"For today's interest rate on home loans and the exchange rate for major currencies, press three とある。"},{"q":"What must people bring to open a new account?","o":["A paper bank statement","A loan application","A credit card","Two forms of identification"],"a":3,"why":"please visit any branch with two forms of identification とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0013","page":"nouns","group":"会計・金融","kind":"株主総会での報告","text":"Good morning, and welcome to the annual shareholder meeting of Polar Air. Copies of the annual report are on your seats. Let me summarize our financial statements. According to the income statement, gross revenue rose six percent to nine hundred million dollars. However, operating expenses also increased, mainly because of fuel prices, so net income fell slightly. Our profit margin is now four percent. The good news is on the balance sheet: we have paid off a third of our debt. We also cut overhead costs by closing two offices. Quarterly earnings will be announced on May second. Since January, our stock price has risen by twelve percent. I will now take your questions.","ja":"おはようございます。ポーラー航空の年次株主総会へようこそ。年次報告書はお席に置いてあります。財務諸表の要点をご説明します。損益計算書によると、総収入は6パーセント増えて9億ドルになりました。しかし、主に燃料価格の影響で営業費用も増えたため、純利益はわずかに減りました。現在の利益率は4パーセントです。良い知らせは貸借対照表にあります。負債の3分の1を返済しました。また、事務所を2か所閉鎖して、間接費も削減しました。四半期の収益は5月2日に発表します。1月以降、当社の株価は12パーセント上がっています。それでは、ご質問をお受けします。","words":[["shareholder meeting","nouns:shareholder meeting"],["annual report","nouns:annual report"],["financial statements","nouns:financial statement"],["income statement","nouns:income statement"],["gross revenue","nouns:gross revenue"],["operating expenses","nouns:operating expenses"],["net income","nouns:net income"],["profit margin","nouns:profit margin"],["balance sheet","nouns:balance sheet"],["overhead costs","nouns:overhead costs"],["Quarterly earnings","nouns:quarterly earnings"],["stock price","nouns:stock price"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is the talk taking place?","o":["At a press conference","At a meeting for shareholders","At an airport","At a staff training session"],"a":1,"why":"welcome to the annual shareholder meeting of Polar Air とある。"},{"q":"Why did net income fall?","o":["Two offices were closed.","Ticket prices were lowered.","The company paid off its debt.","Higher fuel prices raised expenses."],"a":3,"why":"operating expenses also increased, mainly because of fuel prices, so net income fell slightly とある。"},{"q":"What will happen on May second?","o":["Earnings will be announced.","The annual report will be printed.","The stock will be sold.","A new office will open."],"a":0,"why":"Quarterly earnings will be announced on May second とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0014","page":"nouns","group":"会計・金融","kind":"保険会社からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, Mr. Reed. This is Sandra from Shield Insurance. I'm calling about your home insurance policy. Your latest billing statement was returned to us, so I think your billing address may be out of date. The insurance premium of four hundred dollars has a due date of March first, and a late fee of twenty dollars applies after that. If you prefer, we can set up a monthly payment plan and change your payment method to automatic transfer. Please note that the price includes sales tax. Also, part of your insurance coverage for a home office may qualify as a tax deduction, so mention it when you file your tax return. Please call me back on extension two one four.","ja":"リード様、こんにちは。シールド保険のサンドラです。ご自宅の保険契約の件でお電話しました。最新の請求明細書が当社に戻ってきてしまいましたので、ご登録の請求先住所が古くなっているのではないかと思います。保険料400ドルのお支払期日は3月1日で、それを過ぎると20ドルの延滞料がかかります。ご希望でしたら、月払いの支払計画を設定し、お支払方法を自動振替に変更することもできます。なお、この金額には売上税が含まれています。また、自宅の仕事部屋に対する補償の一部は税控除の対象になる場合がありますので、納税申告の際にお伝えください。内線214番まで折り返しお電話ください。","words":[["insurance policy","nouns:insurance policy"],["billing statement","nouns:billing statement"],["billing address","nouns:billing address"],["insurance premium","nouns:insurance premium"],["due date","nouns:due date"],["late fee","nouns:late fee"],["payment plan","nouns:payment plan"],["payment method","nouns:payment method"],["sales tax","nouns:sales tax"],["insurance coverage","nouns:insurance coverage"],["tax deduction","nouns:tax deduction"],["tax return","nouns:tax return"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why does the speaker think the billing address is out of date?","o":["Mr. Reed called to report a move.","A statement was returned.","A payment was late.","The policy has expired."],"a":1,"why":"Your latest billing statement was returned to us, so I think your billing address may be out of date とある。"},{"q":"What will happen after March first?","o":["The policy will be canceled.","The premium will double.","A late fee will be charged.","Sales tax will be added."],"a":2,"why":"has a due date of March first, and a late fee of twenty dollars applies after that とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest Mr. Reed mention when filing his tax return?","o":["His home office coverage","His new address","His monthly payment plan","His automatic transfer"],"a":0,"why":"part of your insurance coverage for a home office may qualify as a tax deduction, so mention it when you file your tax return とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0015","page":"nouns","group":"販売・マーケティング","kind":"営業会議","text":"Let's look at last month's sales figures. As the sales report shows, we reached only eighty percent of our sales target. I spoke to every sales representative, and they all said the same thing: young people do not know our name. So we need a new marketing strategy. We have hired an advertising agency to design an advertising campaign for social media. Our target audience is people aged eighteen to thirty. Before we start, we will hold a focus group next week to test three video ideas. The goal is to raise brand awareness by the summer. We will also run a sales promotion in June, with free delivery on every order. Any comments?","ja":"先月の売上高を見てみましょう。売上報告書にある通り、販売目標の80パーセントにしか届きませんでした。営業担当者全員に話を聞きましたが、皆同じことを言っていました。若い人たちが当社の名前を知らない、ということです。そこで、新しいマーケティング戦略が必要です。SNS向けの広告キャンペーンを作るために、広告代理店と契約しました。対象となる客層は18歳から30歳です。開始前に、来週フォーカスグループを開いて、3つの動画案を試します。目標は、夏までにブランドの認知度を高めることです。また6月には、すべての注文を送料無料にする販売促進も行います。ご意見はありますか。","words":[["sales figures","nouns:sales figures"],["sales report","nouns:sales report"],["sales target","nouns:sales target"],["sales representative","nouns:sales representative"],["marketing strategy","nouns:marketing strategy"],["advertising agency","nouns:advertising agency"],["advertising campaign","nouns:advertising campaign"],["target audience","nouns:target audience"],["focus group","nouns:focus group"],["brand awareness","nouns:brand awareness"],["sales promotion","nouns:sales promotion"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does the speaker mention?","o":["The sales target was not reached.","A sales representative left the company.","The delivery costs went up.","The advertising agency made a mistake."],"a":0,"why":"we reached only eighty percent of our sales target とある。"},{"q":"Who is the target audience of the campaign?","o":["Business owners","Families with children","People aged eighteen to thirty","Retired people"],"a":2,"why":"Our target audience is people aged eighteen to thirty とある。"},{"q":"What will take place next week?","o":["A sales promotion","A product launch","A social media campaign","A focus group"],"a":3,"why":"we will hold a focus group next week to test three video ideas とある。販売促進は6月。"}]},
{"id":"n-0016","page":"nouns","group":"販売・マーケティング","kind":"新製品発表の打ち合わせ","text":"Thanks for coming, everyone. I have exciting news about the product launch. Our new product line of electric bicycles will be shown for the first time at the Berlin trade show in May, and again at the Tokyo trade fair in June. We will hold a press conference on the first morning, followed by a live product demonstration outside the hall. The press release is almost ready, but I need someone to check the product description for each model. The price range is eight hundred to two thousand dollars, and the full price list will be sent to every retail store on our list next week. Who can help with the checking?","ja":"皆さん、お集まりいただきありがとうございます。新製品の発売について、うれしいお知らせがあります。電動自転車の新しい製品ラインナップは、5月にベルリンの展示会で初めて公開し、6月には東京の見本市でも紹介します。初日の午前中に記者会見を開き、そのあと会場の外で製品の実演を行います。報道発表の文面はほぼできていますが、各モデルの製品説明を確認してくれる人が必要です。価格帯は800ドルから2,000ドルで、詳しい価格表は来週、取引先のすべての小売店に送ります。確認を手伝ってくれる人はいますか。","words":[["product launch","nouns:product launch"],["product line","nouns:product line"],["trade show","nouns:trade show"],["trade fair","nouns:trade fair"],["press conference","nouns:press conference"],["product demonstration","nouns:product demonstration"],["press release","nouns:press release"],["product description","nouns:product description"],["price range","nouns:price range"],["price list","nouns:price list"],["retail store","nouns:retail store"]],"qs":[{"q":"What kind of product is being launched?","o":["Electric bicycles","Sports clothing","Car parts","Fitness machines"],"a":0,"why":"Our new product line of electric bicycles とある。"},{"q":"What will happen after the press conference?","o":["A price list will be handed out.","A product demonstration will be given.","The team will fly to Tokyo.","A retail store will open."],"a":1,"why":"We will hold a press conference ..., followed by a live product demonstration とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker ask for?","o":["Ideas for a new model","A lower price range","A list of retail stores","Help with checking descriptions"],"a":3,"why":"I need someone to check the product description for each model. ... Who can help with the checking? とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0017","page":"nouns","group":"販売・マーケティング","kind":"店内放送","text":"Attention, shoppers. Office Plus is celebrating ten years with our biggest price reduction ever. This week only, bring the discount coupon from today's newspaper and save twenty percent at any retail outlet. Shopping online? Enter the promotional code at checkout. Members of our loyalty program earn double points, so don't forget to show your membership card. Business customers, we have something for you too. Place a bulk order of fifty items or more and pay the wholesale price, with an extra bulk discount on paper. Ask our staff for a free price quote. And everyone who spends over one hundred dollars will receive a ten-dollar gift certificate. Hurry, the sale ends Sunday.","ja":"お買い物中の皆さまにお知らせします。オフィス・プラスは10周年を記念して、過去最大の値下げを行っています。今週に限り、今日の新聞に付いている割引クーポンをお持ちいただくと、どの販売店でも20パーセント引きになります。オンラインでお買い物ですか。お会計の際に割引コードを入力してください。ポイント制度の会員の方はポイントが2倍になりますので、会員証のご提示をお忘れなく。法人のお客様にも特典があります。50点以上の大量注文をしていただくと、卸売価格でご購入いただけ、用紙はさらに大口割引となります。無料の価格見積もりは、スタッフにお申し付けください。さらに、100ドルを超えるお買い上げの方全員に、10ドル分の商品券を差し上げます。セールは日曜日までです。お急ぎください。","words":[["price reduction","nouns:price reduction"],["discount coupon","nouns:discount coupon"],["retail outlet","nouns:retail outlet"],["promotional code","nouns:promotional code"],["loyalty program","nouns:loyalty program"],["membership card","nouns:membership card"],["bulk order","nouns:bulk order"],["wholesale price","nouns:wholesale price"],["bulk discount","nouns:bulk discount"],["price quote","nouns:price quote"],["gift certificate","nouns:gift certificate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the store celebrating?","o":["The opening of a new outlet","The end of the year","Its tenth anniversary","A record number of members"],"a":2,"why":"Office Plus is celebrating ten years とある。"},{"q":"How can online shoppers get a discount?","o":["By showing a membership card","By entering a code","By calling the store","By ordering fifty items"],"a":1,"why":"Shopping online? Enter the promotional code at checkout とある。"},{"q":"What will customers who spend over one hundred dollars receive?","o":["A gift certificate","Double points","Free delivery","A price quote"],"a":0,"why":"everyone who spends over one hundred dollars will receive a ten-dollar gift certificate とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0018","page":"nouns","group":"顧客対応・サービス","kind":"顧客対応の研修","text":"Welcome to today's customer service training. Let me start with some numbers. In our latest customer survey, customer satisfaction fell from ninety to eighty-two percent. The most common customer complaint was the long wait at the help desk. This matters, because our customer base is small, and customer loyalty depends on fast, friendly answers. So, from next week, every service representative will follow a new rule: answer each call within three rings. We will also read customer feedback aloud at our Monday meetings, both good and bad. This morning, we will practice in pairs. One of you will play an unhappy caller. Please find a partner now.","ja":"本日の顧客サービス研修へようこそ。まず、数字からお話しします。最新の顧客アンケートで、顧客満足度が90パーセントから82パーセントに下がりました。最も多かった苦情は、問い合わせ窓口での待ち時間の長さです。これは重要な問題です。当社の顧客基盤は小さく、お客様に長く使い続けていただけるかどうかは、素早く感じのよい対応にかかっているからです。そこで来週から、サービス担当者は全員、新しいルールに従います。電話には3コール以内に出る、というものです。また、月曜日の会議では、良いものも悪いものも含めて、お客様の声を読み上げます。今日の午前中は、2人1組で練習します。1人が不満を持った電話のお客様の役をします。では、相手を見つけてください。","words":[["customer service","nouns:customer service"],["customer survey","nouns:customer survey"],["customer satisfaction","nouns:customer satisfaction"],["customer complaint","nouns:customer complaint"],["help desk","nouns:help desk"],["customer base","nouns:customer base"],["customer loyalty","nouns:customer loyalty"],["service representative","nouns:service representative"],["customer feedback","nouns:customer feedback"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the latest survey show?","o":["The customer base has grown.","Satisfaction has dropped.","Complaints have decreased.","Calls are answered faster."],"a":1,"why":"customer satisfaction fell from ninety to eighty-two percent とある。fell を dropped と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What is the new rule for service representatives?","o":["Read feedback every Monday","Work in pairs","Call each customer back","Answer calls within three rings"],"a":3,"why":"every service representative will follow a new rule: answer each call within three rings とある。"},{"q":"What will the listeners do next?","o":["Take a written test","Listen to a recorded call","Find a partner","Fill out a survey"],"a":2,"why":"Please find a partner now とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0019","page":"nouns","group":"顧客対応・サービス","kind":"通販の自動音声案内","text":"Thank you for calling Maple Home Store on our toll-free number. To check your order status, please have your confirmation number ready. You can find it at the top of your order confirmation email. If your package has already been shipped, we will give you a tracking number. Business customers who wish to send a purchase order should use the order form on our website. For questions about our return policy or refund policy, press two. Items may be returned within thirty days, and refunds are made within one week. If you have recently moved, please press three to update your contact information. Otherwise, stay on the line.","ja":"メープル・ホーム・ストアのフリーダイヤルにお電話いただき、ありがとうございます。ご注文の状況を確認される場合は、確認番号をお手元にご用意ください。確認番号は、注文確認メールの一番上に記載されています。お荷物がすでに発送されている場合は、追跡番号をお伝えします。発注書を送りたい法人のお客様は、当社ウェブサイトの注文書をご利用ください。返品規定や返金規定についてのご質問は、2を押してください。商品は30日以内であれば返品でき、返金は1週間以内に行います。最近お引っ越しをされた方は、3を押してご連絡先を更新してください。それ以外の方は、そのままお待ちください。","words":[["toll-free number","nouns:toll-free number"],["order status","nouns:order status"],["confirmation number","nouns:confirmation number"],["order confirmation","nouns:order confirmation"],["tracking number","nouns:tracking number"],["purchase order","nouns:purchase order"],["order form","nouns:order form"],["return policy","nouns:return policy"],["refund policy","nouns:refund policy"],["contact information","nouns:contact information"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where can callers find their confirmation number?","o":["On the package","In an email","On the website","On the order form"],"a":1,"why":"You can find it at the top of your order confirmation email とある。"},{"q":"How long do customers have to return items?","o":["One week","Two weeks","Thirty days","Three months"],"a":2,"why":"Items may be returned within thirty days とある。1週間は返金にかかる期間。"},{"q":"Why would a caller press three?","o":["To update contact information","To send a purchase order","To ask about refunds","To track a package"],"a":0,"why":"please press three to update your contact information とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0020","page":"nouns","group":"顧客対応・サービス","kind":"修理についての留守番電話","text":"Hello, Ms. Carter. This is Brian from CoolAir. I'm returning your call about your air conditioner. I checked our records, and the product warranty is still valid. The warranty period runs until October, and the warranty coverage includes all parts. So our repair service will be free, with no service charge. Our maintenance crew can visit on Thursday morning between nine and twelve. The maintenance work should take about an hour. Before then, please try the reset steps on page ten of the user manual. If you no longer have the instruction manual, you can download it from our website. Please call me back to confirm Thursday. Thank you.","ja":"カーター様、こんにちは。クールエアのブライアンです。エアコンの件でお電話をいただきましたので、折り返しご連絡しました。記録を確認したところ、製品保証はまだ有効です。保証期間は10月までで、保証の範囲にはすべての部品が含まれます。そのため、修理サービスは無料で、サービス料もかかりません。保守作業班は、木曜日の午前9時から12時の間に伺えます。作業は1時間ほどで終わる見込みです。それまでに、取扱説明書の10ページにあるリセットの手順をお試しください。説明書がお手元にない場合は、当社のウェブサイトからダウンロードできます。木曜日でよろしいか、折り返しお電話でお知らせください。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["product warranty","nouns:product warranty"],["warranty period","nouns:warranty period"],["warranty coverage","nouns:warranty coverage"],["repair service","nouns:repair service"],["service charge","nouns:service charge"],["maintenance crew","nouns:maintenance crew"],["maintenance work","nouns:maintenance work"],["user manual","nouns:user manual"],["instruction manual","nouns:instruction manual"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the speaker say about the warranty?","o":["It ended in October.","It covers only some parts.","It must be renewed.","It is still valid."],"a":3,"why":"the product warranty is still valid とある。期間は10月「まで」で、全部品が対象。"},{"q":"When can the maintenance crew visit?","o":["On Thursday morning","On Thursday afternoon","On Friday morning","In October"],"a":0,"why":"Our maintenance crew can visit on Thursday morning between nine and twelve とある。"},{"q":"What is Ms. Carter asked to try before the visit?","o":["Downloading new software","Cleaning the filter","Following steps in the manual","Turning off the power for an hour"],"a":2,"why":"please try the reset steps on page ten of the user manual とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0021","page":"nouns","group":"製造・品質","kind":"工場見学の案内","text":"Welcome to the Norton manufacturing plant. My name is Ravi, and I am the plant manager. Before we enter the factory floor, please put on your safety gear: a helmet, glasses, and gloves. Safety regulations require all visitors to stay inside the yellow lines. Our main production line makes two hundred engines a day, and each assembly line has twelve workers. At the end of the line, you will see the quality control station, where every engine is tested. Thanks to our quality assurance program, the defect rate is below one percent. Finally, we will visit the stock room, where finished parts are kept. Please follow me, and watch your step.","ja":"ノートン製造工場へようこそ。私は工場長のラヴィです。工場の作業現場に入る前に、ヘルメット、保護めがね、手袋といった安全用具を身につけてください。安全規則により、見学の方は全員、黄色い線の内側にいていただく必要があります。主力の生産ラインでは1日に200台のエンジンを作っており、各組立ラインには12人の作業員がいます。ラインの終わりには品質管理の工程があり、そこですべてのエンジンを検査します。品質保証の取り組みのおかげで、不良率は1パーセント未満です。最後に、完成した部品を保管している在庫保管室を見学します。私についてきてください。足元にお気をつけください。","words":[["manufacturing plant","nouns:manufacturing plant"],["plant manager","nouns:plant manager"],["factory floor","nouns:factory floor"],["safety gear","nouns:safety gear"],["Safety regulations","nouns:safety regulations"],["production line","nouns:production line"],["assembly line","nouns:assembly line"],["quality control","nouns:quality control"],["quality assurance","nouns:quality assurance"],["defect rate","nouns:defect rate"],["stock room","nouns:stock room"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the speaker?","o":["A safety inspector","A plant manager","A new worker","An engine designer"],"a":1,"why":"I am the plant manager とある。"},{"q":"What must visitors do on the factory floor?","o":["Wear a company uniform","Test an engine","Take notes for a report","Stay inside the yellow lines"],"a":3,"why":"Safety regulations require all visitors to stay inside the yellow lines とある。"},{"q":"What will the visitors see last?","o":["The stock room","The quality control station","The main office","The assembly line"],"a":0,"why":"Finally, we will visit the stock room とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0022","page":"nouns","group":"製造・品質","kind":"工場内放送","text":"Attention, all workers. Because of last night's storm, the nearby power plant has reduced its supply, and we expect a power outage between two and three o'clock this afternoon. To protect our machines, the production schedule has been changed. The second shift will begin at four instead of two. Our production capacity will be lower today, so the delivery of raw materials has been moved to tomorrow morning. Please use this time for the monthly inventory check in the storage facility. A safety inspection will also take place, so make sure all safety equipment is in its proper place. Remember to follow the usual safety precautions when restarting the machines. For details on inventory control, see your supervisor.","ja":"作業員の皆さんにお知らせします。昨夜の嵐の影響で、近くの発電所が供給を減らしており、今日の午後2時から3時の間に停電が見込まれます。機械を守るため、生産日程を変更しました。2番目のシフトは、2時ではなく4時に始まります。今日は生産能力が下がるので、原材料の搬入は明日の朝に変更しました。この時間を使って、保管施設で毎月の棚卸しを行ってください。安全点検も行いますので、安全装備がすべて決められた場所にあることを確認してください。機械を再び動かすときは、いつもの安全対策を忘れずに守ってください。在庫管理の詳細は、上司に確認してください。","words":[["power plant","nouns:power plant"],["power outage","nouns:power outage"],["production schedule","nouns:production schedule"],["production capacity","nouns:production capacity"],["raw materials","nouns:raw materials"],["inventory check","nouns:inventory check"],["storage facility","nouns:storage facility"],["safety inspection","nouns:safety inspection"],["safety equipment","nouns:safety equipment"],["safety precautions","nouns:safety precautions"],["inventory control","nouns:inventory control"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is expected this afternoon?","o":["A visit from a customer","A storm","A power outage","A delivery of machines"],"a":2,"why":"we expect a power outage between two and three o'clock this afternoon とある。嵐は昨夜のこと。"},{"q":"When will the second shift begin today?","o":["At four o'clock","At two o'clock","At three o'clock","Tomorrow morning"],"a":0,"why":"The second shift will begin at four instead of two とある。"},{"q":"What are the workers asked to do during the outage?","o":["Go home early","Carry out an inventory check","Unload raw materials","Repair the machines"],"a":1,"why":"Please use this time for the monthly inventory check とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0023","page":"nouns","group":["製造・品質","物流・配送"],"kind":"取引先への留守番電話","text":"Hello, this is Emma from Pacific Parts. I'm calling about your order of five hundred pumps. I'm afraid there has been a problem at our production facility, so the delivery date will be one week later than planned. The new delivery schedule is attached to the email I sent this morning. To make up for the delay, we will not charge the shipping fee. The goods will leave our shipping department next Tuesday and should arrive at your distribution center on Thursday. Please check that the shipping address on the packing slip is correct. If you need the parts sooner, overnight delivery is possible for part of the order. Again, I apologize for the inconvenience.","ja":"もしもし、パシフィック・パーツのエマです。ポンプ500台のご注文の件でお電話しました。申し訳ありませんが、当社の生産施設で問題が発生したため、配達日が予定より1週間遅れます。新しい配送日程は、今朝お送りしたメールに添付してあります。遅れのお詫びとして、送料はいただきません。商品は来週火曜日に当社の発送部を出て、木曜日に御社の配送センターに届く見込みです。納品書に記載の配送先住所が正しいか、ご確認ください。お急ぎの場合は、ご注文の一部を翌日配達でお届けすることもできます。ご不便をおかけしますことを、重ねてお詫び申し上げます。","words":[["production facility","nouns:production facility"],["delivery date","nouns:delivery date"],["delivery schedule","nouns:delivery schedule"],["shipping fee","nouns:shipping fee"],["shipping department","nouns:shipping department"],["distribution center","nouns:distribution center"],["shipping address","nouns:shipping address"],["packing slip","nouns:packing slip"],["overnight delivery","nouns:overnight delivery"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the speaker calling?","o":["To confirm a payment","To cancel an order","To ask for a new address","To report a delay"],"a":3,"why":"the delivery date will be one week later than planned（配達日が1週間遅れる）と伝えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker offer to make up for the problem?","o":["A discount on the pumps","Free shipping","Extra pumps","A full refund"],"a":1,"why":"To make up for the delay, we will not charge the shipping fee とある。"},{"q":"What is the listener asked to check?","o":["The address on the packing slip","The number of pumps","The price in the email","The date of the next order"],"a":0,"why":"Please check that the shipping address on the packing slip is correct とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0024","page":"nouns","group":"物流・配送","kind":"倉庫での朝礼","text":"Good morning, team. A few updates before we start. First, a shipping container from Vietnam arrived last night. It is still waiting for customs clearance because the customs declaration was missing one page. Our warehouse manager is fixing that now, so please keep the loading dock clear. Second, as you know, problems in the supply chain have raised our costs. From next month, the freight charge for heavy goods will rise by eight percent, and the delivery charge for small parcels will also go up. Third, we are adding a new distribution channel for online orders. Urgent documents should still go by express mail. That's all. Let's have a safe day.","ja":"おはようございます、皆さん。作業の前に、いくつかお知らせです。1つ目。昨夜、ベトナムからの輸送用コンテナが到着しました。税関申告書が1ページ足りなかったため、まだ通関手続きを待っています。今、倉庫管理者が対応していますので、積み下ろし場は空けておいてください。2つ目。ご存じの通り、供給網の問題で費用が上がっています。来月から、重い貨物の運賃は8パーセント上がり、小さな荷物の配送料も上がります。3つ目。オンライン注文向けに、新しい流通経路を加えます。急ぎの書類は、これまで通り速達で送ってください。以上です。今日も安全に作業しましょう。","words":[["shipping container","nouns:shipping container"],["customs clearance","nouns:customs clearance"],["customs declaration","nouns:customs declaration"],["warehouse manager","nouns:warehouse manager"],["loading dock","nouns:loading dock"],["supply chain","nouns:supply chain"],["freight charge","nouns:freight charge"],["delivery charge","nouns:delivery charge"],["distribution channel","nouns:distribution channel"],["express mail","nouns:express mail"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the container still waiting?","o":["The loading dock is full.","A page was missing from a document.","The warehouse manager is away.","The freight charge has not been paid."],"a":1,"why":"It is still waiting for customs clearance because the customs declaration was missing one page とある。"},{"q":"What will happen next month?","o":["A new container will arrive.","The warehouse will move.","Some charges will increase.","Online orders will stop."],"a":2,"why":"the freight charge for heavy goods will rise by eight percent, and the delivery charge ... will also go up とある。"},{"q":"How should urgent documents be sent?","o":["By express mail","By shipping container","By email","By the new online channel"],"a":0,"why":"Urgent documents should still go by express mail とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0025","page":"nouns","group":"契約・法務","kind":"法務部からの説明","text":"Good afternoon. I'm Helen from the legal department. I'd like to explain the contract renewal with our cleaning company. After a long contract negotiation, we have agreed on new contract terms. The effective date is April first, and the expiration date is three years later. All cleaning staff must wear an identification badge and will sign a confidentiality agreement, because they work near sensitive documents. In addition, our legal counsel has reviewed the lease agreement for the new office. The security deposit is two months' rent. We are still waiting for the building permit for the extra floor. If you have questions about any rental agreement, please email me directly.","ja":"こんにちは。法務部のヘレンです。清掃会社との契約更新についてご説明します。長い契約交渉の末、新しい契約条件で合意しました。発効日は4月1日で、満了日はその3年後です。清掃スタッフは、機密性の高い書類の近くで作業するため、全員が身分証バッジを着用し、秘密保持契約に署名します。また、新しい事務所の賃貸借契約は、当社の法律顧問が確認しました。保証金は家賃の2か月分です。増築する階の建築許可証は、まだ届くのを待っているところです。賃貸契約について質問がある場合は、私に直接メールしてください。","words":[["legal department","nouns:legal department"],["contract renewal","nouns:contract renewal"],["contract negotiation","nouns:contract negotiation"],["contract terms","nouns:contract terms"],["effective date","nouns:effective date"],["expiration date","nouns:expiration date"],["identification badge","nouns:identification badge"],["confidentiality agreement","nouns:confidentiality agreement"],["legal counsel","nouns:legal counsel"],["lease agreement","nouns:lease agreement"],["security deposit","nouns:security deposit"],["building permit","nouns:building permit"],["rental agreement","nouns:rental agreement"]],"qs":[{"q":"When does the new contract begin?","o":["On April first","In three years","In two months","Next week"],"a":0,"why":"The effective date is April first とある。3年後は満了日。"},{"q":"Why must cleaning staff sign a confidentiality agreement?","o":["They handle money.","They are new employees.","They enter the building at night.","They work near sensitive documents."],"a":3,"why":"will sign a confidentiality agreement, because they work near sensitive documents とある。"},{"q":"What is the company still waiting for?","o":["A security deposit","The legal counsel's review","A building permit","A new cleaning company"],"a":2,"why":"We are still waiting for the building permit for the extra floor とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0026","page":"nouns","group":"契約・法務","kind":"入館についての案内","text":"Welcome to Greenfield Research Park. For visitors and new staff, here is some important information. First, please show your parking permit to the security guard at the gate. Cars without a permit will be removed. Second, new security measures began this month. Bags may be checked at the entrance, and photography is not allowed inside the laboratories. Third, staff from overseas should bring their work permit to the personnel office on their first day. Finally, if you are here to discuss a patent application, our lawyers are on the third floor of building C. Maps are available at the information desk. We hope you have a pleasant visit.","ja":"グリーンフィールド研究団地へようこそ。来訪者と新しい職員の皆さまに、大切なご案内をします。まず、門のところで警備員に駐車許可証をお見せください。許可証のない車は移動されます。次に、今月から新しい警備措置が始まりました。入口で手荷物を確認させていただくことがあり、研究室の中での写真撮影はできません。3つ目。海外からの職員の方は、初日に就労許可証を人事課へお持ちください。最後に、特許出願のご相談でお越しの方は、C棟の3階に当施設の弁護士がおります。地図は案内所でお渡ししています。どうぞ良い時間をお過ごしください。","words":[["parking permit","nouns:parking permit"],["security guard","nouns:security guard"],["security measures","nouns:security measures"],["work permit","nouns:work permit"],["patent application","nouns:patent application"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should drivers show at the gate?","o":["A map","A parking permit","A photograph","A patent application"],"a":1,"why":"please show your parking permit to the security guard at the gate とある。"},{"q":"What is NOT allowed inside the laboratories?","o":["Carrying a bag","Talking to staff","Taking photographs","Wearing a badge"],"a":2,"why":"photography is not allowed inside the laboratories とある。手荷物は「確認されることがある」だけ。"},{"q":"Where can visitors get a map?","o":["At the information desk","At the gate","On the third floor of building C","At the personnel office"],"a":0,"why":"Maps are available at the information desk とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0027","page":"nouns","group":"旅行・交通","kind":"旅行代理店からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, Mr. Evans. This is Nina from Blue Sky Travel Agency. I've finished the travel arrangements for your trip to Sydney. Your flight itinerary and a full travel itinerary have been emailed to you. I booked a round-trip ticket, not a one-way ticket, as it was cheaper. You have an aisle seat on the way there and a window seat on the way back. The baggage allowance is two bags. Your hotel reservation is confirmed, and the room rate includes breakfast. The hotel's shuttle service runs from the airport every hour, so you won't need a rental car. If you'd like a tour guide for the weekend, just let me know. Have a great trip.","ja":"エヴァンス様、こんにちは。ブルースカイ旅行代理店のニーナです。シドニーへのご旅行の手配が完了しました。フライトの旅程と、全体の旅程表をメールでお送りしてあります。往復切符のほうが安かったので、片道ではなく往復でお取りしました。行きは通路側の席、帰りは窓側の席です。手荷物の許容量は2個です。ホテルのご予約は確定しており、宿泊料金には朝食が含まれています。ホテルの送迎サービスが空港から1時間おきに出ていますので、レンタカーは必要ありません。週末に観光ガイドをご希望でしたら、お知らせください。良いご旅行を。","words":[["Travel Agency","nouns:travel agency"],["travel arrangements","nouns:travel arrangements"],["flight itinerary","nouns:flight itinerary"],["travel itinerary","nouns:travel itinerary"],["round-trip ticket","nouns:round-trip ticket"],["one-way ticket","nouns:one-way ticket"],["aisle seat","nouns:aisle seat"],["window seat","nouns:window seat"],["baggage allowance","nouns:baggage allowance"],["hotel reservation","nouns:hotel reservation"],["room rate","nouns:room rate"],["shuttle service","nouns:shuttle service"],["rental car","nouns:rental car"],["tour guide","nouns:tour guide"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did the speaker book a round-trip ticket?","o":["It was less expensive.","Mr. Evans asked for one.","One-way tickets were sold out.","It included a hotel room."],"a":0,"why":"I booked a round-trip ticket, not a one-way ticket, as it was cheaper とある。cheaper を less expensive と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What is included in the room rate?","o":["A rental car","A guided tour","Airport parking","Breakfast"],"a":3,"why":"the room rate includes breakfast とある。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, why is a rental car unnecessary?","o":["The hotel is near the airport.","The hotel runs a shuttle service.","A tour guide will drive.","Public transportation is free."],"a":1,"why":"The hotel's shuttle service runs from the airport every hour, so you won't need a rental car とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0028","page":"nouns","group":"旅行・交通","kind":"観光バスの車内案内","text":"Good morning, everyone, and welcome aboard this guided tour of the old town. Our first stop is the castle, the city's most famous tourist attraction. Because of traffic congestion in the center, we will arrive about ten minutes late. There is usually a traffic jam near the train station during rush hour, so we are taking the river road. When we arrive, I will buy your tickets at the ticket booth. The bus will wait in the parking lot behind the castle, not in the parking garage. Please be back by eleven thirty. This afternoon is free, and the easiest way to get around is by public transportation. Our arrival time at the hotel will be about six.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。旧市街をめぐるガイド付きツアーへようこそ。最初の目的地は、この街で最も有名な観光名所であるお城です。中心部の交通渋滞のため、到着は10分ほど遅れます。ラッシュアワーの時間帯は駅の近くでたいてい渋滞が起きるので、川沿いの道を通ります。到着したら、私が切符売り場で皆さんの入場券を買います。バスは立体駐車場ではなく、お城の裏の駐車場で待っています。11時30分までにお戻りください。午後は自由行動で、移動には公共交通機関が一番便利です。ホテルへの到着時刻は6時ごろの予定です。","words":[["guided tour","nouns:guided tour"],["tourist attraction","nouns:tourist attraction"],["traffic congestion","nouns:traffic congestion"],["traffic jam","nouns:traffic jam"],["train station","nouns:train station"],["rush hour","nouns:rush hour"],["ticket booth","nouns:ticket booth"],["parking lot","nouns:parking lot"],["parking garage","nouns:parking garage"],["public transportation","nouns:public transportation"],["arrival time","nouns:arrival time"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will the bus arrive late at the castle?","o":["The driver took a wrong turn.","The castle opens late.","There is heavy traffic.","A passenger was delayed."],"a":2,"why":"Because of traffic congestion in the center, we will arrive about ten minutes late とある。"},{"q":"Where will the bus wait?","o":["In a parking lot behind the castle","In a parking garage","In front of the train station","On the river road"],"a":0,"why":"The bus will wait in the parking lot behind the castle, not in the parking garage とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker recommend for the afternoon?","o":["Joining another tour","Staying at the hotel","Renting a car","Using public transportation"],"a":3,"why":"the easiest way to get around is by public transportation とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0029","page":"nouns","group":"旅行・交通","kind":"空港の案内放送","text":"Attention, passengers arriving on flight 618 from Madrid. Your bags will be delivered to baggage claim area four in about fifteen minutes. If your luggage does not appear, please go to the service counter next to the exit. Passengers who need a car rental will find the offices on the ground floor, opposite the cafe. For those going downtown, the express bus leaves from stop number two every ten minutes. Please note that the east exit is closed today, so use the west doors. We also remind you not to leave your belongings unattended at any time. Thank you for flying with us, and welcome to Lisbon.","ja":"マドリード発618便でご到着のお客様にご案内します。お荷物は、およそ15分後に手荷物受取所の4番に届きます。お荷物が出てこない場合は、出口の隣のサービスカウンターへお越しください。レンタカーをご利用のお客様は、1階のカフェの向かい側に営業所がございます。市内へ向かわれる方には、急行バスが2番乗り場から10分おきに出ています。本日は東口が閉鎖されておりますので、西側のドアをご利用ください。また、お手回り品からは決して目を離さないよう、お願いいたします。ご搭乗ありがとうございました。リスボンへようこそ。","words":[["baggage claim","nouns:baggage claim"],["car rental","nouns:car rental"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where should passengers collect their bags?","o":["At the service counter","At baggage claim area four","At stop number two","On the ground floor"],"a":1,"why":"Your bags will be delivered to baggage claim area four とある。サービスカウンターは荷物が出てこないときに行く場所。"},{"q":"Where are the car rental offices?","o":["Next to the exit","At the east exit","Opposite the cafe","Beside the bus stop"],"a":2,"why":"will find the offices on the ground floor, opposite the cafe とある。"},{"q":"What are passengers told about the east exit?","o":["It is closed today.","It leads to the bus stop.","It is the fastest way out.","It opens in fifteen minutes."],"a":0,"why":"the east exit is closed today, so use the west doors とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0030","page":"nouns","group":"不動産・施設","kind":"不動産業者からの留守番電話","text":"Hi, Ms. Lopez. This is Daniel, the real estate agent you spoke with last week. I've found a rental property that may suit your company. It is on the fourth floor of a new office complex in the commercial district, just ten minutes from the residential area where most of your staff live. The office space is two hundred square meters, and I have emailed you the floor plan. There is a storage room on the same floor and a fitness center in the basement. The rent does not include the utility bill, which is usually about three hundred dollars a month. The property manager can show us around on Friday. Please let me know if that works.","ja":"ロペス様、こんにちは。先週お話しした不動産業者のダニエルです。御社に合いそうな賃貸物件を見つけました。商業地区にある新しいオフィス複合施設の4階で、社員の皆さんの多くが住んでいる住宅地から、わずか10分のところです。オフィスの広さは200平方メートルで、間取り図はメールでお送りしてあります。同じ階に保管室があり、地下にはフィットネスセンターもあります。家賃には公共料金は含まれておらず、そちらは通常、月300ドルほどです。金曜日に、不動産管理人が中を案内してくれます。ご都合がよいかどうか、お知らせください。","words":[["real estate agent","nouns:real estate agent"],["rental property","nouns:rental property"],["office complex","nouns:office complex"],["commercial district","nouns:commercial district"],["residential area","nouns:residential area"],["office space","nouns:office space"],["floor plan","nouns:floor plan"],["storage room","nouns:storage room"],["fitness center","nouns:fitness center"],["utility bill","nouns:utility bill"],["property manager","nouns:property manager"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the call?","o":["To describe an available office","To ask for a rent payment","To cancel a visit","To sell a house"],"a":0,"why":"I've found a rental property that may suit your company とあり、物件を紹介している。"},{"q":"What is NOT included in the rent?","o":["The storage room","The fitness center","Utilities","Parking"],"a":2,"why":"The rent does not include the utility bill とある。"},{"q":"What may happen on Friday?","o":["A contract will be signed.","The staff will move in.","A floor plan will be sent.","A tour of the property will be given."],"a":3,"why":"The property manager can show us around on Friday とある。show around を a tour と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"n-0031","page":"nouns","group":"不動産・施設","kind":"住民へのお知らせ","text":"This is an announcement for residents of Oak Street. The city council has approved a renovation project at the community center, and work begins on Monday. The construction project will last six weeks. During that time, the construction crew will replace the old heating system, install a new air conditioner in the main hall, and change every light fixture. Trucks carrying building materials will use the north gate, so please do not park there. For safety, children must stay away from the construction site. On Wednesday morning, the utility company will turn off the water for two hours. If you have questions, contact the building manager or visit city hall.","ja":"オーク通りにお住まいの皆さまへのお知らせです。市議会が公民館の改装工事を承認し、月曜日から作業が始まります。工事は6週間続きます。その間に、建設作業班が古い暖房設備を取り替え、メインホールに新しいエアコンを設置し、照明器具をすべて交換します。建築資材を運ぶトラックが北門を使いますので、そこには駐車しないでください。安全のため、お子さまは工事現場に近づけないようにしてください。水曜日の午前中は、公共事業会社が2時間、水道を止めます。ご質問がある場合は、ビル管理人にご連絡いただくか、市役所へお越しください。","words":[["city council","nouns:city council"],["renovation project","nouns:renovation project"],["community center","nouns:community center"],["construction project","nouns:construction project"],["construction crew","nouns:construction crew"],["heating system","nouns:heating system"],["air conditioner","nouns:air conditioner"],["light fixture","nouns:light fixture"],["building materials","nouns:building materials"],["construction site","nouns:construction site"],["utility company","nouns:utility company"],["building manager","nouns:building manager"],["city hall","nouns:city hall"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where will the work take place?","o":["At city hall","At a community center","On Oak Street's north side","At a utility company"],"a":1,"why":"a renovation project at the community center とある。"},{"q":"What are residents asked NOT to do?","o":["Use the main hall","Call the building manager","Park near the north gate","Visit city hall"],"a":2,"why":"Trucks ... will use the north gate, so please do not park there とある。"},{"q":"What will happen on Wednesday morning?","o":["The water will be turned off.","The work will be finished.","The city council will meet.","New lights will be delivered."],"a":0,"why":"the utility company will turn off the water for two hours とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0032","page":"nouns","group":"IT・通信","kind":"技術サポートからの連絡","text":"This is a message from technical support. Last night's system upgrade caused a short network outage, and some of you are still having technical difficulties. If you cannot log in, please request a password reset for your user account. Next, please install the latest software update for your web browser before noon. It fixes a serious security problem. We have also learned of a data breach at one of our suppliers, so do not open any email attachment from an address you do not know. Finally, tomorrow's video conference with the London office will use the new program. A short guide has been sent to everyone. Thank you for your patience.","ja":"技術サポートからのお知らせです。昨夜のシステム更新の影響で短時間の通信障害が発生し、まだ技術的な問題が続いている方がいます。ログインできない場合は、ご自分のユーザーアカウントのパスワード再設定を依頼してください。次に、正午までに、ウェブブラウザの最新のソフトウェア更新を入れてください。重大な安全上の問題を修正するものです。また、取引先の1社で情報漏えいがあったことが分かりましたので、知らないアドレスからのメールの添付ファイルは開かないでください。最後に、明日のロンドン事務所とのビデオ会議は、新しいプログラムを使います。簡単な手引きを全員に送ってあります。ご理解に感謝します。","words":[["technical support","nouns:technical support"],["system upgrade","nouns:system upgrade"],["network outage","nouns:network outage"],["technical difficulties","nouns:technical difficulties"],["password reset","nouns:password reset"],["user account","nouns:user account"],["software update","nouns:software update"],["web browser","nouns:web browser"],["data breach","nouns:data breach"],["email attachment","nouns:email attachment"],["video conference","nouns:video conference"]],"qs":[{"q":"What caused the network outage?","o":["A system upgrade","A data breach","A power failure","A new video program"],"a":0,"why":"Last night's system upgrade caused a short network outage とある。"},{"q":"What should the listeners do before noon?","o":["Call the London office","Change their email address","Read a short guide","Update their web browser"],"a":3,"why":"please install the latest software update for your web browser before noon とある。"},{"q":"What are the listeners warned not to do?","o":["Use the new program","Open attachments from unknown senders","Reset their passwords","Log in during the upgrade"],"a":1,"why":"do not open any email attachment from an address you do not know とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0033","page":"nouns","group":"IT・通信","kind":"ソフトウェアの広告","text":"Are you tired of slow, complicated office software? Try DataFlow, the new tool for small businesses. Created by a team of experienced software developers, DataFlow makes database management simple. Data entry takes half the time, and our data analysis charts are ready in one click. The user interface is so clear that no training is needed. DataFlow works on any mobile device without reducing battery life, and automatic backups protect you from a system failure. You can even find any file with our built-in search engine. Join our mailing list today and receive a thirty-day free trial. Visit our website to learn more. DataFlow. Work smarter.","ja":"動作が遅くて複雑な業務用ソフトに、うんざりしていませんか。小規模事業者向けの新しいツール、データフローをお試しください。経験豊富なソフトウェア開発者のチームが作ったデータフローなら、データベース管理が簡単になります。データ入力にかかる時間は半分になり、データ分析のグラフはワンクリックで出来上がります。ユーザーインターフェースがとても分かりやすいので、研修は必要ありません。データフローは、電池の持ち時間を縮めることなく、どの携帯端末でも動きます。自動バックアップがシステム障害から守ります。内蔵の検索エンジンで、どのファイルもすぐに見つかります。今すぐメール配信リストに登録して、30日間の無料体験を手に入れましょう。詳しくはウェブサイトをご覧ください。データフロー。もっと賢く働こう。","words":[["software developers","nouns:software developer"],["database management","nouns:database management"],["Data entry","nouns:data entry"],["data analysis","nouns:data analysis"],["user interface","nouns:user interface"],["mobile device","nouns:mobile device"],["battery life","nouns:battery life"],["system failure","nouns:system failure"],["search engine","nouns:search engine"],["mailing list","nouns:mailing list"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the product designed for?","o":["Software developers","Large banks","Small businesses","University students"],"a":2,"why":"the new tool for small businesses とある。開発者は「作った人たち」。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the user interface?","o":["It is easy to use without training.","It works only on computers.","It was designed by customers.","It will be improved soon."],"a":0,"why":"The user interface is so clear that no training is needed とある。"},{"q":"How can the listeners get a free trial?","o":["By calling a sales office","By joining a mailing list","By buying a mobile device","By visiting a store"],"a":1,"why":"Join our mailing list today and receive a thirty-day free trial とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0034","page":"nouns","group":"イベント・広報","kind":"慈善イベントでの案内","text":"Thank you for joining tonight's charity event for the children's hospital. Please note the venue change: because so many of you signed up, we have moved from the garden room to the banquet hall on the second floor. If you have not yet paid the registration fee, please complete a registration form at the registration desk and pick up your name tag. The seating arrangement is posted beside the door. Dinner, provided by our catering service, will be served at seven. At eight, our guest speaker, Dr. Amy Chen, will talk about her work. This is our largest fund-raising event of the year, so please give generously.","ja":"今夜は、小児病院のための慈善イベントにご参加いただき、ありがとうございます。会場の変更にご注意ください。お申し込みが大変多かったため、ガーデンルームから2階の宴会場に移りました。参加費をまだお支払いでない方は、受付で登録用紙に記入し、名札をお受け取りください。座席の配置は、ドアの横に掲示してあります。ケータリングサービスによる夕食は、7時にお出しします。8時からは、来賓講演者のエイミー・チェン医師が、ご自身の活動についてお話しします。これは今年最大の資金集めのイベントですので、どうぞ温かいご支援をお願いします。","words":[["charity event","nouns:charity event"],["venue change","nouns:venue change"],["banquet hall","nouns:banquet hall"],["registration fee","nouns:registration fee"],["registration form","nouns:registration form"],["registration desk","nouns:registration desk"],["name tag","nouns:name tag"],["seating arrangement","nouns:seating arrangement"],["catering service","nouns:catering service"],["guest speaker","nouns:guest speaker"],["fund-raising event","nouns:fund-raising event"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why was the venue changed?","o":["The garden room was being repaired.","The hospital asked for a larger room.","The catering service requested it.","Many people signed up."],"a":3,"why":"because so many of you signed up, we have moved ... to the banquet hall とある。"},{"q":"Where is the seating arrangement posted?","o":["At the registration desk","Beside the door","On each name tag","In the garden room"],"a":1,"why":"The seating arrangement is posted beside the door とある。"},{"q":"What will happen at eight o'clock?","o":["Dinner will be served.","The doors will close.","A guest speaker will give a talk.","Name tags will be collected."],"a":2,"why":"At eight, our guest speaker, Dr. Amy Chen, will talk about her work とある。夕食は7時。"}]},
{"id":"n-0035","page":"nouns","group":"イベント・広報","kind":"文化施設の広告","text":"The Harbor Arts Center is proud to announce its grand opening on Saturday, June third. The opening ceremony begins at ten, with a speech by the mayor. In the new exhibition hall, you can enjoy an art exhibition of works by fifty local painters. At two o'clock, the author Mia Torres will hold a book signing in the lobby. In the evening, the city's art prizes will be presented at an award ceremony, followed by an awards banquet for invited guests. The theater has a seating capacity of only three hundred, so please arrive early. There is no admission fee on opening day. We look forward to seeing you.","ja":"ハーバー芸術センターは、6月3日土曜日に開館記念イベントを開催します。開会式は10時に始まり、市長があいさつをします。新しい展示場では、地元の画家50人の作品を集めた美術展をお楽しみいただけます。2時には、作家のミア・トーレスさんがロビーでサイン会を開きます。夕方には、授賞式で市の芸術賞が贈られ、続いて招待客のための授賞晩餐会が開かれます。劇場の座席数は300席しかありませんので、お早めにお越しください。開館日は入場料無料です。皆さまのお越しをお待ちしています。","words":[["grand opening","nouns:grand opening"],["opening ceremony","nouns:opening ceremony"],["exhibition hall","nouns:exhibition hall"],["art exhibition","nouns:art exhibition"],["book signing","nouns:book signing"],["award ceremony","nouns:award ceremony"],["awards banquet","nouns:awards banquet"],["seating capacity","nouns:seating capacity"],["admission fee","nouns:admission fee"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen on June third?","o":["An arts center will open.","A painter will give a class.","A theater will close.","A mayor will be elected."],"a":0,"why":"The Harbor Arts Center is proud to announce its grand opening on Saturday, June third とある。"},{"q":"Who will sign books in the lobby?","o":["The mayor","A local painter","An author","An invited guest"],"a":2,"why":"the author Mia Torres will hold a book signing in the lobby とある。"},{"q":"Why are the listeners advised to arrive early?","o":["Parking is difficult.","The number of seats is limited.","Admission is free until ten.","The banquet starts early."],"a":1,"why":"The theater has a seating capacity of only three hundred, so please arrive early とある。"}]},
{"id":"n-0036","page":"nouns","group":"日常・小売","kind":"デパートの店内放送","text":"Good afternoon, shoppers, and welcome to Bayview Department Store. Today, all household appliances on the third floor are twenty percent off, and every kitchen appliance comes with a free cookbook. You will also find new home furnishings on the fourth floor. Please note that the cash register at the north checkout counter is not working, so use the south side. If you wish to return an item without a receipt, a store clerk can offer you store credit. A child's blue jacket was found in a shopping cart and is now at the lost and found. Finally, the dining area and the gift shop on the top floor will close at eight tonight. Thank you for shopping with us.","ja":"お買い物中の皆さま、こんにちは。ベイビュー百貨店へようこそ。本日は、3階の家庭用電化製品がすべて20パーセント引きで、台所用の電化製品には料理本が無料で付きます。4階には、新しい家具や室内装飾品もそろっています。北側のレジの機械が故障していますので、南側のレジをご利用ください。レシートなしで商品を返品される場合は、店員が店内で使えるクレジットをご用意します。買い物カートの中に子ども用の青い上着のお忘れ物があり、現在、遺失物取扱所でお預かりしています。最後に、最上階の食事スペースと土産物店は、今夜8時に閉まります。ご来店ありがとうございます。","words":[["Department Store","nouns:department store"],["household appliances","nouns:household appliances"],["kitchen appliance","nouns:kitchen appliance"],["home furnishings","nouns:home furnishings"],["cash register","nouns:cash register"],["checkout counter","nouns:checkout counter"],["store clerk","nouns:store clerk"],["store credit","nouns:store credit"],["shopping cart","nouns:shopping cart"],["lost and found","nouns:lost and found"],["dining area","nouns:dining area"],["gift shop","nouns:gift shop"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is on sale today?","o":["Cookbooks","Household appliances","Children's jackets","Home furnishings"],"a":1,"why":"all household appliances on the third floor are twenty percent off とある。料理本は無料で付くおまけ。"},{"q":"What is the problem at the north checkout counter?","o":["It is too crowded.","It accepts only cash.","No clerk is available.","The cash register is broken."],"a":3,"why":"the cash register at the north checkout counter is not working とある。"},{"q":"Where is the blue jacket now?","o":["At the lost and found","In a shopping cart","At the gift shop","On the third floor"],"a":0,"why":"is now at the lost and found とある。カートは「見つかった場所」。"}]},
{"id":"n-0037","page":"nouns","group":"日常・小売","kind":"家族への留守番電話","text":"Hi, Sam. It's me. I'm still at the clinic. My medical checkup took longer than I expected, so I can't pick up the kids. Could you do it? Also, I need a few favors on your way home. Please collect my suit from the dry cleaner, and stop at the grocery store for milk and eggs. If it's closed, the convenience store on the corner is fine. My prescription medicine will be ready at the pharmacy after five. Oh, and the weather forecast says it will snow tonight, so could you buy some salt at the hardware store? One last thing: don't forget your dental appointment tomorrow at nine. Thanks. See you tonight.","ja":"もしもし、サム。私です。まだクリニックにいます。健康診断が思ったより長引いて、子どもたちを迎えに行けません。代わりにお願いできますか。それから、帰り道にいくつか頼みたいことがあります。クリーニング店で私のスーツを受け取って、食料品店で牛乳と卵を買ってきてください。閉まっていたら、角のコンビニでかまいません。私の処方薬は、5時以降に薬局で受け取れます。そうそう、天気予報では今夜雪が降るそうなので、金物店で塩を買ってきてもらえますか。最後にもう1つ。明日9時の歯医者の予約を忘れないでね。ありがとう。ではまた今夜。","words":[["medical checkup","nouns:medical checkup"],["dry cleaner","nouns:dry cleaner"],["grocery store","nouns:grocery store"],["convenience store","nouns:convenience store"],["prescription medicine","nouns:prescription medicine"],["weather forecast","nouns:weather forecast"],["hardware store","nouns:hardware store"],["dental appointment","nouns:dental appointment"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the speaker unable to pick up the children?","o":["Her car has broken down.","She has to work late.","Her checkup took longer than expected.","She is at the pharmacy."],"a":2,"why":"My medical checkup took longer than I expected, so I can't pick up the kids とある。"},{"q":"What should Sam buy at the hardware store?","o":["Milk and eggs","Medicine","A snow shovel","Salt"],"a":3,"why":"could you buy some salt at the hardware store? とある。牛乳と卵は食料品店。"},{"q":"What is Sam reminded about?","o":["A dental appointment","A meeting at nine tonight","A delivery of a suit","A school event"],"a":0,"why":"don't forget your dental appointment tomorrow at nine とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0003","page":"idioms","group":["back","blow","brush"],"kind":"同僚との会話","text":"Thanks for meeting me, Carla. I want to talk about the Milan deal. Yesterday, the buyer threatened to back out of the contract unless we lowered the price. I refused to back down, and for a moment I thought he would blow up. He brushed aside our sales figures and brushed off my offer of free delivery. Still, I think the argument will blow over by next week. In the meantime, could you blow up the product photos for a large poster? They will back up our claim about quality. Also, I'll be traveling to Italy in May, so I plan to brush up on my Italian. Can you recommend a good evening class?","ja":"カーラ、時間を取ってくれてありがとう。ミラノの商談について話したいんだ。昨日、先方の買い手が、値下げしなければ契約から手を引くと脅してきた。私は引き下がらなかったので、一瞬、彼がかっとなるかと思ったよ。彼はこちらの販売実績を無視し、送料無料という私の申し出もすげなく断った。それでも、この言い争いは来週までには収まると思う。その間に、大きなポスター用に製品の写真を引き伸ばしてもらえるかな。品質についての私たちの主張を裏付けてくれるはずだ。それと、5月にイタリアへ行くので、イタリア語を学び直すつもりなんだ。良い夜間講座を知っていたら教えてくれないか。","words":[["back out of","idioms:4:back out of"],["back down","idioms:1:back down"],["would blow up","idioms:1:blow up"],["brushed aside","idioms:2:brush aside"],["brushed off","idioms:2:brush off"],["blow over","idioms:1:blow over"],["blow up the product photos","idioms:2:blow up"],["back up","idioms:2:back up"],["brush up on","idioms:4:brush up on"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the buyer threaten to do?","o":["Raise the price","Withdraw from the contract","Change the delivery date","Contact another seller"],"a":1,"why":"the buyer threatened to back out of the contract とある。back out of を withdraw from と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker ask Carla to do?","o":["Enlarge some photos","Call the buyer","Lower the price","Travel to Milan"],"a":0,"why":"could you blow up the product photos for a large poster? とある。blow up（引き伸ばす）を enlarge と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker plan to do before May?","o":["Hire an interpreter","Take a vacation","Design a poster","Improve his Italian"],"a":3,"why":"I plan to brush up on my Italian とある。brush up on を improve と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0004","page":"idioms","group":"break","kind":"夕方のニュース","text":"Here is the evening news. A fire broke out at a furniture warehouse on Dock Road last night after thieves broke in through a side door. Police believe the men also broke into two parked trucks. One suspect was caught when his car broke down a few streets away. In business news, talks between Star Airlines and its pilots have been broken off. A small group of pilots now wants to break away from the main union, and yesterday's meeting broke up after only an hour. On a brighter note, city scientists say they have finally broken through in their search for cleaner fuel. In entertainment, singer Lily Ray has broken up with her manager of ten years. After the weather, our reporter will break down the new tax rules for you.","ja":"夕方のニュースです。昨夜、ドック通りの家具倉庫で火災が発生しました。泥棒が横のドアから押し入ったあとのことでした。警察は、男たちが駐車中のトラック2台にも侵入したと見ています。容疑者の1人は、数本先の通りで車が故障したところを逮捕されました。ビジネスニュースです。スター航空と操縦士の交渉が打ち切られました。現在、一部の操縦士が主要な組合から離脱したいとしており、昨日の会合はわずか1時間で解散しました。明るい話題です。市の科学者たちが、よりクリーンな燃料の研究でついに突破口を開いたと発表しました。芸能では、歌手のリリー・レイさんが10年来のマネージャーと別れました。天気予報のあとは、記者が新しい税制を細かく分けて解説します。","words":[["broke out","idioms:1:break out"],["broke in","idioms:1:break in"],["broke into","idioms:3:break into"],["broke down","idioms:1:break down"],["broken off","idioms:2:break off"],["break away from","idioms:4:break away from"],["broke up","idioms:1:break up"],["broken through","idioms:1:break through"],["broken up with","idioms:4:break up with"],["break down the new tax rules","idioms:2:break down"]],"qs":[{"q":"How did the thieves enter the warehouse?","o":["Through a side door","Through the roof","In a parked truck","Through the main gate"],"a":0,"why":"thieves broke in through a side door とある。"},{"q":"What does a small group of pilots want to do?","o":["End the strike","Meet the airline again","Leave the main union","Change their manager"],"a":2,"why":"A small group of pilots now wants to break away from the main union とある。break away from を leave と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will the listeners hear after the weather?","o":["An interview with a singer","A report on cleaner fuel","News about the fire","An explanation of new tax rules"],"a":3,"why":"our reporter will break down the new tax rules for you とある。break down（細かく分けて説明する）を explanation と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0005","page":"idioms","group":"bring","kind":"会議の冒頭","text":"Good morning, everyone. Before we begin, I'd like to bring up some good news. Our new cereal brought in two million dollars last quarter. The advertising campaign brought about a real change in how shoppers see us. It was a risky plan, but the team brought it off. However, last month's recall brought home to all of us the importance of testing. So, here are the next steps. We will bring forward the safety review from June to April. We also plan to bring out a low-sugar version in the fall and to bring back our classic packaging. Finally, we must bring down delivery costs. Let's start with the review.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。始める前に、良い知らせを1つお伝えしたいと思います。新しいシリアルは、前の四半期に200万ドルの売上をもたらしました。広告キャンペーンは、買い物客の当社に対する見方に本当の変化をもたらしました。危険のある計画でしたが、チームは見事にやってのけました。しかし、先月の製品回収は、検査の大切さを私たち全員に痛感させました。そこで、次の手順をお伝えします。安全審査を6月から4月に前倒しします。また、秋には低糖タイプを発売し、昔ながらのパッケージを復活させる計画です。最後に、配送費を下げなければなりません。まずは審査の話から始めましょう。","words":[["bring up","idioms:2:bring up"],["brought in","idioms:2:bring in"],["brought about","idioms:2:bring about"],["brought it off","idioms:2:bring off"],["brought home to","idioms:5:bring A home to B"],["bring forward","idioms:2:bring forward"],["bring out","idioms:2:bring out"],["bring back","idioms:2:bring back"],["bring down","idioms:2:bring down"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the speaker say about the advertising campaign?","o":["It cost two million dollars.","It changed how shoppers see the company.","It was canceled last month.","It will begin in the fall."],"a":1,"why":"The advertising campaign brought about a real change in how shoppers see us とある。"},{"q":"What will be moved to April?","o":["The product recall","The cereal launch","The safety review","The packaging change"],"a":2,"why":"We will bring forward the safety review from June to April とある。bring forward は「前倒しする」。"},{"q":"What does the company plan to do in the fall?","o":["Release a low-sugar version","Raise delivery costs","Close a factory","Start a new campaign"],"a":0,"why":"We also plan to bring out a low-sugar version in the fall とある。bring out を release と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0006","page":"idioms","group":["call","close"],"kind":"市役所からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, Mr. Shaw. This is Irene from the mayor's office, with news about Saturday's street fair. I'm sorry, but we have had to call off the event. A storm is closing in on the coast, and the weather service is calling for people to stay indoors. We have also called in extra crews to protect the harbor. Several shops on Main Street will close down for the weekend. The mayor will call on local businesses to help with repairs next week, and she hopes you will join us. I tried to call you up earlier, but the line was busy. Please call back when you can.","ja":"ショー様、こんにちは。市長室のアイリーンです。土曜日のストリートフェアについてお知らせがあります。申し訳ありませんが、催しを中止せざるを得なくなりました。嵐が沿岸に迫っており、気象当局は屋内にとどまるよう求めています。港を守るため、追加の作業班も呼び寄せました。大通りのいくつかの店は、週末の間、店を閉めます。市長は来週、地元の事業者に修復への協力を求める予定で、ショー様にもご参加いただければと願っています。先ほどお電話したのですが、話し中でした。ご都合のよいときに、折り返しお電話ください。","words":[["call off","idioms:2:call off"],["closing in on","idioms:4:close in on"],["calling for","idioms:3:call for"],["called in","idioms:2:call in"],["close down","idioms:1:close down"],["call on","idioms:3:call on"],["call you up","idioms:2:call up"],["call back","idioms:1:call back"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why has the event been canceled?","o":["The harbor is closed.","Too few shops signed up.","The mayor is away.","A storm is approaching."],"a":3,"why":"A storm is closing in on the coast とある。closing in on を approaching と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will the mayor ask local businesses to do?","o":["Help with repairs","Close for a week","Pay for the fair","Move to Main Street"],"a":0,"why":"The mayor will call on local businesses to help with repairs とある。call on は「～に求める」。"},{"q":"Why could the speaker not reach Mr. Shaw earlier?","o":["He was at the harbor.","The line was busy.","The office was closed.","His number had changed."],"a":1,"why":"I tried to call you up earlier, but the line was busy とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0007","page":"idioms","group":["carry","catch"],"kind":"休暇制度の説明","text":"Let me explain the changes to our vacation policy. Until now, unused days could not be carried over to the next year. From January, you may keep up to five days. The idea has caught on at many companies, and we want to catch up with them. We carried out a survey last month, and ninety percent of you supported the change. We will carry this reform through in two stages. In the meantime, please carry on with your current plans. If you return from a long break, your manager will give you time to catch up on email. That is the main point. Now, let's carry on. Are there any questions?","ja":"休暇制度の変更についてご説明します。これまで、使わなかった休暇を翌年に繰り越すことはできませんでした。1月からは、5日まで残しておけるようになります。この考え方は多くの会社で広まっており、当社もそれに追いつきたいと考えています。先月アンケートを実施したところ、皆さんの90パーセントが変更に賛成でした。この改革は、2段階に分けてやり遂げます。それまでは、今の予定をそのまま続けてください。長い休みから戻ったときは、たまったメールを片付ける時間を上司が用意します。要点は以上です。では、先に進みましょう。質問はありますか。","words":[["carried over","idioms:2:carry over"],["caught on","idioms:1:catch on"],["catch up with","idioms:4:catch up with"],["carried out","idioms:2:carry out"],["carry this reform through","idioms:2:carry through"],["carry on with","idioms:4:carry on with"],["catch up on","idioms:4:catch up on"],["carry on","idioms:1:carry on"]],"qs":[{"q":"How many unused vacation days may employees keep from January?","o":["Two","Five","Nine","Ninety"],"a":1,"why":"From January, you may keep up to five days とある。"},{"q":"What did last month's survey show?","o":["Most employees supported the change.","Few employees take long breaks.","Managers opposed the policy.","Other companies had no such rule."],"a":0,"why":"ninety percent of you supported the change とある。"},{"q":"What will managers give employees who return from a long break?","o":["An extra day off","A copy of the survey","Time to deal with email","A new work plan"],"a":2,"why":"your manager will give you time to catch up on email とある。catch up on は「たまった分を片付ける」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0008","page":"idioms","group":["check","clear"],"kind":"ホテルの館内放送","text":"Good morning, and welcome to the Seaside Inn. A few notes for our guests. You may check in from two o'clock, and we ask that you check out by eleven. The rain should clear up by noon, so the pool will open this afternoon. Our staff are clearing the garden paths of fallen branches after last night's storm. If you had a problem with your bill, please see the front desk, and we will clear up any mistakes right away. Guests in the east wing, please note that workers will clear out the old storage room today, so there may be some noise. A manager will check up on the work each hour. Finally, do check out our new rooftop cafe.","ja":"おはようございます。シーサイド・インへようこそ。お客様にいくつかご案内します。チェックインは2時から、チェックアウトは11時までにお願いします。雨は正午までには上がる見込みですので、プールは午後から開きます。昨夜の嵐のあと、スタッフが庭の小道から落ちた枝を取り除いています。ご請求に問題があった場合は、フロントへお越しください。誤りはすぐに解決します。東館にお泊まりのお客様にお知らせです。本日、作業員が古い物置を片付けますので、音がすることがあります。支配人が1時間ごとに作業の様子を確かめます。最後に、新しい屋上のカフェもぜひのぞいてみてください。","words":[["check in","idioms:1:check in"],["check out by eleven","idioms:1:check out"],["clear up by noon","idioms:1:clear up"],["clearing the garden paths of","idioms:5:clear A of B"],["clear up any mistakes","idioms:2:clear up"],["clear out","idioms:2:clear out"],["check up on","idioms:4:check up on"],["check out our new rooftop cafe","idioms:2:check out"]],"qs":[{"q":"By what time must guests leave their rooms?","o":["By eleven o'clock","By noon","By two o'clock","By this afternoon"],"a":0,"why":"we ask that you check out by eleven とある。"},{"q":"Why might there be noise in the east wing?","o":["The pool is being repaired.","A storm is coming.","A storage room is being emptied.","A cafe is being built."],"a":2,"why":"workers will clear out the old storage room today, so there may be some noise とある。clear out を be emptied と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker recommend?","o":["Checking the bill at once","Staying indoors today","Using the garden paths","Visiting the rooftop cafe"],"a":3,"why":"do check out our new rooftop cafe とある。ここの check out は「見てみる」の意味。"}]},
{"id":"i-0009","page":"idioms","group":"come","kind":"スポーツニュース","text":"And now, a remarkable story from the world of sports. Runner Jake Morris came down with a serious fever two days before the national marathon. Tickets were hard to come by, and his family had flown in to watch. During the race, he fell at the halfway point and only came to after a doctor arrived. Yet he stood up and finished. How did this come about? Morris says his coach, who first opposed the idea of running, finally came around. The decision has come in for criticism, and race officials have come under pressure to change the rules, which come into force next year. Still, the comeback came off, and Morris came through without lasting injury.","ja":"続いて、スポーツ界から驚きの話題です。ランナーのジェイク・モリス選手は、全国マラソンの2日前にひどい熱を出しました。チケットは手に入りにくく、家族は観戦のために飛行機で駆けつけていました。レース中、彼は中間地点で倒れ、医師が到着してようやく意識を取り戻しました。それでも彼は立ち上がり、完走しました。どうしてこんなことが起きたのでしょうか。モリス選手によると、最初は出場に反対していたコーチが、最後には考えを変えたそうです。この判断は批判を受けており、大会の運営側は、来年から効力を持つ規則を変えるよう圧力を受けています。それでも復活劇は成功し、モリス選手は後遺症もなく切り抜けました。","words":[["came down with","idioms:4:come down with"],["come by","idioms:3:come by"],["came to","idioms:1:come to"],["come about","idioms:1:come about"],["came around","idioms:1:come around"],["come in for","idioms:4:come in for"],["come under","idioms:3:come under"],["come into","idioms:3:come into"],["came off","idioms:1:come off"],["came through","idioms:1:come through"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened two days before the marathon?","o":["Morris injured his leg.","Morris became ill.","The race rules were changed.","Morris's coach resigned."],"a":1,"why":"came down with a serious fever two days before the national marathon とある。come down with を became ill と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Who changed his mind about the race?","o":["A doctor","A race official","Morris's father","Morris's coach"],"a":3,"why":"his coach, who first opposed the idea of running, finally came around とある。come around は「意見を変える」。"},{"q":"What are race officials under pressure to do?","o":["Cancel next year's race","Sell more tickets","Change the rules","Hire more doctors"],"a":2,"why":"race officials have come under pressure to change the rules とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0010","page":"idioms","group":["count","cut"],"kind":"チームへの連絡","text":"Hi, team. I have to tell you about the budget. Head office has cut back our travel funds by thirty percent, so we need to cut back on flights. From now on, please use video calls when you can. We also have to cut down on printing. I have cut out an article about saving paper and pinned it to the board. One more thing: the phone company cut off our service this morning by mistake, but it is working again. Now, about Friday's volunteer day. I know I can count on most of you. If you want to join, tell me and I'll count you in. If you're busy, I'll count you out. Sorry, Ben, I didn't mean to cut in. Go ahead.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。予算についてお伝えしなければなりません。本社が出張費を30パーセント削減したので、飛行機での移動を減らす必要があります。これからは、できるだけビデオ通話を使ってください。印刷の量も減らさなければなりません。紙の節約についての記事を切り抜いて、掲示板に貼っておきました。もう1つ。今朝、電話会社が手違いで回線を止めてしまいましたが、今は元通り使えます。さて、金曜日のボランティアの日についてです。ほとんどの皆さんを当てにできると思っています。参加したい人は教えてください。人数に入れます。忙しい人は、外しておきます。ごめん、ベン、話に割り込むつもりはなかったんだ。続けて。","words":[["cut back our","idioms:2:cut back"],["cut back on","idioms:4:cut back on"],["cut down on","idioms:4:cut down on"],["cut out","idioms:2:cut out"],["cut off","idioms:2:cut off"],["count on","idioms:3:count on"],["count you in","idioms:2:count in"],["count you out","idioms:2:count out"],["cut in","idioms:1:cut in"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has head office reduced?","o":["The number of staff","The printing budget","The travel funds","The phone service"],"a":2,"why":"Head office has cut back our travel funds by thirty percent とある。"},{"q":"What happened this morning?","o":["The phone service was stopped by mistake.","A video call failed.","An article was published.","The board meeting was canceled."],"a":0,"why":"the phone company cut off our service this morning by mistake とある。"},{"q":"What will take place on Friday?","o":["A budget meeting","A flight to head office","A training session","A volunteer day"],"a":3,"why":"about Friday's volunteer day とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0011","page":"idioms","group":["deal","die","do"],"kind":"ラジオの店紹介","text":"Today on Town Talk, we visit Rosa's, a small shop that deals in handmade lace. Owner Rosa Vidal says the craft is dying out, because few young people want to learn it. When she bought the building, it was in poor condition, so she did up the whole ground floor herself. The first window display looked wrong, and she had to do it over twice. Business was slow at first, but complaints about her prices have died down, and customers now come from other cities. Rosa has done away with plastic bags and says she cannot do without her old sewing machine. Her advice for new owners? Learn to deal with problems calmly. We'll be back after this song.","ja":"今日の「タウン・トーク」は、手作りのレースを扱う小さな店「ローザズ」を訪ねます。店主のローザ・ビダルさんによると、習いたがる若者がほとんどいないため、この工芸は廃れつつあるそうです。建物を買ったときは状態が悪かったので、1階全体を自分で改装しました。最初のショーウィンドーの飾り付けはしっくりこず、2回もやり直さなければなりませんでした。はじめは商売も低調でしたが、値段への苦情は静まり、今では他の町からもお客さんが来ます。ローザさんはレジ袋を廃止し、古いミシンなしではやっていけないと話します。新しく店を始める人への助言は何でしょうか。問題には落ち着いて対処できるようになること、だそうです。この曲のあと、また戻ります。","words":[["deals in","idioms:3:deal in"],["dying out","idioms:1:die out"],["did up","idioms:2:do up"],["do it over","idioms:2:do over"],["died down","idioms:1:die down"],["done away with","idioms:4:do away with"],["do without","idioms:3:do without"],["deal with","idioms:3:deal with"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does Rosa's shop sell?","o":["Handmade lace","Sewing machines","Plastic bags","Window displays"],"a":0,"why":"a small shop that deals in handmade lace とある。deal in は「～を商う」。"},{"q":"According to Rosa, why is the craft disappearing?","o":["The materials are too expensive.","Customers prefer other cities.","Few young people want to learn it.","The shop is in poor condition."],"a":2,"why":"the craft is dying out, because few young people want to learn it とある。"},{"q":"What advice does Rosa give to new owners?","o":["Lower their prices","Buy an old building","Use social media","Handle problems calmly"],"a":3,"why":"Learn to deal with problems calmly とある。deal with を handle と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0012","page":"idioms","group":["draw","drop"],"kind":"学校からの留守番電話","text":"Hi, Leo. It's Hannah from the community college. I'm calling about the evening course you asked about. Our lawyers have drawn up the teaching contract, so please drop by my office to sign it. You can also drop off your certificates at the front desk. We hope the course will draw in at least twenty students. Last term, attendance dropped off in winter, and three people dropped out, so we would like you to draw on your business experience to keep the lessons practical. Some students are shy, and a good teacher can draw them out. By the way, the director likes to drop in on new classes, so don't be surprised. Talk soon.","ja":"もしもし、レオ。コミュニティカレッジのハンナです。お問い合わせの夜間講座の件でお電話しました。弁護士が講師契約書を作成しましたので、私の事務室に立ち寄って署名してください。資格証明書は受付に預けていただいてもかまいません。この講座には、少なくとも20人の受講生を集めたいと考えています。前の学期は、冬に出席者が減り、3人が途中でやめてしまいました。ですから、ご自身の実務経験を生かして、実践的な授業にしていただきたいのです。内気な受講生もいますが、良い先生はうまく話を引き出せるものです。ところで、校長は新しい授業をふらりと見に来るのが好きなので、驚かないでくださいね。ではまた。","words":[["drawn up","idioms:2:draw up"],["drop by","idioms:1:drop by"],["drop off your certificates","idioms:2:drop off"],["draw in","idioms:2:draw in"],["dropped off in winter","idioms:1:drop off"],["dropped out","idioms:1:drop out"],["draw on","idioms:3:draw on"],["draw them out","idioms:2:draw out"],["drop in on","idioms:4:drop in on"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should Leo do at Hannah's office?","o":["Pay a course fee","Sign a contract","Meet the students","Collect his certificates"],"a":1,"why":"please drop by my office to sign it とある。it は the teaching contract。"},{"q":"What happened last term?","o":["Twenty students joined.","The director canceled a class.","Attendance fell in winter.","The course fee was raised."],"a":2,"why":"Last term, attendance dropped off in winter, and three people dropped out とある。drop off を fell と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What might the director do?","o":["Visit the class without notice","Teach the first lesson","Change the contract","Interview each student"],"a":0,"why":"the director likes to drop in on new classes とある。drop in on は「ふらりと訪ねる」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0013","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ① 動詞＋副詞（自動詞）","kind":"企業ニュース","text":"In business news, the toy maker Bright Blocks reported its results today. Sales slowed down sharply last year when orders from Europe dried up. Many analysts expected the decline to continue, but demand has now leveled off. The company is trying to bounce back by branching out into video games. Its first game was released in March. Early sales were strong, although they tapered off in the summer. The chief executive admitted that not every new idea will pan out, but she said the company must change to survive. A second game will be released in November, in time for the holiday season. Shares rose three percent on the news.","ja":"ビジネスニュースです。玩具メーカーのブライト・ブロックスが本日、業績を発表しました。昨年は、ヨーロッパからの注文が途絶え、売上が急激に鈍りました。多くの専門家は落ち込みが続くと見ていましたが、現在、需要は横ばいになっています。同社は、テレビゲームへと事業を広げることで立ち直ろうとしています。最初のゲームは3月に発売されました。初めの売れ行きは好調でしたが、夏には次第に減りました。最高経営責任者は、新しい案がすべてうまくいくわけではないと認めつつ、生き残るためには会社が変わらなければならないと述べました。2作目のゲームは、年末商戦に間に合うよう11月に発売されます。この発表を受けて、株価は3パーセント上がりました。","words":[["slowed down","idioms:1:slow down"],["dried up","idioms:1:dry up"],["leveled off","idioms:1:level off"],["bounce back","idioms:1:bounce back"],["branching out","idioms:1:branch out"],["tapered off","idioms:1:taper off"],["pan out","idioms:1:pan out"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did sales slow down last year?","o":["A game was released late.","The holiday season was short.","The share price fell.","Orders from Europe stopped."],"a":3,"why":"Sales slowed down sharply last year when orders from Europe dried up とある。dry up を stopped と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What new area is the company moving into?","o":["Video games","Children's books","Online toy stores","European markets"],"a":0,"why":"by branching out into video games とある。branch out は「事業の範囲を広げる」。"},{"q":"What will happen in November?","o":["The chief executive will retire.","A second game will be released.","Results will be reported.","A factory will open."],"a":1,"why":"A second game will be released in November とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0014","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ① 動詞＋副詞（自動詞）","kind":"交通と天気の情報","text":"Good evening, drivers. Here is the traffic and weather report. The heavy rain is expected to ease off around nine tonight, and the fog should fade away by morning. The tunnel on Highway Six will shut down from midnight to five for cleaning. Tonight's football crowd has left the stadium, so traffic in the north should peter out within the hour. If you are driving a long distance, take a break every two hours. Police say several accidents this month happened when tired drivers dozed off. Finally, fuel prices differ widely across the city this week, so it pays to shop around before you fill your tank. Drive safely.","ja":"運転中の皆さん、こんばんは。交通情報と天気予報です。強い雨は今夜9時ごろには弱まり、霧は朝までに消える見込みです。国道6号線のトンネルは、清掃のため深夜0時から5時まで閉鎖されます。今夜のサッカーの観客はすでにスタジアムを出ましたので、北部の混雑は1時間以内に収まるでしょう。長距離を運転される方は、2時間ごとに休憩を取ってください。警察によると、今月は、疲れたドライバーがうとうとしたことによる事故が何件か起きています。最後に、今週は市内で燃料の値段に大きな差がありますので、給油の前に見て回って比べるのがお得です。安全運転でお願いします。","words":[["ease off","idioms:1:ease off"],["fade away","idioms:1:fade away"],["shut down","idioms:1:shut down"],["peter out","idioms:1:peter out"],["dozed off","idioms:1:doze off"],["shop around","idioms:1:shop around"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen at midnight?","o":["The rain will stop.","A football game will end.","A tunnel will close.","Fuel prices will change."],"a":2,"why":"The tunnel on Highway Six will shut down from midnight to five とある。"},{"q":"According to the police, what caused several accidents this month?","o":["Thick fog","Drivers who fell asleep","Heavy rain","Crowds near the stadium"],"a":1,"why":"several accidents this month happened when tired drivers dozed off とある。doze off を fell asleep と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker advise about fuel?","o":["Compare prices before buying","Buy it before midnight","Avoid stations in the north","Fill the tank every two hours"],"a":0,"why":"it pays to shop around before you fill your tank とある。shop around は「見て回って比較する」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0015","page":"idioms","group":"fall","kind":"プロジェクト会議","text":"Let's talk about the Lisbon office project. I'm sorry to say the plan has almost fallen apart. Our main builder fell behind in March, and now we have also fallen behind with payments to the designer. The first cost estimate fell short of the real figure by twenty percent. I'm afraid we fell for a price that was too good to be true. If the bank loan falls through, we will have to fall back on our savings. Demand for office space has also fallen off this year. The final decision falls on the board, since spending of this size falls under their authority. They meet on the tenth. Please prepare your reports by then.","ja":"リスボン事務所の計画について話しましょう。残念ながら、計画はほとんど崩れかけています。主な建設業者の作業が3月に遅れ、今ではデザイナーへの支払いも遅れています。最初の費用見積もりは、実際の金額に20パーセント届いていませんでした。うますぎる話の価格に、私たちはだまされてしまったようです。銀行の融資がだめになれば、蓄えに頼らざるを得ません。今年はオフィス用スペースの需要も落ち込んでいます。この規模の支出は取締役会の権限に該当するので、最終的な決定の責任は取締役会にかかっています。取締役会は10日に開かれます。それまでに報告書を用意してください。","words":[["fallen apart","idioms:1:fall apart"],["fell behind in March","idioms:1:fall behind"],["fallen behind with","idioms:4:fall behind with"],["fell short of","idioms:4:fall short of"],["fell for","idioms:3:fall for"],["falls through","idioms:1:fall through"],["fall back on","idioms:4:fall back on"],["fallen off","idioms:1:fall off"],["falls on","idioms:3:fall on"],["falls under","idioms:3:fall under"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was the problem with the first cost estimate?","o":["It arrived too late.","It was too low.","It was written by the designer.","It did not include the loan."],"a":1,"why":"The first cost estimate fell short of the real figure by twenty percent とある。実際の額に届かない＝低すぎた。"},{"q":"What will the company do if the bank loan fails?","o":["Cancel the project","Hire a new builder","Sell the office","Use its savings"],"a":3,"why":"If the bank loan falls through, we will have to fall back on our savings とある。fall back on は「（最後の手段に）頼る」。"},{"q":"Who will make the final decision?","o":["The board","The builder","The bank","The designer"],"a":0,"why":"The final decision falls on the board とある。fall on は「（責任が）～にかかる」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0016","page":"idioms","group":["fill","follow","kick"],"kind":"会議前日の連絡","text":"Good morning, everyone. I'm Grace, and I'm filling in for Mr. Ahmed, who is away this week. Our sales conference kicks off at nine tomorrow, and the director will kick off the first session with a short film. Before you arrive, please fill out the online form with your meal choice. Could two volunteers also fill up the water jugs before the first break? Mr. Ahmed asked me to fill you in on one change: the afternoon workshop has moved to room six. Also, I want to follow up on last month's customer survey. We promised faster replies, and we must follow through with that promise. Good ideas mean nothing if we do not follow through. Thank you.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。グレースです。今週不在のアーメドさんの代理を務めます。営業会議は明日9時に始まり、最初の部は、部長が短い映像で開始します。来場前に、オンラインの用紙に食事の希望を記入してください。それから、最初の休憩の前に水差しをいっぱいにしてくれるボランティアを2人お願いできますか。アーメドさんから、変更点を1つ伝えるよう頼まれています。午後のワークショップは第6会議室に移りました。また、先月の顧客アンケートの続きについても取り上げたいと思います。私たちはもっと早い返答を約束しましたから、その約束を最後までやり通さなければなりません。良い案も、やり通さなければ意味がありません。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["filling in for","idioms:4:fill in for"],["kicks off at nine","idioms:1:kick off"],["kick off the first session","idioms:2:kick off"],["fill out","idioms:2:fill out"],["fill up","idioms:2:fill up"],["fill you in","idioms:2:fill in"],["follow up on","idioms:4:follow up on"],["follow through with","idioms:4:follow through with"],["do not follow through","idioms:1:follow through"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is Grace speaking today?","o":["Mr. Ahmed is away.","The director asked her to.","She organized the survey.","She is the new manager."],"a":0,"why":"I'm filling in for Mr. Ahmed, who is away this week とある。fill in for は「～の代理を務める」。"},{"q":"What must the listeners do before arriving tomorrow?","o":["Watch a short film","Bring a water jug","Complete an online form","Book room six"],"a":2,"why":"please fill out the online form with your meal choice とある。fill out を complete と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What has changed?","o":["The date of the conference","The topic of the survey","The time of the first break","The room for the workshop"],"a":3,"why":"the afternoon workshop has moved to room six とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0017","page":"idioms","group":"get","kind":"ラジオの仕事相談","text":"Welcome back to Career Corner. Today's caller asks how to get ahead in a new job. Here is my advice. First, good teams get along, so be friendly to everyone. Second, speak simply. If you cannot get your ideas across in one minute, they are probably too complicated. Third, when your manager criticizes your work, try to understand what she is getting at before you reply. You will make mistakes, but you will get over them. In the first year, you may have a mountain of reading to get through, and you may only just get by on your starting salary. Finally, rest matters. Try to get away for a weekend once a month. More calls after the break.","ja":"「キャリア・コーナー」、番組を続けます。今日の相談は、新しい職場でどうすれば成功できるか、というものです。私の助言はこうです。第一に、良いチームは仲良くやっているものですから、誰にでも感じよく接しましょう。第二に、簡単な言葉で話すこと。自分の考えを1分で伝えられないなら、おそらく複雑すぎます。第三に、上司に仕事を批判されたときは、言い返す前に、相手が何を言おうとしているのかを理解するよう努めましょう。失敗はするでしょうが、乗り越えられます。1年目は、読み終えなければならない資料が山ほどあるかもしれませんし、初任給では何とかやっていくのがやっとかもしれません。最後に、休息も大切です。月に一度は、週末にどこかへ出かけるようにしましょう。休憩のあと、さらに相談をお受けします。","words":[["get ahead","idioms:1:get ahead"],["get along","idioms:1:get along"],["get your ideas across","idioms:2:get across"],["getting at","idioms:3:get at"],["get over","idioms:3:get over"],["get through","idioms:3:get through"],["get by","idioms:1:get by"],["get away","idioms:1:get away"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the caller's question about?","o":["Finding a new job","Succeeding in a new job","Asking for a higher salary","Dealing with a difficult manager"],"a":1,"why":"how to get ahead in a new job とある。get ahead を succeed と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about ideas?","o":["They should be explained briefly.","They should be written down.","They should be shared with a manager first.","They should be tested for a year."],"a":0,"why":"If you cannot get your ideas across in one minute, they are probably too complicated とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker recommend doing once a month?","o":["Reading a new book","Meeting a manager","Taking a short trip","Asking for advice"],"a":2,"why":"Try to get away for a weekend once a month とある。get away は「休みを取って出かける」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0018","page":"idioms","group":"get","kind":"同僚への留守番電話","text":"Hi, Nick. It's Paula. Sorry I didn't get back to you yesterday. I only got through with the audit at eight last night. Listen, we need to get down to work on the Baker report. I know you wanted to get out of writing the finance section, but there is no way to get around it, because you know the numbers best. Last time we handed it in late and got away with it, but the new director is strict. She is easy to get along with, though, so don't worry. I still haven't got around to booking the meeting room, so could you do that? Let's meet at ten tomorrow. Bye.","ja":"もしもし、ニック。ポーラです。昨日は折り返し連絡できなくてごめんなさい。監査をやり終えたのが、昨夜8時になってしまって。ところで、ベイカー社向けの報告書に本腰を入れて取りかからないといけません。財務の部分を書くのを逃れたがっていたのは知っているけれど、避ける方法はありません。数字を一番よく分かっているのはあなただから。前回は提出が遅れてもとがめられずに済んだけれど、新しい部長は厳しい人です。でも、付き合いやすい人だから心配しないで。会議室の予約がまだできていないので、お願いできますか。明日10時に会いましょう。じゃあね。","words":[["get back to","idioms:4:get back to"],["got through with","idioms:4:get through with"],["get down to","idioms:4:get down to"],["get out of","idioms:4:get out of"],["get around it","idioms:3:get around"],["got away with","idioms:4:get away with"],["get along with","idioms:4:get along with"],["got around to","idioms:4:get around to"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Paula not call Nick yesterday?","o":["She was meeting the director.","She forgot his number.","She was out of the office.","She was busy with an audit until late."],"a":3,"why":"I only got through with the audit at eight last night とある。get through with は「～をやり遂げる」。"},{"q":"Why does Paula want Nick to write the finance section?","o":["He knows the numbers best.","He has the most free time.","The director asked for him.","He wrote it last time."],"a":0,"why":"because you know the numbers best とある。"},{"q":"What does Paula ask Nick to do?","o":["Hand in the report today","Reserve a meeting room","Call the new director","Finish the audit"],"a":1,"why":"I still haven't got around to booking the meeting room, so could you do that? とある。book を reserve と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0019","page":"idioms","group":"give","kind":"店長から従業員への話","text":"Thanks for coming in early, everyone. I have a few things to share. First, the old freezer finally gave out last night, and it is giving off a strange smell, so please keep the back door open. Second, this Saturday we will give away free coffee to the first fifty customers. Mia will give out the coupons at the entrance. Third, a customer left a wallet here yesterday. If he returns, please give it back and ask him to sign the book. Now, I know some of you want me to raise wages. I have not given up on the idea, and I will not give in to pressure from head office. But I cannot promise anything yet. Please don't give up hope.","ja":"皆さん、早く来てくれてありがとう。伝えたいことがいくつかあります。まず、古い冷凍庫が昨夜とうとう動かなくなり、変なにおいを出しているので、裏口のドアは開けておいてください。次に、今週の土曜日は、先着50名のお客様に無料でコーヒーを配ります。ミアが入口でクーポンを配ります。3つ目。昨日、お客様が財布を忘れていきました。戻ってこられたら、財布をお返しして、帳簿に署名をお願いしてください。さて、賃上げを望んでいる人がいることは分かっています。私はその考えに見切りをつけてはいませんし、本社からの圧力に屈するつもりもありません。ただ、まだ何も約束はできません。どうか希望を捨てないでください。","words":[["gave out last night","idioms:1:give out"],["giving off","idioms:2:give off"],["give away","idioms:2:give away"],["give out the coupons","idioms:2:give out"],["give it back","idioms:2:give back"],["given up on","idioms:4:give up on"],["give in to","idioms:4:give in to"],["give up hope","idioms:2:give up"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened last night?","o":["A wallet was stolen.","A freezer stopped working.","The back door was left open.","A customer complained."],"a":1,"why":"the old freezer finally gave out last night とある。give out は「動かなくなる」。"},{"q":"What will happen on Saturday?","o":["Wages will be raised.","The store will open early.","A new freezer will arrive.","Free coffee will be offered."],"a":3,"why":"this Saturday we will give away free coffee to the first fifty customers とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about raising wages?","o":["He cannot promise anything yet.","Head office has agreed.","It will happen next month.","He has dropped the idea."],"a":0,"why":"But I cannot promise anything yet とある。考え自体は捨てていない（have not given up on the idea）。"}]},
{"id":"i-0020","page":"idioms","group":"go","kind":"ホテル支配人の朝礼","text":"Good morning, team. Let's go over today's plan. As you know, the fire alarm went off twice last night, and we still do not know what is going on. An engineer will go through every room this morning, so guests on the third floor may go without hot water for an hour. Please go ahead and offer them free breakfast. Next, the owners have decided to go ahead with the new restaurant, which goes against my advice, I must say. Still, I will go along with the decision. Finally, a reminder: as the months go by, small problems grow, so report them quickly. I won't go into details now. Any questions?","ja":"おはようございます、皆さん。今日の予定を確認しましょう。ご存じの通り、昨夜は火災報知器が2回鳴りましたが、何が起きているのかまだ分かっていません。今朝は技術者がすべての部屋をくまなく調べますので、3階のお客様は1時間ほどお湯なしで過ごしていただくことになるかもしれません。どうぞ遠慮なく、無料の朝食をご案内してください。次に、オーナーが新しいレストランの計画を進めることを決めました。正直に言うと、私の助言には反する決定です。それでも、私はその決定に従います。最後に念のため。月日が過ぎるうちに、小さな問題は大きくなります。早めに報告してください。今は詳しいことは述べません。質問はありますか。","words":[["go over","idioms:3:go over"],["went off","idioms:1:go off"],["going on","idioms:1:go on"],["go through","idioms:3:go through"],["go without","idioms:3:go without"],["go ahead and","idioms:1:go ahead"],["go ahead with","idioms:4:go ahead with"],["goes against","idioms:3:go against"],["go along with","idioms:4:go along with"],["go by","idioms:1:go by"],["go into","idioms:3:go into"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened last night?","o":["A guest complained about breakfast.","A restaurant opened.","The hot water stopped.","The fire alarm sounded twice."],"a":3,"why":"the fire alarm went off twice last night とある。go off は「（警報が）鳴る」。"},{"q":"What should the staff offer guests on the third floor?","o":["A room change","A free breakfast","A discount on their stay","A late checkout"],"a":1,"why":"Please go ahead and offer them free breakfast とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the new restaurant?","o":["He disagrees but will accept the decision.","He suggested the idea.","It will open this morning.","The owners have canceled it."],"a":0,"why":"which goes against my advice ... Still, I will go along with the decision とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0021","page":"idioms","group":["go","hand","hang"],"kind":"上司からの留守番電話","text":"Hi, Kenji. It's Mr. Blake. I tried your desk, but you had already hung up. A few things. First, please hand in your sales report by Friday. I will hand out copies at Monday's meeting. Second, I've decided to go for the cheaper printer, which goes with our current system. Third, hang on to the Wilson file. Don't hand it over to anyone, because the family business was handed down from the founder, and the details are private. Also, I know you promised to go through with the Osaka trip. Please don't go back on that, even though our rival went under last week. Do you still go in for golf? Mr. Wilson plays. Hang on, someone is at my door. Don't hang around after six tonight. Go home.","ja":"もしもし、健二。ブレイクです。席に電話したのですが、もう切られていました。いくつか連絡です。まず、販売報告書を金曜日までに提出してください。月曜日の会議で私が写しを配ります。次に、安いほうのプリンターを選ぶことにしました。今のシステムに合うからです。3つ目。ウィルソン社のファイルは手放さないでください。誰にも引き渡してはいけません。あの同族会社は創業者から代々受け継がれてきたもので、内容は内密だからです。それから、大阪出張をやり抜くと約束してくれましたね。先週、競合が倒産しましたが、その約束は破らないでください。今もゴルフはやっていますか。ウィルソンさんはゴルフをするんですよ。ちょっと待って、誰かがドアのところに来ました。今夜は6時以降、ぶらぶら残っていないで、帰ってくださいね。","words":[["hung up","idioms:1:hang up"],["hand in","idioms:2:hand in"],["hand out","idioms:2:hand out"],["go for","idioms:3:go for"],["goes with","idioms:3:go with"],["hang on to","idioms:4:hang on to"],["hand it over","idioms:2:hand over"],["handed down","idioms:2:hand down"],["go through with","idioms:4:go through with"],["go back on","idioms:4:go back on"],["went under","idioms:1:go under"],["go in for","idioms:4:go in for"],["Hang on, someone","idioms:1:hang on"],["hang around","idioms:1:hang around"]],"qs":[{"q":"What must Kenji do by Friday?","o":["Submit a sales report","Buy a printer","Travel to Osaka","Play golf with a client"],"a":0,"why":"please hand in your sales report by Friday とある。hand in を submit と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Why should Kenji not give the Wilson file to anyone?","o":["It has not been finished.","The printer is broken.","Its details are private.","Mr. Wilson asked for it."],"a":2,"why":"Don't hand it over to anyone, because ... the details are private とある。"},{"q":"What happened to a rival company last week?","o":["It bought a new system.","It went out of business.","It moved to Osaka.","It hired the founder."],"a":1,"why":"our rival went under last week とある。go under は「倒産する」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0022","page":"idioms","group":"hold","kind":"記者会見の冒頭","text":"Thank you for waiting, and I'm sorry we held up the start. Please hold on while I read a short statement. As you know, our factory was closed for two days after the flood. Our stock of parts will hold out for about a week. We are holding off the launch of the new model until we are sure it is safe, and the board meeting has been held over until Monday. Some of you have asked whether we held back information from the public. We did not. If the inspection finds a fault, I will hold myself accountable for it. Meanwhile, we are working to hold down costs and to hold on to every job. I will now take questions.","ja":"お待たせしました。開始を遅らせてしまい、申し訳ありません。短い声明を読み上げますので、そのままお待ちください。ご存じの通り、当社の工場は洪水のあと2日間閉鎖されました。部品の在庫は、およそ1週間は持ちこたえます。新モデルの発売は、安全だと確信できるまで延期します。取締役会も月曜日まで延期されました。当社が情報を世間に隠していたのではないか、というご質問をいただいています。そのようなことはしていません。検査で欠陥が見つかった場合は、私がその責任を負います。その間も、私たちは費用を抑え、すべての雇用を守るよう努めています。それでは、ご質問をお受けします。","words":[["held up","idioms:2:hold up"],["hold on while","idioms:1:hold on"],["hold out","idioms:1:hold out"],["holding off","idioms:2:hold off"],["held over","idioms:2:hold over"],["held back","idioms:2:hold back"],["hold myself accountable for","idioms:5:hold A accountable for B"],["hold down","idioms:2:hold down"],["hold on to","idioms:4:hold on to"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why was the factory closed?","o":["There was a fire.","Parts ran out.","There was a flood.","An inspection failed."],"a":2,"why":"our factory was closed for two days after the flood とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the new model?","o":["Its launch has been delayed.","It will be cheaper.","It was damaged.","It has passed inspection."],"a":0,"why":"We are holding off the launch of the new model until we are sure it is safe とある。hold off を delayed と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker promise to do if a fault is found?","o":["Close the factory","Cut jobs","Hold another press conference","Take responsibility"],"a":3,"why":"I will hold myself accountable for it とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0023","page":"idioms","group":"keep","kind":"建設現場の朝礼","text":"Morning, everyone. Before we start, a few safety points. First, keep away from the crane while it is moving, and keep off the wet concrete on level two. Visitors must keep out of the storage area. Second, we are two days ahead of schedule. That is excellent work, so keep it up. To keep up with the plan, we will pour the next floor on Thursday. Third, costs. We must keep them down, so please do not waste materials. Fourth, the wind. Strong wind kept us from working last Friday, and it may return tomorrow. If it does, keep to the indoor tasks on your list. Finally, if you see a problem, keep on reporting it, even if nobody answers at first.","ja":"おはようございます、皆さん。作業の前に、安全についていくつか確認します。1つ目。クレーンが動いている間は近づかないこと、2階のまだ乾いていないコンクリートには立ち入らないこと。来訪者は保管区域に入ってはいけません。2つ目。工程は予定より2日進んでいます。素晴らしい仕事ぶりですので、この調子を保ってください。計画に遅れずについていくために、次の階のコンクリートは木曜日に流し込みます。3つ目は費用です。費用を抑えなければなりませんので、資材を無駄にしないでください。4つ目は風です。先週の金曜日は強風のせいで作業ができませんでしたが、明日また吹くかもしれません。その場合は、一覧にある屋内の作業に専念してください。最後に、問題を見つけたら、最初は誰も応じてくれなくても、報告し続けてください。","words":[["keep away from","idioms:4:keep away from"],["keep off","idioms:3:keep off"],["keep out of","idioms:4:keep out of"],["keep it up","idioms:2:keep up"],["keep up with","idioms:4:keep up with"],["keep them down","idioms:2:keep down"],["kept us from","idioms:5:keep A from B"],["keep to","idioms:3:keep to"],["keep on","idioms:1:keep on"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where must workers not walk?","o":["In the storage area","On the wet concrete","Near the office","On the next floor"],"a":1,"why":"keep off the wet concrete on level two とある。保管区域に入れないのは来訪者。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the schedule?","o":["The work is two days late.","The plan has been canceled.","Thursday's work will be skipped.","The work is ahead of schedule."],"a":3,"why":"we are two days ahead of schedule とある。"},{"q":"What should workers do if strong wind returns tomorrow?","o":["Do the indoor tasks","Go home early","Pour the concrete","Move the crane"],"a":0,"why":"If it does, keep to the indoor tasks on your list とある。keep to は「～から外れない」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0024","page":"idioms","group":["lay","leave","live"],"kind":"経営者の説明","text":"Thank you all for coming. I want to lay out our plans clearly. I will not leave out the bad news. Because of falling orders, we must lay off twenty workers at the Harbor plant. The law lays down strict rules for this, and we will follow every one. Each person will receive three months' pay, which should be enough to live on while looking for work. We have laid aside money for retraining as well. I know some of you feel we have left you behind. We have not. Please leave the details to the personnel team, who will meet each of you this week. This company has not always lived up to its promises, but this time, we will.","ja":"皆さん、お集まりいただきありがとうございます。当社の計画をはっきりと説明したいと思います。悪い知らせも省かずにお話しします。注文の減少により、ハーバー工場で20人の従業員を一時解雇しなければなりません。法律はこれについて厳しい規則を定めており、当社はそのすべてに従います。対象となる方には給与の3か月分をお支払いします。仕事を探す間の生活を支えるには足りるはずです。再訓練のための資金も取ってあります。置き去りにされたと感じている方がいることは承知しています。そのようなことはありません。詳細は人事チームに任せてください。今週、一人ひとりと面談します。この会社は、これまで常に約束に応えてきたわけではありません。しかし今回は、必ず応えます。","words":[["lay out","idioms:2:lay out"],["leave out","idioms:2:leave out"],["lay off","idioms:2:lay off"],["lays down","idioms:2:lay down"],["live on","idioms:3:live on"],["laid aside","idioms:2:lay aside"],["left you behind","idioms:2:leave behind"],["leave the details to","idioms:5:leave A to B"],["lived up to","idioms:4:live up to"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will workers be laid off?","o":["Orders have fallen.","The plant is moving.","A law has changed.","Wages have risen."],"a":0,"why":"Because of falling orders, we must lay off twenty workers とある。"},{"q":"What will each affected worker receive?","o":["A new job at another plant","A letter from the president","Three months' pay","Twenty days of leave"],"a":2,"why":"Each person will receive three months' pay とある。"},{"q":"Who will meet the workers this week?","o":["The plant manager","The personnel team","A lawyer","A retraining teacher"],"a":1,"why":"Please leave the details to the personnel team, who will meet each of you this week とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0025","page":"idioms","group":["let","lose","mark"],"kind":"セール前の店内ミーティング","text":"Good evening, team. Tomorrow is the big sale, so listen carefully. We have marked down all winter coats by forty percent. However, shoes were marked up last week by mistake, so please check each price tag. Doors open at nine. Let the customers in slowly, ten at a time. Last year, we lost out to the store across the street because our doors opened late, and many shoppers lost out on the best items. I will not let that happen again. Please don't let me down. One more thing: do not let out any details of Friday's special offer. I will let you in on the secret tomorrow morning. If the crowd does not let up by noon, I will call in extra staff.","ja":"皆さん、こんばんは。明日は大きなセールですので、よく聞いてください。冬物のコートはすべて40パーセント値下げしました。ただ、靴は先週、手違いで値上げされていましたので、値札を1つずつ確認してください。開店は9時です。お客様は10人ずつ、ゆっくり中へお入れしてください。去年は開店が遅れたせいで、通りの向かいの店に負けてしまい、多くのお客様が一番良い商品を取り逃がしました。同じことは二度と起こさせません。どうか私を失望させないでください。もう1つ。金曜日の特別企画の内容は、決して外に漏らさないでください。その秘密は、明日の朝、皆さんにお教えします。正午になっても混雑が弱まらなければ、追加のスタッフを呼びます。","words":[["marked down","idioms:2:mark down"],["marked up","idioms:2:mark up"],["Let the customers in","idioms:2:let in"],["lost out to","idioms:4:lose out to"],["lost out on","idioms:4:lose out on"],["let me down","idioms:2:let down"],["let out","idioms:2:let out"],["let you in on","idioms:5:let A in on B"],["let up","idioms:1:let up"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the speaker ask the staff to check?","o":["The opening time","The number of customers","The staff schedule","The price tags"],"a":3,"why":"shoes were marked up last week by mistake, so please check each price tag とある。"},{"q":"What went wrong last year?","o":["The doors opened late.","The coats sold out.","The prices were too high.","Too few staff came."],"a":0,"why":"because our doors opened late とある。"},{"q":"What will the speaker do tomorrow morning?","o":["Lower the price of shoes","Tell the staff about a special offer","Open the doors early","Visit the store across the street"],"a":1,"why":"I will let you in on the secret tomorrow morning とある。secret は Friday's special offer の内容。"}]},
{"id":"i-0026","page":"idioms","group":"look","kind":"新任マネージャーのあいさつ","text":"Hello, everyone. I'm Sofia Marin, your new regional manager. I have been looking forward to meeting you. I spent last week looking over your reports, and I must say that business is looking up. Sales in this region have grown for three months. I have always looked up to this team, even when I worked at head office. Some people there look down on small branches, but I never did. I look on each of you as a partner. In return, please look to me for support whenever you need it. This week, I will look into the delivery problems you reported. I am also looking for two volunteers to help train new staff. Looking back on my career, the best ideas always came from people like you.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。新しく地域担当マネージャーになったソフィア・マリンです。皆さんにお会いするのを楽しみにしていました。先週は皆さんの報告書に目を通していましたが、業績は上向いていると言えます。この地域の売上は3か月続けて伸びています。本社で働いていたころから、私はこのチームをずっと尊敬してきました。本社には小さな支店を見下す人もいますが、私は決してそうではありませんでした。私は皆さん一人ひとりをパートナーだと考えています。その代わり、必要なときはいつでも私を頼ってください。今週は、皆さんから報告のあった配送の問題を調査します。また、新人研修を手伝ってくれるボランティアを2人探しています。これまでの経歴を振り返ると、最良の案はいつも皆さんのような方々から生まれました。","words":[["looking forward to","idioms:4:look forward to"],["looking over","idioms:2:look over"],["looking up","idioms:1:look up"],["looked up to","idioms:4:look up to"],["look down on","idioms:4:look down on"],["look on each of you as","idioms:5:look on A as B"],["look to me for","idioms:5:look to A for B"],["look into","idioms:3:look into"],["looking for","idioms:3:look for"],["Looking back on","idioms:4:look back on"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the speaker say about sales in the region?","o":["They have fallen for three months.","They are the lowest in the company.","They have been increasing.","They depend on head office."],"a":2,"why":"Sales in this region have grown for three months とある。直前の business is looking up（上向いている）とも合う。"},{"q":"What will the speaker do this week?","o":["Investigate delivery problems","Return to head office","Close a small branch","Write a report"],"a":0,"why":"This week, I will look into the delivery problems you reported とある。look into を investigate と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What is the speaker looking for?","o":["A new office","Two volunteers","A delivery company","Sales reports"],"a":1,"why":"I am also looking for two volunteers to help train new staff とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0027","page":"idioms","group":["look","give"],"kind":"ボランティアへの説明","text":"Welcome to the city library's guide for new volunteers. Your main job is to look after the children's reading room on weekends. If a visitor asks about a book, look up the title on the computer by the door. If you cannot find it, look through the returns cart, as many books have not been put back yet. Please look out for small children near the stairs. New volunteers often look to Mrs. Hall, our head librarian, when they are unsure, and she is happy to help. One rule: children may ask to borrow more than five books, but please do not give in. Thank you for giving your time.","ja":"市立図書館の、新しいボランティアの皆さんへの説明です。主な仕事は、週末に子ども読書室の世話をすることです。来館者から本について尋ねられたら、ドアのそばのコンピューターで題名を調べてください。見つからない場合は、返却用のカートに目を通してください。まだ棚に戻されていない本がたくさんあるからです。階段の近くにいる小さな子どもには、気をつけてあげてください。新しいボランティアは、迷ったときに図書館長のホールさんを頼ることが多く、ホールさんも喜んで助けてくれます。規則が1つあります。子どもたちが5冊より多く借りたいと頼んでくることがありますが、折れないでください。お時間を割いていただき、ありがとうございます。","words":[["look after","idioms:3:look after"],["look up the title","idioms:2:look up"],["look through","idioms:3:look through"],["look out for","idioms:4:look out for"],["look to","idioms:3:look to"],["give in","idioms:1:give in"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the volunteers' main job?","o":["Putting books back on shelves","Repairing the computer","Taking care of the children's reading room","Teaching children to read"],"a":2,"why":"Your main job is to look after the children's reading room とある。look after を take care of と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Where should volunteers check if a book cannot be found on the computer?","o":["In the returns cart","Near the stairs","At Mrs. Hall's desk","In another library"],"a":0,"why":"If you cannot find it, look through the returns cart とある。"},{"q":"What rule does the speaker mention?","o":["Children must stay away from the door.","Children may not borrow more than five books.","Volunteers must work every weekend.","Volunteers must ask Mrs. Hall first."],"a":1,"why":"children may ask to borrow more than five books, but please do not give in とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0028","page":"idioms","group":"make","kind":"ローカルニュース","text":"In local news, thieves made off with three paintings from the Hillside Gallery early this morning. A second group is believed to have made away with cash from the gift shop. The gallery, which was made over only last year, had new cameras, but the pictures are so dark that police cannot make out the men's faces. The owner said the stolen works make up a third of the collection. Visitors today will have to make do with a smaller exhibition. To make up for the disappointment, tickets will be half price this week. The owner still plans to make the old storeroom into a cafe, and she says good lighting makes for a safer building.","ja":"地元のニュースです。今朝早く、ヒルサイド画廊から泥棒が絵画3点を持ち逃げしました。別のグループが、土産物店から現金を持ち去ったと見られています。昨年改装されたばかりのこの画廊には新しいカメラがありましたが、映像が暗すぎて、警察は男たちの顔を見分けられずにいます。オーナーによると、盗まれた作品は収蔵品の3分の1を占めています。今日の来館者は、規模の小さい展示で間に合わせるしかありません。がっかりさせる埋め合わせとして、今週は入場券が半額になります。オーナーは今も古い倉庫をカフェに作り変える計画で、明るい照明は建物をより安全にするのに役立つと話しています。","words":[["made off with","idioms:4:make off with"],["made away with","idioms:4:make away with"],["made over","idioms:2:make over"],["make out","idioms:2:make out"],["make up a third","idioms:2:make up"],["make do with","idioms:4:make do with"],["make up for","idioms:4:make up for"],["make the old storeroom into","idioms:5:make A into B"],["makes for","idioms:3:make for"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was taken from the gallery?","o":["Three paintings","A camera","The owner's car","Old furniture"],"a":0,"why":"thieves made off with three paintings from the Hillside Gallery とある。"},{"q":"Why are the police unable to identify the thieves?","o":["The cameras were broken.","The men wore masks.","The gallery was closed.","The pictures are too dark."],"a":3,"why":"the pictures are so dark that police cannot make out the men's faces とある。"},{"q":"What is the gallery offering this week?","o":["A free cafe meal","Half-price tickets","A larger exhibition","A talk by the owner"],"a":1,"why":"tickets will be half price this week とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0029","page":"idioms","group":"pass","kind":"追悼のあいさつ","text":"Good afternoon. We are here to remember Walter Simms, who passed away last month at the age of ninety. Walter joined this bakery at sixteen. He once told me that he nearly passed out from the heat on his first day. He never passed up a chance to learn, and by thirty he could pass for a master baker. His recipes were passed down from his grandmother, and he passed them on to three generations of our staff. He also liked to pass on advice: taste everything twice. In a moment, we will pass out copies of his favorite bread recipe. Please take one home, and bake it for someone you love.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。今日は、先月90歳で亡くなったウォルター・シムズさんをしのぶために集まりました。ウォルターさんは16歳でこのパン屋に入りました。初日には暑さで気を失いかけた、と話してくれたことがあります。彼は学ぶ機会を決して逃さず、30歳になるころには、熟練のパン職人として通るほどになっていました。彼のレシピは祖母から受け継いだもので、彼はそれを当店の3世代のスタッフに伝えました。助言を伝えるのも好きでした。「何でも2回味見しなさい」というものです。このあと、彼のお気に入りのパンのレシピの写しをお配りします。どうぞお持ち帰りになって、大切な人のために焼いてください。","words":[["passed away","idioms:1:pass away"],["passed out from","idioms:1:pass out"],["passed up","idioms:2:pass up"],["pass for","idioms:3:pass for"],["passed down","idioms:2:pass down"],["passed them on to","idioms:5:pass A on to B"],["pass on advice","idioms:2:pass on"],["pass out copies","idioms:2:pass out"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the talk?","o":["To open a new bakery","To introduce a master baker","To remember a former employee","To teach a bread recipe"],"a":2,"why":"We are here to remember Walter Simms, who passed away last month とある。"},{"q":"Where did Walter's recipes come from?","o":["A baking school","His first employer","A cookbook","His grandmother"],"a":3,"why":"His recipes were passed down from his grandmother とある。"},{"q":"What will the listeners receive?","o":["Copies of a recipe","A loaf of bread","A photograph of Walter","A bakery discount"],"a":0,"why":"we will pass out copies of his favorite bread recipe とある。pass out は「～を配る」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0030","page":"idioms","group":["pay","pick"],"kind":"友人への留守番電話","text":"Hi, Dana. It's Marcus. Good news: the cafe's sales picked up in December, so I can finally pay you back. I'll transfer the money tomorrow. Your advice about the menu really paid off. By March, I hope to pay off the bank loan as well. I also want to thank you for something else. You picked up on the problem with my supplier before I did. He was picking on my young staff and charging us too much. Now, could you help me pick out new chairs this weekend? I'll pay for lunch. I can pick you up at eleven. Call me back when you get this.","ja":"もしもし、デイナ。マーカスです。良い知らせがあります。12月にカフェの売上が回復したので、やっとお金を返せます。明日、振り込みます。メニューについての助言は、本当に実を結びました。3月までには、銀行の借金も完済したいと思っています。もう1つ、お礼を言いたいことがあります。仕入先の問題に、私より先に気づいてくれましたよね。彼はうちの若いスタッフをいじめて、しかも代金を取りすぎていました。ところで、今週末、新しい椅子を選ぶのを手伝ってもらえませんか。昼ごはんは私がおごります。11時に車で迎えに行けます。これを聞いたら、折り返し電話をください。","words":[["picked up in December","idioms:1:pick up"],["pay you back","idioms:2:pay back"],["paid off","idioms:1:pay off"],["pay off the bank loan","idioms:2:pay off"],["picked up on","idioms:4:pick up on"],["picking on","idioms:3:pick on"],["pick out","idioms:2:pick out"],["pay for","idioms:3:pay for"],["pick you up","idioms:2:pick up"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened in December?","o":["The cafe closed.","Sales improved.","A loan was paid off.","The menu was changed."],"a":1,"why":"the cafe's sales picked up in December とある。pick up を improved と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What problem did Dana notice?","o":["A supplier was charging too much.","The chairs were broken.","The bank made an error.","The staff were arriving late."],"a":0,"why":"You picked up on the problem with my supplier ... charging us too much とある。"},{"q":"What does Marcus ask Dana to do this weekend?","o":["Lend him money","Meet his supplier","Help him choose chairs","Work at the cafe"],"a":2,"why":"could you help me pick out new chairs this weekend? とある。pick out を choose と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0031","page":"idioms","group":"pull","kind":"夕方のニュース","text":"Good evening. The old Royal Theater will not be pulled down after all. Last spring, the main sponsor pulled out of the rescue plan, and many feared the worst. When a second sponsor pulled out in June, the campaign seemed finished. But the town pulled together. Volunteers raised two million dollars in six months, and tonight the mayor confirmed that the theater has pulled through. Organizers admit they did not expect to pull it off. The celebration caused some traffic problems. Dozens of cars pulled up outside the theater, and police asked drivers to pull over on Park Road instead. The theater will reopen with a free concert next Saturday.","ja":"こんばんは。古いロイヤル劇場は、結局、取り壊されないことになりました。昨年の春、主要なスポンサーが救済計画から撤退し、多くの人が最悪の事態を心配しました。6月に2社目のスポンサーが手を引いたときには、運動は終わったかに見えました。しかし、町は力を合わせました。ボランティアが半年で200万ドルを集め、今夜、市長が劇場は危機を乗り切ったと正式に認めました。主催者たちは、やってのけられるとは思っていなかったと打ち明けています。祝賀の集まりで、交通にも少し影響が出ました。数十台の車が劇場の前に止まり、警察は代わりにパーク通りの路肩に寄せるよう運転者に求めました。劇場は来週土曜日、無料コンサートで再開します。","words":[["pulled down","idioms:2:pull down"],["pulled out of","idioms:4:pull out of"],["pulled out in June","idioms:1:pull out"],["pulled together","idioms:1:pull together"],["pulled through","idioms:1:pull through"],["pull it off","idioms:2:pull off"],["pulled up","idioms:1:pull up"],["pull over","idioms:1:pull over"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was announced tonight?","o":["A new sponsor has been found.","The mayor will resign.","The theater will be demolished.","The theater has been saved."],"a":3,"why":"The old Royal Theater will not be pulled down after all、the theater has pulled through とある。"},{"q":"Who raised the money?","o":["Volunteers","The main sponsor","The police","A concert promoter"],"a":0,"why":"Volunteers raised two million dollars in six months とある。"},{"q":"What will happen next Saturday?","o":["A fund-raising dinner","A free concert","A road closure","A vote on the plan"],"a":1,"why":"The theater will reopen with a free concert next Saturday とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0032","page":"idioms","group":"put","kind":"演劇クラブへの連絡","text":"Attention, members of the Riverside Drama Club. This year we will put on a musical in June. Because of repairs to the hall, the first rehearsal has been put off until next Tuesday. The committee has put forward two possible stories, and members may put forth other ideas until Friday. We have put aside five hundred dollars for costumes. Tom's team will put together the stage set this month. After each rehearsal, please put away the chairs and put out all the lights before you leave. Last week, the heater was left on all night. If you would like to help sell tickets, write your name on the list by the door.","ja":"リバーサイド演劇クラブの皆さんにお知らせします。今年は6月にミュージカルを上演します。ホールの修理のため、最初の稽古は来週火曜日まで延期になりました。委員会は2つの物語の候補を提案しており、会員の皆さんは金曜日まで別の案を出すことができます。衣装のために500ドルを取ってあります。舞台装置は、今月トムのチームが組み立てます。稽古が終わるたびに、椅子を片付け、帰る前にすべての明かりを消してください。先週は、暖房が一晩中つけっぱなしでした。チケット販売を手伝ってくださる方は、ドアのそばの名簿に名前を書いてください。","words":[["put on","idioms:2:put on"],["put off","idioms:2:put off"],["put forward","idioms:2:put forward"],["put forth","idioms:2:put forth"],["put aside","idioms:2:put aside"],["put together","idioms:2:put together"],["put away","idioms:2:put away"],["put out","idioms:2:put out"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why has the first rehearsal been delayed?","o":["The story has not been chosen.","The hall is being repaired.","The costumes are not ready.","Tom's team is busy."],"a":1,"why":"Because of repairs to the hall, the first rehearsal has been put off とある。"},{"q":"What will Tom's team do this month?","o":["Sell tickets","Choose the musical","Build the stage set","Buy the costumes"],"a":2,"why":"Tom's team will put together the stage set this month とある。put together を build と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are members asked to do after each rehearsal?","o":["Tidy up and turn off the lights","Write their names on a list","Turn on the heater","Pay five hundred dollars"],"a":0,"why":"please put away the chairs and put out all the lights before you leave とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0033","page":"idioms","group":"put","kind":"電話応対の研修","text":"Welcome to day two of telephone training. Yesterday, several of you said you find angry callers hard to put up with. That is normal. Most people put their anger down to long waiting times, not to you. Here are three rules. First, put down the caller's name and number at once. Second, put your answer across in short, clear sentences. Third, if you cannot help, say that you will put the call through, and put the caller through to a supervisor. Do not simply transfer the call in silence. This afternoon, you will put these rules into practice with real calls. By the way, anyone who wants to put in for the evening shift should see me at lunch.","ja":"電話応対研修の2日目へようこそ。昨日、怒っている相手は我慢しにくい、と話してくれた人が何人かいました。それは普通のことです。ほとんどの人は、怒りの原因は長い待ち時間にあると考えていて、あなた自身のせいだとは思っていません。ルールを3つお伝えします。第一に、相手の名前と電話番号をすぐに書き留めること。第二に、短くはっきりした文で、答えをうまく伝えること。第三に、自分では対応できない場合は、電話をおつなぎしますと伝えたうえで、上司につなぐこと。黙ったまま転送してはいけません。今日の午後は、実際の電話でこのルールを実行に移します。ところで、夜のシフトを申請したい人は、昼休みに私のところへ来てください。","words":[["put up with","idioms:4:put up with"],["put their anger down to","idioms:5:put A down to B"],["put down the caller's name","idioms:2:put down"],["put your answer across","idioms:2:put across"],["put the call through","idioms:2:put through"],["put the caller through to","idioms:5:put A through to B"],["put these rules into","idioms:5:put A into B"],["put in for","idioms:4:put in for"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the training about?","o":["Selling by telephone","Repairing telephones","Writing reports","Handling telephone calls"],"a":3,"why":"telephone training で、怒っている電話の相手への対応のルールを説明している。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, why are most callers angry?","o":["They had to wait a long time.","The staff were rude.","The prices were too high.","Their calls were cut off."],"a":0,"why":"Most people put their anger down to long waiting times とある。put A down to B は「AをBのせいにする」。"},{"q":"What will the trainees do this afternoon?","o":["Meet a supervisor","Practice with real calls","Work the evening shift","Take a written test"],"a":1,"why":"you will put these rules into practice with real calls とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0034","page":"idioms","group":["refer","scale","sell","show"],"kind":"企業ニュース","text":"In business news, the electric car maker Volta, which fans refer to as the green giant, has changed its plans. The company will scale back production of its luxury model and scale up output of its small city car. The first one thousand city cars sold out in a single day. To raise cash, Volta will sell off its battery plant in Texas. The chief executive showed up at yesterday's motor show to show off the new model in person. Asked about job losses, she referred reporters to a written statement. The statement refers to a new training program for workers. Shares in the company rose five percent this morning.","ja":"ビジネスニュースです。ファンから「緑の巨人」と呼ばれている電気自動車メーカーのボルタが、計画を変更しました。同社は高級モデルの生産を縮小し、小型のシティカーの生産を拡大します。最初の1,000台のシティカーは、たった1日で売り切れました。資金を集めるため、ボルタはテキサス州の電池工場を売却します。最高経営責任者は昨日のモーターショーに姿を見せ、新モデルを自ら披露しました。雇用の削減について尋ねられると、記者たちに、書面の声明を見るよう促しました。声明は、従業員向けの新しい研修プログラムに触れています。今朝、同社の株価は5パーセント上がりました。","words":[["refer to as","idioms:5:refer to A as B"],["scale back","idioms:2:scale back"],["scale up","idioms:2:scale up"],["sold out","idioms:1:sell out"],["sell off","idioms:2:sell off"],["showed up","idioms:1:show up"],["show off","idioms:1:show off"],["referred reporters to","idioms:5:refer A to B"],["refers to","idioms:3:refer to"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will Volta increase?","o":["Production of its small car","Production of its luxury model","The number of its plants","The price of its cars"],"a":0,"why":"scale up output of its small city car とある。高級モデルは縮小（scale back）する側。"},{"q":"Why will Volta sell its battery plant?","o":["The plant is too old.","It is moving to Texas.","It wants to raise cash.","Workers went on strike."],"a":2,"why":"To raise cash, Volta will sell off its battery plant in Texas とある。"},{"q":"What does the written statement mention?","o":["A new motor show","A change of chief executive","A fall in share prices","A training program for workers"],"a":3,"why":"The statement refers to a new training program for workers とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0035","page":"idioms","group":"run","kind":"選挙の話題を伝えるニュース","text":"In local politics, Laura Chen announced today that she will run for mayor. Ms. Chen, who owns a chain of bakeries, says she ran into the problems of small businesses every day. She ran through her main ideas this morning. Her campaign has already run up against criticism from the current mayor, who ran down her lack of experience. Ms. Chen replied that the city is running short of time to fix its roads, and that a bus ran over a traffic sign last week because of a hole in the street. Her team admits it may run out of money before the vote, as printing has run up a large bill. A reporter who ran across her old speeches says her views have not changed. The vote takes place when the mayor's term runs out in May.","ja":"地元の政治の話題です。ローラ・チェン氏が本日、市長選に立候補すると発表しました。パン屋のチェーンを経営するチェン氏は、小さな事業者の抱える問題に毎日ぶつかってきたと話しています。今朝は、主な政策をざっと説明しました。チェン氏の陣営はすでに現市長からの批判に直面しており、現市長はチェン氏の経験不足をけなしました。これに対しチェン氏は、市には道路を直すための時間が不足してきており、先週は道路に開いた穴のせいでバスが交通標識をひいてしまった、と応じました。陣営は、印刷で多額の請求が積み上がっているため、投票の前に資金を使い果たすかもしれないと認めています。チェン氏の昔の演説を偶然見つけた記者は、主張は変わっていないと話しています。投票は、市長の任期が切れる5月に行われます。","words":[["run for","idioms:3:run for"],["ran into","idioms:3:run into"],["ran through","idioms:3:run through"],["run up against","idioms:4:run up against"],["ran down","idioms:2:run down"],["running short of","idioms:4:run short of"],["ran over","idioms:3:run over"],["run out of","idioms:4:run out of"],["run up a large bill","idioms:2:run up"],["ran across","idioms:3:run across"],["runs out","idioms:1:run out"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did Laura Chen announce today?","o":["She will be a candidate for mayor.","She will open a new bakery.","She will repair the city's roads.","She will leave politics."],"a":0,"why":"she will run for mayor とある。run for は「～に立候補する」。"},{"q":"What did the current mayor criticize?","o":["Her bakery business","Her old speeches","Her lack of experience","Her printing costs"],"a":2,"why":"the current mayor, who ran down her lack of experience とある。run down は「～をけなす」。"},{"q":"What does Ms. Chen's team admit?","o":["The roads cannot be fixed.","Her views have changed.","The vote will be delayed.","It may not have enough money."],"a":3,"why":"Her team admits it may run out of money before the vote とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0036","page":"idioms","group":["set","step"],"kind":"新規事業の説明会","text":"Good morning. I'd like to set forth our plan for the new delivery service. We set up a small team in January, and they set about studying the market at once. The report they produced sets down three clear goals. First, speed: fast delivery sets us apart from our rivals. Second, cost: we have set aside two million dollars for new vans. Third, safety. A strike at the port set back our schedule by a month, and it also set off a debate about working hours. When winter sets in, deliveries become harder, so we must step up driver training now. If problems appear, I will step in myself. The first vans set out from the depot on Monday, and I will set off with them. As you know, Mr. Ito will step down as director in June.","ja":"おはようございます。新しい配送サービスの計画をご説明します。1月に小さなチームを立ち上げ、チームはすぐに市場の調査に取りかかりました。チームがまとめた報告書は、3つの明確な目標を定めています。第一に速さです。配送の速さが、当社を競合から際立たせます。第二に費用です。新しいバンのために200万ドルを取ってあります。第三に安全です。港でのストライキによって日程は1か月遅れ、労働時間についての議論も引き起こされました。冬が本格的に始まると配送は難しくなりますので、今のうちに運転手の研修を強化しなければなりません。問題が起きた場合は、私が自ら介入します。最初のバンは月曜日に車庫を出発し、私も一緒に出発します。ご存じの通り、伊藤さんは6月に部長を退任します。","words":[["set forth","idioms:2:set forth"],["set up","idioms:2:set up"],["set about","idioms:3:set about"],["sets down","idioms:2:set down"],["sets us apart from","idioms:5:set A apart from B"],["set aside","idioms:2:set aside"],["set back","idioms:2:set back"],["set off a debate","idioms:2:set off"],["sets in","idioms:1:set in"],["step up","idioms:2:step up"],["step in","idioms:1:step in"],["set out","idioms:1:set out"],["set off with","idioms:1:set off"],["step down","idioms:1:step down"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the talk mainly about?","o":["A strike at the port","A plan for a new delivery service","A change of office","A report on working hours"],"a":1,"why":"I'd like to set forth our plan for the new delivery service とある。"},{"q":"What delayed the schedule by a month?","o":["Bad winter weather","A shortage of vans","A lack of drivers","A strike at the port"],"a":3,"why":"A strike at the port set back our schedule by a month とある。set back は「～を遅らせる」。"},{"q":"What will happen in June?","o":["A director will leave his position.","The first vans will leave.","Driver training will end.","The team will be set up."],"a":0,"why":"Mr. Ito will step down as director in June とある。step down は「辞任する」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0037","page":"idioms","group":["settle","sign","wear"],"kind":"新居に移った友人への留守番電話","text":"Hi, Ben. It's Olivia. I hope you are settling down well in the new town. I wanted to tell you that I finally settled on a house. It is smaller than I wanted, but I decided to settle for it because the location is perfect. The bank must sign off on the loan this week. Oh, and I have signed up for the Spanish class you recommended. There is a sign-up sheet at the library, so you could sign up too. I must say, the excitement of moving wore off quickly, and packing has worn me out. One more thing: I still owe you for the concert tickets. Let me settle up with you on Saturday. Call me.","ja":"もしもし、ベン。オリビアです。新しい町での暮らしに、うまく落ち着けているといいのですが。お伝えしたかったのは、やっと家を決めたということです。希望より小さいのですが、場所が申し分ないので、これで妥協することにしました。今週、銀行に融資を承認してもらわなければなりません。そうそう、すすめてくれたスペイン語の講座に申し込みました。図書館に申込用紙があるので、あなたも申し込めますよ。正直に言うと、引っ越しのわくわくした気持ちはすぐに薄れてしまい、荷造りですっかり疲れ果てました。もう1つ。コンサートのチケット代をまだ返していませんでしたね。土曜日に清算させてください。電話をください。","words":[["settling down","idioms:1:settle down"],["settled on","idioms:3:settle on"],["settle for","idioms:3:settle for"],["sign off on","idioms:4:sign off on"],["signed up for","idioms:4:sign up for"],["sign up too","idioms:1:sign up"],["wore off","idioms:1:wear off"],["worn me out","idioms:2:wear out"],["settle up with","idioms:4:settle up with"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Olivia choose the house?","o":["It is large.","It is cheap.","It is in a perfect location.","It is near the bank."],"a":2,"why":"I decided to settle for it because the location is perfect とある。settle for は「～で妥協する」。"},{"q":"What has Olivia registered for?","o":["A Spanish class","A library card","A moving service","A concert"],"a":0,"why":"I have signed up for the Spanish class you recommended とある。"},{"q":"What does Olivia want to do on Saturday?","o":["Visit the library","Pay Ben what she owes","Start packing","See the new town"],"a":1,"why":"I still owe you for the concert tickets. Let me settle up with you on Saturday とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0038","page":"idioms","group":["stand","speak","stick"],"kind":"市民集会での発言","text":"Thank you for letting me speak. My name is Rita Gomez, and I have lived on Mill Road for thirty years. I am here to speak out against the plan to close our library. I do not stand out as a public speaker, so tell me to speak up if you cannot hear. The council says the building costs too much. But a library stands for equal chances for everyone. Some officials would rather stand by and watch, but we will stand up to this decision and stand up for our children. I will stick to the facts tonight, and I ask the council to stand by its promise of last year. If the committee head cannot do that, he should stand down. Our teachers stick up for this library, and Mr. Lee is standing in for them tonight.","ja":"発言の機会をいただき、ありがとうございます。リタ・ゴメスと申します。ミル通りに30年住んでいます。今日は、私たちの図書館を閉鎖する計画に、はっきり反対を表明するために来ました。人前で話すのが目立って上手なわけではありませんので、聞こえないときは、もっと大きな声でと言ってください。議会は、建物に費用がかかりすぎると言います。しかし図書館は、誰にでも平等な機会があることを表しています。傍観して眺めているほうがよいという役人もいますが、私たちはこの決定に立ち向かい、子どもたちを守ります。今夜、私は事実だけを述べます。そして議会には、昨年の約束を守るよう求めます。委員長にそれができないのなら、辞任すべきです。先生方はこの図書館を擁護しており、今夜はリーさんが先生方の代理を務めています。","words":[["speak out against","idioms:4:speak out against"],["stand out","idioms:1:stand out"],["speak up","idioms:1:speak up"],["stands for","idioms:3:stand for"],["stand by and watch","idioms:1:stand by"],["stand up to","idioms:4:stand up to"],["stand up for","idioms:4:stand up for"],["stick to","idioms:3:stick to"],["stand by its promise","idioms:3:stand by"],["stand down","idioms:1:stand down"],["stick up for","idioms:4:stick up for"],["standing in for","idioms:4:stand in for"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the speaker at the meeting?","o":["To apply for a job at the library","To thank the council","To ask for a new road","To oppose the closing of a library"],"a":3,"why":"I am here to speak out against the plan to close our library とある。"},{"q":"According to the council, what is the problem with the building?","o":["It is too small.","It costs too much.","It is too old.","It is far from Mill Road."],"a":1,"why":"The council says the building costs too much とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker ask the council to do?","o":["Keep its promise","Build a larger library","Hire more teachers","Lower local taxes"],"a":0,"why":"I ask the council to stand by its promise of last year とある。stand by は「（約束を）守る」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0039","page":"idioms","group":"take","kind":"同僚との雑談","text":"Hi, Greg. How was the flight? I heard the plane took off two hours late. Listen, I want to ask you about the new intern. Everyone says she takes after her father, the famous designer. At first, I took her for a customer because she was so quiet. But she really took to the work. Yesterday, she took apart the old printer and repaired it in an hour. I was completely taken in by her modest manner, because she knows more than I do. I said something rude last week, and I'd like to take it back. I was tired and took my bad mood out on her. Anyway, she offered to teach me the new software, and I think I'll take her up on that. Could you introduce us properly?","ja":"やあ、グレッグ。フライトはどうだった。飛行機の離陸が2時間遅れたと聞いたよ。ところで、新しいインターンについて聞きたいんだ。皆が、彼女は有名なデザイナーの父親に似ていると言っている。とても物静かだったから、最初はお客さんだと思い込んでしまった。でも、彼女は仕事がすっかり気に入ったようだ。昨日は古いプリンターを分解して、1時間で直してしまった。控えめな態度にすっかりだまされたよ。私よりずっと詳しいんだから。先週、失礼なことを言ってしまったので、撤回したいんだ。疲れていて、機嫌の悪さを彼女にぶつけてしまった。とにかく、彼女が新しいソフトを教えようかと申し出てくれたので、その申し出に応じようと思う。きちんと紹介してもらえないかな。","words":[["took off","idioms:1:take off"],["takes after","idioms:3:take after"],["took her for","idioms:5:take A for B"],["took to","idioms:3:take to"],["took apart","idioms:2:take apart"],["taken in","idioms:2:take in"],["take it back","idioms:2:take back"],["took my bad mood out on","idioms:5:take A out on B"],["take her up on","idioms:5:take A up on B"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the speaker first think about the intern?","o":["She was a customer.","She was a designer.","She was a pilot.","She was a repair worker."],"a":0,"why":"At first, I took her for a customer とある。take A for B は「AをBだと思い込む」。"},{"q":"What did the intern do yesterday?","o":["She designed some software.","She arrived two hours late.","She repaired a printer.","She met a famous designer."],"a":2,"why":"she took apart the old printer and repaired it in an hour とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker plan to do?","o":["Buy a new printer","Accept the intern's offer","Take a later flight","Change the software"],"a":1,"why":"she offered to teach me the new software, and I think I'll take her up on that とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0040","page":"idioms","group":["talk","think","wind"],"kind":"起業セミナーの締めくくり","text":"We are winding down now, so let me finish with one story. Ten years ago, I had a safe job at a bank. A friend tried to talk me into opening a cafe with her. My parents tried to talk me out of it. I asked for a week to think it over. During that week, we thought up a simple idea: coffee and books in one room. I did not think of myself as a business owner, but I said yes. If I had refused, I might have wound up regretting it for the rest of my life. So, talk over your idea with people you trust, and then decide. Let's wind up today's session here. Thank you for coming.","ja":"そろそろ終わりに近づいてきましたので、最後に1つ話をさせてください。10年前、私は銀行で安定した仕事に就いていました。ある友人が、一緒にカフェを開こうと私を説得しようとしました。両親は、やめるよう私を説得しようとしました。私は、じっくり考えるために1週間ほしいと頼みました。その1週間の間に、私たちは単純な案を考え出しました。1つの部屋にコーヒーと本を置く、というものです。私は自分を事業主だとは考えていませんでしたが、やると答えました。もし断っていたら、結局、一生後悔することになっていたかもしれません。ですから、信頼できる人と自分の案について話し合い、そのうえで決めてください。今日の講座はここで終わりにしましょう。お越しいただき、ありがとうございました。","words":[["winding down","idioms:1:wind down"],["talk me into","idioms:5:talk A into B"],["talk me out of","idioms:5:talk A out of B"],["think it over","idioms:2:think over"],["thought up","idioms:2:think up"],["think of myself as","idioms:5:think of A as B"],["wound up regretting","idioms:1:wind up"],["talk over","idioms:2:talk over"],["wind up today's session","idioms:2:wind up"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where did the speaker work ten years ago?","o":["At a cafe","At a bookstore","At a school","At a bank"],"a":3,"why":"Ten years ago, I had a safe job at a bank とある。"},{"q":"What did the speaker's parents do?","o":["They tried to stop her.","They lent her money.","They opened a cafe.","They thought up the idea."],"a":0,"why":"My parents tried to talk me out of it とある。talk A out of B は「AにBをやめるよう説得する」。"},{"q":"What advice does the speaker give?","o":["Keep a safe job","Discuss your idea with people you trust","Decide within a week","Never borrow from a bank"],"a":1,"why":"talk over your idea with people you trust, and then decide とある。talk over を discuss と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0041","page":"idioms","group":"turn","kind":"ラジオのインタビュー紹介","text":"My guest today is Carlos Rivera, the man who turned a failing bus company into a success. When he arrived, the firm was losing money, and the owner was ready to turn it over to the bank. Carlos turned down a safer job to take the position. He turned to the drivers for ideas, and many good ones turned up. It turned out that passengers wanted cleaner buses, not cheaper tickets. Within two years, he had turned the company around, and losses turned into profits. Customers who had turned away from public transport came back. Carlos never turns away a visitor, and he still drives one route himself. Later, he will explain why he turned in his company car. First, the news.","ja":"今日のゲストは、経営難のバス会社を成功へと変えた人物、カルロス・リベラさんです。彼が着任したとき、会社は赤字で、オーナーは会社を銀行に引き渡すつもりでいました。カルロスさんは、もっと安定した仕事を断って、この職に就きました。彼は運転手たちに案を求め、良い案がたくさん出てきました。乗客が求めていたのは安い運賃ではなく、きれいなバスだということが分かったのです。2年のうちに、彼は会社を立て直し、赤字は黒字に変わりました。公共交通機関に背を向けていた人たちが、戻ってきました。カルロスさんは訪ねてくる人を決して追い返さず、今でも自ら1つの路線を運転しています。このあと、彼がなぜ社用車を返却したのかを話してくれます。その前に、ニュースです。","words":[["turned a failing bus company into","idioms:5:turn A into B"],["turn it over to","idioms:5:turn A over to B"],["turned down","idioms:2:turn down"],["turned to","idioms:3:turn to"],["turned up","idioms:1:turn up"],["turned out","idioms:1:turn out"],["turned the company around","idioms:2:turn around"],["turned into profits","idioms:3:turn into"],["turned away from","idioms:4:turn away from"],["turns away","idioms:2:turn away"],["turned in","idioms:2:turn in"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was the situation when Carlos arrived?","o":["The buses were new.","The drivers were on strike.","The company was losing money.","The bank had closed."],"a":2,"why":"When he arrived, the firm was losing money とある。"},{"q":"What did passengers want?","o":["Cleaner buses","Cheaper tickets","More routes","Faster service"],"a":0,"why":"It turned out that passengers wanted cleaner buses, not cheaper tickets とある。"},{"q":"What will Carlos explain later?","o":["Why he drives a bus","Why he refused a job","Why he sold the company","Why he gave back his company car"],"a":3,"why":"he will explain why he turned in his company car とある。turn in を gave back と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0042","page":"idioms","group":["turn","work","wrap"],"kind":"上司から部下への留守番電話","text":"Hi, Amy. It's Robert. I'm about to turn in for the night, but I wanted to call first. Please turn over the last page of the contract and check the date. Then, could you work out the total cost for me? I've been working on the figures all day, and I hope everything will work out. As you know, I work for a demanding client, and we are working toward a deadline on Friday. I usually work off stress at the gym, but tonight I am too tired. Tomorrow, the factory will turn out the first samples. During the visit, please turn down the volume of the radio, and do not turn up the heating. Start with easy questions and work up to the difficult ones. Let's wrap up the report by noon. The visit should wrap up at three.","ja":"もしもし、エイミー。ロバートです。もう寝るところなのですが、その前に電話しておきたくて。契約書の最後のページをめくって、日付を確認してください。それから、総費用を計算してもらえますか。私は一日中その数字に取り組んでいたので、すべてうまくいくよう願っています。ご存じの通り、私は要求の厳しい顧客のために働いていて、金曜日の締め切りを目指して進めているところです。いつもはジムで運動してストレスを解消するのですが、今夜は疲れすぎています。明日、工場が最初の見本を生産します。訪問の間は、ラジオの音量を下げ、暖房は強くしないでください。簡単な質問から始めて、難しいものへと徐々に進めましょう。報告書は正午までに仕上げましょう。訪問は3時に終わる見込みです。","words":[["turn in for the night","idioms:1:turn in"],["turn over","idioms:2:turn over"],["work out the total cost","idioms:2:work out"],["working on","idioms:3:work on"],["will work out","idioms:1:work out"],["work for","idioms:3:work for"],["working toward","idioms:3:work toward"],["work off","idioms:2:work off"],["turn out the first samples","idioms:2:turn out"],["turn down the volume","idioms:2:turn down"],["turn up the heating","idioms:2:turn up"],["work up to","idioms:4:work up to"],["wrap up the report","idioms:2:wrap up"],["should wrap up at three","idioms:1:wrap up"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does Robert ask Amy to calculate?","o":["The total cost","The number of samples","The length of the visit","The date of the contract"],"a":0,"why":"could you work out the total cost for me? とある。work out を calculate と言い換えている。"},{"q":"When is the deadline?","o":["Tonight","Tomorrow at noon","On Friday","At three o'clock"],"a":2,"why":"we are working toward a deadline on Friday とある。"},{"q":"What will the factory do tomorrow?","o":["Close for the day","Produce the first samples","Repair the heating","Send the contract"],"a":1,"why":"Tomorrow, the factory will turn out the first samples とある。turn out を produce と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0043","page":"idioms","group":["write","opt","bear"],"kind":"年金制度のお知らせ","text":"Good afternoon. This is a reminder about the company pension plan. Starting next month, all staff will join the new plan automatically. If you prefer the old one, you may opt out by filling in form B. So far, most people have opted for the new plan, and the numbers bear out our view that it offers better value. If you opt out of both plans, please write down your reasons on the form, because the personnel office must write up a report for the board. One more point: the bank has agreed to write off the small fees charged in error last year. Our website is slow today, so please bear with us.","ja":"こんにちは。会社の年金制度についての再度のお知らせです。来月から、全従業員が自動的に新しい制度に加入します。これまでの制度のほうがよい場合は、用紙Bに記入すれば、新制度への加入をやめることができます。今のところ大半の人が新しい制度を選んでおり、その数字は、新制度のほうが得だという当社の見方を裏付けています。どちらの制度からも外れる場合は、用紙に理由を書き留めてください。人事課が取締役会向けの報告書を文書にまとめなければならないからです。もう1点。昨年、誤って請求された少額の手数料について、銀行が帳消しにすることに同意しました。本日はウェブサイトの動きが遅くなっていますので、どうかご辛抱ください。","words":[["opt out by","idioms:1:opt out"],["opted for","idioms:3:opt for"],["bear out","idioms:2:bear out"],["opt out of","idioms:4:opt out of"],["write down","idioms:2:write down"],["write up","idioms:2:write up"],["write off","idioms:2:write off"],["bear with","idioms:3:bear with"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen next month?","o":["Staff will join the new plan automatically.","The old plan will end.","Fees will be charged.","The board will meet."],"a":0,"why":"Starting next month, all staff will join the new plan automatically とある。"},{"q":"What must employees who leave both plans do?","o":["Visit the bank","Attend a board meeting","Give their reasons in writing","Pay a small fee"],"a":2,"why":"If you opt out of both plans, please write down your reasons on the form とある。"},{"q":"What has the bank agreed to do?","o":["Open a new branch","Cancel fees that were charged by mistake","Lend money to staff","Repair the website"],"a":1,"why":"the bank has agreed to write off the small fees charged in error last year とある。write off を cancel、in error を by mistake と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0044","page":"idioms","group":["phase","root","trade","adapt"],"kind":"運転手への連絡","text":"Attention, all drivers. As you know, the company will phase out its diesel vans this year and phase in electric models. From Monday, you can trade in your old van at the depot. Many of you have asked whether you can trade your van for a larger model. The answer is yes, if your route requires it. We know it takes time to adapt to a new vehicle, so trainers will adapt the lessons to your experience. We are also working to root out the charging problems reported last month. Finally, our depot team has reached the final of the city safety contest. Please come and root for them on Saturday.","ja":"運転手の皆さんにお知らせします。ご存じの通り、当社は今年、ディーゼルのバンを段階的に廃止し、電気自動車を段階的に導入します。月曜日から、車庫で古いバンを下取りに出すことができます。今のバンを大きな車種と交換できるか、という質問を多くいただいています。担当の路線で必要であれば、できます。新しい車に慣れるには時間がかかりますので、指導員が皆さんの経験に合わせて講習の内容を調整します。先月報告のあった充電の不具合も、根本からなくすよう取り組んでいます。最後に、車庫のチームが市の安全コンテストの決勝に進みました。土曜日は、ぜひ応援に来てください。","words":[["phase out","idioms:2:phase out"],["phase in","idioms:2:phase in"],["trade in","idioms:2:trade in"],["trade your van for","idioms:5:trade A for B"],["adapt to","idioms:3:adapt to"],["adapt the lessons to","idioms:5:adapt A to B"],["root out","idioms:2:root out"],["root for","idioms:3:root for"]],"qs":[{"q":"What vehicles will the company stop using?","o":["Electric vans","Large trucks","Company cars","Diesel vans"],"a":3,"why":"the company will phase out its diesel vans this year とある。phase out を stop using と言い換えている。"},{"q":"When can a driver get a larger model?","o":["When the route requires it","After one year of driving","After passing a test","When the depot is full"],"a":0,"why":"The answer is yes, if your route requires it とある。"},{"q":"What will take place on Saturday?","o":["A training lesson","The final of a safety contest","The delivery of new vans","A meeting about charging"],"a":1,"why":"our depot team has reached the final of the city safety contest. Please come and root for them on Saturday とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0045","page":"idioms","group":["apply","consist","correspond","impose"],"kind":"大学の説明会","text":"Welcome to the open day at Lakeview College. Let me explain how to apply for our business course. The course consists of twelve units, and each unit corresponds to one month of study. In my view, good teaching consists in linking ideas to real work, so you will apply each theory to a real company. These rules apply to both full-time and evening students. We do not impose a heavy workload on new students in the first term. Each student also corresponds with a mentor from a local firm by email. I don't wish to impose on your time, so I will stop here. Forms are on the table.","ja":"レイクビュー大学の公開説明会へようこそ。ビジネス課程への申し込み方法をご説明します。課程は12の単元から成り、1つの単元が1か月の学習に相当します。私の考えでは、良い教育の本質は、考え方を実際の仕事と結びつけることにあります。そのため、皆さんには1つひとつの理論を実在の会社に当てはめてもらいます。これらの決まりは、全日制と夜間の学生の両方に当てはまります。最初の学期は、新入生に重い課題を課すことはしません。また、学生は一人ひとり、地元企業の指導役とメールでやり取りします。皆さんのお時間を取りすぎたくありませんので、ここで終わりにします。用紙はテーブルにあります。","words":[["apply for","idioms:3:apply for"],["consists of","idioms:3:consist of"],["corresponds to","idioms:3:correspond to"],["consists in","idioms:3:consist in"],["apply each theory to","idioms:5:apply A to B"],["apply to both","idioms:3:apply to"],["impose a heavy workload on","idioms:5:impose A on B"],["corresponds with","idioms:3:correspond with"],["impose on your time","idioms:3:impose on"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the talk?","o":["To introduce a new teacher","To describe a local company","To explain how to apply for a course","To collect course fees"],"a":2,"why":"Let me explain how to apply for our business course とある。"},{"q":"How many units does the course have?","o":["Twelve","Two","Six","Twenty"],"a":0,"why":"The course consists of twelve units とある。"},{"q":"What does each student do with a mentor?","o":["Meets every month","Works at the same company","Shares a classroom","Exchanges emails"],"a":3,"why":"Each student also corresponds with a mentor from a local firm by email とある。correspond with は「～とやり取りする」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0046","page":"idioms","group":["inquire","provide","result","succeed"],"kind":"水道会社からのお知らせ","text":"This is a message for customers of Northern Water. Many of you have called to inquire about last week's service failure. The problem resulted from a broken pump, and it resulted in three days without water for two thousand homes. An independent team will inquire into the cause. Meanwhile, we are providing bottled water for all affected families, and we will provide each household with a refund of fifty dollars. Our contract provides for such payments. Engineers succeeded in repairing the pump last night. Finally, Ms. Jane Holt has succeeded to the position of director, following Mr. Park's retirement. She will write to every customer this week.","ja":"ノーザン水道をご利用のお客様へのお知らせです。先週の給水停止について、多くのお問い合わせをいただいています。この問題はポンプの故障に起因するもので、その結果、2,000世帯で3日間水が出ない状態になりました。原因については、独立したチームが調査します。その間、影響を受けたすべてのご家庭にペットボトルの水をお届けしており、各世帯に50ドルを返金いたします。当社の契約には、こうした支払いについての定めがあります。技術者は昨夜、ポンプの修理に成功しました。最後に、パーク氏の退職に伴い、ジェーン・ホルト氏が所長の職を継ぎました。ホルト氏は今週、すべてのお客様に書面でご連絡します。","words":[["inquire about","idioms:3:inquire about"],["resulted from","idioms:3:result from"],["resulted in","idioms:3:result in"],["inquire into","idioms:3:inquire into"],["providing bottled water for","idioms:5:provide A for B"],["provide each household with","idioms:5:provide A with B"],["provides for","idioms:3:provide for"],["succeeded in","idioms:3:succeed in"],["succeeded to","idioms:3:succeed to"]],"qs":[{"q":"What caused the service failure?","o":["A broken pump","Heavy rain","A power cut","A staff shortage"],"a":0,"why":"The problem resulted from a broken pump とある。result from は「～に起因する」。"},{"q":"What will each household receive?","o":["A new water meter","A visit from an engineer","A fifty-dollar refund","Free water for a year"],"a":2,"why":"we will provide each household with a refund of fifty dollars とある。"},{"q":"Who is the new director?","o":["Mr. Park","Ms. Holt","An independent engineer","A customer representative"],"a":1,"why":"Ms. Jane Holt has succeeded to the position of director とある。succeed to は「～を継ぐ」。パーク氏は退職した側。"}]},
{"id":"i-0047","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ④ 動詞＋副詞＋前置詞","kind":"ビジネス番組","text":"Welcome to Business Week. Our topic today is online shopping. In the end, success in this market boils down to trust. Last year, several firms tried to cash in on the holiday season with huge discounts, but their service did not measure up to their promises. Thousands of customers missed out on their gifts. Only one company owned up to its mistakes and paid everyone back. Now the government plans to crack down on false advertising. My advice to shoppers is simple. Read up on a store before you buy. And my advice to companies? Face up to your problems early, before your customers leave. We'll take your calls after the break.","ja":"「ビジネス・ウィーク」へようこそ。今日のテーマはネット通販です。結局のところ、この市場での成功は「信頼」に行き着きます。昨年、いくつかの会社が大幅な値引きで年末商戦に乗じてもうけようとしましたが、サービスは約束した水準に達していませんでした。何千人ものお客が、贈り物を受け取り損ねました。過ちを認めて全員に返金したのは、1社だけでした。現在、政府は虚偽の広告を厳しく取り締まる計画です。買い物をする方への私の助言は単純です。買う前に、その店について調べておきましょう。では、会社への助言は何でしょうか。お客が離れる前に、早めに問題を直視することです。休憩のあと、皆さんからのお電話をお受けします。","words":[["boils down to","idioms:4:boil down to"],["cash in on","idioms:4:cash in on"],["measure up to","idioms:4:measure up to"],["missed out on","idioms:4:miss out on"],["owned up to","idioms:4:own up to"],["crack down on","idioms:4:crack down on"],["Read up on","idioms:4:read up on"],["Face up to","idioms:4:face up to"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is today's topic?","o":["Holiday travel","Government spending","Advertising jobs","Online shopping"],"a":3,"why":"Our topic today is online shopping とある。"},{"q":"What does the government plan to do?","o":["Take strict action against false advertising","Lower prices during the holidays","Give refunds to shoppers","Close online stores"],"a":0,"why":"the government plans to crack down on false advertising とある。crack down on は「厳しく取り締まる」。"},{"q":"What does the speaker advise shoppers to do?","o":["Wait for larger discounts","Research a store before buying","Call the program","Shop only during the holidays"],"a":1,"why":"Read up on a store before you buy とある。read up on を research と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0048","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ④ 動詞＋副詞＋前置詞","kind":"大雪への備え","text":"Good morning. A major snowstorm will reach the city tonight. Here is some advice from the emergency office. First, stock up on food and water for three days. Second, steer clear of the river road, which freezes quickly, and watch out for fallen power lines. Third, do not shy away from asking for help. The city has teamed up with local taxi companies to carry elderly residents to shelters for free. Volunteers, please do not walk out on your shift early, because we are short of staff. Our reporters will zero in on the worst areas throughout the night. Keep your radio on, and stay safe.","ja":"おはようございます。今夜、大きな吹雪が市内に到達します。防災担当からの助言をお伝えします。第一に、3日分の食料と水を買いだめしておいてください。第二に、すぐに凍る川沿いの道は避け、切れて落ちた電線に注意してください。第三に、助けを求めることをためらわないでください。市は地元のタクシー会社と協力し、高齢の住民を無料で避難所へ運んでいます。ボランティアの皆さん、人手が足りませんので、担当の時間の途中で持ち場を離れないでください。当局の記者が、夜通し、被害の大きい地域に的を絞ってお伝えします。ラジオはつけたままにして、安全にお過ごしください。","words":[["stock up on","idioms:4:stock up on"],["steer clear of","idioms:4:steer clear of"],["watch out for","idioms:4:watch out for"],["shy away from","idioms:4:shy away from"],["teamed up with","idioms:4:team up with"],["walk out on","idioms:4:walk out on"],["zero in on","idioms:4:zero in on"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen tonight?","o":["The river will flood.","A snowstorm will arrive.","The power will be cut.","Shelters will close."],"a":1,"why":"A major snowstorm will reach the city tonight とある。"},{"q":"Which road should people avoid?","o":["The road to the shelters","The main highway","The river road","The road near the emergency office"],"a":2,"why":"steer clear of the river road, which freezes quickly とある。steer clear of は「～を避ける」。"},{"q":"What is being offered for free?","o":["Taxi rides for elderly residents","Food and water","Radios","Winter clothing"],"a":0,"why":"to carry elderly residents to shelters for free とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0049","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ② 動詞＋副詞（他動詞）","kind":"航空会社のニュース","text":"In business news, the government has refused to bail out the airline Sky East for a second time. Instead, a group of investors plans to buy out the current owners. Fuel costs have driven up ticket prices this year, and the airline has tried to drum up business with cheap weekend flights. Staff say they can barely eke out a living after last year's pay cuts. The new owners promise to beef up safety checks and to cross out the most unpopular routes from the timetable. They have also dreamed up a new name for the company, which will be announced on Friday. We'll have more after the weather.","ja":"ビジネスニュースです。政府は、航空会社スカイ・イーストを再び救済することを拒否しました。その代わりに、投資家のグループが現在の所有者から会社を買い取る計画です。今年は燃料費が航空券の価格を押し上げており、同社は週末の格安便で懸命に客を集めようとしてきました。従業員は、昨年の賃金カットのあと、かろうじて生計を立てている状態だと話しています。新しい所有者は、安全点検を強化し、最も人気のない路線を時刻表から消すと約束しています。また、会社の新しい名前も考え出しており、金曜日に発表されます。天気予報のあと、さらに詳しくお伝えします。","words":[["bail out","idioms:2:bail out"],["buy out","idioms:2:buy out"],["driven up","idioms:2:drive up"],["drum up","idioms:2:drum up"],["eke out","idioms:2:eke out"],["beef up","idioms:2:beef up"],["cross out","idioms:2:cross out"],["dreamed up","idioms:2:dream up"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has the government refused to do?","o":["Raise ticket prices","Buy new aircraft","Announce a new name","Rescue the airline"],"a":3,"why":"the government has refused to bail out the airline Sky East とある。bail out を rescue と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Why have ticket prices risen this year?","o":["Fuel costs have increased.","Staff were given a pay rise.","Routes were added.","Safety checks became stricter."],"a":0,"why":"Fuel costs have driven up ticket prices this year とある。"},{"q":"What will be announced on Friday?","o":["The timetable","The pay cuts","The company's new name","The weekend flights"],"a":2,"why":"They have also dreamed up a new name for the company, which will be announced on Friday とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0050","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ② 動詞＋副詞（他動詞）","kind":"計画をまとめる会議","text":"Thanks, everyone. Let's try to hammer out a final plan today. First, the budget. When I factor in the cost of shipping, we are ten thousand dollars over. I cannot figure out why the March numbers are so high, so I have asked Lin to ferret out the cause. Second, staffing. If we move two people from sales, we can even out the workload and head off complaints about overtime. Third, competition. A rival is copying our design, and we need a lawyer to fend off any legal claim. Finally, the proposal itself is too thin. Raj, could you flesh out section three with real examples by Thursday?","ja":"皆さん、ありがとう。今日こそ、最終的な計画をまとめ上げましょう。まず予算です。配送費を考慮に入れると、1万ドルの超過になります。3月の数字がなぜこんなに高いのか分からないので、リンに原因を探し出すよう頼みました。次に人員です。営業から2人移せば、仕事量を均等にでき、残業への不満を未然に防げます。3つ目は競合です。ある競合他社が当社のデザインをまねており、法的な申し立てをかわすために弁護士が必要です。最後に、提案書そのものの中身が薄すぎます。ラジ、木曜日までに、第3章を実例で肉付けしてもらえますか。","words":[["hammer out","idioms:2:hammer out"],["factor in","idioms:2:factor in"],["figure out","idioms:2:figure out"],["ferret out","idioms:2:ferret out"],["even out","idioms:2:even out"],["head off","idioms:2:head off"],["fend off","idioms:2:fend off"],["flesh out","idioms:2:flesh out"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does the speaker mention about the budget?","o":["It has not been approved.","It is over by ten thousand dollars.","It does not include salaries.","It was cut in March."],"a":1,"why":"we are ten thousand dollars over とある。"},{"q":"What has Lin been asked to do?","o":["Hire a lawyer","Move to the sales team","Find the cause of the high numbers","Write the proposal"],"a":2,"why":"I have asked Lin to ferret out the cause とある。ferret out を find と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What should Raj do by Thursday?","o":["Add examples to a section","Reduce overtime","Copy the design","Contact the rival"],"a":0,"why":"could you flesh out section three with real examples by Thursday? とある。flesh out は「肉付けする」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0051","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ② 動詞＋副詞（他動詞）","kind":"企画会議","text":"Good morning. Our task today is to map out the launch of the new phone. Let me sum up where we stand. We have narrowed down the launch cities to three, and I'd like to pin down the exact date this week. Please jot down your ideas as we talk. The first press release was too long, so Marta pared it down to one page. We also need to iron out a problem with the battery supplier before we go further. I know some of you want more time to mull over the price. That's fine. I'll pencil in another meeting for Friday morning. For now, let's begin with the cities.","ja":"おはようございます。今日の課題は、新しい携帯電話の発売を綿密に計画することです。現状を要約します。発売する都市は3つに絞り込みました。正確な日付は、今週中に確定させたいと思います。話し合いながら、思いついたことを書き留めてください。最初の報道発表の文面は長すぎたので、マルタが1ページに削りました。先へ進む前に、電池の仕入先との問題も解消しなければなりません。価格についてもう少しじっくり考える時間がほしい、という人がいるのは分かっています。それでかまいません。金曜日の午前中に、もう一度会議を仮に入れておきます。では、まず都市の話から始めましょう。","words":[["map out","idioms:2:map out"],["sum up","idioms:2:sum up"],["narrowed down","idioms:2:narrow down"],["pin down","idioms:2:pin down"],["jot down","idioms:2:jot down"],["pared it down","idioms:2:pare down"],["iron out","idioms:2:iron out"],["mull over","idioms:2:mull over"],["pencil in","idioms:2:pencil in"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the meeting about?","o":["Planning a product launch","Hiring a battery supplier","Writing a press release","Choosing a new office"],"a":0,"why":"Our task today is to map out the launch of the new phone とある。"},{"q":"What did Marta do?","o":["She chose three cities.","She set the launch date.","She shortened a press release.","She called the supplier."],"a":2,"why":"Marta pared it down to one page とある。pare down を shorten と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will the speaker schedule for Friday morning?","o":["A visit to a supplier","A press conference","A product test","Another meeting"],"a":3,"why":"I'll pencil in another meeting for Friday morning とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0052","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ② 動詞＋副詞（他動詞）","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"Turning to the economy. The central bank said today that it cannot rule out another rise in interest rates. Officials played down fears of a recession and pointed out that exports are still growing. However, the government has had to prop up two regional banks, and it is trying to rein in public spending at the same time. Meanwhile, the online retailer Zenda racked up record sales last month. The firm will roll out its delivery service in ten more cities this year. Shoppers snapped up its discounted televisions within hours. Critics say the company must spell out how it will protect customer data. Investors have so far shrugged off those concerns.","ja":"続いて経済です。中央銀行は本日、さらなる利上げの可能性を否定できないと述べました。当局は景気後退への懸念を重く扱わず、輸出は依然として伸びていると指摘しました。しかし政府は、地方銀行2行を支えざるを得なくなっており、同時に公共支出を抑えようとしています。一方、ネット通販のゼンダは、先月、過去最高の売上を積み上げました。同社は今年、さらに10の都市で配送サービスを展開します。値下げされたテレビは、数時間のうちに買い物客が飛びつくように買っていきました。批判する人々は、同社が顧客のデータをどう守るのか、詳しく説明すべきだと述べています。投資家は今のところ、そうした懸念を受け流しています。","words":[["rule out","idioms:2:rule out"],["played down","idioms:2:play down"],["pointed out","idioms:2:point out"],["prop up","idioms:2:prop up"],["rein in","idioms:2:rein in"],["racked up","idioms:2:rack up"],["roll out","idioms:2:roll out"],["snapped up","idioms:2:snap up"],["spell out","idioms:2:spell out"],["shrugged off","idioms:2:shrug off"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the central bank say?","o":["Interest rates will fall.","Interest rates may rise again.","Exports have stopped growing.","A recession has begun."],"a":1,"why":"it cannot rule out another rise in interest rates とある。可能性を否定できない＝上がるかもしれない。"},{"q":"What will Zenda do this year?","o":["Expand its delivery service","Stop selling televisions","Buy two regional banks","Reduce its prices"],"a":0,"why":"The firm will roll out its delivery service in ten more cities this year とある。"},{"q":"What do critics want the company to explain?","o":["How it racked up record sales","Why its televisions were discounted","When it will open stores","How it will protect customer data"],"a":3,"why":"the company must spell out how it will protect customer data とある。spell out を explain と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0053","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ② 動詞＋副詞（他動詞）","kind":"地域ニュース","text":"In regional news, police sealed off the old market this morning after a gas leak. Officers rounded up shoppers and moved them to the car park. Nobody was hurt. In other news, the storm that wiped out most of the apple harvest has left many farms short of money. The council has promised a loan to tide them over until spring. Workers have begun to tear down the damaged bridge at Oak Hill. Elsewhere, a clerk at the town hall has been accused of siphoning off public funds. A colleague tipped off the police last week. Finally, a new program aims to weed out fake online reviews. Shops that use up their three warnings will be named publicly.","ja":"地域のニュースです。今朝、ガス漏れがあったため、警察が古い市場を封鎖しました。警察官が買い物客を集めて、駐車場へ移動させました。けが人はいませんでした。次のニュースです。リンゴの収穫の大半を壊滅させた嵐により、多くの農家が資金不足に陥っています。議会は、春まで乗り切れるよう融資を約束しました。オーク・ヒルでは、作業員が壊れた橋の取り壊しを始めています。また、役場の職員が公金を流用した疑いをかけられています。先週、同僚が警察に内報しました。最後に、偽のネット口コミを取り除くことを目指す新しい取り組みが始まります。3回の警告を使い切った店は、名前が公表されます。","words":[["sealed off","idioms:2:seal off"],["rounded up","idioms:2:round up"],["wiped out","idioms:2:wipe out"],["tide them over","idioms:2:tide over"],["tear down","idioms:2:tear down"],["siphoning off","idioms:2:siphon off"],["tipped off","idioms:2:tip off"],["weed out","idioms:2:weed out"],["use up","idioms:2:use up"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did police close the old market?","o":["A bridge collapsed.","A storm was coming.","There was a gas leak.","Money was stolen."],"a":2,"why":"police sealed off the old market this morning after a gas leak とある。"},{"q":"What has the council promised farmers?","o":["A loan","New apple trees","A lower tax","Free equipment"],"a":0,"why":"The council has promised a loan to tide them over until spring とある。"},{"q":"What will happen to shops that receive three warnings?","o":["They will be closed.","Their names will be made public.","They will pay a fine.","They will lose their reviews."],"a":1,"why":"Shops that use up their three warnings will be named publicly とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0054","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ② 動詞＋副詞（他動詞）","kind":"店長会議","text":"Thanks for coming. Let me explain how we plan to win over younger shoppers. First, we must size up the competition. The new store across the road looks similar to ours, and customers can hardly tell the two apart. So we will try out a new layout in April. Second, security. We have had three thefts this month, and better lighting should help to ward off thieves. Third, the loyalty program. Head office wanted to water down the rewards, but I refused. Instead, we will whittle down the number of membership levels from five to three. The bank loan will shore up our finances until summer and help us stave off any job cuts. I would like to single out the night team for praise. They sorted out the stock room in a single weekend.","ja":"お集まりいただきありがとうございます。若い買い物客をどうやって味方につけるか、計画をご説明します。第一に、競合の実力を見極めなければなりません。道の向かいの新しい店はうちとよく似ていて、お客様は2つの店をほとんど見分けられません。そこで、4月に新しい売り場の配置を試してみます。第二に、防犯です。今月は盗難が3件ありました。照明を良くすれば、泥棒を防ぐのに役立つはずです。第三に、ポイント制度です。本社は特典の中身を薄めたがっていましたが、私は断りました。その代わり、会員の段階の数を5つから3つへと徐々に減らします。銀行からの融資は、夏まで当店の財務を支え、人員削減を食い止める助けになります。ここで、夜間のチームを特に取り上げて称えたいと思います。たった一度の週末で、在庫保管室を整理してくれました。","words":[["win over","idioms:2:win over"],["size up","idioms:2:size up"],["tell the two apart","idioms:2:tell apart"],["try out","idioms:2:try out"],["ward off","idioms:2:ward off"],["water down","idioms:2:water down"],["whittle down","idioms:2:whittle down"],["shore up","idioms:2:shore up"],["stave off","idioms:2:stave off"],["single out","idioms:2:single out"],["sorted out","idioms:2:sort out"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will the store try in April?","o":["A new layout","Longer opening hours","A lower price range","A new loyalty card"],"a":0,"why":"we will try out a new layout in April とある。"},{"q":"What did head office want to do?","o":["Hire more security staff","Close the stock room","Add membership levels","Reduce the rewards"],"a":3,"why":"Head office wanted to water down the rewards とある。water down（薄める）を reduce と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Why does the speaker praise the night team?","o":["They caught a thief.","They organized the stock room.","They won a contest.","They trained new staff."],"a":1,"why":"They sorted out the stock room in a single weekend とある。sort out を organize と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0055","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ③ 動詞＋前置詞","kind":"就業規則の説明","text":"Welcome to the team. Before you start, I must explain a few rules. All staff must abide by the safety code and comply with instructions from the floor manager. Please adhere to the schedule on the wall and refrain from using your phone near the machines. Uniforms must conform to the company standard. We do not approve of smoking anywhere on the site. If you object to any rule, please tell me today. You will report to Ms. Vega, who presides over the weekly safety meeting. She will attend to your questions. Finally, never tamper with the alarm system, and dispose of used gloves in the yellow bins. Thank you.","ja":"チームへようこそ。仕事を始める前に、いくつか規則を説明しなければなりません。従業員は全員、安全規定に従い、現場責任者の指示を守らなければなりません。壁に貼ってある予定を守り、機械の近くでは携帯電話の使用を控えてください。制服は、会社の基準に合っていなければなりません。敷地内での喫煙は、どこであっても認めていません。規則に反対の点があれば、今日のうちに私に伝えてください。皆さんはベガさんの直属になります。ベガさんは、毎週の安全会議の議長を務めています。皆さんの質問にも対応してくれます。最後に、警報装置には決して勝手に手を加えないこと、使用済みの手袋は黄色い容器に処分することを守ってください。以上です。","words":[["abide by","idioms:3:abide by"],["comply with","idioms:3:comply with"],["adhere to","idioms:3:adhere to"],["refrain from","idioms:3:refrain from"],["conform to","idioms:3:conform to"],["approve of","idioms:3:approve of"],["object to","idioms:3:object to"],["report to","idioms:3:report to"],["presides over","idioms:3:preside over"],["attend to","idioms:3:attend to"],["tamper with","idioms:3:tamper with"],["dispose of","idioms:3:dispose of"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who are the listeners?","o":["Safety inspectors","Visitors to the site","New employees","Uniform suppliers"],"a":2,"why":"Welcome to the team. Before you start とあり、新しく入った従業員への説明だと分かる。"},{"q":"What should the listeners not do near the machines?","o":["Use their phones","Wear gloves","Talk to the manager","Read the schedule"],"a":0,"why":"refrain from using your phone near the machines とある。"},{"q":"Where should used gloves be placed?","o":["Near the alarm","In the yellow bins","On the wall","In the manager's office"],"a":1,"why":"dispose of used gloves in the yellow bins とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0056","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ③ 動詞＋前置詞","kind":"教授の紹介","text":"It is my pleasure to introduce Professor Elena Russo. Professor Russo majored in chemistry at Milan University and now specializes in clean energy. Her work has contributed to three major patents, and many firms rely on her advice. She believes in sharing knowledge freely, which is why she participates in public events like this one. Tonight, she will elaborate on her latest research and touch on the future of solar power. She may also allude to a new project that she cannot yet discuss in detail. Young scientists who aspire to a career in research will benefit from her talk. Afterward, she will respond to your questions. Please welcome Professor Russo.","ja":"エレナ・ルッソ教授をご紹介できることを、うれしく思います。ルッソ教授はミラノ大学で化学を専攻し、現在はクリーンエネルギーを専門としています。教授の研究は3つの主要な特許に貢献しており、多くの企業が教授の助言を頼りにしています。教授は、知識を惜しみなく分かち合うことの価値を信じており、だからこそ、このような一般向けの催しに参加されています。今夜は、最新の研究について詳しく述べ、太陽光発電の将来にも軽く触れていただきます。まだ詳しくは話せない新しい計画を、ほのめかされるかもしれません。研究の道を志す若い科学者の皆さんは、このお話から得るものがあるでしょう。講演のあと、皆さんの質問に答えていただきます。それでは、ルッソ教授をお迎えください。","words":[["majored in","idioms:3:major in"],["specializes in","idioms:3:specialize in"],["contributed to","idioms:3:contribute to"],["rely on","idioms:3:rely on"],["believes in","idioms:3:believe in"],["participates in","idioms:3:participate in"],["elaborate on","idioms:3:elaborate on"],["touch on","idioms:3:touch on"],["allude to","idioms:3:allude to"],["aspire to","idioms:3:aspire to"],["benefit from","idioms:3:benefit from"],["respond to","idioms:3:respond to"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is Professor Russo's field?","o":["Public speaking","Patent law","Mathematics","Clean energy"],"a":3,"why":"now specializes in clean energy とある。"},{"q":"Why does she take part in public events?","o":["She believes in sharing knowledge.","She is paid by firms.","She is looking for students.","She wants to sell her patents."],"a":0,"why":"She believes in sharing knowledge freely, which is why she participates in public events とある。"},{"q":"What will she do after her talk?","o":["Sign copies of her book","Answer questions","Show a film","Visit a laboratory"],"a":1,"why":"Afterward, she will respond to your questions とある。respond to を answer と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0057","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ③ 動詞＋前置詞","kind":"相談番組","text":"Welcome to Money Talk. Today's letter comes from a listener who is grappling with debt. She writes that she can no longer cope with her monthly payments and that she longs for a simple life. She confided in a friend, who told her to borrow more. Please do not resort to that. Here is my advice. First, reflect on where your money goes each month. Do not dwell on past mistakes. Second, do not bank on a pay rise that may never come. Your plan should not hinge on luck. Third, insist on speaking to your bank in person. Most banks will not yield to pressure, but they do care for honest customers. And remember, you can depend on free advice centers in every city.","ja":"「マネー・トーク」へようこそ。今日のお便りは、借金に苦しんでいるリスナーの方からです。毎月の返済にもう対処できず、簡素な暮らしを切望している、と書かれています。友人に打ち明けたところ、もっと借りるように言われたそうです。どうか、その手段には訴えないでください。私の助言はこうです。第一に、毎月お金がどこへ出ていくのかをよく考えましょう。過去の失敗をくよくよ考えてはいけません。第二に、実現しないかもしれない昇給を当てにしないこと。あなたの計画が、運次第であってはなりません。第三に、銀行と直接会って話すことを強く求めてください。たいていの銀行は圧力には屈しませんが、誠実なお客を大切にはしてくれます。そして、どの都市にもある無料の相談所を頼れることを覚えておいてください。","words":[["grappling with","idioms:3:grapple with"],["cope with","idioms:3:cope with"],["longs for","idioms:3:long for"],["confided in","idioms:3:confide in"],["resort to","idioms:3:resort to"],["reflect on","idioms:3:reflect on"],["dwell on","idioms:3:dwell on"],["bank on","idioms:3:bank on"],["hinge on","idioms:3:hinge on"],["insist on","idioms:3:insist on"],["yield to","idioms:3:yield to"],["care for","idioms:3:care for"],["depend on","idioms:3:depend on"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the listener's problem?","o":["She has lost her job.","She cannot find a bank.","She is struggling with debt.","Her friend owes her money."],"a":2,"why":"a listener who is grappling with debt とある。grapple with を struggle with と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What did the listener's friend suggest?","o":["Borrowing more money","Moving to another city","Asking for a pay rise","Visiting an advice center"],"a":0,"why":"She confided in a friend, who told her to borrow more とある。話し手はそれに反対している。"},{"q":"What does the speaker advise the listener to do?","o":["Wait for a pay rise","Change banks","Forget about the debt","Talk to her bank in person"],"a":3,"why":"insist on speaking to your bank in person とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0058","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ③ 動詞＋前置詞","kind":"市の公聴会についてのニュース","text":"The city council met last night to discuss the new shopping center. Residents say the building would encroach on the public park and infringe on their right to quiet. Noise from the site already interferes with classes at the nearby school. A lawyer for the builder said the company would not dispense with the planned garden. She added that the complaints stem from a misunderstanding. The total cost will amount to ninety million dollars, and parking fees will account for part of the income. The plan must still qualify for a state grant. Two council members sided with the residents, but the mayor persisted in defending the project. Officials will sift through two hundred written comments this week, and a final vote will follow.","ja":"市議会は昨夜、新しいショッピングセンターについて話し合うために開かれました。住民は、この建物が公共の公園を侵害し、静かに暮らす権利も侵害すると主張しています。現場からの騒音は、すでに近くの学校の授業を妨げています。建設会社の弁護士は、予定されている庭園を取りやめることはないと述べました。また、苦情は誤解に由来するものだと付け加えました。総費用は9,000万ドルにのぼり、収入の一部は駐車料金が占める見込みです。計画はさらに、州の補助金の資格を得なければなりません。議員2人が住民の側につきましたが、市長はあくまでも計画を擁護し続けました。当局は今週、書面で寄せられた200件の意見をふるいにかけて調べ、そのあと最終的な採決が行われます。","words":[["encroach on","idioms:3:encroach on"],["infringe on","idioms:3:infringe on"],["interferes with","idioms:3:interfere with"],["dispense with","idioms:3:dispense with"],["stem from","idioms:3:stem from"],["amount to","idioms:3:amount to"],["account for","idioms:3:account for"],["qualify for","idioms:3:qualify for"],["sided with","idioms:3:side with"],["persisted in","idioms:3:persist in"],["sift through","idioms:3:sift through"]],"qs":[{"q":"What do residents say about the new building?","o":["It would be too expensive.","It would take over part of the park.","It would have no parking.","It would close the school."],"a":1,"why":"the building would encroach on the public park とある。encroach on を take over part of と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What did the builder's lawyer say?","o":["The garden will still be built.","The cost will be reduced.","The school will be moved.","The grant has been approved."],"a":0,"why":"the company would not dispense with the planned garden とある。取りやめない＝作る。"},{"q":"What will officials do this week?","o":["Visit the park","Hold a final vote","Read written comments","Meet the mayor"],"a":2,"why":"Officials will sift through two hundred written comments this week とある。採決はそのあと。"}]},
{"id":"i-0059","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ③ 動詞＋前置詞","kind":"オンライン講座の広告","text":"Are you ready to embark on a new career? Then enroll in a course at Summit Online College. We cater to busy adults, with evening lessons that allow for full-time work. More than five thousand students already subscribe to our weekly newsletter. Do not lag behind in a changing job market. Our programs help you capitalize on skills you already have, and every student engages in real projects with local firms. Many graduates say they could not conceive of studying any other way. You can register for the spring term until March first. Visit our website today, and take the first step toward a better future.","ja":"新しい仕事の道に乗り出す準備はできていますか。それなら、サミット・オンライン・カレッジの講座に登録しましょう。当校は忙しい社会人の要望に応えており、夜間の授業は、フルタイムの仕事との両立を考慮した内容になっています。すでに5,000人を超える受講生が、当校の週刊ニュースレターを購読しています。変化する雇用市場で、後れを取らないでください。当校の課程は、あなたがすでに持っている技能をうまく生かす手助けをします。また、受講生は全員、地元企業との実際のプロジェクトに取り組みます。多くの修了生が、ほかの学び方は想像できないと話しています。春学期の登録は3月1日まで受け付けています。今すぐウェブサイトをご覧になり、より良い未来への第一歩を踏み出しましょう。","words":[["embark on","idioms:3:embark on"],["enroll in","idioms:3:enroll in"],["cater to","idioms:3:cater to"],["allow for","idioms:3:allow for"],["subscribe to","idioms:3:subscribe to"],["lag behind","idioms:3:lag behind"],["capitalize on","idioms:3:capitalize on"],["engages in","idioms:3:engage in"],["conceive of","idioms:3:conceive of"],["register for","idioms:3:register for"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who are the courses designed for?","o":["Busy adults","High school students","Company owners","Retired teachers"],"a":0,"why":"We cater to busy adults とある。cater to は「～の要望に応える」。"},{"q":"What does every student do?","o":["Writes a weekly newsletter","Studies abroad for a term","Works on real projects with local firms","Teaches an evening lesson"],"a":2,"why":"every student engages in real projects with local firms とある。"},{"q":"By when must students register for the spring term?","o":["By next week","By March first","By the end of spring","By the first lesson"],"a":1,"why":"You can register for the spring term until March first とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0060","page":"idioms","group":["その他 ② 動詞＋副詞（他動詞）","その他 ③ 動詞＋前置詞"],"kind":"特別番組の予告","text":"Tonight's special report delves into the collapse of the Brent Bridge. Our team spent six months poring over documents and wading through thousands of emails. Most of them pertain to safety inspections. The official report glosses over one key fact: an engineer warned of cracks two years ago. Three former workers have agreed to testify to this, and a senior manager vouches for their honesty. It slowly dawned on our reporters that the warnings had simply been ignored. When the city council voted on repairs, four members abstained from voting. Since then, the builder and the city have tried to patch up their differences, but many questions remain. The full report begins at nine.","ja":"今夜の特別報道は、ブレント橋の崩落を掘り下げます。取材班は6か月をかけて文書を熟読し、何千通ものメールを苦労して読み進めました。その大半は、安全検査に関するものです。公式の報告書は、ある重要な事実をごまかしています。2年前に、技術者がひび割れについて警告していたのです。元作業員3人がこのことを証言すると同意しており、ある上級管理職が彼らの誠実さを保証しています。取材班は、その警告が単に無視されていたのだということに、次第に気づきました。市議会が修理について採決したとき、4人の議員が投票を棄権しました。その後、建設会社と市は対立を修復しようとしてきましたが、多くの疑問が残っています。特別報道の全編は、9時から放送します。","words":[["delves into","idioms:3:delve into"],["poring over","idioms:3:pore over"],["wading through","idioms:3:wade through"],["pertain to","idioms:3:pertain to"],["glosses over","idioms:3:gloss over"],["testify to","idioms:3:testify to"],["vouches for","idioms:3:vouch for"],["dawned on","idioms:3:dawn on"],["abstained from","idioms:3:abstain from"],["patch up","idioms:2:patch up"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the special report about?","o":["A new city council","The collapse of a bridge","A strike by engineers","A change in safety law"],"a":1,"why":"Tonight's special report delves into the collapse of the Brent Bridge とある。"},{"q":"What fact does the official report avoid?","o":["The bridge was built ten years ago.","Four council members resigned.","The repairs cost too much.","An engineer warned of cracks."],"a":3,"why":"The official report glosses over one key fact: an engineer warned of cracks two years ago とある。gloss over は「ごまかす」。"},{"q":"When does the full report begin?","o":["At nine o'clock","At six o'clock","Tomorrow night","After the vote"],"a":0,"why":"The full report begins at nine とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0061","page":"idioms","group":["その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","blame","charge"],"kind":"裁判のニュース","text":"In court news, a jury has acquitted businessman Tom Reed of fraud. Prosecutors had accused him of hiding losses from investors and charged him with three crimes. Police first suspected him of the offense two years ago. His former partner, however, was convicted of theft last month and has been stripped of his license. Reed's lawyer blamed the media for the long delay and said the case had robbed her client of his reputation. She added that two years of hearings had deprived his family of a normal life. The partner, meanwhile, blames the losses on bad advice from a bank. He will be sentenced on Friday.","ja":"裁判のニュースです。陪審は、実業家トム・リード氏に対し、詐欺について無罪を言い渡しました。検察は、投資家に損失を隠したとして同氏を告発し、3つの罪で起訴していました。警察が最初にこの犯罪の疑いを同氏にかけたのは、2年前のことです。一方、同氏の元共同経営者は先月、窃盗で有罪判決を受け、免許を剥奪されました。リード氏の弁護士は、裁判が長引いたのはメディアのせいだと非難し、この事件が依頼人から名声を奪ったと述べました。また、2年に及ぶ審理が、家族から普通の暮らしを奪ったとも付け加えました。元共同経営者のほうは、損失は銀行の誤った助言のせいだとしています。判決は金曜日に言い渡されます。","words":[["acquitted businessman Tom Reed of","idioms:5:acquit A of B"],["accused him of","idioms:5:accuse A of B"],["charged him with","idioms:5:charge A with B"],["suspected him of","idioms:5:suspect A of B"],["convicted of","idioms:5:convict A of B"],["stripped of","idioms:5:strip A of B"],["blamed the media for","idioms:5:blame A for B"],["robbed her client of","idioms:5:rob A of B"],["deprived his family of","idioms:5:deprive A of B"],["blames the losses on","idioms:5:blame A on B"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was the result for Tom Reed?","o":["He lost his license.","He was sent to prison.","He was found not guilty.","He was fined."],"a":2,"why":"a jury has acquitted businessman Tom Reed of fraud とある。acquit を found not guilty と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What happened to Reed's former partner last month?","o":["He was found guilty of theft.","He started a new business.","He sued a bank.","He gave an interview."],"a":0,"why":"His former partner, however, was convicted of theft last month とある。"},{"q":"What will happen on Friday?","o":["Reed will speak to the media.","The partner will be sentenced.","A new trial will begin.","The bank will be charged."],"a":1,"why":"He will be sentenced on Friday とある。He は the partner。"}]},
{"id":"i-0062","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"住宅管理事務所からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, Ms. Tran. This is Peter from the housing office. I'm calling to inform you of a change to your rent, and to remind you of the meeting on the twelfth. We will notify all tenants of the new amount in writing. I must also warn you of some noise next week, when workers replace the roof. I can assure you of one thing: the work will finish by Friday. I know the last repair did not convince residents of our good intentions. If you have a complaint, please attach a photo to your message and submit the form to my office. I will forward it to the manager the same day.","ja":"トラン様、こんにちは。住宅管理事務所のピーターです。家賃の変更についてお知らせすることと、12日の会合を思い出していただくことのために、お電話しました。新しい金額は、入居者の皆さま全員に書面で通知します。また、来週、作業員が屋根を取り替える際に音がすることを、あらかじめお伝えしておかなければなりません。1つだけ保証できることがあります。作業は金曜日までに終わります。前回の修理では、当事務所の誠意を住民の皆さまに納得していただけなかったことは承知しています。苦情がある場合は、メッセージに写真を添付し、用紙を私の事務所に提出してください。その日のうちに、管理責任者へ転送します。","words":[["inform you of","idioms:5:inform A of B"],["remind you of","idioms:5:remind A of B"],["notify all tenants of","idioms:5:notify A of B"],["warn you of","idioms:5:warn A of B"],["assure you of","idioms:5:assure A of B"],["convince residents of","idioms:5:convince A of B"],["attach a photo to","idioms:5:attach A to B"],["submit the form to","idioms:5:submit A to B"],["forward it to","idioms:5:forward A to B"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the speaker calling?","o":["To cancel a meeting","To ask for a photograph","To report a complaint","To tell a tenant about a rent change"],"a":3,"why":"I'm calling to inform you of a change to your rent とある。"},{"q":"What will happen next week?","o":["The roof will be replaced.","The rent will be collected.","The manager will visit.","The office will close."],"a":0,"why":"next week, when workers replace the roof とある。"},{"q":"What should Ms. Tran include with a complaint?","o":["Her rent receipt","A letter from a neighbor","A photo","Her phone number"],"a":2,"why":"please attach a photo to your message とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0063","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"研究所の計画説明","text":"Good morning. Let me explain the plan for the new research center. The board has allocated five million dollars to the project and assigned twelve scientists to the first team. We will equip every laboratory with the latest tools, and a local firm will supply us with clean power. The city will furnish the staff with free parking. I am glad to say that the board has entrusted Dr. Kim with the role of director. Many people credit her with our success in battery design, and nature has endowed her with great patience. I want to praise the building team for finishing early. Finally, on opening day, the mayor will present Dr. Kim with a gold key.","ja":"おはようございます。新しい研究センターの計画をご説明します。取締役会はこの事業に500万ドルを割り当て、最初のチームに12人の科学者を配属しました。すべての研究室に最新の機器を備え付け、地元の企業がクリーンな電力を供給してくれます。市は、職員に無料の駐車場を提供します。うれしいことに、取締役会はキム博士に所長の役目を任せました。電池の設計における当社の成功は、彼女の功績だと多くの人が考えています。また彼女は、生まれつき大変な忍耐強さに恵まれています。予定より早く完成させてくれた建設チームを称えたいと思います。最後に、開所の日には、市長がキム博士に金の鍵を贈ります。","words":[["allocated five million dollars to","idioms:5:allocate A to B"],["assigned twelve scientists to","idioms:5:assign A to B"],["equip every laboratory with","idioms:5:equip A with B"],["supply us with","idioms:5:supply A with B"],["furnish the staff with","idioms:5:furnish A with B"],["entrusted Dr. Kim with","idioms:5:entrust A with B"],["credit her with","idioms:5:credit A with B"],["endowed her with","idioms:5:endow A with B"],["praise the building team for","idioms:5:praise A for B"],["present Dr. Kim with","idioms:5:present A with B"]],"qs":[{"q":"How much money has been set aside for the project?","o":["Twelve thousand dollars","Five million dollars","Twelve million dollars","Five hundred thousand dollars"],"a":1,"why":"The board has allocated five million dollars to the project とある。"},{"q":"Who will be the director?","o":["The mayor","A local firm's owner","A member of the building team","Dr. Kim"],"a":3,"why":"the board has entrusted Dr. Kim with the role of director とある。"},{"q":"What will happen on opening day?","o":["The mayor will give Dr. Kim a gold key.","The scientists will give a tour.","The building team will be paid.","New tools will be delivered."],"a":0,"why":"the mayor will present Dr. Kim with a gold key とある。present A with B を give と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0064","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"施設見学の案内","text":"Welcome to the tour of the old Harbor Mill. Ten years ago, the city decided to convert the empty factory into a public library. The architect transformed the dark engine room into a bright reading hall and combined the original brick walls with modern glass. She also incorporated the old crane into the design of the cafe. The library divides its books into four main sections and classifies children's books into three reading levels. All signs have been translated into five languages. Last year, the city integrated the library into its online system and added ten thousand new titles to the collection. Please follow me to the second floor.","ja":"旧ハーバー製粉所の見学ツアーへようこそ。10年前、市は空き工場を公共の図書館に作り変えることを決めました。建築家は、暗い機関室を明るい読書ホールに変え、もとのレンガの壁を現代的なガラスと組み合わせました。古いクレーンも、カフェのデザインに組み込みました。図書館は蔵書を4つの主な部門に分け、子ども向けの本は3つの読書レベルに分類しています。案内表示はすべて、5つの言語に翻訳されています。昨年、市はこの図書館をオンラインのシステムに統合し、1万点の新しい本を蔵書に加えました。では、2階へご案内します。","words":[["convert the empty factory into","idioms:5:convert A into B"],["transformed the dark engine room into","idioms:5:transform A into B"],["combined the original brick walls with","idioms:5:combine A with B"],["incorporated the old crane into","idioms:5:incorporate A into B"],["divides its books into","idioms:5:divide A into B"],["classifies children's books into","idioms:5:classify A into B"],["translated into","idioms:5:translate A into B"],["integrated the library into","idioms:5:integrate A into B"],["added ten thousand new titles to","idioms:5:add A to B"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was the building originally?","o":["A library","A cafe","A factory","A school"],"a":2,"why":"convert the empty factory into a public library とある。"},{"q":"What happened to the old crane?","o":["It became part of the cafe's design.","It was sold to the city.","It was moved to the engine room.","It was removed ten years ago."],"a":0,"why":"She also incorporated the old crane into the design of the cafe とある。"},{"q":"What will the listeners do next?","o":["Visit the cafe","Go to the second floor","Join the online system","Borrow some books"],"a":1,"why":"Please follow me to the second floor とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0065","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"料理番組","text":"Welcome back to Kitchen Science. Today's topic is butter and margarine. Many shoppers confuse margarine with butter, and some even mistake one for the other on the shelf. So how can you distinguish real butter from its rivals? First, read the label. Second, compare the color with that of milk. People often associate yellow with quality, but color can be added. Older listeners may identify margarine with hard times, and one writer likened it to candle wax. Today's products are far better. If you prefer butter to margarine, that is fine, but you can substitute olive oil for either in most recipes. One tip: always separate the egg whites from the yolks before mixing. Now, let's start cooking.","ja":"「キッチン・サイエンス」、番組を続けます。今日のテーマはバターとマーガリンです。多くの買い物客がマーガリンをバターと混同し、売り場で一方をもう一方と間違える人さえいます。では、本物のバターを似た商品とどう区別すればよいでしょうか。まず、ラベルを読みましょう。次に、色を牛乳の色と比べてみましょう。黄色を品質の良さと結びつけて考える人が多いのですが、色はあとから付けられます。年配の方は、マーガリンを苦しい時代と同一視されるかもしれません。ある作家は、マーガリンをろうそくのろうにたとえました。今の製品は、はるかに良くなっています。マーガリンよりバターを好むのであれば、それでかまいませんが、たいていのレシピでは、どちらの代わりにもオリーブ油を使うことができます。1つコツを。混ぜる前に、必ず卵白を卵黄から分けてください。では、料理を始めましょう。","words":[["confuse margarine with","idioms:5:confuse A with B"],["mistake one for","idioms:5:mistake A for B"],["distinguish real butter from","idioms:5:distinguish A from B"],["compare the color with","idioms:5:compare A with B"],["associate yellow with","idioms:5:associate A with B"],["identify margarine with","idioms:5:identify A with B"],["likened it to","idioms:5:liken A to B"],["prefer butter to","idioms:5:prefer A to B"],["substitute olive oil for","idioms:5:substitute A for B"],["separate the egg whites from","idioms:5:separate A from B"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is today's topic?","o":["Milk and cheese","Butter and margarine","Eggs and oil","Candles and wax"],"a":1,"why":"Today's topic is butter and margarine とある。"},{"q":"What is the first piece of advice for telling butter from other products?","o":["Compare the color","Check the price","Taste it","Read the label"],"a":3,"why":"First, read the label とある。色を比べるのは2番目。"},{"q":"According to the speaker, what can be used instead of butter or margarine?","o":["Olive oil","Egg whites","Milk","Candle wax"],"a":0,"why":"you can substitute olive oil for either in most recipes とある。substitute A for B は「Bの代わりにAを使う」。"}]},
{"id":"i-0066","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"公園の案内放送","text":"Attention, visitors to Eagle Mountain Park. For your safety, new rules begin today. The park prohibits visitors from lighting fires anywhere on the mountain. Fences have been built to prevent hikers from entering the north cliff area and to protect rare birds from disturbance. Please confine your walks to the marked paths, and limit your group to ten people. High fines are meant to deter people from leaving litter. Rangers will not try to dissuade you from climbing, but bad weather may discourage beginners from going to the top. Local residents are exempted from the parking fee. Finally, road work will divert traffic from the main gate until Friday, so please use the east entrance.","ja":"イーグル山公園にお越しの皆さまにお知らせします。安全のため、本日から新しい規則が始まります。公園では、山のどこであっても、来園者が火を使うことを禁じています。ハイキングの方が北の崖の区域に入るのを防ぎ、珍しい鳥を人の立ち入りから守るために、柵が設けられました。散策は、標識のある道だけにとどめ、グループは10人までに制限してください。高い罰金は、ごみを残していくのを思いとどまらせるためのものです。レンジャーは登山を思いとどまらせようとはしませんが、悪天候の場合、初心者の方は頂上へ行く気をなくされるかもしれません。地元の住民の方は、駐車料金が免除されます。最後に、道路工事のため、金曜日まで車は正門を通れませんので、東口をご利用ください。","words":[["prohibits visitors from","idioms:5:prohibit A from B"],["prevent hikers from","idioms:5:prevent A from B"],["protect rare birds from","idioms:5:protect A from B"],["confine your walks to","idioms:5:confine A to B"],["limit your group to","idioms:5:limit A to B"],["deter people from","idioms:5:deter A from B"],["dissuade you from","idioms:5:dissuade A from B"],["discourage beginners from","idioms:5:discourage A from B"],["exempted from","idioms:5:exempt A from B"],["divert traffic from","idioms:5:divert A from B"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is not allowed in the park?","o":["Lighting fires","Climbing the mountain","Walking in groups","Watching birds"],"a":0,"why":"The park prohibits visitors from lighting fires anywhere on the mountain とある。"},{"q":"Who does not have to pay for parking?","o":["Park rangers","Beginners","Local residents","Groups of ten"],"a":2,"why":"Local residents are exempted from the parking fee とある。"},{"q":"Which entrance should drivers use until Friday?","o":["The main gate","The east entrance","The north cliff gate","The west entrance"],"a":1,"why":"road work will divert traffic from the main gate until Friday, so please use the east entrance とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0067","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"番組でのゲスト紹介","text":"Our next guest is the economist Dr. Paul Varga. Many people regard him as the leading expert on small business. Critics once described his first book as too simple, but readers viewed it as a breath of fresh air. Dr. Varga defines success as steady growth, not quick profit. He bases his ideas on thirty years of data, and he derives many of his examples from family shops. He attributes most failures to poor planning, while others ascribe them to bad luck. Dr. Varga says he owes his career to a teacher who lent him a book at sixteen. His new book comes out next week. Dr. Varga, welcome to the show.","ja":"次のゲストは、経済学者のポール・ヴァルガ博士です。多くの人が、博士を小規模事業の第一人者とみなしています。批評家たちはかつて、博士の最初の著書を単純すぎると評しましたが、読者はそれを新鮮な風と受け止めました。ヴァルガ博士は、成功とは目先の利益ではなく、着実な成長であると定義しています。博士の考えは30年分のデータに基づいており、実例の多くは家族経営の店から引き出されています。博士は、失敗の大半は計画の甘さが原因だと考えていますが、それを不運のせいにする人もいます。ヴァルガ博士は、今の経歴があるのは、16歳のときに1冊の本を貸してくれた先生のおかげだと語っています。新しい著書は来週発売されます。ヴァルガ博士、番組へようこそ。","words":[["regard him as","idioms:5:regard A as B"],["described his first book as","idioms:5:describe A as B"],["viewed it as","idioms:5:view A as B"],["defines success as","idioms:5:define A as B"],["bases his ideas on","idioms:5:base A on B"],["derives many of his examples from","idioms:5:derive A from B"],["attributes most failures to","idioms:5:attribute A to B"],["ascribe them to","idioms:5:ascribe A to B"],["owes his career to","idioms:5:owe A to B"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is Dr. Varga?","o":["A bookstore owner","A family shop manager","A school teacher","An economist"],"a":3,"why":"Our next guest is the economist Dr. Paul Varga とある。"},{"q":"According to Dr. Varga, what causes most business failures?","o":["Poor planning","Bad luck","Quick profit","Too much data"],"a":0,"why":"He attributes most failures to poor planning とある。不運のせいにするのは「ほかの人たち」。"},{"q":"What will happen next week?","o":["Dr. Varga will give a lecture.","A family shop will open.","Dr. Varga's new book will be released.","The show will end."],"a":2,"why":"His new book comes out next week とある。come out を be released と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"i-0068","page":"idioms","group":["その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","charge"],"kind":"鉄道会社の自動音声案内","text":"Thank you for calling Swift Rail customer service. Because of yesterday's delays, we will compensate all passengers for their lost time. If you took a taxi, we will reimburse you for the fare. Please keep your receipt. Your ticket entitles you to a full refund, or you may exchange it for a travel voucher. We will not charge you for changing your seat, and we will not bill you for a new ticket. We have replaced the old booking system with a faster one, so refunds now take three days. We spend two million dollars on track repairs each year, and we will share the results of our inquiry with the public next month. To speak to an agent, press one.","ja":"スウィフト鉄道のお客様サービスにお電話いただき、ありがとうございます。昨日の遅延につきまして、すべてのお客様に、失われたお時間の補償をいたします。タクシーをご利用になった場合は、その運賃を払い戻します。領収書は保管しておいてください。お手持ちの乗車券で全額の払い戻しを受ける権利があり、旅行券と交換することもできます。座席の変更について料金をいただくことはなく、新しい乗車券の代金を請求することもありません。古い予約システムをより速いものに取り替えましたので、払い戻しは3日で完了します。当社は毎年200万ドルを線路の修理に費やしており、調査の結果は来月、皆さまに公表いたします。係員とお話しになる場合は、1を押してください。","words":[["compensate all passengers for","idioms:5:compensate A for B"],["reimburse you for","idioms:5:reimburse A for B"],["entitles you to","idioms:5:entitle A to B"],["exchange it for","idioms:5:exchange A for B"],["charge you for","idioms:5:charge A for B"],["bill you for","idioms:5:bill A for B"],["replaced the old booking system with","idioms:5:replace A with B"],["spend two million dollars on","idioms:5:spend A on B"],["share the results of our inquiry with","idioms:5:share A with B"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the company offering compensation?","o":["A station was closed.","There were delays yesterday.","Tickets were overpriced.","The booking system failed."],"a":1,"why":"Because of yesterday's delays, we will compensate all passengers とある。"},{"q":"What should passengers who took a taxi keep?","o":["Their receipt","Their travel voucher","Their seat number","Their old ticket"],"a":0,"why":"If you took a taxi, we will reimburse you for the fare. Please keep your receipt とある。"},{"q":"How long do refunds take now?","o":["One day","One week","One month","Three days"],"a":3,"why":"refunds now take three days とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0069","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"退職する看護師への感謝","text":"Tonight we honor Nurse Maria Lopez, who is retiring after forty years. Maria devoted her life to caring for others and dedicated her evenings to training young nurses. Her work exposed her to many dangers, and long night shifts subjected her to great stress. Yet she never complained. When the old hospital was consigned to history, she was transferred to this building and helped to design the children's ward. She tailored each care plan to the patient, and she always found a way to reconcile strict rules with kindness. The hospital has committed fifty thousand dollars to a training fund in her name. Maria, tonight we relieve you of all your duties. Please enjoy your rest.","ja":"今夜は、40年の勤務を終えて退職する看護師、マリア・ロペスさんを称えます。マリアさんは人の世話をすることに人生を捧げ、夜の時間を若い看護師の指導に充ててきました。その仕事は彼女を多くの危険にさらし、長い夜勤は大きな負担を強いるものでした。それでも、彼女は決して不満を口にしませんでした。古い病院が過去のものとなったとき、彼女はこの建物に移り、小児病棟の設計を手伝いました。彼女は一人ひとりの看護計画を患者に合わせて作り、厳しい規則と思いやりを両立させる方法をいつも見つけてきました。病院は、彼女の名前を付けた研修基金に5万ドルを充てることを決めました。マリアさん、今夜、私たちはあなたをすべての職務から解放します。どうぞ、ゆっくりお休みください。","words":[["devoted her life to","idioms:5:devote A to B"],["dedicated her evenings to","idioms:5:dedicate A to B"],["exposed her to","idioms:5:expose A to B"],["subjected her to","idioms:5:subject A to B"],["consigned to","idioms:5:consign A to B"],["transferred to","idioms:5:transfer A to B"],["tailored each care plan to","idioms:5:tailor A to B"],["reconcile strict rules with","idioms:5:reconcile A with B"],["committed fifty thousand dollars to","idioms:5:commit A to B"],["relieve you of","idioms:5:relieve A of B"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the talk?","o":["To open a new ward","To raise money for a hospital","To honor a retiring nurse","To welcome new nurses"],"a":2,"why":"Tonight we honor Nurse Maria Lopez, who is retiring after forty years とある。"},{"q":"What did Maria help to design?","o":["The children's ward","The old hospital","The training program","The night shift schedule"],"a":0,"why":"helped to design the children's ward とある。"},{"q":"What has the hospital created in her name?","o":["A new building","A training fund","An annual award","A children's garden"],"a":1,"why":"The hospital has committed fifty thousand dollars to a training fund in her name とある。"}]},
{"id":"i-0070","page":"idioms","group":"その他 ⑤ 動詞＋A＋前置詞＋B","kind":"ローカルニュース","text":"Now for the local news. The university has conferred an honorary degree on Dr. Sara Wells, whose new treatment has cured hundreds of patients of a rare skin disease. The mayor congratulated her on the award and bestowed the city medal on her at a ceremony last night. In other news, last week's storm inflicted serious damage on the fishing port. Residents criticized the council for its slow response, and the port manager was reprimanded for ignoring a weather warning. The council has promised to rid the harbor of wrecked boats by Friday, and repairs to the sea wall will begin next month. Finally, the weather: sunshine is expected all weekend.","ja":"続いて地元のニュースです。大学は、サラ・ウェルズ博士に名誉学位を授与しました。博士の新しい治療法は、何百人もの患者の珍しい皮膚病を治してきました。昨夜の式典で、市長は受賞を祝い、博士に市の勲章を授けました。次のニュースです。先週の嵐は、漁港に深刻な被害を与えました。住民は対応の遅さについて議会を批判し、港の管理者は気象警報を無視したことで叱責されました。議会は、金曜日までに港から壊れた船を取り除くと約束しており、防波堤の修理は来月始まります。最後に天気です。週末はずっと晴れる見込みです。","words":[["conferred an honorary degree on","idioms:5:confer A on B"],["cured hundreds of patients of","idioms:5:cure A of B"],["congratulated her on","idioms:5:congratulate A on B"],["bestowed the city medal on","idioms:5:bestow A on B"],["inflicted serious damage on","idioms:5:inflict A on B"],["criticized the council for","idioms:5:criticize A for B"],["reprimanded for","idioms:5:reprimand A for B"],["rid the harbor of","idioms:5:rid A of B"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did Dr. Wells receive from the university?","o":["A research grant","A new laboratory","A teaching position","An honorary degree"],"a":3,"why":"The university has conferred an honorary degree on Dr. Sara Wells とある。"},{"q":"Why did residents criticize the council?","o":["It responded slowly.","It raised taxes.","It ignored the mayor.","It closed the port."],"a":0,"why":"Residents criticized the council for its slow response とある。"},{"q":"What has the council promised to do by Friday?","o":["Repair the sea wall","Remove wrecked boats from the harbor","Hold a ceremony","Issue a weather warning"],"a":1,"why":"The council has promised to rid the harbor of wrecked boats by Friday とある。rid A of B を remove と言い換えている。防波堤の修理は来月。"}]},
{"id":"f-0001","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"空港のアナウンス","text":"Attention, passengers on Coral Air Flight 62 to Lisbon. Your airplane has now arrived at the airport, but because of strong winds, we will depart about forty minutes late. We are sorry to start your vacation with a delay. While you wait, please check that each suitcase you are carrying fits in the measuring frame beside the gate. Larger luggage must be checked at the counter, free of charge. Every traveler should have a passport and boarding pass ready before boarding begins. If Lisbon is not your final destination and you have a hotel reservation that may be affected, please speak to our staff at Gate 14. Thank you for your patience, and we will make another announcement shortly.","ja":"コーラル航空62便リスボン行きをご利用のお客様にご案内します。ご搭乗の飛行機はすでに空港に到着しておりますが、強風のため、出発が約40分遅れます。休暇の始まりが遅れますことをおわびします。お待ちの間、お持ちのスーツケースが搭乗口横の計測枠に収まるかをご確認ください。大きな手荷物は、カウンターで無料でお預かりします。ご搭乗が始まる前に、どなたもパスポートと搭乗券をご用意ください。リスボンが最終目的地ではなく、影響を受けそうなホテルの予約をお持ちの方は、14番搭乗口の係員にお申し出ください。お待ちいただきありがとうございます。まもなく次のご案内をいたします。","words":[["airplane","freq:airplane"],["airport","freq:airport"],["depart","freq:depart"],["vacation","freq:vacation"],["suitcase","freq:suitcase"],["luggage","freq:luggage"],["traveler","freq:traveler"],["passport","freq:passport"],["destination","freq:destination"],["reservation","freq:reservation"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the flight delayed?","o":["The plane has not arrived yet.","The weather is windy.","A crew member is late.","The gate was changed."],"a":1,"why":"because of strong winds（強風のため）出発が遅れると言っている。飛行機そのものはすでに到着している。"},{"q":"What are passengers asked to check while they wait?","o":["The size of their bags","The number of their seats","The time of their connecting flights","The name on their tickets"],"a":0,"why":"each suitcase ... fits in the measuring frame（スーツケースが計測枠に収まるか）を確かめるよう求めている。"},{"q":"Who should speak to the staff at Gate 14?","o":["Passengers who lost their boarding passes","Passengers traveling with children","Passengers who want to check large bags","Passengers with hotel bookings that may be affected"],"a":3,"why":"have a hotel reservation that may be affected（影響を受けそうなホテルの予約がある）人は14番搭乗口の係員に、とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0002","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"部門の朝礼","text":"Good morning, everyone. I have two changes to announce. First, the safety workshop planned for this Thursday has been postponed, because the trainer is ill. We will reschedule it for next week, and I will notify you by e-mail as soon as the new date is fixed. Please read the memo I sent yesterday for the details. Second, the deadline for the Benton report has moved forward to Friday. This is a big assignment, so if you are short of time, ask a coworker to check your figures before you hand them in. Your supervisor will collect the finished sections on Friday morning. Finally, please remember the upcoming office move and start packing anything you do not use every day.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。変更が2点あります。まず、今週木曜に予定していた安全研修は、講師の体調不良のため延期になりました。来週に日程を組み直し、新しい日が決まり次第、メールでお知らせします。詳しくは、昨日送った社内連絡を読んでください。次に、ベントン報告書の締め切りが金曜に早まりました。大きな課題ですので、時間が足りない人は、提出の前に同僚に数字を確認してもらってください。金曜の朝に、各自の上司ができあがった部分を集めます。最後に、近く行われる事務所の引っ越しを忘れず、毎日は使わない物から荷造りを始めてください。","words":[["workshop","freq:workshop"],["postponed","freq:postpone"],["reschedule","freq:reschedule"],["notify","freq:notify"],["memo","freq:memo"],["deadline","freq:deadline"],["assignment","freq:assignment"],["coworker","freq:coworker"],["supervisor","freq:supervisor"],["upcoming","freq:upcoming"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why was the workshop postponed?","o":["The room was not available.","Too few people signed up.","The trainer is sick.","The report is not finished."],"a":2,"why":"because the trainer is ill（講師が病気のため）と理由を述べている。"},{"q":"What has changed about the Benton report?","o":["It is due earlier.","It was canceled.","It will be written by another team.","It must be shorter."],"a":0,"why":"the deadline ... has moved forward to Friday（締め切りが金曜に早まった）とある。moved forward を due earlier と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What are listeners asked to start doing?","o":["Booking a meeting room","Packing things they rarely use","Training new coworkers","Sending e-mails to clients"],"a":1,"why":"start packing anything you do not use every day（毎日は使わない物から荷造りを始める）よう求めている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0003","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"留守番電話","text":"Hello, this is Dana Reyes, the accountant at Pine Street Kitchen Supply. I am calling about your order of restaurant goods. Our records show that the shipment left our warehouse on Monday, but I am afraid we charged you twice for the same merchandise. I am very sorry about that. We will send a refund to your account within three days, and I will fax you a corrected invoice this afternoon. Please keep the new receipt for your records and throw away the old one. Also, two of the items you asked for are not in our inventory right now, so they will follow next week at no extra cost. As a valued client, you can call me directly at 555-0142 with any questions.","ja":"もしもし、パイン・ストリート厨房用品の経理担当、デイナ・レイエスです。ご注文いただいた飲食店向けの商品の件でお電話しました。当社の記録では、荷物は月曜に倉庫を出ておりますが、申し訳ないことに、同じ商品の代金を二重にご請求しておりました。大変失礼いたしました。3日以内にお客様の口座へ返金し、本日午後に訂正した請求書をファックスでお送りします。新しい領収書を控えとして保管し、古いものは破棄してください。また、ご依頼の品のうち2点は現在在庫がないため、来週、追加料金なしでお届けします。大切なお客様ですので、ご不明な点は555-0142の私あてに直接お電話ください。","words":[["accountant","freq:accountant"],["goods","freq:goods"],["shipment","freq:shipment"],["merchandise","freq:merchandise"],["refund","freq:refund"],["fax","freq:fax"],["invoice","freq:invoice"],["receipt","freq:receipt"],["inventory","freq:inventory"],["client","freq:client"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does the speaker mention?","o":["A delivery was sent to the wrong address.","A customer was charged twice.","Some items arrived broken.","A payment was not received."],"a":1,"why":"we charged you twice for the same merchandise（同じ商品を二重に請求した）と言っている。"},{"q":"What will the speaker send this afternoon?","o":["A new catalog","A discount coupon","A list of missing items","A corrected bill"],"a":3,"why":"I will fax you a corrected invoice（訂正した請求書をファックスする）とある。invoice を bill と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Why will two items arrive next week?","o":["They are not in stock now.","They were ordered late.","They are being repaired.","They are shipped from overseas."],"a":0,"why":"not in our inventory right now（今は在庫にない）ので来週届く、と説明している。"}]},
{"id":"f-0004","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"ビルの入館案内","text":"Welcome to Harbor Tower. Before you go upstairs, please listen to this short guide for visitors. All guests must stop at the reception desk in the lobby and show photo identification. The receptionist will give you a visitor card, which you need to use the elevator. If you arrived by car, an attendant will park it for you in the underground garage. Simply leave your key with the clerk at the entrance. Coats and umbrellas can be left in the cabinet next to the front desk. The cafeteria on the second floor is open to visitors from eleven until two, and it accepts cash only. We hope you have a pleasant visit.","ja":"ハーバータワーへようこそ。上の階へ行かれる前に、来訪者向けの短いご案内をお聞きください。お客様は皆、ロビーの受付に立ち寄り、写真付きの身分証明書をご提示ください。受付係が来訪者カードをお渡しします。このカードはエレベーターのご利用に必要です。お車でお越しの場合は、係員が地下の車庫に駐車します。入口の係の者に鍵をお預けください。コートや傘は、受付横の戸棚にお預けいただけます。2階の社員食堂は11時から2時まで来訪者の方もご利用でき、お支払いは現金のみです。どうぞ快適にお過ごしください。","words":[["reception","freq:reception"],["lobby","freq:lobby"],["identification","freq:identification"],["receptionist","freq:receptionist"],["elevator","freq:elevator"],["attendant","freq:attendant"],["garage","freq:garage"],["clerk","freq:clerk"],["cabinet","freq:cabinet"],["cafeteria","freq:cafeteria"]],"qs":[{"q":"What must visitors show at the desk?","o":["A parking ticket","A letter of invitation","An ID with a photo","A business card"],"a":2,"why":"show photo identification（写真付きの身分証明書を見せる）とある。"},{"q":"Why do visitors need a visitor card?","o":["To ride the elevator","To pay for lunch","To enter the garage","To open the cabinet"],"a":0,"why":"a visitor card, which you need to use the elevator（エレベーターの利用に必要）と言っている。"},{"q":"What is said about the cafeteria?","o":["It is closed to visitors.","It is on the first floor.","It opens at two.","It takes only cash."],"a":3,"why":"it accepts cash only（現金のみ）とある。来訪者も11時から2時まで使える。"}]},
{"id":"f-0005","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"求人の案内","text":"Riverside Language School is looking for a full-time English instructor to start in April. Each applicant must have a valid teaching license and at least two years of experience. To apply, send us your résumé and enclose copies of your certificates. Please also write your current occupation on the first page. You can obtain an application form at our front desk or on our Web site. People we select will be invited to a one-day seminar, where you will teach a short sample lesson. Do not worry about the equipment. A technician will set up the classroom computers for you. We sincerely thank everyone who applies, and we will reply to all letters by the end of March.","ja":"リバーサイド語学学校では、4月から働ける常勤の英語講師を募集しています。応募者は皆、有効な教員免許と2年以上の経験が必要です。応募するには、履歴書を送り、資格証明書の写しを同封してください。1ページ目に、現在の職業もお書きください。応募用紙は、受付または当校のウェブサイトで手に入ります。選ばれた方は1日の講習会に招かれ、そこで短い模擬授業をしていただきます。機材の心配はいりません。技術者が教室のコンピューターを準備します。ご応募くださる皆様に心から感謝します。3月末までに、すべてのお手紙にお返事します。","words":[["instructor","freq:instructor"],["applicant","freq:applicant"],["valid","freq:valid"],["résumé","freq:résumé"],["enclose","freq:enclose"],["occupation","freq:occupation"],["obtain","freq:obtain"],["seminar","freq:seminar"],["technician","freq:technician"],["sincerely","freq:sincerely"]],"qs":[{"q":"What position is being advertised?","o":["A school receptionist","A computer technician","An English teacher","A seminar organizer"],"a":2,"why":"a full-time English instructor（常勤の英語講師）を募集している。instructor を teacher と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What should be sent with the résumé?","o":["A photograph","Copies of certificates","A sample lesson plan","A letter from an employer"],"a":1,"why":"enclose copies of your certificates（資格証明書の写しを同封）とある。"},{"q":"What will selected people do at the seminar?","o":["Teach a short lesson","Take a written test","Meet the students' parents","Repair classroom computers"],"a":0,"why":"you will teach a short sample lesson（短い模擬授業をする）と言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0006","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"商品の広告","text":"Is your old computer slowing you down? This month only, Bright Electronics invites you to upgrade to the new Vela 5 laptop. It is so compact and light that you can carry it all day, and its quiet keyboard is perfect for the library or the train. Every Vela 5 comes with a three-year warranty. If any electrical part fails during that time, we will give you a free replacement within two days. The printed manual is short and easy to follow, and you can even connect your cellphone to the screen with one touch. Bright Electronics also sells every kind of home appliance, from toasters to washing machines. Visit us on Canal Street today.","ja":"古いコンピューターのせいで作業が遅くなっていませんか。今月限り、ブライト電器は新型ノートパソコン「ヴェラ5」への買い替えをおすすめします。とても小型で軽いので一日中持ち歩けますし、静かなキーボードは図書館や電車にぴったりです。ヴェラ5にはすべて3年間の保証が付きます。その間に電気部品が故障したら、2日以内に無料で交換品をお渡しします。紙の説明書は短くて分かりやすく、携帯電話もワンタッチで画面につなげられます。ブライト電器は、トースターから洗濯機まで、あらゆる家電製品も販売しています。今日、キャナル通りの店へお越しください。","words":[["upgrade","freq:upgrade"],["laptop","freq:laptop"],["compact","freq:compact"],["keyboard","freq:keyboard"],["warranty","freq:warranty"],["electrical","freq:electrical"],["replacement","freq:replacement"],["manual","freq:manual"],["cellphone","freq:cellphone"],["appliance","freq:appliance"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is said about the Vela 5?","o":["It is small and light.","It is the cheapest model.","It has a large screen.","It is sold only online."],"a":0,"why":"so compact and light that you can carry it all day（小型で軽く一日中持ち歩ける）とある。"},{"q":"How long is the warranty?","o":["One year","Two years","Three years","Five years"],"a":2,"why":"a three-year warranty（3年保証）と言っている。two days は交換品が届くまでの日数。"},{"q":"What else does the store sell?","o":["Office furniture","Mobile phone plans","Computer books","Home appliances"],"a":3,"why":"also sells every kind of home appliance（あらゆる家電製品も売っている）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0007","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"地域ラジオの交通情報","text":"Good morning, this is your City Radio traffic report. If you are heading downtown today, leave the car at home. Main Street is closed until noon for the outdoor food market, so the most convenient way to travel is the subway. The fare is only one dollar today, thanks to the city's clean air campaign. You can also borrow a bicycle for free at any station until six o'clock this evening. The market itself is beside the new supermarket on Lake Avenue, and more than fifty farmers are selling there. One more thing: the sky is clear now, but showers are expected this afternoon, so do not forget your umbrella. We will be back with another report in thirty minutes.","ja":"おはようございます。シティラジオの交通情報です。今日、中心街へ向かう方は、車を家に置いていってください。メイン通りは屋外の食品市のため正午まで通行止めですので、いちばん便利な移動手段は地下鉄です。市の「きれいな空気」運動のおかげで、今日の運賃はたったの1ドルです。また、今夕6時までは、どの駅でも自転車を無料で借りられます。市の会場はレイク通りの新しいスーパーマーケットの隣で、50を超える農家が出店しています。もう一つ。今は晴れていますが、午後はにわか雨の見込みですので、傘をお忘れなく。30分後にまた情報をお伝えします。","words":[["downtown","freq:downtown"],["noon","freq:noon"],["outdoor","freq:outdoor"],["convenient","freq:convenient"],["subway","freq:subway"],["fare","freq:fare"],["bicycle","freq:bicycle"],["o'clock","freq:o'clock"],["supermarket","freq:supermarket"],["umbrella","freq:umbrella"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is Main Street closed?","o":["A market is being held.","The road is being repaired.","There was an accident.","A parade is passing."],"a":0,"why":"closed until noon for the outdoor food market（屋外の食品市のため正午まで通行止め）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the subway today?","o":["It is running late.","It is cheaper than usual.","It is free until six.","It does not stop downtown."],"a":1,"why":"The fare is only one dollar today（今日の運賃は1ドルだけ）とある。無料なのは自転車の貸し出し。"},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest listeners bring?","o":["A shopping bag","A bicycle lock","An umbrella","Some cash"],"a":2,"why":"showers are expected ... do not forget your umbrella（にわか雨の見込みなので傘を忘れずに）と言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0008","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"レストランの自動音声案内","text":"Thank you for calling Olive Garden Bistro. We are closed this week for renovation, and we will open again on the first of May. After ten years in the same building, we have signed a new lease, and our dining room will be twice as large. Our chef, Marco Bell, has also written a new menu, and every waiter is being trained to explain it. From May, guests will dine at tables covered with fine white cloth, and our rental room upstairs will be available for private parties of up to thirty people. To receive a color brochure and a coupon for a free dessert, please leave your name and address after the tone. One small note: callers asking for mister Bell should use his direct line, 555-0177.","ja":"オリーブ・ガーデン・ビストロにお電話ありがとうございます。今週は改装のため休業しており、5月1日に営業を再開します。同じ建物で10年営業してまいりましたが、新たに賃貸契約を結び、食堂は2倍の広さになります。料理長のマルコ・ベルも新しいメニューを考案し、ウェイターは皆、その説明ができるよう研修を受けています。5月からは、上質な白い布を掛けたテーブルでお食事いただけます。2階の貸し部屋は、30名様までの貸し切りパーティーにご利用いただけます。カラーのパンフレットとデザート無料のクーポンをご希望の方は、発信音の後にお名前とご住所をお残しください。なお、ベルさんあてのお電話は、直通の555-0177へお願いします。","words":[["renovation","freq:renovation"],["lease","freq:lease"],["chef","freq:chef"],["waiter","freq:waiter"],["dine","freq:dine"],["cloth","freq:cloth"],["rental","freq:rental"],["brochure","freq:brochure"],["coupon","freq:coupon"],["mister","freq:mister"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the restaurant closed this week?","o":["It is being renovated.","The chef is on vacation.","It is moving to another city.","A private party is being held."],"a":0,"why":"closed this week for renovation（改装のため今週は休業）と言っている。"},{"q":"What will change about the dining room?","o":["It will move upstairs.","It will have fewer tables.","It will be open later.","It will be larger."],"a":3,"why":"our dining room will be twice as large（食堂が2倍の広さになる）とある。"},{"q":"How can callers get a coupon?","o":["By visiting on the first of May","By leaving their name and address","By calling the chef directly","By booking a private party"],"a":1,"why":"please leave your name and address after the tone（発信音の後に名前と住所を残す）と案内している。"}]},
{"id":"f-0009","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"ラジオ番組の案内","text":"You are listening to Book Hour on Radio Nine. Today's guest is the writer Helen Park, whose new novel we will publish in our studio shop next week. You can buy it in paper or as an e-book. Listeners with a yearly subscription to our magazine can read a free preview of the first chapter online tonight. Helen will also speak at the City Library on Saturday, and admission is free, so please come sometime between two and five. Before we begin, one correction. Last week I said that Helen was once a dentist. In fact, she was a nurse, and one kind caller helped me say it correctly today. The local media have praised this book highly, so let's find out why.","ja":"ラジオ・ナインの「ブック・アワー」をお聞きいただいています。今日のゲストは作家のヘレン・パークさんで、新作の小説は来週、スタジオの売店で発売します。紙の本でも電子書籍でもお求めいただけます。本誌を年間購読しているリスナーの方は、今夜、第1章の試し読みをオンラインで無料でご覧になれます。ヘレンさんは土曜に市立図書館でも講演します。入場は無料ですので、2時から5時の間のいつかにお越しください。始める前に、訂正が一つあります。先週、ヘレンさんは以前歯科医だったとお伝えしました。実際は看護師で、親切に電話をくださった方のおかげで、今日は正しくお伝えできます。地元の報道機関もこの本を高く評価しています。その理由を探っていきましょう。","words":[["publish","freq:publish"],["e-book","freq:e-book"],["subscription","freq:subscription"],["preview","freq:preview"],["admission","freq:admission"],["sometime","freq:sometime"],["dentist","freq:dentist"],["caller","freq:caller"],["correctly","freq:correctly"],["media","freq:media"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is Helen Park?","o":["A librarian","A radio host","An author","A magazine editor"],"a":2,"why":"the writer Helen Park, whose new novel ...（新作小説を出す作家）と紹介している。writer を author と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What can magazine subscribers do tonight?","o":["Read part of the book for free","Meet the writer at the studio","Buy the book at half price","Listen to the program again"],"a":0,"why":"can read a free preview of the first chapter（第1章の試し読みが無料でできる）とある。"},{"q":"What mistake did the speaker make last week?","o":["He gave the wrong date for an event.","He said the wrong title of the book.","He forgot to thank a caller.","He described the guest's former job wrongly."],"a":3,"why":"先週は dentist（歯科医）と言ったが、実際は nurse（看護師）だったと訂正している。以前の職業を間違えた。"}]},
{"id":"f-0010","page":"freq","group":"1〜100","kind":"試験対策講座の講義","text":"Welcome back to our reading skills class. Today's tactic is for questions that ask what the writer suggests but does not say directly. To answer them, you must infer the meaning from the text. First, underline the key words in the question. Next, look for a clue in the sentences that precede and follow those words in the passage. A good inference is always logical. It never goes further than the facts allow. If an answer choice seems to contradict any sentence in the passage, cross it out at once. When you are sure, fill in the oval on your answer sheet completely. For more practice, read the explanatory notes at the back of your book tonight. Now, let's try question one together.","ja":"読解スキル講座へお帰りなさい。今日の作戦は、筆者がはっきりとは述べずにほのめかしている内容を問う問題に使うものです。こうした問題に答えるには、本文から意味を推測しなければなりません。まず、設問の重要語に下線を引きます。次に、本文の中で、その語の前に来る文と後に続く文から手がかりを探します。よい推論は必ず筋が通っています。事実が許す範囲を超えることはありません。本文のどれかの文と矛盾しそうな選択肢は、すぐに消してください。確信が持てたら、解答用紙の楕円を完全に塗りつぶします。さらに練習したい人は、今夜、本の巻末にある解説を読んでください。では、第1問を一緒にやってみましょう。","words":[["tactic","freq:tactic"],["infer","freq:infer"],["underline","freq:underline"],["clue","freq:clue"],["precede","freq:precede"],["inference","freq:inference"],["logical","freq:logical"],["contradict","freq:contradict"],["oval","freq:oval"],["explanatory","freq:explanatory"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main topic of the talk?","o":["How to read faster","How to answer questions about suggested meaning","How to write a clear passage","How to fill in an answer sheet"],"a":1,"why":"筆者が直接は述べない内容を問う問題（what the writer suggests but does not say directly）への作戦を説明している。"},{"q":"What should students do first?","o":["Underline key words in the question","Read the notes at the back","Cross out a wrong choice","Fill in the oval"],"a":0,"why":"First, underline the key words in the question（まず設問の重要語に下線）と言っている。"},{"q":"What should students do with a choice that goes against the passage?","o":["Mark it as correct","Ask the teacher about it","Remove it right away","Check it again later"],"a":2,"why":"cross it out at once（すぐに消す）とある。cross out を remove と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0011","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"会議の閉会あいさつ","text":"Thank you all for joining this year's sales conference. Before the banquet begins, I have a few short notes. Dinner will be served shortly in the Rose Room, and every attendee should sit at the table shown on the back of the name card. After the meal, we will honor the recipient of this year's award for outstanding service, and each winner will also receive a certificate. A photographer will be taking pictures all evening, so please smile. Tomorrow's itinerary is on your chairs. Please note one change: the departure time of the bus to the factory is now eight thirty, not nine. Finally, next year's venue will be Vancouver. I hope to see you all there.","ja":"今年の営業会議にご参加いただき、ありがとうございます。宴会が始まる前に、短いお知らせがいくつかあります。夕食はまもなくローズ・ルームでお出しします。出席者の皆様は、名札の裏に書かれたテーブルにお座りください。食事の後、優れた働きをたたえる今年の賞の受賞者を表彰し、受賞者にはそれぞれ証明書もお渡しします。写真家が今晩ずっと撮影しますので、どうぞ笑顔でお願いします。明日の旅程表は椅子の上に置いてあります。変更が一つあります。工場行きのバスの出発時刻は、9時ではなく8時半になりました。最後に、来年の会場はバンクーバーです。皆様とまたお会いできることを願っています。","words":[["banquet","freq:banquet"],["shortly","freq:shortly"],["attendee","freq:attendee"],["recipient","freq:recipient"],["outstanding","freq:outstanding"],["certificate","freq:certificate"],["photographer","freq:photographer"],["itinerary","freq:itinerary"],["departure","freq:departure"],["venue","freq:venue"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where should attendees sit?","o":["Wherever they like","Next to their managers","At the table named on their name cards","In the front row"],"a":2,"why":"sit at the table shown on the back of the name card（名札の裏にあるテーブルに座る）と言っている。"},{"q":"What will happen after the meal?","o":["An award will be presented.","A bus will leave for the factory.","A group photo will be taken.","A new product will be shown."],"a":0,"why":"we will honor the recipient of this year's award（今年の賞の受賞者を表彰する）とある。"},{"q":"What has changed about tomorrow's schedule?","o":["The factory visit was canceled.","The bus will leave earlier.","The meeting moved to Vancouver.","Breakfast will be served later."],"a":1,"why":"バスの出発が eight thirty, not nine（9時ではなく8時半）になった。出発が早まっている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0012","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"住民への連絡（留守番電話）","text":"This is a message for every tenant of Maple Court. Starting Monday, we will renovate the entrance hall and the stairs on the east side. The architect has finished the plans, and the contractor will begin work at eight each morning. During this time, please use the rear exit near the parking lot. For safety reasons, we must prohibit residents from storing bicycles or boxes in the hallway closet until the work is done. On Thursday, a city officer will inspect the new fire doors, and a second inspection will follow when the stairs are finished. We apologize for the inconvenience and thank you for your understanding. If you have questions, please call the building office.","ja":"メープル・コートにお住まいの皆様へのお知らせです。月曜から、玄関ホールと東側の階段を改修します。建築家が設計を終え、請負業者が毎朝8時に作業を始めます。この期間は、駐車場近くの裏の出口をご利用ください。安全のため、工事が終わるまで、廊下の収納室に自転車や箱を置くことは禁止させていただきます。木曜に市の担当者が新しい防火扉を検査し、階段が完成した時点で2回目の検査を行います。ご不便をおかけしますことをおわびし、ご理解に感謝します。ご質問は建物の管理事務所までお電話ください。","words":[["tenant","freq:tenant"],["renovate","freq:renovate"],["architect","freq:architect"],["contractor","freq:contractor"],["exit","freq:exit"],["prohibit","freq:prohibit"],["closet","freq:closet"],["inspect","freq:inspect"],["inspection","freq:inspection"],["inconvenience","freq:inconvenience"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will be renovated?","o":["The parking lot","The roof","The fire doors","The entrance hall and some stairs"],"a":3,"why":"renovate the entrance hall and the stairs on the east side（玄関ホールと東側の階段を改修）とある。"},{"q":"What are residents asked to do during the work?","o":["Use a different exit","Park on the street","Leave home by eight","Call the architect"],"a":0,"why":"please use the rear exit near the parking lot（駐車場近くの裏の出口を使う）よう求めている。"},{"q":"What will happen on Thursday?","o":["The stairs will be finished.","New doors will be checked.","The closet will be emptied.","The office will be closed."],"a":1,"why":"a city officer will inspect the new fire doors（市の担当者が新しい防火扉を検査する）とある。inspect を check と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0013","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"店の広告","text":"Are you hungry for something new? The Blue Door café on Station Road now opens at seven every morning. Stop by for a hot beverage and a fresh sandwich made to order, or pick up a quick snack on your way to work. Every ingredient we use comes from farms within fifty kilometers. In the afternoon, try a slice of our lemon cake. Our customers say it is the most delicious dessert in town. And if it is your birthday, just tell your waitress when you order, and your coffee is free. The Blue Door, right across from the station. Come in and taste the difference today.","ja":"何か新しいものを食べたくてお腹がすいていませんか。ステーション通りのカフェ「ブルー・ドア」は、毎朝7時に開店するようになりました。温かい飲み物と、注文を受けてから作る新鮮なサンドイッチを召し上がりにお立ち寄りください。通勤の途中に、手軽な軽食を買うこともできます。当店で使う材料はすべて、50キロ以内の農場から届きます。午後には、レモンケーキをひと切れお試しください。お客様からは、町でいちばんおいしいデザートだと言われています。お誕生日の方は、注文の際にウェイトレスにお伝えいただくだけで、コーヒーが無料になります。ブルー・ドアは駅の真向かいです。今日お越しになって、違いを味わってください。","words":[["hungry","freq:hungry"],["café","freq:café"],["beverage","freq:beverage"],["sandwich","freq:sandwich"],["snack","freq:snack"],["ingredient","freq:ingredient"],["delicious","freq:delicious"],["dessert","freq:dessert"],["birthday","freq:birthday"],["waitress","freq:waitress"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has changed at the café?","o":["Its location","Its opening time","Its owner","Its prices"],"a":1,"why":"now opens at seven every morning（毎朝7時に開くようになった）と言っている。"},{"q":"What is said about the ingredients?","o":["They are organic.","They are imported.","They are delivered every hour.","They come from nearby farms."],"a":3,"why":"comes from farms within fifty kilometers（50キロ以内の農場から来る）とある。"},{"q":"How can a customer get free coffee?","o":["By ordering a dessert","By coming before seven","By telling the staff it is their birthday","By bringing a friend"],"a":2,"why":"if it is your birthday, just tell your waitress ... your coffee is free（誕生日だと伝えればコーヒーが無料）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0014","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"新入社員への説明","text":"Let me show you how to use the office equipment. The copier is in the corner by the window. To photocopy a document, first enter your password on the screen. If the machine runs out of ink, you will find a new cartridge in the top drawer of the gray cabinet. Please put used ones in the green folder box so that we can return them. To call another department, dial the four numbers on this list. The wireless mouse on each desk needs a new battery about once a month, and spare ones are kept at the front desk. Lastly, you can download the staff guide from our home page. Any questions so far?","ja":"事務所の機器の使い方をお見せします。コピー機は窓のそばの角にあります。書類をコピーするには、まず画面でパスワードを入力します。インクが切れたら、灰色の戸棚のいちばん上の引き出しに新しいカートリッジがあります。使用済みのものは返却できるよう、緑の書類箱に入れてください。ほかの部署に電話するには、この一覧にある4けたの番号をダイヤルします。各机の無線マウスは月に1回ほど電池の交換が必要で、予備は受付に置いてあります。最後に、社員向けの手引きは当社のホームページからダウンロードできます。ここまでで質問はありますか。","words":[["copier","freq:copier"],["photocopy","freq:photocopy"],["password","freq:password"],["ink","freq:ink"],["cartridge","freq:cartridge"],["drawer","freq:drawer"],["folder","freq:folder"],["dial","freq:dial"],["battery","freq:battery"],["download","freq:download"]],"qs":[{"q":"What must staff do before making a copy?","o":["Enter a password","Ask a manager","Fill in a form","Turn on the machine"],"a":0,"why":"first enter your password on the screen（まず画面でパスワードを入力）と言っている。"},{"q":"Where are new cartridges kept?","o":["At the front desk","In the green box","In a drawer of the gray cabinet","Next to the window"],"a":2,"why":"in the top drawer of the gray cabinet（灰色の戸棚のいちばん上の引き出し）とある。受付にあるのは予備の電池。"},{"q":"How can staff get the staff guide?","o":["By asking at the front desk","By downloading it","By calling another department","By copying it"],"a":1,"why":"you can download the staff guide from our home page（ホームページからダウンロードできる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0015","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"人事部からのお知らせ","text":"Good afternoon. This is a message from Human Resources about our workplace health program. From next month, every full-time employee will be eligible for free membership at the Lakeview fitness center, which has a gym and an indoor pool. The center is open every weekday from six in the morning until ten at night. Your membership will expire after one year, but you can renew it at no cost as long as you work here. We know that many of you have worked overtime this season, and we want you to stay healthy. As a small bonus, the first fifty people to sign up will receive a free sports bag. Please register at the HR desk by Friday.","ja":"こんにちは。人事部から、職場の健康づくり制度についてのお知らせです。来月から、常勤の従業員は全員、レイクビュー・フィットネスセンターの会員資格を無料で得られます。センターにはジムと屋内プールがあります。平日は毎日、朝6時から夜10時まで開いています。会員資格は1年で切れますが、当社で働いている間は無料で更新できます。今期は多くの方が残業をしたことを承知しており、皆さんには健康でいてほしいと考えています。ささやかな特典として、最初に申し込んだ50名にはスポーツバッグを差し上げます。金曜までに人事部の窓口で登録してください。","words":[["workplace","freq:workplace"],["eligible","freq:eligible"],["fitness","freq:fitness"],["gym","freq:gym"],["indoor","freq:indoor"],["weekday","freq:weekday"],["expire","freq:expire"],["renew","freq:renew"],["overtime","freq:overtime"],["bonus","freq:bonus"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who can get the free membership?","o":["All visitors","Part-time staff only","Managers only","Full-time employees"],"a":3,"why":"every full-time employee will be eligible（常勤の従業員は全員資格がある）とある。"},{"q":"What happens after one year?","o":["The membership ends unless it is renewed.","The fee goes up.","The center closes.","Members receive a bag."],"a":0,"why":"Your membership will expire after one year, but you can renew it（1年で切れるが更新できる）と言っている。"},{"q":"What will the first fifty people receive?","o":["A cash bonus","Extra days off","A sports bag","A free lesson"],"a":2,"why":"the first fifty people to sign up will receive a free sports bag（先着50名にスポーツバッグ）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0016","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"店内放送","text":"Attention, shoppers. Welcome to Greenfield Mall. For your convenience, a shopping cart is now available at every entrance. Today only, the Wool House in aisle four is offering any sweater for thirty dollars. Just look for the red tag. Next door, Star Jewelry is selling silver rings at half price until five. If you are shopping with small children, visit the new mini play area on the second floor, where trained staff will watch them for up to one hour. Finally, every shopper who spends more than fifty dollars today will receive a free bag with the mall's new logo. Simply show your receipts at the information desk. Thank you for shopping with us.","ja":"お買い物中の皆様にお知らせします。グリーンフィールド・モールへようこそ。皆様の便宜のため、すべての入口でショッピングカートをご利用いただけるようになりました。本日限り、4番通路のウール・ハウスでは、どのセーターも30ドルです。赤い札が目印です。お隣のスター・ジュエリーでは、5時まで銀の指輪を半額で販売しています。小さなお子様連れの方は、2階の新しい小さな遊び場をご利用ください。研修を受けた係員が最長1時間お子様をお預かりします。最後に、本日50ドルを超えてお買い上げの方には、モールの新しいロゴ入りのバッグを差し上げます。案内所でレシートをご提示ください。ご来店ありがとうございます。","words":[["shoppers","freq:shopper"],["Mall","freq:mall"],["convenience","freq:convenience"],["cart","freq:cart"],["aisle","freq:aisle"],["sweater","freq:sweater"],["tag","freq:tag"],["Jewelry","freq:jewelry"],["mini","freq:mini"],["logo","freq:logo"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is on sale at the Wool House?","o":["Rings","Sweaters","Bags","Children's toys"],"a":1,"why":"offering any sweater for thirty dollars（どのセーターも30ドル）とある。指輪が半額なのは隣のスター・ジュエリー。"},{"q":"What is available on the second floor?","o":["A place for children to play","A jewelry store","The information desk","A café"],"a":0,"why":"the new mini play area on the second floor（2階の新しい小さな遊び場）と言っている。"},{"q":"How can shoppers get a free bag?","o":["By arriving before five","By buying a sweater","By using a shopping cart","By spending over fifty dollars"],"a":3,"why":"every shopper who spends more than fifty dollars ... will receive a free bag（50ドルを超えて買うとバッグがもらえる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0017","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"港のアナウンス","text":"Good morning, and welcome to Harbor Point. This announcement is for passengers on the three-day cruise to the Sand Islands. Boarding begins at ten at Terminal B. Please leave your large baggage with our staff in front of the building, but keep your passport and any briefcase or small bag with you. The weather is cloudy this morning, but it will be sunny by the time we sail. One note for drivers: Highway 9 is very busy with commuter traffic until nine, so allow extra time. If your car needs attention while you are away, a mechanic at the port garage can look at it. Overnight parking costs twelve dollars a day. We wish you a pleasant trip.","ja":"おはようございます。ハーバー・ポイントへようこそ。サンド諸島への3日間の船旅にご参加のお客様へのご案内です。ご乗船は10時にBターミナルで始まります。大きな手荷物は建物の前で係員にお預けください。ただし、パスポートと書類かばんや小さなかばんは、お手元にお持ちください。今朝は曇っていますが、出航の頃には晴れる見込みです。お車の方へ一点。9号幹線道路は9時まで通勤者の車でたいへん混みますので、時間に余裕を持ってください。ご不在の間にお車の点検が必要でしたら、港の修理工場の整備士が見ることもできます。夜をまたぐ駐車は1日12ドルです。どうぞよい旅を。","words":[["cruise","freq:cruise"],["Terminal","freq:terminal"],["baggage","freq:baggage"],["briefcase","freq:briefcase"],["cloudy","freq:cloudy"],["sunny","freq:sunny"],["Highway","freq:highway"],["commuter","freq:commuter"],["mechanic","freq:mechanic"],["Overnight","freq:overnight"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should passengers keep with them?","o":["Their car keys","Their large bags","Their passports","Their parking tickets"],"a":2,"why":"keep your passport and any briefcase or small bag with you（パスポートと小さなかばんは手元に）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the weather?","o":["It will improve later.","It will rain all day.","It will be windy at sea.","It will be cold tonight."],"a":0,"why":"cloudy this morning, but it will be sunny by the time we sail（今朝は曇りだが出航の頃には晴れる）とある。"},{"q":"Why should drivers allow extra time?","o":["A road is closed.","There is heavy traffic.","The garage is far away.","Parking is limited."],"a":1,"why":"Highway 9 is very busy with commuter traffic（9号線は通勤の車で混んでいる）ためと言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0018","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"地域ニュース","text":"In local news, the Eastside Youth Club is asking for your help. The club's soccer team has reached the national finals, which will be held at Victory Stadium in June, but it needs money for travel. You can donate in three ways. First, bring cans and bottles to the club's warehouse on Dock Street. The club will recycle them for cash. Second, put coins in the yellow container at any Marlow supermarket. Third, make a donation online. The dates of the team's games are on the club calendar, and results will appear in its monthly newsletter. For more information, look at the bulletin board at the community center. Now, here is the weather.","ja":"地域のニュースです。イーストサイド青少年クラブが皆さんの協力を求めています。クラブのサッカーチームが全国大会の決勝に進み、6月にビクトリー・スタジアムで試合が行われますが、遠征の費用が足りません。寄付の方法は3つあります。1つ目は、缶やびんをドック通りにあるクラブの倉庫に持ち込むことです。クラブがそれを再利用に回してお金に換えます。2つ目は、マーロウ・スーパー各店の黄色い容器に硬貨を入れることです。3つ目は、オンラインでの寄付です。試合の日程はクラブの予定表に載っており、結果は月刊の会報に掲載されます。詳しくは、公民館の掲示板をご覧ください。では、天気予報です。","words":[["soccer","freq:soccer"],["Stadium","freq:stadium"],["donate","freq:donate"],["warehouse","freq:warehouse"],["recycle","freq:recycle"],["container","freq:container"],["donation","freq:donation"],["calendar","freq:calendar"],["newsletter","freq:newsletter"],["bulletin","freq:bulletin"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why does the club need money?","o":["To build a new stadium","To buy uniforms","To hire a coach","To pay for travel"],"a":3,"why":"it needs money for travel（遠征の費用が必要）と言っている。"},{"q":"What will the club do with cans and bottles?","o":["Use them at games","Recycle them for money","Sell them at supermarkets","Store them until June"],"a":1,"why":"The club will recycle them for cash（再利用に回してお金に換える）とある。"},{"q":"Where can listeners find more information?","o":["On a bulletin board","In a supermarket","At the stadium","On the radio station's Web site"],"a":0,"why":"look at the bulletin board at the community center（公民館の掲示板を見る）と案内している。"}]},
{"id":"f-0019","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"Good evening. I am your announcer, Lee Harmon, with tonight's business news. Two of the region's largest Internet companies have agreed to a merger. Northnet, a service provider with two million customers, will join Clearline, which is known for its innovative research lab. The new company will be led by Clearline's president, who will supervise both teams from March. An independent audit of the two firms' finances will be completed next month. One financial advisor told us that the deal will have a positive impact on prices, since the two firms will share the cost of new cables. However, another aspect worries workers: no one has said how many jobs will remain. We will bring you more details tomorrow.","ja":"こんばんは。アナウンサーのリー・ハーモンが今夜の経済ニュースをお伝えします。この地域で最大級のインターネット企業2社が合併に合意しました。200万人の顧客を持つ接続事業者のノースネットが、革新的な研究所で知られるクリアラインと一緒になります。新会社はクリアラインの社長が率い、3月から両方のチームを監督します。2社の財務についての独立した監査は来月終わる予定です。ある金融の助言者は、2社が新しいケーブルの費用を分け合うため、この取引は料金によい影響を与えると話しています。ただ、別の面で従業員は不安を抱いています。いくつの職が残るのか、誰も明らかにしていないからです。詳しくは明日お伝えします。","words":[["announcer","freq:announcer"],["merger","freq:merger"],["provider","freq:provider"],["innovative","freq:innovative"],["lab","freq:lab"],["supervise","freq:supervise"],["audit","freq:audit"],["advisor","freq:advisor"],["impact","freq:impact"],["aspect","freq:aspect"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the news report mainly about?","o":["A new research lab","Two companies joining together","A rise in Internet prices","A change in the law"],"a":1,"why":"Two of the region's largest Internet companies have agreed to a merger（2社が合併に合意）とある。merger を joining together と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will be completed next month?","o":["A check of the companies' finances","The laying of new cables","The hiring of a president","A customer survey"],"a":0,"why":"An independent audit of the two firms' finances will be completed next month（財務の監査が来月終わる）とある。"},{"q":"What are workers worried about?","o":["Higher prices","Longer working hours","Moving to another city","How many jobs will remain"],"a":3,"why":"no one has said how many jobs will remain（いくつの職が残るか誰も言っていない）点が不安だと伝えている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0020","page":"freq","group":"101〜200","kind":"講師の話","text":"Thank you for your feedback on last week's practice test. Almost every respondent said that the reading comprehension section was the hardest part, so let's look at it again. The passage was a leaflet about a common medication. Many of you chose answer B in question three, but B is a distractor. It uses words from the leaflet, yet the idea is unreal: no doctor would give that advice. Next time, skim the whole text first and then read the question. For homework, please rewrite your answers to questions three to six and explain your reasons. The deadline for submission is Thursday. If you would like to inquire about your score, please see me after class.","ja":"先週の模擬試験について感想を寄せてくれてありがとうございます。回答者のほぼ全員が、読解の部分がいちばん難しかったと答えていましたので、もう一度見てみましょう。本文は、よく使われる薬についての説明書でした。第3問で多くの人がBを選びましたが、Bは誤答に誘う選択肢です。説明書の語を使ってはいますが、内容は現実離れしています。そんな助言をする医師はいません。次回は、まず全文にざっと目を通し、それから設問を読んでください。宿題として、第3問から第6問の答えを書き直し、理由を説明してください。提出の締め切りは木曜です。自分の点数について問い合わせたい人は、授業の後に私のところへ来てください。","words":[["feedback","freq:feedback"],["respondent","freq:respondent"],["comprehension","freq:comprehension"],["medication","freq:medication"],["distractor","freq:distractor"],["unreal","freq:unreal"],["skim","freq:skim"],["rewrite","freq:rewrite"],["submission","freq:submission"],["inquire","freq:inquire"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did most students find hardest?","o":["The listening section","The grammar questions","The reading section","The time limit"],"a":2,"why":"the reading comprehension section was the hardest part（読解の部分がいちばん難しかった）とほぼ全員が答えている。"},{"q":"What does the speaker advise students to do next time?","o":["Read the question first","Look over the whole text first","Choose answer B","Ask a doctor"],"a":1,"why":"skim the whole text first and then read the question（まず全文にざっと目を通す）と助言している。skim を look over と言い換えている。"},{"q":"When is the homework due?","o":["Thursday","Tomorrow","Next week","After class today"],"a":0,"why":"The deadline for submission is Thursday（提出の締め切りは木曜）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0021","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"社長の発表","text":"Good morning, everyone. I have important news. In October, we will relocate our main office from the city center to Westbrook Park, where we will be headquartered in a new six-story building. The developer has promised completion by the end of September. The new office can accommodate all four hundred of us, and each team will have its own suite. There will also be a staff lounge on the top floor. I know that some of you are worried about a longer commute, so a free shuttle will run from Central Station every fifteen minutes. We believe that more space and better light will raise productivity and make work more pleasant for everyone. Details will follow by e-mail this week.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。重要なお知らせがあります。10月に、本社を市の中心部からウエストブルック・パークへ移転し、新しい6階建ての建物に本社を置くことになります。開発業者は9月末までの完成を約束しています。新しい事務所は400人全員を収容でき、各チームに専用の続き部屋が用意されます。最上階には社員用のラウンジもできます。通勤が長くなることを心配している方もいると思いますので、中央駅から15分おきに無料のシャトルバスを走らせます。より広く、より明るい環境が生産性を高め、誰にとっても仕事が快適になると考えています。詳しくは今週メールでお伝えします。","words":[["relocate","freq:relocate"],["headquartered","freq:headquarter"],["developer","freq:developer"],["completion","freq:completion"],["accommodate","freq:accommodate"],["suite","freq:suite"],["lounge","freq:lounge"],["commute","freq:commute"],["shuttle","freq:shuttle"],["productivity","freq:productivity"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the speaker announcing?","o":["A new president","A move to a new office","The opening of a branch","A change in working hours"],"a":1,"why":"we will relocate our main office ... to Westbrook Park（本社をウエストブルック・パークへ移転する）と発表している。"},{"q":"When is the building expected to be finished?","o":["By the end of September","In October","This week","Next year"],"a":0,"why":"The developer has promised completion by the end of September（9月末までの完成）とある。10月は移転の時期。"},{"q":"What will the company provide for staff with a longer trip to work?","o":["Extra pay","A parking space","Flexible hours","A free bus service"],"a":3,"why":"a free shuttle will run from Central Station（中央駅から無料のシャトルバスを走らせる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0022","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"ホテルの客室案内","text":"Welcome to the Linden Hotel. Here is some information about your stay. A complimentary breakfast buffet is served in the Garden Room from six thirty until ten, with fresh bread, fruit, and salad. Room service is available until midnight. In your room, you will find extra towels in the bathroom and a reading lamp beside the sofa. If you would like to stay another night, please ask the front desk about availability as early as you can, because occupancy is very high during the trade fair this week. Finally, if you need a cab to the airport or the station, our doorman will call one for you. Please allow ten minutes. We hope you enjoy your stay.","ja":"リンデン・ホテルへようこそ。ご滞在についてのご案内です。無料の朝食ビュッフェは、ガーデン・ルームで6時半から10時までご用意しており、焼きたてのパン、果物、サラダがございます。ルームサービスは午前0時までご利用いただけます。お部屋には、浴室に予備のタオル、ソファの横に読書用のランプがございます。もう1泊をご希望の場合は、できるだけ早く、空き状況をフロントにお尋ねください。今週は見本市のため、客室の稼働率がたいへん高くなっております。最後に、空港や駅までタクシーが必要な場合は、ドアマンがお呼びします。10分ほどお時間をください。どうぞごゆっくりお過ごしください。","words":[["complimentary","freq:complimentary"],["buffet","freq:buffet"],["salad","freq:salad"],["midnight","freq:midnight"],["bathroom","freq:bathroom"],["lamp","freq:lamp"],["sofa","freq:sofa"],["availability","freq:availability"],["occupancy","freq:occupancy"],["cab","freq:cab"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is said about breakfast?","o":["It costs extra.","It is served in the rooms.","It is free.","It ends at midnight."],"a":2,"why":"A complimentary breakfast buffet（無料の朝食ビュッフェ）とある。complimentary は「無料の」。"},{"q":"Why should guests ask early about staying another night?","o":["The hotel is nearly full this week.","The price will go up.","The front desk closes at ten.","The trade fair ends tomorrow."],"a":0,"why":"occupancy is very high during the trade fair（見本市で稼働率がとても高い）ためと説明している。"},{"q":"Who will call a cab for guests?","o":["The room service staff","The front desk manager","The driver","The doorman"],"a":3,"why":"our doorman will call one for you（ドアマンが呼ぶ）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0023","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"経理部からの連絡","text":"This is a reminder from the administrative office about expense claims. Lately, a number of forms have reached us incomplete, and this slows down the paperwork for everyone. According to the memorandum sent in May, every claim over two hundred dollars needs the signature of your department head. Only a department head has the authority to authorize such a payment. Before you hand in a form, please verify that the date and amount of each transaction match your receipts. Forms without receipts will be returned. If you have questions, do not reply to this message. All correspondence about claims should go to Ms. Ortiz in Room 210. Thank you for your cooperation.","ja":"経費の請求について、管理事務室からのお知らせです。このところ、不備のある用紙がいくつも届いており、全員の事務処理が遅れています。5月にお送りした社内連絡のとおり、200ドルを超える請求にはすべて、部門長の署名が必要です。そうした支払いを許可する権限があるのは部門長だけです。用紙を提出する前に、各取引の日付と金額が領収書と合っているかを確かめてください。領収書のない用紙は返却します。ご質問がある場合、このメッセージには返信しないでください。請求に関する連絡はすべて、210号室のオルティスさんあてにお願いします。ご協力ありがとうございます。","words":[["administrative","freq:administrative"],["incomplete","freq:incomplete"],["paperwork","freq:paperwork"],["memorandum","freq:memorandum"],["signature","freq:signature"],["authority","freq:authority"],["authorize","freq:authorize"],["verify","freq:verify"],["transaction","freq:transaction"],["correspondence","freq:correspondence"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does the speaker mention?","o":["Receipts are being lost.","Forms are not filled in fully.","Payments are late.","A manager is away."],"a":1,"why":"a number of forms have reached us incomplete（不備のある用紙がいくつも届いている）と言っている。"},{"q":"What is needed for claims over two hundred dollars?","o":["A department head's signature","A second receipt","A copy of the memorandum","A visit to Room 210"],"a":0,"why":"every claim over two hundred dollars needs the signature of your department head（部門長の署名が必要）とある。"},{"q":"Where should questions be sent?","o":["To the administrative office","To the department head","To Ms. Ortiz","To the sender of this message"],"a":2,"why":"All correspondence about claims should go to Ms. Ortiz in Room 210（連絡はオルティスさんへ）とある。このメッセージに返信してはいけない。"}]},
{"id":"f-0024","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"社内イベントの案内","text":"Hello, everyone. To celebrate the company's twentieth anniversary, we are holding a staff picnic at Pine Lake Park on Saturday, June 8. A local restaurant will cater lunch, and refreshments will be served all afternoon. There will even be an ice cream stand with a different flavor every hour. If you like sports, you can join a baseball game at one or a basketball contest at three. For those who prefer something quiet, a guide will lead a one-hour hike around the lake. Families are welcome. If the day turns out to be rainy, we will move everything to the company gym. Please tell your manager by Friday how many people you will bring.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。会社の創立20周年を祝って、6月8日の土曜にパイン・レイク公園で社員のピクニックを開きます。地元のレストランが昼食を仕出しし、午後はずっと軽い飲食物をお出しします。1時間ごとに味が変わるアイスクリームの屋台まであります。スポーツが好きな方は、1時の野球の試合か、3時のバスケットボールの対抗戦に参加できます。静かに過ごしたい方には、ガイドが湖のまわりを1時間ハイキングで案内します。ご家族も歓迎です。当日が雨の場合は、すべて会社の体育館に移します。金曜までに、何人で参加するかを上司に伝えてください。","words":[["anniversary","freq:anniversary"],["picnic","freq:picnic"],["cater","freq:cater"],["refreshments","freq:refreshment"],["ice cream","freq:ice cream"],["flavor","freq:flavor"],["baseball","freq:baseball"],["basketball","freq:basketball"],["hike","freq:hike"],["rainy","freq:rainy"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the event being held?","o":["To welcome new staff","To celebrate the company's anniversary","To open a new park","To thank customers"],"a":1,"why":"To celebrate the company's twentieth anniversary（創立20周年を祝って）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen at three o'clock?","o":["A basketball contest","A baseball game","A hike","Lunch"],"a":0,"why":"a baseball game at one or a basketball contest at three（1時に野球、3時にバスケットボール）とある。"},{"q":"What should staff do by Friday?","o":["Pay for lunch","Choose a sport","Book the gym","Tell their manager how many will come"],"a":3,"why":"tell your manager by Friday how many people you will bring（金曜までに参加人数を上司に伝える）よう求めている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0025","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"研修の開始あいさつ","text":"Welcome to the first day of our sales training. My name is Carla Diaz, and I will coordinate the program. The duration of the course is two weeks. Each morning, a different presenter from the head office will speak, and in the afternoon your trainer will work with you in small groups. Every trainee will receive a little homework each night. It should take about thirty minutes. We want this course to be productive, so please be thorough when you complete the questionnaire at the end of each day. Your answers help us improve. On the final Friday, there will be a short test of your proficiency with our ordering software. Now, let's begin by introducing ourselves.","ja":"営業研修の初日へようこそ。カーラ・ディアスと申します。この研修のまとめ役を務めます。研修の期間は2週間です。毎朝、本社から来た発表者が日替わりで話をし、午後は指導員が少人数のグループで皆さんを指導します。研修生には毎晩、少しずつ宿題が出ます。30分ほどで終わるはずです。この研修を実りあるものにしたいので、毎日の終わりにアンケートに答えるときは、丁寧に書いてください。皆さんの回答が改善に役立ちます。最終日の金曜には、当社の受注ソフトをどれだけ使いこなせるかを見る短いテストがあります。では、自己紹介から始めましょう。","words":[["coordinate","freq:coordinate"],["duration","freq:duration"],["presenter","freq:presenter"],["trainer","freq:trainer"],["trainee","freq:trainee"],["homework","freq:homework"],["productive","freq:productive"],["thorough","freq:thorough"],["questionnaire","freq:questionnaire"],["proficiency","freq:proficiency"]],"qs":[{"q":"How long does the course last?","o":["One day","One week","Two weeks","One month"],"a":2,"why":"The duration of the course is two weeks（研修の期間は2週間）とある。"},{"q":"What will trainees do each afternoon?","o":["Listen to a speaker from the head office","Work in small groups","Take a test","Visit customers"],"a":1,"why":"in the afternoon your trainer will work with you in small groups（午後は少人数のグループで指導を受ける）とある。本社の発表者の話は午前。"},{"q":"What will happen on the last Friday?","o":["A test on the ordering software","A party for the trainees","A visit to the head office","A talk by the president"],"a":0,"why":"a short test of your proficiency with our ordering software（受注ソフトの習熟度を見る短いテスト）がある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0026","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"店の広告","text":"Back-to-school season is here, and Page One has everything you need at an affordable price. Our bookstore on Elm Street is offering every notebook, pen, and other stationery item at twenty percent off this week. Need a calculator for math class? We have twelve models, and any salesperson will be glad to help you choose. Here is a real bargain: buy three textbooks and get a fourth free. This offer is exclusive to members of our reading club. Not a member yet? You can subscribe at the counter in two minutes, and renewal each year costs only five dollars. Page One is next to the Elm Street grocery store. We are open every day until eight.","ja":"新学期の季節がやって来ました。ページ・ワンには、必要なものがすべて手ごろな価格でそろっています。エルム通りの当書店では今週、ノート、ペン、そのほかの文房具がすべて2割引です。数学の授業に計算機が必要ですか。12機種を取りそろえており、販売員が喜んで選ぶお手伝いをします。本当にお買い得な話をひとつ。教科書を3冊買うと、4冊目が無料になります。この特典は読書クラブの会員限定です。まだ会員でない方は、カウンターで2分で加入できます。毎年の更新はたったの5ドルです。ページ・ワンはエルム通りの食料品店の隣です。毎日8時まで営業しています。","words":[["affordable","freq:affordable"],["bookstore","freq:bookstore"],["stationery","freq:stationery"],["calculator","freq:calculator"],["salesperson","freq:salesperson"],["bargain","freq:bargain"],["exclusive","freq:exclusive"],["subscribe","freq:subscribe"],["renewal","freq:renewal"],["grocery","freq:grocery"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is twenty percent off this week?","o":["Textbooks","Calculators","Club memberships","Stationery"],"a":3,"why":"every notebook, pen, and other stationery item at twenty percent off（文房具がすべて2割引）とある。"},{"q":"Who can get a fourth textbook free?","o":["Students with an ID","Members of the reading club","Customers who pay in cash","Anyone who comes before eight"],"a":1,"why":"This offer is exclusive to members of our reading club（読書クラブの会員限定）と言っている。"},{"q":"How much does it cost to renew a membership each year?","o":["Five dollars","Two dollars","Twelve dollars","Twenty dollars"],"a":0,"why":"renewal each year costs only five dollars（毎年の更新は5ドル）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0027","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"工場の朝の連絡","text":"Good morning, team. I have an urgent notice about yesterday's shipment. A customer in Germany found a defect in several of the pumps we sent last week. It seems that one piece of machinery on Line 2 was set up wrongly. Until the engineers have checked it, please stack all finished pumps from Line 2 at the north dock and do not load them. Our usual carrier will not collect them today. If we find any defective units, we will send new ones by express courier at our own cost. Our distribution center ships worldwide, so one small mistake here can be seen in thirty countries. Thank you for your quick action on this.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。昨日の出荷について、緊急のお知らせです。ドイツのお客様が、先週お送りしたポンプのうち数台に欠陥を見つけました。2番ラインの機械の1台が、誤って設定されていたようです。技術者の点検が終わるまで、2番ラインでできあがったポンプはすべて北側の荷さばき場に積んでおき、積み込まないでください。今日は、いつもの運送会社は引き取りに来ません。欠陥のある製品が見つかった場合は、当社の負担で、速達の宅配便で新しいものを送ります。当社の流通センターは世界中に出荷しています。ここでの小さなミス一つが、30か国で目に触れることになります。迅速な対応に感謝します。","words":[["urgent","freq:urgent"],["defect","freq:defect"],["machinery","freq:machinery"],["stack","freq:stack"],["dock","freq:dock"],["carrier","freq:carrier"],["defective","freq:defective"],["courier","freq:courier"],["distribution","freq:distribution"],["worldwide","freq:worldwide"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem was found?","o":["Some products had a fault.","A shipment was lost.","A customer did not pay.","A truck broke down."],"a":0,"why":"A customer in Germany found a defect in several of the pumps（数台のポンプに欠陥が見つかった）とある。"},{"q":"What should workers do with pumps from Line 2?","o":["Load them at once","Send them to Germany","Keep them at the north dock","Throw them away"],"a":2,"why":"stack all finished pumps from Line 2 at the north dock and do not load them（北側の荷さばき場に積み、積み込まない）と指示している。"},{"q":"How will replacement units be sent?","o":["By the usual carrier","By express courier","By sea","By the customer's own truck"],"a":1,"why":"we will send new ones by express courier at our own cost（速達の宅配便で送る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0028","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"ビル管理室からの放送","text":"May I have your attention, please. This is the building office. Tomorrow morning, a painter will be working in the third-floor hallway, so you may see a ladder and some covers on the floor. Please walk carefully. At the same time, the installation of the new photocopier in Room 305 will take place, and a plumber will repair the leak in the kitchen ceiling. We know that the noise may annoy some of you, but in spite of the work, all offices will stay open. One more thing: our cleaner has asked everyone to put garbage only in the designated bins near the elevators, not in the hallway. Thank you for your help.","ja":"皆様にお知らせします。こちらは建物の管理室です。明日の午前、3階の廊下で塗装工が作業をしますので、はしごや床の覆いを見かけることがあります。足元にご注意ください。同じ時間に、305号室で新しいコピー機の設置が行われ、配管工が台所の天井の水漏れを修理します。騒音でご迷惑をおかけするかもしれませんが、工事があっても、すべての事務所は通常どおり開いています。もう一点。清掃員からのお願いです。ごみは廊下ではなく、エレベーター近くの指定されたごみ箱にだけ入れてください。ご協力ありがとうございます。","words":[["painter","freq:painter"],["ladder","freq:ladder"],["installation","freq:installation"],["photocopier","freq:photocopier"],["leak","freq:leak"],["annoy","freq:annoy"],["spite","freq:spite"],["cleaner","freq:cleaner"],["garbage","freq:garbage"],["designated","freq:designate"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where will the painter be working?","o":["In Room 305","In the kitchen","Near the elevators","In the third-floor hallway"],"a":3,"why":"a painter will be working in the third-floor hallway（3階の廊下で塗装工が作業する）とある。"},{"q":"What will be repaired tomorrow?","o":["A photocopier","A water leak","An elevator","A ladder"],"a":1,"why":"a plumber will repair the leak in the kitchen ceiling（台所の天井の水漏れを修理）とある。コピー機は新しく設置されるもの。"},{"q":"What does the cleaner ask people to do?","o":["Use the designated bins","Stay out of the kitchen","Close their offices","Clean their own desks"],"a":0,"why":"put garbage only in the designated bins near the elevators（指定のごみ箱にだけ入れる）よう求めている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0029","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"薬局の店内放送","text":"Good afternoon, and thank you for shopping at Green Cross Pharmacy. Winter is here, and the flu has been spreading quickly in our city lately. Doctors advise everyone to get a flu shot annually, and you can get one here without an appointment. It is a myth that healthy people seldom catch the flu. It commonly affects people of every age. If you need to pick up a prescription, please take a number at the back counter. We are sorry that some patrons were unhappy with the long wait last week, so we have added two more staff members. And if you are trying to quit smoking, ask about our free advice service. Our dental care products are also on sale today.","ja":"こんにちは。グリーンクロス薬局をご利用いただきありがとうございます。冬になり、このところ市内でインフルエンザが急速に広がっています。医師は、誰もが毎年予防接種を受けるよう勧めています。当店では予約なしで受けられます。健康な人はめったにインフルエンザにかからない、というのは誤解です。どの年齢の人も普通にかかります。処方薬を受け取る方は、奥のカウンターで番号札をお取りください。先週は待ち時間が長く、ご不満を持たれたお客様がいらっしゃいましたので、係員を2名増やしました。禁煙したい方は、無料の相談サービスについてお尋ねください。本日は歯のお手入れ用品もお買い得です。","words":[["flu","freq:flu"],["lately","freq:lately"],["annually","freq:annually"],["seldom","freq:seldom"],["commonly","freq:commonly"],["prescription","freq:prescription"],["patrons","freq:patron"],["unhappy","freq:unhappy"],["quit","freq:quit"],["dental","freq:dental"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the speaker say about flu shots at the store?","o":["They are free.","They are only for older people.","No appointment is needed.","They are given at the back counter."],"a":2,"why":"you can get one here without an appointment（予約なしで受けられる）とある。"},{"q":"Why did the store add more staff?","o":["Customers had to wait a long time.","The store became larger.","The flu made some staff sick.","A sale is being held."],"a":0,"why":"some patrons were unhappy with the long wait（待ち時間が長く不満が出た）ため、2名増やしたと言っている。"},{"q":"What is on sale today?","o":["Flu medicine","Dental care products","Vitamins","Smoking aids"],"a":1,"why":"Our dental care products are also on sale today（歯のお手入れ用品がお買い得）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0030","page":"freq","group":"201〜300","kind":"地域ラジオのお知らせ","text":"This weekend, Harbor City will hold its first Winter Arts Fair, and young and old alike are invited. It may seem illogical to hold a fair in January, but all events are indoors at the Civic Hall. You will find a photography show, a sculpture garden made of ice, and a display of each classic automobile owned by the city museum. The captain of our fire department will judge a soup recipe contest at noon, and a delegate from our sister city in Norway will give the prizes. To enter the contest, fill in the online form by Thursday. Please do not omit your phone number. We will have to delete any entry without one. See you there!","ja":"今週末、ハーバー・シティでは初めての「冬の芸術祭」が開かれます。若い方も年配の方も同じように歓迎します。1月に祭りを開くのは理屈に合わないように思えるかもしれませんが、催しはすべて市民ホールの屋内で行われます。写真展、氷でできた彫刻の庭、そして市立博物館が所有するクラシックカーの展示がご覧になれます。正午には消防署の隊長がスープの調理法コンテストの審査をし、ノルウェーの姉妹都市から来た代表が賞を手渡します。コンテストに参加するには、木曜までにオンラインの用紙に記入してください。電話番号は省かないでください。番号のない申し込みは削除せざるを得ません。会場でお会いしましょう。","words":[["alike","freq:alike"],["illogical","freq:illogical"],["photography","freq:photography"],["sculpture","freq:sculpture"],["automobile","freq:automobile"],["captain","freq:captain"],["recipe","freq:recipe"],["delegate","freq:delegate"],["omit","freq:omit"],["delete","freq:delete"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where will the fair be held?","o":["In a park","At the city museum","At the fire station","Inside the Civic Hall"],"a":3,"why":"all events are indoors at the Civic Hall（催しはすべて市民ホールの屋内）とある。"},{"q":"Who will judge the contest?","o":["A museum director","The head of the fire department","A visitor from Norway","A radio host"],"a":1,"why":"The captain of our fire department will judge（消防署の隊長が審査する）とある。ノルウェーの代表は賞を渡す役。"},{"q":"What will happen to entries without a phone number?","o":["They will be removed.","They will be judged last.","They will be returned by mail.","They will be accepted on Friday."],"a":0,"why":"We will have to delete any entry without one（番号のない申し込みは削除する）とある。delete を remove と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0031","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"学生への説明会","text":"Good morning, and welcome to the business department. This talk is for students who want to enroll in our summer internship program. Each intern will spend six weeks at a local company during the break after the spring semester. Before you start, you must attend a one-day orientation on May 20. There you will receive an information packet with a short booklet about office rules. You do not need to buy a textbook. The program is optional, but it counts toward your final grade. Our career advisors are very knowledgeable about local employers, so please talk to them before you choose a company. Application forms are on the table by the door.","ja":"おはようございます。経営学科へようこそ。この話は、夏の実務研修プログラムに登録したい学生のためのものです。実習生はそれぞれ、春学期の後の休みに、地元の企業で6週間を過ごします。始める前に、5月20日にある1日の説明会に必ず出席してください。そこで、職場の決まりについての短い小冊子が入った資料一式を受け取ります。教科書を買う必要はありません。このプログラムは任意ですが、最終成績に算入されます。就職相談の担当者は地元の雇用主についてとても詳しいので、企業を選ぶ前に相談してください。応募用紙はドアのそばの机の上にあります。","words":[["enroll","freq:enroll"],["internship","freq:internship"],["intern","freq:intern"],["semester","freq:semester"],["orientation","freq:orientation"],["packet","freq:packet"],["booklet","freq:booklet"],["textbook","freq:textbook"],["optional","freq:optional"],["knowledgeable","freq:knowledgeable"]],"qs":[{"q":"How long is the internship?","o":["One day","Six weeks","One semester","Two months"],"a":1,"why":"Each intern will spend six weeks at a local company（地元企業で6週間）とある。"},{"q":"What will students receive at the orientation?","o":["A packet of information","A textbook","A final grade","A list of employers"],"a":0,"why":"you will receive an information packet with a short booklet（小冊子入りの資料一式を受け取る）とある。教科書は買う必要がない。"},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest students do before choosing a company?","o":["Visit the company","Read the booklet","Talk to a career advisor","Finish the spring semester"],"a":2,"why":"please talk to them before you choose a company（企業を選ぶ前に相談する）と勧めている。them は career advisors。"}]},
{"id":"f-0032","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"駅のアナウンス","text":"We are sorry to interrupt your journey. This is the conductor speaking. Because of windy weather on the coast, the ferry that connects with this train at Port Hale will not sail this afternoon. Passengers in transit to the islands may choose one of two options. You can stay on the train and take tomorrow's first boat. In that case, we will give you a hotel voucher at the station. Or you can ask for a cancellation of your ticket and receive your money back. Either way, please show your booking confirmation to the staff at Port Hale. If you booked a sleeping cabin on the boat, please tell us promptly so that we can move your booking.","ja":"ご乗車中に失礼いたします。車掌からのお知らせです。沿岸部の強風のため、ポート・ヘイルでこの列車に接続するフェリーは、本日午後は欠航となります。島へ乗り継ぐお客様は、2つのうちどちらかをお選びいただけます。このまま列車に乗り、明日の始発の船をご利用いただく方法です。その場合は、駅でホテルの引換券をお渡しします。もう一つは、乗車券の取り消しを申し出て、払い戻しを受ける方法です。いずれの場合も、ポート・ヘイルの係員に予約確認書をお見せください。船の寝台個室を予約されている方は、予約を移せるよう、速やかにお申し出ください。","words":[["interrupt","freq:interrupt"],["conductor","freq:conductor"],["windy","freq:windy"],["ferry","freq:ferry"],["transit","freq:transit"],["voucher","freq:voucher"],["cancellation","freq:cancellation"],["confirmation","freq:confirmation"],["cabin","freq:cabin"],["promptly","freq:promptly"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will the ferry not sail?","o":["It needs repairs.","The train is late.","The wind is too strong.","There are too few passengers."],"a":2,"why":"Because of windy weather on the coast（沿岸部の強風のため）とある。"},{"q":"What will passengers who wait until tomorrow receive?","o":["A free meal","A voucher for a hotel","A new train ticket","A seat upgrade"],"a":1,"why":"we will give you a hotel voucher at the station（駅でホテルの引換券を渡す）とある。"},{"q":"What should passengers show at Port Hale?","o":["Their booking confirmation","Their passport","Their hotel key","Their train seat number"],"a":0,"why":"please show your booking confirmation to the staff（予約確認書を係員に見せる）と求めている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0033","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"ラジオのお金相談","text":"Welcome back to Money Matters. Today's caller asked why her bills are always overdue. My answer is simple: plan on the day your paycheck arrives. First, look at every deduction on your pay slip, such as tax and insurance, so that you know exactly what is left. Next, set up automatic payments for rent and each utility bill. If you pay late, you will incur a fee every time. Third, if your employer owes you travel costs, ask the office administrator to reimburse you within the month. Finally, keep less cash in your wallet. As a former banker, I have seen that cash disappears fastest. And before you put savings into shares, talk to a licensed broker.","ja":"「マネー・マターズ」に戻りました。今日お電話をくださった方は、なぜ請求書の支払いがいつも期限を過ぎてしまうのかと質問されました。私の答えは簡単です。給料が入る日に計画を立てることです。まず、給与明細にある税金や保険などの控除をすべて確認し、手元にいくら残るのかを正確に把握します。次に、家賃と公共料金の請求は、それぞれ自動支払いに設定します。支払いが遅れると、そのたびに手数料を負うことになります。3つ目に、勤め先が出張費を払っていない場合は、その月のうちに払い戻してもらうよう事務の管理者に頼みます。最後に、財布に入れておく現金を減らしましょう。元銀行員として見てきましたが、いちばん早く消えるのは現金です。貯金を株に回す前には、免許を持つ仲介業者に相談してください。","words":[["overdue","freq:overdue"],["paycheck","freq:paycheck"],["deduction","freq:deduction"],["utility","freq:utility"],["incur","freq:incur"],["administrator","freq:administrator"],["reimburse","freq:reimburse"],["wallet","freq:wallet"],["banker","freq:banker"],["broker","freq:broker"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the caller's problem?","o":["She cannot find a job.","Her bills are paid late.","Her bank made a mistake.","Her rent is too high."],"a":1,"why":"why her bills are always overdue（なぜ請求の支払いがいつも期限を過ぎるのか）と質問している。"},{"q":"What does the speaker recommend for rent and utility bills?","o":["Paying them in cash","Paying them every week","Asking the employer to pay","Setting up automatic payments"],"a":3,"why":"set up automatic payments for rent and each utility bill（自動支払いに設定する）と勧めている。"},{"q":"What did the speaker do in the past?","o":["He worked at a bank.","He sold insurance.","He managed an office.","He traded shares."],"a":0,"why":"As a former banker（元銀行員として）と言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0034","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"営業会議での発表","text":"Thank you all for coming. I would like to give a short overview of our results. Please look at the first graph. It shows the cumulative number of new subscribers to our meal-kit service since January. As you can see, our popularity has grown fastest in cities where we work with a large retailer. The second graph shows the three stores that joined us as a franchise last year. All three became profitable within eight months. So what comes next? Our prediction is that we can reach two hundred thousand subscribers by December. I believe that this goal is realistic, but only if we open two more kitchens. I will explain the costs after the break.","ja":"お集まりいただきありがとうございます。当社の成績の概要を手短にお伝えします。最初のグラフをご覧ください。1月以降、当社の食材キットサービスに新しく加入した方の累計を示しています。ご覧のとおり、大手の小売業者と組んでいる都市で、人気が最も速く伸びています。2つ目のグラフは、昨年フランチャイズとして加わった3店舗を示しています。3店とも8か月以内に利益が出るようになりました。では、次はどうなるでしょうか。当社の予測では、12月までに加入者20万人に届きます。この目標は現実的だと考えていますが、それは調理場をあと2か所開いた場合に限ります。費用については休憩の後にご説明します。","words":[["overview","freq:overview"],["graph","freq:graph"],["cumulative","freq:cumulative"],["subscribers","freq:subscriber"],["popularity","freq:popularity"],["retailer","freq:retailer"],["franchise","freq:franchise"],["profitable","freq:profitable"],["prediction","freq:prediction"],["realistic","freq:realistic"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the first graph show?","o":["The total number of new subscribers","The cost of each meal kit","The number of stores","Sales in December"],"a":0,"why":"the cumulative number of new subscribers ... since January（1月以降の新規加入者の累計）を示している。"},{"q":"What is said about the three franchise stores?","o":["They closed last year.","They are in large cities.","They made a profit within eight months.","They need new kitchens."],"a":2,"why":"All three became profitable within eight months（3店とも8か月以内に利益が出た）とある。"},{"q":"What is needed to reach the goal?","o":["A lower price","Two more kitchens","A new retailer","More franchise stores"],"a":1,"why":"only if we open two more kitchens（調理場をあと2か所開いた場合に限り）と条件を述べている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0035","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"不動産の広告","text":"Looking for a new home? Parkside Apartments now has a vacancy on the fifth floor. This spacious two-bedroom apartment has a modern kitchen with a large refrigerator and a new oven. An air conditioner is included in every room. You may even bring your pet. Small dogs and cats are welcome. There is no need to worry about repairs. A plumber and an electrician are on call day and night. Trash is collected at your door three times a week, and waste disposal is included in the rent. For a small extra fee, a housekeeper will clean your apartment every Friday. To arrange a visit, call Parkside at 555-0199 today.","ja":"新しい住まいをお探しですか。パークサイド・アパートメンツでは、5階に空室が出ました。この広々とした2寝室の部屋には、大型の冷蔵庫と新しいオーブンを備えた現代的な台所があります。エアコンは全室に付いています。ペットを連れてくることもできます。小型の犬や猫は歓迎です。修理の心配はいりません。配管工と電気技師が昼夜を問わず待機しています。ごみは週3回、玄関先で回収し、廃棄物の処分費は家賃に含まれています。少額の追加料金で、客室係が毎週金曜にお部屋を掃除します。見学のご予約は、今日、パークサイド555-0199までお電話ください。","words":[["vacancy","freq:vacancy"],["spacious","freq:spacious"],["refrigerator","freq:refrigerator"],["oven","freq:oven"],["conditioner","freq:conditioner"],["pet","freq:pet"],["plumber","freq:plumber"],["Trash","freq:trash"],["disposal","freq:disposal"],["housekeeper","freq:housekeeper"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is being advertised?","o":["A hotel room","A cleaning service","A kitchen appliance store","An apartment for rent"],"a":3,"why":"Parkside Apartments now has a vacancy（アパートに空室が出た）と言っており、賃貸の部屋の広告。"},{"q":"What is included in the rent?","o":["Waste disposal","Weekly cleaning","Electricity","Parking"],"a":0,"why":"waste disposal is included in the rent（廃棄物の処分は家賃に含まれる）とある。掃除は追加料金。"},{"q":"What costs extra?","o":["Having a pet","A cleaning service on Fridays","Repairs by a plumber","An air conditioner"],"a":1,"why":"For a small extra fee, a housekeeper will clean your apartment every Friday（追加料金で毎週金曜に掃除）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0036","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"表彰の昼食会","text":"Good afternoon, everyone. Can you all hear me? This microphone was not working a moment ago. On behalf of the board, welcome to our annual staff luncheon. Today we honor Mr. Samuel Ito, who is retiring after thirty years as our chief engineer. His greatest accomplishment was the design of the Harbor Bridge, and his expertise has guided every project since. Mr. Ito has been a loyal friend to all of us, and he was always generous with his time for young engineers. In a moment, we will show some photos of his work on the projector. But first, please join me in offering our warmest congratulations. I would also like to thank the organizer of today's event, Ms. Lin.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。私の声は聞こえますか。このマイクは先ほどまで動いていませんでした。役員会を代表して、毎年恒例の社員昼食会へようこそ。本日は、主任技師として30年勤め、退職されるサミュエル・イトウさんをたたえます。イトウさんの最大の業績はハーバー橋の設計で、その専門知識は以後のすべての事業を導いてきました。イトウさんは私たち全員にとって誠実な友人であり、若い技師のためにいつも惜しみなく時間を割いてくれました。この後、プロジェクターでイトウさんの仕事の写真をお見せします。その前に、どうぞ私と一緒に、心からのお祝いを贈りましょう。本日の催しの主催者であるリンさんにも感謝します。","words":[["microphone","freq:microphone"],["behalf","freq:behalf"],["luncheon","freq:luncheon"],["accomplishment","freq:accomplishment"],["expertise","freq:expertise"],["loyal","freq:loyal"],["generous","freq:generous"],["projector","freq:projector"],["congratulations","freq:congratulation"],["organizer","freq:organizer"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is Mr. Ito being honored?","o":["He won a design prize.","He is leaving after a long career.","He became chief engineer.","He joined the board."],"a":1,"why":"who is retiring after thirty years as our chief engineer（主任技師を30年務めて退職する）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about Mr. Ito?","o":["He organized the event.","He took many photos.","He helped young engineers.","He will give a speech."],"a":2,"why":"he was always generous with his time for young engineers（若い技師のために惜しみなく時間を割いた）とある。"},{"q":"What will be shown on the projector?","o":["Photos of his work","A map of the bridge","The lunch menu","A list of award winners"],"a":0,"why":"we will show some photos of his work on the projector（仕事の写真をプロジェクターで見せる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0037","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"工場の安全連絡","text":"Attention, all staff. A government safety inspector will visit our plant on Wednesday morning. Before the visit, we will hold a fire drill at nine tomorrow. Your team leader will instruct you where to go. Please remember three rules. First, wear every protective garment listed for your area, including gloves and glasses. Second, clean your machine thoroughly at the end of each shift. Third, check that each part meets the customer's specification before it leaves your station. Next month, we will automate the packing line, which will help us work more efficiently and minimize the risk of injury from heavy lifting. Until then, please lift boxes in pairs. Thank you.","ja":"全従業員にお知らせします。水曜の午前、政府の安全検査官が当工場を訪れます。その前に、明日9時に防火訓練を行います。どこへ行くかは、班長が指示します。次の3つの決まりを忘れないでください。1つ目、手袋や眼鏡など、自分の持ち場に定められた保護用の衣類をすべて着用すること。2つ目、各勤務の終わりに機械を徹底的に掃除すること。3つ目、部品が自分の持ち場を離れる前に、お客様の仕様を満たしているか確かめること。来月には梱包ラインを自動化します。これにより、より効率よく働けるようになり、重い物を持ち上げることによるけがの危険を最小限にできます。それまでは、箱は2人一組で持ち上げてください。以上です。","words":[["inspector","freq:inspector"],["drill","freq:drill"],["instruct","freq:instruct"],["protective","freq:protective"],["garment","freq:garment"],["thoroughly","freq:thoroughly"],["specification","freq:specification"],["automate","freq:automate"],["efficiently","freq:efficiently"],["minimize","freq:minimize"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen tomorrow at nine?","o":["An inspector will arrive.","A new line will open.","Machines will be cleaned.","A fire drill will be held."],"a":3,"why":"we will hold a fire drill at nine tomorrow（明日9時に防火訓練）とある。検査官が来るのは水曜。"},{"q":"What should workers do at the end of each shift?","o":["Clean their machines","Check the customer's order","Report to the inspector","Count the boxes"],"a":0,"why":"clean your machine thoroughly at the end of each shift（勤務の終わりに機械を徹底的に掃除）とある。"},{"q":"What will change next month?","o":["A new team leader will come.","Packing will be done by machine.","Shifts will be shorter.","Gloves will no longer be needed."],"a":1,"why":"we will automate the packing line（梱包ラインを自動化する）とある。automate を done by machine と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0038","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"店の広告","text":"This Saturday, Miller Auto opens its new showroom on River Road, and you are invited. Come and see the Swift, the most economical small car on the market. It uses half the fuel of most family cars. Miller is the number one seller of used cars in the state, and every car comes with a one-year guarantee. Bring the flyer from today's newspaper to our cashier, and you will get a free car wash. While you are here, visit the outlet store next door, where casual shirts and pants with our racing team logo are thirty percent off. We will decorate the whole building with balloons, so you cannot miss us. Doors open at nine.","ja":"今週の土曜、ミラー自動車はリバー通りに新しいショールームを開店します。ぜひお越しください。市場で最も経済的な小型車「スウィフト」をご覧いただけます。燃料の消費は、たいていのファミリーカーの半分です。ミラーは州内で中古車の販売台数第1位の販売店で、どの車にも1年間の保証が付きます。今日の新聞に入っているちらしを会計係にお持ちいただくと、洗車が無料になります。お越しの際は、隣の直販店にもお立ち寄りください。当社のレーシングチームのロゴが入った普段着のシャツやズボンが3割引です。建物全体を風船で飾りますので、見逃すことはありません。開店は9時です。","words":[["Auto","freq:auto"],["showroom","freq:showroom"],["economical","freq:economical"],["seller","freq:seller"],["flyer","freq:flyer"],["cashier","freq:cashier"],["outlet","freq:outlet"],["casual","freq:casual"],["pants","freq:pant"],["decorate","freq:decorate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is said about the Swift?","o":["It is the largest car on sale.","It is a used car.","It uses little fuel.","It comes with a free wash."],"a":2,"why":"the most economical small car ... uses half the fuel（燃料の消費が半分で経済的）とある。"},{"q":"How can customers get a free car wash?","o":["By bringing a flyer","By buying a shirt","By arriving at nine","By test-driving a car"],"a":0,"why":"Bring the flyer from today's newspaper to our cashier（新聞のちらしを会計係に持っていく）とある。"},{"q":"What is sold at the outlet store?","o":["Car parts","Balloons","Used cars","Clothing"],"a":3,"why":"casual shirts and pants ... are thirty percent off（普段着のシャツやズボンが3割引）とある。衣類を売っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0039","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"観光バスのガイド","text":"Welcome aboard the City Circle bus. If this is your first time to sightsee in Riverton, you have chosen a perfect day. On your left is the Old Square, with its famous fountain from 1820. Many people like to sit on a bench there and watch the street musicians. Our first stop is Market Lane, a narrow street where you can try the local fish soup or a glass of fresh apple juice. There are also plenty of choices for vegetarian visitors. Please stay on the sidewalk, because bicycles pass very quickly here. You will see a poster for tonight's concert at each bus stop. One last request: please be polite and do not take photos of people without asking.","ja":"シティ・サークル・バスへようこそ。リバートンを観光するのが初めての方は、最高の日を選ばれました。左手に見えるのは旧広場で、1820年に作られた有名な噴水があります。そこのベンチに座って、大道芸の音楽家を眺めるのを好む人がたくさんいます。最初の停留所はマーケット小路です。この細い通りでは、地元の魚のスープや、しぼりたてのりんごジュースを試せます。菜食の方が選べる料理もたくさんあります。ここは自転車がとても速く通りますので、歩道を歩いてください。各バス停に、今夜のコンサートのポスターがあります。最後にお願いです。礼儀正しく、断りなく人の写真を撮らないでください。","words":[["sightsee","freq:sightsee"],["fountain","freq:fountain"],["bench","freq:bench"],["Lane","freq:lane"],["soup","freq:soup"],["juice","freq:juice"],["vegetarian","freq:vegetarian"],["sidewalk","freq:sidewalk"],["poster","freq:poster"],["polite","freq:polite"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is in the Old Square?","o":["A market","A fountain","A concert hall","A bus station"],"a":1,"why":"the Old Square, with its famous fountain from 1820（1820年の有名な噴水がある旧広場）とある。"},{"q":"Why should visitors stay on the sidewalk on Market Lane?","o":["The street is being repaired.","Buses stop there.","Bicycles go by fast.","Musicians are playing."],"a":2,"why":"because bicycles pass very quickly here（自転車がとても速く通る）ためと言っている。"},{"q":"What does the guide ask visitors not to do?","o":["Photograph people without permission","Eat on the bus","Sit on the benches","Buy concert tickets"],"a":0,"why":"do not take photos of people without asking（断りなく人の写真を撮らない）と頼んでいる。"}]},
{"id":"f-0040","page":"freq","group":"301〜400","kind":"上司からの留守番電話","text":"Hi, Paula. It's Victor. I am about to board the company jet to Singapore, so here are a few things for this week. First, please finalize the contract with Delmar Foods. I need a definite answer from them by Thursday. Remember that the prices in it are confidential, so do not send them by ordinary e-mail. Second, the report on water usage at the plant has some errors. Please check that every figure is recorded accurately. Third, the staff shortage in the call center continues to frustrate our customers. Ask each survey taker to work one extra hour if they can. You will find their numbers in the staff directory. I will call you when I land. Thanks.","ja":"もしもし、ポーラ。ビクターです。これから会社のジェット機でシンガポールへ向かうところなので、今週の用件をいくつか伝えます。まず、デルマー食品との契約を最終的にまとめてください。木曜までに先方からはっきりした返事が必要です。契約書の価格は機密ですので、普通のメールでは送らないでください。次に、工場の水の使用量についての報告書に誤りがいくつかあります。すべての数字が正確に記録されているか確かめてください。3つ目に、コールセンターの人手不足が、引き続きお客様をいらだたせています。調査の担当者それぞれに、可能なら1時間多く働いてもらうよう頼んでください。番号は社員名簿に載っています。着陸したら電話します。よろしく。","words":[["jet","freq:jet"],["finalize","freq:finalize"],["definite","freq:definite"],["confidential","freq:confidential"],["usage","freq:usage"],["accurately","freq:accurately"],["shortage","freq:shortage"],["frustrate","freq:frustrate"],["taker","freq:taker"],["directory","freq:directory"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is the speaker going?","o":["To a food company","To Singapore","To the call center","To the plant"],"a":1,"why":"board the company jet to Singapore（会社のジェット機でシンガポールへ）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the prices in the contract?","o":["They are too high.","They will change on Thursday.","They have errors.","They must be kept secret."],"a":3,"why":"the prices in it are confidential（価格は機密）なので普通のメールで送らないように、とある。"},{"q":"What problem is there at the call center?","o":["There are not enough staff.","The phones are broken.","The survey is too long.","The directory is out of date."],"a":0,"why":"the staff shortage in the call center（コールセンターの人手不足）がお客様をいらだたせている、と言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0041","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"診療所の自動音声案内","text":"Thank you for calling Northgate Family Clinic. Please listen carefully, because our hours have changed. The clinic is temporarily closed on Wednesday afternoons while new equipment is installed. During flu season, it is mandatory for every visitor to wear a mask in the waiting room. If you do not have one, please ask at the front desk. We also ask you to wash your hands with soap when you arrive. Our nurses wear a new pair of gloves for every patient, so you can feel safe. If you only need advice about medicine, the pharmacist at Hill Pharmacy, which is adjacent to our building, offers a free consultation every morning. To make an appointment, press one now.","ja":"ノースゲート・ファミリー診療所にお電話ありがとうございます。診療時間が変わりましたので、よくお聞きください。新しい機器を設置している間、水曜の午後は一時的に休診します。インフルエンザの季節は、待合室では来院者全員にマスクの着用を義務づけています。お持ちでない方は受付でお申し出ください。到着されたら、石けんで手を洗うこともお願いしています。看護師は患者さんごとに新しい手袋を着けますので、ご安心ください。薬についての助言だけが必要な方は、当院の建物に隣接するヒル薬局の薬剤師が、毎朝無料で相談に応じています。ご予約は、今、1を押してください。","words":[["Clinic","freq:clinic"],["temporarily","freq:temporarily"],["mandatory","freq:mandatory"],["mask","freq:mask"],["soap","freq:soap"],["gloves","freq:glove"],["pharmacist","freq:pharmacist"],["Pharmacy","freq:pharmacy"],["adjacent","freq:adjacent"],["consultation","freq:consultation"]],"qs":[{"q":"When is the clinic closed for now?","o":["Wednesday afternoons","Every morning","During flu season","On weekends"],"a":0,"why":"temporarily closed on Wednesday afternoons（水曜の午後は一時的に休診）とある。"},{"q":"What must visitors do in the waiting room?","o":["Fill in a form","Wear a mask","Show an ID","Turn off their phones"],"a":1,"why":"it is mandatory for every visitor to wear a mask（全員マスク着用が義務）とある。"},{"q":"Where can callers get free advice about medicine?","o":["At the clinic's front desk","From a nurse","By pressing one","At the pharmacy next door"],"a":3,"why":"the pharmacist at Hill Pharmacy, which is adjacent to our building, offers a free consultation（隣の薬局の薬剤師が無料で相談に応じる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0042","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"機内アナウンス","text":"Ladies and gentlemen, this is your captain speaking. First, please accept my apology for the delay. During our final check, the engineers found a mechanical problem: a faulty part in one brake on the left wheel. It is not a serious malfunction, but your safety comes first, so we have asked for a new part. In the meantime, the cargo doors will stay open, and you may use your phones. If the repair takes more than an hour, we will move you to an alternate aircraft at Gate 9. Passengers who miss a connecting flight will not be charged any extra airfare for a later one. Thank you for your patience. I will speak to you again in fifteen minutes.","ja":"皆様、機長です。まず、出発の遅れをおわび申し上げます。最終点検の際、技術者が機械的な問題を見つけました。左の車輪のブレーキの一つに、欠陥のある部品があったのです。深刻な故障ではありませんが、皆様の安全が第一ですので、新しい部品を手配しました。その間、貨物室の扉は開けたままにし、お客様は電話をお使いいただけます。修理に1時間以上かかる場合は、9番搭乗口の代わりの機体にお移りいただきます。乗り継ぎ便に間に合わなかったお客様には、後の便の追加の航空運賃はいただきません。お待ちいただきありがとうございます。15分後にもう一度ご案内します。","words":[["apology","freq:apology"],["mechanical","freq:mechanical"],["faulty","freq:faulty"],["brake","freq:brake"],["malfunction","freq:malfunction"],["meantime","freq:meantime"],["cargo","freq:cargo"],["alternate","freq:alternate"],["airfare","freq:airfare"],["patience","freq:patience"]],"qs":[{"q":"What caused the delay?","o":["Bad weather","A late crew member","A problem with a brake part","A missing bag"],"a":2,"why":"a faulty part in one brake on the left wheel（左の車輪のブレーキに欠陥のある部品）が見つかったと説明している。"},{"q":"What will happen if the repair takes over an hour?","o":["Passengers will change planes.","The flight will be canceled.","Passengers will get a refund.","A meal will be served."],"a":0,"why":"we will move you to an alternate aircraft at Gate 9（9番搭乗口の代わりの機体に移る）とある。"},{"q":"What does the captain say about connecting flights?","o":["They will wait for this plane.","A later flight will cost nothing extra.","They leave from Gate 9.","Passengers should call the airline."],"a":1,"why":"will not be charged any extra airfare for a later one（後の便の追加運賃はかからない）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0043","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"In business news tonight, Castle Bank has announced that it will merge with Union Savings by the end of the year. A spokesperson for Castle said that the decision was made in a six-hour boardroom meeting on Sunday. The news follows the resignation of Union's president last month and a quarterly report showing that profits had fallen considerably. Castle will terminate Union's telephone banking service in March, but customers will still be able to make a withdrawal at any branch. For investors, there is good news: the yearly dividend will rise from two dollars to three dollars a share. The new bank will have more than six hundred branches. Now, over to sports.","ja":"今夜の経済ニュースです。キャッスル銀行は、年末までにユニオン貯蓄銀行と合併すると発表しました。キャッスルの広報担当者によると、この決定は日曜に役員会議室で行われた6時間の会議で下されました。この知らせの前には、先月、ユニオンの社長が辞任し、四半期報告書で利益が大幅に落ち込んだことが明らかになっていました。キャッスルは3月にユニオンの電話による銀行取引サービスを終了しますが、顧客はこれまでどおり、どの支店でも預金を引き出せます。投資家にはよい知らせがあります。年間の配当金が1株2ドルから3ドルに上がります。新しい銀行の支店は600を超えます。では、スポーツです。","words":[["merge","freq:merge"],["spokesperson","freq:spokesperson"],["boardroom","freq:boardroom"],["resignation","freq:resignation"],["quarterly","freq:quarterly"],["considerably","freq:considerably"],["terminate","freq:terminate"],["withdrawal","freq:withdrawal"],["yearly","freq:yearly"],["dividend","freq:dividend"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main news?","o":["A bank is closing its branches.","A bank president was hired.","Profits rose at two banks.","Two banks will become one."],"a":3,"why":"Castle Bank ... will merge with Union Savings（キャッスル銀行がユニオン貯蓄銀行と合併する）とある。"},{"q":"What will end in March?","o":["Union's telephone banking","Withdrawals at branches","The quarterly report","The dividend"],"a":0,"why":"Castle will terminate Union's telephone banking service in March（3月に電話による銀行取引を終了）とある。"},{"q":"What is the good news for investors?","o":["Share prices doubled.","More branches will open.","The dividend will go up.","Fees will be cut."],"a":2,"why":"the yearly dividend will rise from two dollars to three dollars a share（年間配当が1株2ドルから3ドルに上がる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0044","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"情報システム部の連絡","text":"Hello, everyone. This is Raj from the IT department. As you know, much of our computer hardware is outdated, and repairs have become costly. Starting next month, we will replace every desktop computer in the building. We will also equip all meeting rooms with wireless projectors. According to my calculation, the change will cut our electricity bill by ten percent. The new machines make an automatic copy of your files every night, so you will never lose your work. Our vendor will deliver the first fifty units on June 3. One request: there has been a revision to the schedule, so please check the new list on the notice board to see when your floor will be done.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。情報システム部のラジです。ご存じのとおり、当社のコンピューター機器の多くは古くなっており、修理に費用がかかるようになっています。来月から、建物内のデスクトップパソコンをすべて入れ替えます。また、すべての会議室に無線のプロジェクターを備え付けます。私の計算では、この変更で電気代が1割減ります。新しい機械は毎晩ファイルの写しを自動で作りますので、作業内容を失うことはありません。販売業者が6月3日に最初の50台を納入します。お願いが一つあります。日程に修正がありましたので、自分の階がいつ作業になるかは、掲示板の新しい一覧で確認してください。","words":[["hardware","freq:hardware"],["outdated","freq:outdated"],["costly","freq:costly"],["desktop","freq:desktop"],["equip","freq:equip"],["wireless","freq:wireless"],["calculation","freq:calculation"],["automatic","freq:automatic"],["vendor","freq:vendor"],["revision","freq:revision"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will the computers be replaced?","o":["They are old and expensive to fix.","They were stolen.","The staff asked for laptops.","The vendor offered a discount."],"a":0,"why":"much of our computer hardware is outdated, and repairs have become costly（古くなり修理に費用がかかる）とある。"},{"q":"What do the new machines do every night?","o":["Turn themselves off","Update the schedule","Copy files automatically","Send a report to IT"],"a":2,"why":"make an automatic copy of your files every night（毎晩ファイルの写しを自動で作る）とある。"},{"q":"What are listeners asked to check?","o":["Their electricity use","The new schedule on the notice board","The number of projectors","Their file sizes"],"a":1,"why":"please check the new list on the notice board（掲示板の新しい一覧を確認する）よう求めている。日程が修正されたため。"}]},
{"id":"f-0045","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"不動産業者の案内","text":"Hi, this is Grace Bell, your realtor at Key Homes. I have found a house that may suit you. It is on Cedar Street, in a quiet residential area ten minutes from the station. The owner has agreed to furnish the living room and bedrooms, so you will not need to buy much. A local carpenter built the kitchen shelves, which are very durable, and he can assemble a desk for the study if you like. The house also has a laundry room with a new washing machine, and a built-in vacuum system. The price is quite inexpensive for this part of town. Another purchaser is interested, though, so please call me back today if you would like to see it.","ja":"もしもし、キー・ホームズの不動産担当、グレース・ベルです。ご希望に合いそうな家が見つかりました。場所はシーダー通りで、駅から10分の静かな住宅地にあります。所有者が居間と寝室に家具を備え付けることに同意しましたので、あまり買い足す必要はありません。台所の棚は地元の大工が作ったもので、とても丈夫です。ご希望なら、書斎用の机も組み立ててくれます。新しい洗濯機を置いた洗濯室と、作り付けの掃除機の設備もあります。価格は、この地区としてはかなり手ごろです。ただ、ほかにも購入を考えている方がいますので、ご覧になりたい場合は今日中に折り返しお電話ください。","words":[["realtor","freq:realtor"],["residential","freq:residential"],["furnish","freq:furnish"],["carpenter","freq:carpenter"],["durable","freq:durable"],["assemble","freq:assemble"],["laundry","freq:laundry"],["vacuum","freq:vacuum"],["inexpensive","freq:inexpensive"],["purchaser","freq:purchaser"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is the house?","o":["In the city center","Next to the station","In an office district","In a quiet residential area"],"a":3,"why":"in a quiet residential area ten minutes from the station（駅から10分の静かな住宅地）とある。"},{"q":"What has the owner agreed to do?","o":["Provide furniture","Lower the price","Build a study","Replace the washing machine"],"a":0,"why":"The owner has agreed to furnish the living room and bedrooms（居間と寝室に家具を備え付ける）とある。"},{"q":"Why should the listener call back today?","o":["The price will rise tomorrow.","Someone else may buy the house.","The realtor is going away.","The carpenter needs an answer."],"a":1,"why":"Another purchaser is interested（ほかにも購入希望者がいる）ためと言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0046","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"イベント会場の事前説明","text":"Good morning, team. Before the doors open, here are today's rules. Every guest must wear a badge, and security is strictly enforced. If you see a bag or purse left unattended, do not touch it. Call me at once. The mayor arrives at eleven, and two of you will escort her from the side door to the stage. Please make sure that the path stays accessible for wheelchairs. At twelve, the caterer will bring lunch, and each server will carry one tray at a time through the kitchen door only. After lunch, we need to rearrange the chairs into a circle for the afternoon talk. If you have any problem, speak to Dana, our floor coordinator.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。開場の前に、今日の決まりを伝えます。来場者は全員、名札を着けなければならず、警備は厳しく行います。置きっぱなしのかばんやハンドバッグを見つけたら、触らないでください。すぐに私に連絡してください。市長は11時に到着しますので、2人が横の入口から舞台まで付き添って案内します。通路は車椅子でも通れる状態に保ってください。12時に仕出し業者が昼食を届けます。給仕は一度に盆を1枚ずつ持ち、台所の扉だけを通ります。昼食の後は、午後の講演に向けて椅子を円形に並べ替える必要があります。何か問題があれば、会場のまとめ役のデイナに話してください。","words":[["badge","freq:badge"],["strictly","freq:strictly"],["purse","freq:purse"],["unattended","freq:unattended"],["escort","freq:escort"],["accessible","freq:accessible"],["caterer","freq:caterer"],["tray","freq:tray"],["rearrange","freq:rearrange"],["coordinator","freq:coordinator"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should staff do if they see an unattended bag?","o":["Open it","Take it to the stage","Contact the speaker immediately","Give it to the mayor"],"a":2,"why":"do not touch it. Call me at once（触らずにすぐ連絡する）と指示している。"},{"q":"What will happen at eleven?","o":["The mayor will arrive.","Lunch will be served.","The doors will open.","A talk will begin."],"a":0,"why":"The mayor arrives at eleven（市長は11時に到着）とある。"},{"q":"What must be done after lunch?","o":["The kitchen must be cleaned.","The chairs must be moved.","The badges must be collected.","The stage must be taken down."],"a":1,"why":"we need to rearrange the chairs into a circle（椅子を円形に並べ替える）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0047","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"就職フェアの開会あいさつ","text":"Welcome to the Lakeside Career Fair. Whether you are a first-time job seeker or an experienced businessperson looking for a change, more than eighty employers are waiting to meet you. Do not worry about your inexperience. Many prospective employers here offer training, and several pay an hourly wage even during that time. Students should visit booth twelve, where you can learn about a scholarship that includes an exemption from tuition for two years. The mood today is informal, so feel free to ask questions anytime. Before we start, I would like to congratulate last year's visitors: sixty percent of them found work within three months. Now, please enjoy the fair.","ja":"レイクサイド就職フェアへようこそ。初めて仕事を探す方も、転職を考えている経験豊富な会社員の方も、80を超える雇用主が皆さんを待っています。経験不足を心配する必要はありません。ここにいる将来の雇用主の多くは研修を用意しており、研修中も時給を支払うところがいくつもあります。学生の方は12番ブースへお立ち寄りください。2年間の授業料免除を含む奨学金について知ることができます。今日は形式ばらない雰囲気ですので、いつでも気軽に質問してください。始める前に、昨年の来場者の皆さんにお祝いを述べたいと思います。その6割が3か月以内に仕事を見つけました。それでは、フェアをお楽しみください。","words":[["seeker","freq:seeker"],["businessperson","freq:businessperson"],["inexperience","freq:inexperience"],["prospective","freq:prospective"],["hourly","freq:hourly"],["scholarship","freq:scholarship"],["exemption","freq:exemption"],["informal","freq:informal"],["anytime","freq:anytime"],["congratulate","freq:congratulate"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the fair for?","o":["Only students","Only experienced workers","Employers looking for offices","Both new and experienced job seekers"],"a":3,"why":"a first-time job seeker or an experienced businessperson（初めての求職者も経験豊富な会社員も）対象だと述べている。"},{"q":"What can students learn about at booth twelve?","o":["A scholarship","An hourly job","A training course","A tuition loan"],"a":0,"why":"you can learn about a scholarship（奨学金について知ることができる）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about last year's visitors?","o":["Most of them were students.","Many of them found jobs quickly.","Eighty of them became employers.","They asked many questions."],"a":1,"why":"sixty percent of them found work within three months（6割が3か月以内に仕事を見つけた）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0048","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"劇場からのお知らせ","text":"Good evening, and welcome to the Grand Theater, which was able to reopen this month after a lengthy repair. Tonight's play is a new English translation of a French comedy. The lead actress, Maria Stone, was praised by every reviewer in the city, and each performer on stage tonight has worked with her for two years. In the lobby, you will find promotional items, including a postcard set with graphic art from the show. All profits go to the city library, and the head librarian is here tonight to thank you in person. The play lasts two hours, with one break. Please turn off your phones now. Enjoy the show.","ja":"こんばんは。グランド劇場へようこそ。当劇場は長期にわたる修理を終え、今月、再開することができました。今夜の劇は、フランスの喜劇を新しく英語に翻訳したものです。主演女優のマリア・ストーンは市内のすべての評論家から称賛されており、今夜舞台に立つ演者は皆、彼女と2年間一緒に活動してきました。ロビーには、公演の絵柄を使った絵はがきセットなど、販売促進用の品物をご用意しています。収益はすべて市立図書館に寄付され、今夜は図書館長が直接お礼を述べるために来ています。上演時間は2時間で、休憩が1回あります。ここで携帯電話の電源をお切りください。どうぞお楽しみください。","words":[["reopen","freq:reopen"],["lengthy","freq:lengthy"],["translation","freq:translation"],["actress","freq:actress"],["reviewer","freq:reviewer"],["performer","freq:performer"],["promotional","freq:promotional"],["postcard","freq:postcard"],["graphic","freq:graphic"],["librarian","freq:librarian"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened this month?","o":["The theater opened again.","A new actress joined.","The play was translated.","The library moved."],"a":0,"why":"was able to reopen this month after a lengthy repair（長い修理の後、今月再開できた）とある。"},{"q":"What is said about tonight's play?","o":["It is a French film.","It is a translated comedy.","It was written by Maria Stone.","It lasts three hours."],"a":1,"why":"a new English translation of a French comedy（フランスの喜劇の新しい英語訳）とある。"},{"q":"Where will the profits from the items go?","o":["To the theater's repair fund","To the actors","To the city library","To a French school"],"a":2,"why":"All profits go to the city library（収益はすべて市立図書館へ）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0049","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"保養施設の案内","text":"Welcome to Silver Lake Lodge, the perfect place to spend your leisure time. Let me tell you about tomorrow. Early risers can jog with our fitness coach along a five-kilometer path around the lake. Please bring a towel from your room. At ten, there is a half-day excursion to the old mill, and the bus leaves from the front gate. If cooking is your hobby, join our chef at two to bake bread and make pizza with fresh tomato sauce from our own garden. Of course, you may prefer to do nothing at all. Many guests simply take a nap in the garden chairs after lunch. Dinner is at seven. We hope you enjoy your stay.","ja":"シルバー・レイク・ロッジへようこそ。余暇を過ごすのに最適な場所です。明日の予定をご案内します。早起きの方は、フィットネスの指導員と一緒に、湖を一周する5キロメートルの道をジョギングできます。お部屋のタオルをお持ちください。10時には、古い水車小屋への半日の小旅行があり、バスは正門から出ます。料理が趣味の方は、2時に料理長と一緒にパンを焼き、当施設の菜園でとれたトマトの新鮮なソースでピザを作りましょう。もちろん、何もしないのもよいでしょう。昼食の後、庭の椅子でただ昼寝をするお客様もたくさんいらっしゃいます。夕食は7時です。どうぞごゆっくりお過ごしください。","words":[["leisure","freq:leisure"],["jog","freq:jog"],["kilometer","freq:kilometer"],["towel","freq:towel"],["excursion","freq:excursion"],["hobby","freq:hobby"],["bake","freq:bake"],["pizza","freq:pizza"],["tomato","freq:tomato"],["nap","freq:nap"]],"qs":[{"q":"What can guests do early in the morning?","o":["Go jogging","Bake bread","Visit a mill","Have breakfast in the garden"],"a":0,"why":"Early risers can jog with our fitness coach（早起きの方は指導員とジョギングできる）とある。"},{"q":"Where does the excursion bus leave from?","o":["The lake","The kitchen","The old mill","The front gate"],"a":3,"why":"the bus leaves from the front gate（バスは正門から出る）とある。"},{"q":"What will guests make with the chef?","o":["Tomato soup","Garden salad","Bread and pizza","Sandwiches"],"a":2,"why":"bake bread and make pizza with fresh tomato sauce（パンを焼き、トマトソースでピザを作る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0050","page":"freq","group":"401〜500","kind":"郵便室の研修","text":"Welcome to the mail room. In a few days, you will be accustomed to the routine, so let me explain it. Every morning, we classify incoming mail by department. If the sender is unfamiliar or the package has no return address, do not open it. Take it to your superior, Mr. Cole, and he will decide what to do. Please do not let your phone distract you while you sort, because one mistake can delay an important contract. In the afternoon, we cooperate with the delivery drivers to load outgoing boxes. Afterward, we record every item in the log book. To reinforce these steps, I will work beside you this week. Finally, as a sign of our appreciation, lunch is free on your first day.","ja":"郵便室へようこそ。数日すれば仕事の流れに慣れますので、説明しておきます。毎朝、届いた郵便物を部署ごとに分類します。差出人に見覚えがない場合や、荷物に返送先の住所がない場合は、開けないでください。上司のコールさんのところへ持っていけば、どうするかを決めてくれます。仕分けの間は、電話に気を取られないようにしてください。たった一つのミスで、重要な契約が遅れることがあります。午後は、配達の運転手と協力して、発送する箱を積み込みます。その後、すべての品物を記録簿に書き込みます。この手順を定着させるため、今週は私が隣で一緒に作業します。最後に、感謝の気持ちとして、初日の昼食は無料です。","words":[["accustomed","freq:accustom"],["classify","freq:classify"],["sender","freq:sender"],["unfamiliar","freq:unfamiliar"],["superior","freq:superior"],["distract","freq:distract"],["cooperate","freq:cooperate"],["Afterward","freq:afterward"],["reinforce","freq:reinforce"],["appreciation","freq:appreciation"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should workers do with a package from an unknown sender?","o":["Open it carefully","Take it to Mr. Cole","Return it to the driver","Put it in the log book"],"a":1,"why":"do not open it. Take it to your superior, Mr. Cole（開けずに上司のコールさんへ持っていく）とある。"},{"q":"What happens in the afternoon?","o":["Mail is sorted by department.","Contracts are signed.","Outgoing boxes are loaded.","Phones are collected."],"a":2,"why":"we cooperate with the delivery drivers to load outgoing boxes（運転手と協力して発送する箱を積む）とある。仕分けは朝。"},{"q":"What will new workers receive on their first day?","o":["A free lunch","A log book","A phone","A uniform"],"a":0,"why":"lunch is free on your first day（初日の昼食は無料）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0051","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"朝の交通情報","text":"Good morning. Here is a weather alert from the City Traffic Center. Roads are icy across the northern part of the city after last night's snow. Police have announced the closure of the Hill Street tunnel until at least ten o'clock, which is causing a long traffic jam on Route 5. Drivers should expect serious disruption on all roads into the center. If you ride a motorcycle, please leave it at home today. Every pedestrian should also use caution, especially on bridges and stairs. Buses are running, but about twenty minutes late. If you must drive, slow down and keep a wide space in front of you so that you arrive safely. Our next report is at eight.","ja":"おはようございます。市交通センターから、天候に関する警報をお伝えします。昨夜の雪で、市の北部全域の道路が凍結しています。警察は、ヒル通りのトンネルを少なくとも10時まで閉鎖すると発表しました。そのため5号線で長い渋滞が起きています。中心部へ向かうすべての道路で、大きな混乱が見込まれます。オートバイに乗る方は、今日は家に置いてきてください。歩行者の方も、特に橋や階段では注意してください。バスは運行していますが、約20分遅れています。どうしても運転する場合は、速度を落とし、前の車との間隔を広く取って、安全に到着してください。次の情報は8時です。","words":[["alert","freq:alert"],["icy","freq:icy"],["closure","freq:closure"],["tunnel","freq:tunnel"],["jam","freq:jam"],["disruption","freq:disruption"],["motorcycle","freq:motorcycle"],["pedestrian","freq:pedestrian"],["caution","freq:caution"],["safely","freq:safely"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the tunnel closed?","o":["The roads are icy.","An accident happened.","It is being repaired.","A bus broke down."],"a":0,"why":"Roads are icy ... after last night's snow（昨夜の雪で道路が凍結）しており、警察がトンネルを閉鎖した。"},{"q":"What is said about the buses?","o":["They are not running.","They are free today.","They are late.","They use Route 5."],"a":2,"why":"Buses are running, but about twenty minutes late（運行しているが約20分遅れ）とある。"},{"q":"What advice is given to drivers?","o":["Take the tunnel","Drive slowly and keep a distance","Leave before eight","Follow the buses"],"a":1,"why":"slow down and keep a wide space in front of you（速度を落とし前との間隔を広く取る）と助言している。"}]},
{"id":"f-0052","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"求人の案内","text":"Do you love to solve problems? Brightpath, one of the fastest-growing tech companies in the region, is hiring. I am Naomi Field, the chief recruiter, and we have twelve openings for a programmer and two managerial positions. For the programming jobs, we welcome people straight after graduation. You do not need a certification, but please send a portfolio of projects you have built. If you have no experience at all, you can start as an apprentice and learn beside our senior engineers for six months with full pay. Above all, we want people who are eager to learn and enthusiastic about teamwork. Interviews begin on Monday. Apply today at our Web site.","ja":"問題を解くのが好きですか。この地域で最も急成長している技術系企業の一つ、ブライトパスが人材を募集しています。採用責任者のナオミ・フィールドです。プログラマーの募集が12名、管理職の募集が2名あります。プログラミングの仕事では、卒業したばかりの方も歓迎します。資格の認定は必要ありませんが、これまでに作った成果物をまとめた作品集を送ってください。まったく経験のない方は見習いとして入社し、6か月間、給与を全額受け取りながら先輩技師の隣で学ぶことができます。何よりも、学ぶ意欲があり、チームで働くことに熱心な方を求めています。面接は月曜に始まります。今日、当社のウェブサイトから応募してください。","words":[["tech","freq:tech"],["recruiter","freq:recruiter"],["programmer","freq:programmer"],["managerial","freq:managerial"],["graduation","freq:graduation"],["certification","freq:certification"],["portfolio","freq:portfolio"],["apprentice","freq:apprentice"],["eager","freq:eager"],["enthusiastic","freq:enthusiastic"]],"qs":[{"q":"What kind of company is Brightpath?","o":["A school","A bank","A design studio","A technology company"],"a":3,"why":"one of the fastest-growing tech companies（急成長している技術系企業）とある。"},{"q":"What should applicants for programming jobs send?","o":["A collection of their projects","A certificate","A letter from a teacher","A list of managers"],"a":0,"why":"please send a portfolio of projects you have built（作った成果物の作品集を送る）とある。資格は不要。"},{"q":"What is offered to people with no experience?","o":["A short unpaid course","A paid six-month period of learning","A managerial position","A job at another company"],"a":1,"why":"start as an apprentice ... for six months with full pay（見習いとして6か月、給与全額で学べる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0053","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"Now for the business headlines. Marden Health, the pharmaceutical company, has completed its takeover of Rexon Labs, which went bankrupt in March. At a meeting yesterday, more than ninety percent of Marden's stockholders voted for the deal. Rexon's workforce of eight hundred will keep their jobs for at least two years. According to government statistics, the drug industry has grown steadily for five years, and one economist told us she is optimistic about the future. Her projection is that Marden's sales will double by next spring, when two new medicines are expected to reach the market. Marden's share price rose four percent this morning. We will have more after the weather.","ja":"続いて経済の主なニュースです。製薬会社のマーデン・ヘルスが、3月に破産したレクソン研究所の買収を完了しました。昨日の総会では、マーデンの株主の9割以上がこの取引に賛成票を投じました。レクソンの従業員800人は、少なくとも2年間は雇用が守られます。政府の統計によると、製薬業界は5年間着実に成長しており、ある経済学者は将来について楽観的だと話しています。彼女の予測では、新薬2種類が市場に出る見込みの来春までに、マーデンの売上は2倍になります。マーデンの株価は今朝、4パーセント上昇しました。天気予報の後で、さらに詳しくお伝えします。","words":[["pharmaceutical","freq:pharmaceutical"],["takeover","freq:takeover"],["bankrupt","freq:bankrupt"],["stockholders","freq:stockholder"],["workforce","freq:workforce"],["statistics","freq:statistics"],["steadily","freq:steadily"],["economist","freq:economist"],["optimistic","freq:optimistic"],["projection","freq:projection"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did Marden Health do?","o":["It went bankrupt.","It closed a lab.","It bought another company.","It cut eight hundred jobs."],"a":2,"why":"has completed its takeover of Rexon Labs（レクソン研究所の買収を完了した）とある。takeover を bought と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will happen to Rexon's workers?","o":["They will keep their jobs for at least two years.","They will move to Marden's office.","They will receive shares.","They will lose their jobs in March."],"a":0,"why":"will keep their jobs for at least two years（少なくとも2年は雇用が守られる）とある。"},{"q":"What does the economist predict?","o":["Drug prices will fall.","The industry will stop growing.","Marden's shares will drop.","Marden's sales will double."],"a":3,"why":"Her projection is that Marden's sales will double by next spring（来春までに売上が2倍になるという予測）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0054","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"人事部の説明","text":"Good afternoon. I am from the payroll office, and I would like to explain three changes that begin in April. First, the health insurance premium will rise by ten dollars a month, and we will deduct it from your salary as usual. Second, staff who work irregular hours, such as night shifts, will be compensated with an extra two dollars per hour. Third, if you are absent for more than three days, a verbal report to your manager is no longer enough. To comply with the new labor law, you must hand in a doctor's note. Managers must adhere to this rule as well. Finally, your yearly appraisal will take place in May, not June. Any questions?","ja":"こんにちは。給与担当の者です。4月から始まる3つの変更についてご説明します。まず、健康保険の保険料が月10ドル上がります。これまでどおり、給与から差し引きます。次に、夜勤など不規則な時間に働く従業員には、1時間あたり2ドルを上乗せして補償します。3つ目に、3日を超えて欠勤する場合、上司に口頭で報告するだけでは足りなくなります。新しい労働法に従うため、医師の診断書を提出しなければなりません。管理職もこの決まりを守る必要があります。最後に、年に一度の人事評価は、6月ではなく5月に行います。ご質問はありますか。","words":[["payroll","freq:payroll"],["premium","freq:premium"],["deduct","freq:deduct"],["irregular","freq:irregular"],["compensated","freq:compensate"],["absent","freq:absent"],["verbal","freq:verbal"],["comply","freq:comply"],["adhere","freq:adhere"],["appraisal","freq:appraisal"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will rise by ten dollars a month?","o":["The hourly wage","The insurance premium","The night-shift bonus","The cost of a doctor's note"],"a":1,"why":"the health insurance premium will rise by ten dollars a month（保険料が月10ドル上がる）とある。"},{"q":"What is required after more than three days of absence?","o":["A note from a doctor","A phone call to payroll","A meeting with the manager","A written apology"],"a":0,"why":"you must hand in a doctor's note（医師の診断書を提出する）とある。口頭の報告だけでは足りない。"},{"q":"When will the yearly appraisal be held?","o":["In April","In June","In May","In March"],"a":2,"why":"will take place in May, not June（6月ではなく5月）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0055","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"家主からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, this is Mr. Novak, your landlord. I am calling about the plan to remodel your apartment next week. On Monday, an electrician will put new lights in the kitchen ceiling. On Tuesday, the workers will change the layout of the bathroom upstairs, so please use the one downstairs that day. They will also put up a coat rack by the front door. I have asked them not to drive a single nail into the old wooden wall in the hall. Finally, the gardener will cut the lawn on Wednesday morning, so please move your bicycle off the grass. The work should be finished by Friday. Call me if any of these days is a problem.","ja":"もしもし、家主のノバックです。来週、お部屋を改装する計画の件でお電話しました。月曜には、電気技師が台所の天井に新しい照明を取り付けます。火曜には、作業員が2階の浴室の配置を変えますので、その日は1階のものをお使いください。玄関のそばにコート掛けも取り付けます。廊下の古い木の壁には、くぎを1本も打たないよう頼んであります。最後に、水曜の朝に庭師が芝生を刈りますので、自転車を芝の上から動かしておいてください。工事は金曜までに終わる見込みです。都合の悪い日があればお電話ください。","words":[["landlord","freq:landlord"],["remodel","freq:remodel"],["electrician","freq:electrician"],["ceiling","freq:ceiling"],["layout","freq:layout"],["upstairs","freq:upstairs"],["downstairs","freq:downstairs"],["rack","freq:rack"],["nail","freq:nail"],["lawn","freq:lawn"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will the electrician do on Monday?","o":["Repair the bathroom","Put up a coat rack","Check the heating","Install kitchen lights"],"a":3,"why":"an electrician will put new lights in the kitchen ceiling（台所の天井に新しい照明を付ける）とある。"},{"q":"What should the tenant do on Tuesday?","o":["Use the downstairs bathroom","Stay out of the kitchen","Leave the front door open","Move the furniture"],"a":0,"why":"please use the one downstairs that day（その日は1階のものを使う）とある。2階の浴室が工事になるため。"},{"q":"Why should the bicycle be moved?","o":["The hall will be painted.","The grass will be cut.","The workers need parking.","The wall is old."],"a":1,"why":"the gardener will cut the lawn ... please move your bicycle off the grass（芝を刈るので自転車を動かす）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0056","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"地域ラジオのお知らせ","text":"Here is what is happening in Brookfield this weekend. On Saturday, the city zoo celebrates its fiftieth birthday with a colorful parade. Children who come in an animal costume get in free. At lunchtime, a new statue of the zoo's first elephant will be shown for the first time, and a local celebrity, the singer Dana Cruz, will cut the ribbon. On Sunday, the Science Museum in the northern suburb opens a show about the wildlife of our rivers. At three, a firefighter who rescued two deer from last year's flood will speak in the museum's auditorium. Seats are limited, so come early. Both events are free for city residents.","ja":"今週末のブルックフィールドの催しをお伝えします。土曜には、市立動物園が開園50周年を、色とりどりのパレードで祝います。動物の衣装で来たお子さんは入場無料です。昼食の時間には、動物園の最初の象をかたどった新しい像が初めて公開され、地元の有名人である歌手のデイナ・クルーズさんがテープカットをします。日曜には、北の郊外にある科学博物館で、この地域の川の野生生物についての展示が始まります。3時には、昨年の洪水で鹿2頭を救助した消防士が、博物館の講堂で話をします。席に限りがありますので、お早めにお越しください。どちらの催しも、市民は無料です。","words":[["zoo","freq:zoo"],["colorful","freq:colorful"],["costume","freq:costume"],["lunchtime","freq:lunchtime"],["statue","freq:statue"],["celebrity","freq:celebrity"],["suburb","freq:suburb"],["wildlife","freq:wildlife"],["firefighter","freq:firefighter"],["auditorium","freq:auditorium"]],"qs":[{"q":"How can children enter the zoo for free on Saturday?","o":["By coming with a parent","By arriving at lunchtime","By wearing an animal costume","By joining the parade"],"a":2,"why":"Children who come in an animal costume get in free（動物の衣装で来た子どもは無料）とある。"},{"q":"What will Dana Cruz do?","o":["Cut a ribbon","Sing in the parade","Speak at the museum","Feed the elephants"],"a":0,"why":"will cut the ribbon（テープカットをする）とある。"},{"q":"Who will speak at the museum?","o":["A scientist","A zoo keeper","A singer","A firefighter"],"a":3,"why":"a firefighter who rescued two deer ... will speak in the museum's auditorium（鹿を救助した消防士が講堂で話す）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0057","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"共有オフィスの利用案内","text":"Welcome to Hive Workspace. Here is how to use our new booking system, which we built to simplify your day. First, connect to the internet and open our home page. Your login name is your e-mail address. Once inside, you can reserve any vacant meeting room with one click, and members on the gold plan get unlimited hours. The system will also facilitate printing: just send your file and collect it at the front desk. If you misplace your door card, tell us at once, and we will make a duplicate for five dollars. Please note the expiration date of your plan on the first screen. To avoid any unexpected loss of service, renew at least three days before that date.","ja":"ハイブ・ワークスペースへようこそ。皆さんの一日を簡単にするために作った、新しい予約システムの使い方をご案内します。まず、インターネットに接続し、当社のホームページを開きます。ログイン名はメールアドレスです。中に入ると、空いている会議室をどれでもワンクリックで予約でき、ゴールドプランの会員は時間無制限で利用できます。このシステムは印刷も容易にします。ファイルを送って、受付で受け取るだけです。入館カードを置き忘れた場合は、すぐにお知らせください。5ドルで複製を作ります。最初の画面にある、プランの有効期限にご注意ください。思いがけずサービスが止まるのを避けるため、その日の少なくとも3日前に更新してください。","words":[["simplify","freq:simplify"],["internet","freq:internet"],["login","freq:login"],["vacant","freq:vacant"],["unlimited","freq:unlimited"],["facilitate","freq:facilitate"],["misplace","freq:misplace"],["duplicate","freq:duplicate"],["expiration","freq:expiration"],["unexpected","freq:unexpected"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is a member's login name?","o":["Their member number","Their e-mail address","Their phone number","Their room number"],"a":1,"why":"Your login name is your e-mail address（ログイン名はメールアドレス）とある。"},{"q":"What do gold plan members receive?","o":["Free printing","A second door card","Unlimited meeting room hours","A private desk"],"a":2,"why":"members on the gold plan get unlimited hours（ゴールドプランは時間無制限）とある。"},{"q":"What should members do before their plan expires?","o":["Renew at least three days ahead","Return the door card","Print their files","Change their password"],"a":0,"why":"renew at least three days before that date（期限の3日前までに更新する）よう勧めている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0058","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"サービスエリアの案内放送","text":"Welcome to Oak Ridge Service Area. Whether you are a truck driver or a businessman on a long trip, we have what you need. Gasoline is five cents cheaper per liter until six this evening. Inside, the newsstand sells today's papers and every kind of phone accessory. In our clothing corner, long-sleeve shirts are two for twenty dollars. Just take a basket at the door. Feeling hungry? The Ridge Diner serves hot meals all day, and its specialty is homemade chicken pie. Clip the coupon from our free map and get a cup of coffee for one dollar. Please look at the overhead signs to find the restrooms and the exit. Drive safely.","ja":"オーク・リッジ・サービスエリアへようこそ。トラックの運転手の方にも、長距離移動中の会社員の方にも、必要なものがそろっています。ガソリンは今夕6時まで、1リットルあたり5セント安くなっています。館内の新聞・雑誌売り場では、今日の新聞と、あらゆる種類の携帯電話の付属品を販売しています。衣料品コーナーでは、長袖のシャツが2枚で20ドルです。入口でかごをお取りください。お腹がすいていませんか。リッジ・ダイナーでは一日中温かい食事をお出ししており、名物は自家製のチキンパイです。無料の地図に付いているクーポンを切り取ると、コーヒー1杯が1ドルになります。お手洗いと出口は、頭上の案内板でご確認ください。安全運転でどうぞ。","words":[["businessman","freq:businessman"],["Gasoline","freq:gasoline"],["newsstand","freq:newsstand"],["accessory","freq:accessory"],["sleeve","freq:sleeve"],["basket","freq:basket"],["Diner","freq:diner"],["specialty","freq:specialty"],["Clip","freq:clip"],["overhead","freq:overhead"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is cheaper until six this evening?","o":["Coffee","Shirts","Newspapers","Gasoline"],"a":3,"why":"Gasoline is five cents cheaper per liter until six this evening（ガソリンが6時まで安い）とある。"},{"q":"What is the diner's specialty?","o":["Chicken pie","Hot soup","Hamburgers","Fresh bread"],"a":0,"why":"its specialty is homemade chicken pie（名物は自家製のチキンパイ）とある。"},{"q":"How can visitors get coffee for one dollar?","o":["By buying gasoline","By using a coupon from the map","By ordering a meal","By showing a receipt"],"a":1,"why":"Clip the coupon from our free map（無料の地図のクーポンを切り取る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0059","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"健康番組の解説","text":"Welcome to Health Check. Today's topic is vitamin and mineral pills. Many people dislike vegetables and hope that a pill can do the same job. Some advertisements even claim that their product will cure a headache in minutes or make you look ten years younger. These claims may sound plausible, but they often mislead the public. Last month, an editorial in a leading medical journal called such advertising inappropriate, because the effectiveness of most pills has never been tested properly. When scientists looked at several products under a microscope, they found that some contained almost nothing useful. So what should you do? Eat fresh food, sleep well, and ask your doctor before you buy.","ja":"「ヘルス・チェック」へようこそ。今日の話題は、ビタミンやミネラルの錠剤です。野菜が嫌いで、錠剤が同じ働きをしてくれればと期待する人は多くいます。広告の中には、自社の製品が数分で頭痛を治すとか、10歳若く見せるとまで主張するものもあります。こうした主張はもっともらしく聞こえますが、人々を誤解させることがよくあります。先月、ある有力な医学誌の社説は、そうした広告を不適切だと述べました。ほとんどの錠剤の有効性は、きちんと検証されたことがないからです。科学者がいくつかの製品を顕微鏡で調べたところ、役に立つものがほとんど入っていないものもありました。では、どうすればよいのでしょうか。新鮮なものを食べ、よく眠り、買う前に医師に相談してください。","words":[["vitamin","freq:vitamin"],["mineral","freq:mineral"],["dislike","freq:dislike"],["headache","freq:headache"],["plausible","freq:plausible"],["mislead","freq:mislead"],["editorial","freq:editorial"],["inappropriate","freq:inappropriate"],["effectiveness","freq:effectiveness"],["microscope","freq:microscope"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the talk mainly about?","o":["How to cure a headache","Vitamin and mineral pills","How to cook vegetables","A new medical journal"],"a":1,"why":"Today's topic is vitamin and mineral pills（今日の話題はビタミンやミネラルの錠剤）とある。"},{"q":"What did the editorial say about the advertising?","o":["It is too expensive.","It is helpful to doctors.","It is not appropriate.","It is aimed at young people."],"a":2,"why":"called such advertising inappropriate（そうした広告を不適切だと述べた）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker advise listeners to do?","o":["Ask a doctor before buying","Take pills every day","Read more advertisements","Stop eating vegetables"],"a":0,"why":"ask your doctor before you buy（買う前に医師に相談する）と勧めている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0060","page":"freq","group":"501〜600","kind":"旅行会社からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, Ms. Tanaka. This is Leo, your trip planner at Globe Tours. I am calling about your group's visit to India. First, everyone needs a visa, and the embassy takes about ten days to issue one. Please proofread each form before you send it, because a single wrong letter can cause a delay. Second, we have received half of the payment. The remainder is due by May 1. Third, on the day of departure, your group should meet in the assembly area on the third floor of Terminal 1. If you are unsure where it is, I will send a map. One more thing: the hotel in Delhi is still unspecified, but I will confirm it this week. Travel insurance is a necessity, and your points will accumulate with each trip.","ja":"もしもし、タナカ様。グローブ・ツアーズで旅行の企画を担当しているレオです。皆様のインド旅行の件でお電話しました。まず、全員にビザが必要で、大使館が発給するまでに10日ほどかかります。たった1文字の誤りでも遅れの原因になりますので、送る前に用紙を1枚ずつ見直してください。次に、代金の半分をいただいております。残りは5月1日が期限です。3つ目に、出発当日は、第1ターミナル3階の集合場所にお集まりください。場所がはっきり分からない場合は、地図をお送りします。もう一点。デリーのホテルはまだ決まっていませんが、今週中に確定します。旅行保険は必ず必要です。ポイントはご旅行のたびにたまっていきます。","words":[["planner","freq:planner"],["visa","freq:visa"],["embassy","freq:embassy"],["proofread","freq:proofread"],["remainder","freq:remainder"],["assembly","freq:assembly"],["unsure","freq:unsure"],["unspecified","freq:unspecified"],["necessity","freq:necessity"],["accumulate","freq:accumulate"]],"qs":[{"q":"How long does it take to get a visa?","o":["One day","Three days","One month","About ten days"],"a":3,"why":"the embassy takes about ten days to issue one（大使館の発給に10日ほど）とある。"},{"q":"What is due by May 1?","o":["The visa forms","The rest of the payment","The hotel booking","The insurance form"],"a":1,"why":"The remainder is due by May 1（残りの代金は5月1日が期限）とある。"},{"q":"What has not been decided yet?","o":["The hotel in Delhi","The meeting place","The departure date","The price of the tour"],"a":0,"why":"the hotel in Delhi is still unspecified（デリーのホテルはまだ決まっていない）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0061","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"客船の船内放送","text":"Good morning, and welcome aboard the Ocean Star. We are leaving the harbor now, so please stay seated and fasten your belt if you are in the small boats. The weather today is mild, with plenty of sunshine, and the sea is calm, so we expect to sail smoothly all the way to Port Reno. The pool on the upper deck opens at ten. On the lower level, you will find a sauna, and you can book a massage at the spa desk. A printed timetable of today's shows is in your room. If you would like to reserve a table for dinner, our concierge on the main floor will be happy to help. Have a wonderful day at sea.","ja":"おはようございます。オーシャン・スター号へようこそ。ただいま港を出るところですので、小型ボートにお乗りの方は席に着いたまま、ベルトをお締めください。今日は穏やかな天気で日ざしもたっぷりあり、海も静かですので、ポート・リノまでずっと順調に航行できる見込みです。上のデッキのプールは10時に開きます。下の階にはサウナがあり、スパの受付でマッサージの予約もできます。本日の催しの時刻表は、印刷したものがお部屋にございます。夕食の席をご予約になりたい方は、メインフロアの接客係が喜んでお手伝いします。海の上でのすばらしい一日をお過ごしください。","words":[["aboard","freq:aboard"],["fasten","freq:fasten"],["mild","freq:mild"],["sunshine","freq:sunshine"],["smoothly","freq:smoothly"],["deck","freq:deck"],["sauna","freq:sauna"],["massage","freq:massage"],["timetable","freq:timetable"],["concierge","freq:concierge"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the speaker say about the weather?","o":["It is pleasant.","It is stormy.","It will get cold.","It will rain at ten."],"a":0,"why":"The weather today is mild, with plenty of sunshine（穏やかで日ざしもたっぷり）とある。"},{"q":"Where is the pool?","o":["On the lower level","Next to the spa desk","On the upper deck","On the main floor"],"a":2,"why":"The pool on the upper deck opens at ten（上のデッキのプール）とある。下の階にあるのはサウナ。"},{"q":"Who can help with a dinner reservation?","o":["The captain","The concierge","The spa staff","The show manager"],"a":1,"why":"our concierge on the main floor will be happy to help（メインフロアの接客係が手伝う）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0062","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"人事部長の報告","text":"Good morning. I would like to report on recruitment and staff turnover. Last year, too many young employees left us within twelve months. When we asked why, most said they saw no path to advancement. So we made three changes. First, every new employee now has a mentor for the first year. Second, we allocate two days a month to training. Third, managers can nominate anyone who performs consistently well for our leadership course. The results have been exceptional: turnover has fallen by half. We also pay a bonus of five hundred dollars for each successful referral from our own staff. Our goal for next year is ambitious, but I believe we can keep ninety percent of our new hires.","ja":"おはようございます。採用と離職率についてご報告します。昨年は、あまりにも多くの若手社員が12か月以内に退職しました。理由を尋ねたところ、ほとんどが昇進への道が見えないと答えました。そこで3つの変更を行いました。1つ目、新入社員には全員、最初の1年間、指導役を付けています。2つ目、月に2日を研修に割り当てています。3つ目、管理職は、一貫して優れた働きをする人なら誰でも、当社の指導者養成講座に推薦できます。結果は並外れたものでした。離職率は半分に下がりました。また、社員からの紹介で採用が決まるたびに、500ドルの報奨金を支払っています。来年の目標は意欲的ですが、新規採用者の9割を引き留められると信じています。","words":[["recruitment","freq:recruitment"],["turnover","freq:turnover"],["advancement","freq:advancement"],["mentor","freq:mentor"],["allocate","freq:allocate"],["nominate","freq:nominate"],["consistently","freq:consistently"],["exceptional","freq:exceptional"],["referral","freq:referral"],["ambitious","freq:ambitious"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did many young employees leave?","o":["The pay was low.","The hours were long.","The training was too hard.","They saw no chance of promotion."],"a":3,"why":"most said they saw no path to advancement（昇進への道が見えないと答えた）とある。advancement を promotion と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What does every new employee now have?","o":["A mentor","A private office","A company car","A bonus"],"a":0,"why":"every new employee now has a mentor for the first year（最初の1年、指導役が付く）とある。"},{"q":"What happens when staff recommend someone who is hired?","o":["They get extra training days.","They receive five hundred dollars.","They join the leadership course.","They become mentors."],"a":1,"why":"a bonus of five hundred dollars for each successful referral（紹介が採用につながるたびに500ドル）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0063","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"起業家向けセミナー","text":"Thank you for joining tonight's seminar for the new entrepreneur. My name is Paul Grant, and I am an attorney who works with small companies. Let's say you have a great invention. What should you do first? Apply for a patent before you show it to anyone. Without one, another firm could copy your idea, and that would not even be a violation of the law. Next, keep clear documentation of every test and drawing. When you work with a partner, get written consent before you share any details. If you sell overseas, a government office must certify your product, and you may need special authorization to export it. These are only preliminary steps, but they will protect you later.","ja":"新しく起業する方のための今夜のセミナーにご参加いただき、ありがとうございます。ポール・グラントと申します。小さな会社を相手に仕事をしている弁護士です。たとえば、すばらしい発明をしたとしましょう。最初に何をすべきでしょうか。誰かに見せる前に、特許を出願してください。特許がなければ、ほかの会社があなたのアイデアをまねても、法律の違反にすらなりません。次に、あらゆる試験や図面について、はっきりした書類を残してください。協力相手と仕事をするときは、詳しい内容を伝える前に、書面で同意を得ておきます。海外で販売する場合は、役所が製品を認定しなければならず、輸出に特別な許可が必要になることもあります。これらは準備段階の手順にすぎませんが、後になって皆さんを守ってくれます。","words":[["entrepreneur","freq:entrepreneur"],["attorney","freq:attorney"],["invention","freq:invention"],["patent","freq:patent"],["violation","freq:violation"],["documentation","freq:documentation"],["consent","freq:consent"],["certify","freq:certify"],["authorization","freq:authorization"],["preliminary","freq:preliminary"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the speaker?","o":["An inventor","A government officer","A lawyer","An exporter"],"a":2,"why":"I am an attorney who works with small companies（小さな会社を相手にする弁護士）とある。attorney を lawyer と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What should an inventor do first?","o":["Show the idea to a partner","Apply for a patent","Sell the product overseas","Hire a designer"],"a":1,"why":"Apply for a patent before you show it to anyone（誰かに見せる前に特許を出願する）とある。"},{"q":"What is needed before sharing details with a partner?","o":["Written consent","A government stamp","A test report","An export permit"],"a":0,"why":"get written consent before you share any details（詳細を伝える前に書面で同意を得る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0064","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"大学の新入生案内","text":"Hello, and congratulations on your acceptance to the Hartley Institute of Science. I am your student guide today. This short tour will familiarize you with the campus. We are now standing in front of the chemistry building. The labs are on the second floor, and you will find a locker for your coat and bag in the basement. Please remember your locker number. The library is on your right. It gives an informative talk for new students every Friday at four. One note about money: your tuition for the first term must be paid by September 10. You can pay online through the student webpage. Now, let's walk over to the dining hall.","ja":"こんにちは。ハートリー科学研究所への合格、おめでとうございます。今日は私が学生ガイドを務めます。この短い見学で、構内に慣れていただきます。今、化学棟の前に立っています。実験室は2階にあり、コートやかばんを入れるロッカーは地下にあります。ロッカーの番号を覚えておいてください。右手にあるのが図書館です。毎週金曜の4時に、新入生向けのためになる説明会を開いています。お金について一点。1学期の授業料は9月10日までに納めなければなりません。学生用のウェブページからオンラインで支払えます。では、食堂へ歩いていきましょう。","words":[["acceptance","freq:acceptance"],["Institute","freq:institute"],["familiarize","freq:familiarize"],["campus","freq:campus"],["chemistry","freq:chemistry"],["locker","freq:locker"],["basement","freq:basement"],["informative","freq:informative"],["tuition","freq:tuition"],["webpage","freq:webpage"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where are the lockers?","o":["In the basement","On the second floor","In the library","In the dining hall"],"a":0,"why":"you will find a locker ... in the basement（ロッカーは地下）とある。2階にあるのは実験室。"},{"q":"What does the library offer every Friday?","o":["A free lunch","A campus tour","A chemistry class","A talk for new students"],"a":3,"why":"It gives an informative talk for new students every Friday at four（毎週金曜4時に新入生向けの説明会）とある。"},{"q":"What must be done by September 10?","o":["Choosing a locker","Visiting the lab","Paying tuition","Signing up for the tour"],"a":2,"why":"your tuition for the first term must be paid by September 10（1学期の授業料は9月10日までに納める）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0065","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"通販の自動音声案内","text":"Thank you for calling the Bell and Moss customer hotline. All of our staff are unavailable right now, so please listen to the following information. If you wish to return an item, detach the lower half of your delivery slip and put it in the box. Return postage is free for orders over forty dollars. For smaller orders, a fee of three dollars is payable by the customer. Gift cards are sold separately and cannot be returned. Discount codes are applicable only at checkout on our Web site, not by phone. If you did not receive our confirmation e-mail, please look in your spam folder. Alternatively, press two to leave a message, and we will call you back within one day.","ja":"ベル・アンド・モスのお客様相談窓口にお電話ありがとうございます。ただいま係員は全員、対応できません。以下のご案内をお聞きください。商品を返品される場合は、納品書の下半分を切り離し、箱に入れてください。40ドルを超えるご注文は、返送の郵便料金が無料です。それより少額のご注文は、3ドルの手数料をお客様にお支払いいただきます。ギフトカードは別売りで、返品できません。割引コードが使えるのは、当社ウェブサイトの会計の画面だけで、お電話ではご利用になれません。確認メールが届いていない場合は、迷惑メールのフォルダーをご覧ください。あるいは、2を押して伝言をお残しいただければ、1日以内に折り返しお電話します。","words":[["hotline","freq:hotline"],["unavailable","freq:unavailable"],["detach","freq:detach"],["postage","freq:postage"],["payable","freq:payable"],["separately","freq:separately"],["applicable","freq:applicable"],["checkout","freq:checkout"],["spam","freq:spam"],["Alternatively","freq:alternatively"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should customers put in the box when returning an item?","o":["A gift card","Part of the delivery slip","A discount code","A copy of the e-mail"],"a":1,"why":"detach the lower half of your delivery slip and put it in the box（納品書の下半分を切り離して箱に入れる）とある。"},{"q":"When is return postage free?","o":["When the order is over forty dollars","When the item is a gift card","When the customer calls first","When the item is broken"],"a":0,"why":"Return postage is free for orders over forty dollars（40ドルを超える注文は無料）とある。"},{"q":"Where can discount codes be used?","o":["On the phone","In the store","In an e-mail","At the online checkout"],"a":3,"why":"applicable only at checkout on our Web site, not by phone（ウェブサイトの会計の画面でだけ使える）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0066","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"新聞社の営業会議","text":"Good morning, team. Let's talk about advertising sales. As you know, the economic downturn has hit us hard, and our circulation has dropped by eight percent. Accordingly, some of our biggest advertisers have cut their budgets. But I see a chance here. First, stop sending the same generic offer to everyone. Every salesman should study the client's business before calling. Second, seasonal pages work well. Last December's holiday section sold out in a week, so let's plan one for spring. Third, we must cut unnecessary costs. Our printing bill is excessive, and I will speak to the supplier myself. If we do these three things, I am sure we can maximize our income in the second half of the year.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。広告の営業について話しましょう。ご存じのとおり、景気の低迷で当社は大きな打撃を受け、発行部数は8パーセント落ちました。それに伴って、最大手の広告主の一部が予算を削っています。しかし、私はここに好機があると見ています。まず、同じありきたりの提案を全員に送るのはやめましょう。販売員は皆、電話をかける前に顧客の事業を調べるべきです。次に、季節の特集ページは成果が出ます。昨年12月の年末特集は1週間で完売しましたので、春にも企画しましょう。3つ目に、不必要な費用を削らなければなりません。印刷代は度を越しており、私が自分で業者と話します。この3つを実行すれば、下半期の収入を最大限に伸ばせると確信しています。","words":[["downturn","freq:downturn"],["circulation","freq:circulation"],["Accordingly","freq:accordingly"],["advertisers","freq:advertiser"],["generic","freq:generic"],["salesman","freq:salesman"],["seasonal","freq:seasonal"],["unnecessary","freq:unnecessary"],["excessive","freq:excessive"],["maximize","freq:maximize"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has happened to the newspaper's circulation?","o":["It has doubled.","It has stayed the same.","It has fallen.","It has moved online."],"a":2,"why":"our circulation has dropped by eight percent（発行部数が8パーセント落ちた）とある。"},{"q":"What should each salesman do before calling a client?","o":["Learn about the client's business","Send a generic offer","Lower the price","Visit the printer"],"a":0,"why":"Every salesman should study the client's business before calling（電話の前に顧客の事業を調べる）とある。"},{"q":"What will the speaker do about the printing bill?","o":["Pay it at once","Talk to the supplier","Ask advertisers for help","Print fewer pages"],"a":1,"why":"Our printing bill is excessive, and I will speak to the supplier myself（印刷代は高すぎるので自分で業者と話す）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0067","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"料理イベントの案内","text":"Good evening, food lovers. The Riverside Culinary Festival returns next weekend, and it will be bigger than ever. More than forty chefs of national renown will cook with ingredients grown locally. Do not miss the baking tent, where you can taste a warm apple pie straight from the oven and decorate your own cookie. There is a candy workshop for children at eleven each day. In the evening, enjoy an elegant dinner on the balcony of the Grand Pavilion while a jazz band plays below. Tickets for the dinner are sixty dollars, and they usually sell out in a few days. Entry to the festival itself is free. For details, visit our Web site.","ja":"食を愛する皆さん、こんばんは。リバーサイド料理祭が来週末に帰ってきます。これまでで最大の規模です。全国的に名声のある料理人40人以上が、地元で育った食材を使って腕をふるいます。焼き菓子のテントをお見逃しなく。オーブンから出したばかりの温かいりんごのパイを味わい、自分だけのクッキーに飾り付けができます。毎日11時には、子ども向けのキャンディー作り教室があります。夜は、下でジャズバンドが演奏する中、グランド・パビリオンのバルコニーで上品な夕食をお楽しみください。夕食のチケットは60ドルで、たいてい数日で売り切れます。祭りそのものへの入場は無料です。詳しくは当ウェブサイトをご覧ください。","words":[["Culinary","freq:culinary"],["renown","freq:renown"],["locally","freq:locally"],["apple","freq:apple"],["pie","freq:pie"],["cookie","freq:cookie"],["candy","freq:candy"],["elegant","freq:elegant"],["balcony","freq:balcony"],["jazz","freq:jazz"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is said about the chefs?","o":["They are students.","They come from overseas.","They own the pavilion.","They are well known across the country."],"a":3,"why":"chefs of national renown（全国的に名声のある料理人）とある。"},{"q":"What can children do at eleven each day?","o":["Join a candy workshop","Listen to jazz","Bake an apple pie","Meet the chefs"],"a":0,"why":"There is a candy workshop for children at eleven each day（毎日11時に子ども向けのキャンディー教室）とある。"},{"q":"What is said about the dinner tickets?","o":["They are free.","They sell out quickly.","They are sold at the door.","They include a concert."],"a":1,"why":"they usually sell out in a few days（たいてい数日で売り切れる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0068","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"運動イベントの説明","text":"Welcome, volunteers, and thank you for helping with Sunday's City Fun Run. Let me explain the day. The event begins at nine with a parade of school bands. Every runner will collect a kit at the front tent with a number, a water bottle, and a pair of running socks. A physician will be on duty at the finish line all day. Too much sun can be harmful, so please remind people to wear a hat. After the run, there are recreational games for families, and each game needs one referee. We will rehearse the opening ceremony on Saturday at four. Please read the safety guide beforehand. See you this weekend.","ja":"ボランティアの皆さん、ようこそ。日曜の「シティ・ファン・ラン」へのご協力に感謝します。当日の流れを説明します。催しは9時に、学校の楽団によるパレードで始まります。走者は全員、正面のテントで、番号札、水のボトル、ランニング用の靴下1足が入った一式を受け取ります。医師が一日中、ゴール地点で待機します。日光を浴びすぎると体に害がありますので、帽子をかぶるよう皆さんに声をかけてください。走った後は、家族向けの娯楽のゲームがあり、各ゲームに審判が1人必要です。開会式の予行演習は土曜の4時に行います。前もって安全の手引きを読んでおいてください。では今週末に。","words":[["parade","freq:parade"],["runner","freq:runner"],["kit","freq:kit"],["socks","freq:sock"],["physician","freq:physician"],["harmful","freq:harmful"],["recreational","freq:recreational"],["referee","freq:referee"],["rehearse","freq:rehearse"],["beforehand","freq:beforehand"]],"qs":[{"q":"How will the event begin?","o":["With a speech","With a family game","With a parade","With a safety talk"],"a":2,"why":"The event begins at nine with a parade of school bands（学校の楽団のパレードで始まる）とある。"},{"q":"Who will be at the finish line all day?","o":["A doctor","A referee","A school band","A photographer"],"a":0,"why":"A physician will be on duty at the finish line all day（医師がゴール地点で待機）とある。physician を doctor と言い換えている。"},{"q":"What will happen on Saturday at four?","o":["The kits will be handed out.","The opening ceremony will be practiced.","The games will be tested.","The run will start."],"a":1,"why":"We will rehearse the opening ceremony on Saturday at four（土曜4時に開会式の予行演習）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0069","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"管理人の朝の連絡","text":"Good morning, everyone. Here are today's jobs. First, a truck will tow the old car that has been left in space twelve, and snow removal in the parking lot starts at eight. Second, the pool pump stopped last night. Before you call the repair company, check that someone did not simply pull out the plug. Third, please polish the brass doors in the lobby and put fresh flowers in the vase at the front desk. Guests notice small things, and we must not overlook them. I check the rooms periodically, and last week the results were satisfactory, but the noise from the ongoing roof work continues to irritate some guests. Offer them a room on the quiet side.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。今日の作業を伝えます。まず、12番の区画に放置されている古い車を、トラックがけん引して運び出します。駐車場の除雪は8時に始まります。次に、昨夜プールのポンプが止まりました。修理会社に電話する前に、誰かが単にプラグを抜いただけではないか確かめてください。3つ目に、ロビーの真ちゅうの扉を磨き、フロントの花びんに新しい花を生けてください。お客様は小さなことに気づきますので、私たちは見落としてはいけません。私は定期的に客室を点検しており、先週の結果は満足のいくものでした。ただ、続いている屋根工事の騒音が、引き続き一部のお客様をいらだたせています。そうした方には静かな側の部屋をご案内してください。","words":[["tow","freq:tow"],["removal","freq:removal"],["plug","freq:plug"],["polish","freq:polish"],["vase","freq:vase"],["overlook","freq:overlook"],["periodically","freq:periodically"],["satisfactory","freq:satisfactory"],["ongoing","freq:ongoing"],["irritate","freq:irritate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen to the car in space twelve?","o":["It will be washed.","It will be sold.","It will be repaired.","It will be taken away."],"a":3,"why":"a truck will tow the old car（トラックが古い車をけん引する）とある。"},{"q":"What should staff check before calling the repair company?","o":["Whether the pump is plugged in","Whether the pool is clean","Whether the lobby doors are locked","Whether the snow has been cleared"],"a":0,"why":"check that someone did not simply pull out the plug（プラグが抜かれただけではないか確かめる）とある。"},{"q":"What is bothering some guests?","o":["The cold weather","The noise from roof work","The smell of the flowers","The small rooms"],"a":1,"why":"the noise from the ongoing roof work continues to irritate some guests（続いている屋根工事の騒音）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0070","page":"freq","group":"601〜700","kind":"テレビ番組の案内","text":"Here is tonight's lineup on Channel Six. At seven, we present a documentary about the great earthquake of 1923, with descriptive letters written by people who lived through it. At eight, Language Lab looks at intonation: how the same English sentence can sound friendly or rude. Our guest is a translator who has worked at the United Nations. At nine, Treasure Hunt visits an auction where a farmer sells the coin collection of a lifetime. If you want to amuse the children, switch to our kids' channel for Ocean Friends, in which a young dog learns to surf. Viewers can also opt to watch any of these programs later on our Web site. Stay with us.","ja":"チャンネル6の今夜の番組をご案内します。7時は、1923年の大地震についての記録映画です。地震を生き延びた人々が書いた、描写の細かい手紙を紹介します。8時の「ランゲージ・ラボ」は、抑揚を取り上げます。同じ英語の文が、どうして親しげにも失礼にも聞こえるのかを探ります。ゲストは、国際連合で働いたことのある翻訳者です。9時の「トレジャー・ハント」は、ある農家の方が生涯をかけて集めた硬貨を売る競売を訪ねます。お子さんを楽しませたいなら、子ども向けチャンネルの「オーシャン・フレンズ」に切り替えてください。子犬が波乗りを覚えるお話です。これらの番組は、後で当ウェブサイトで見ることも選べます。チャンネルはそのままで。","words":[["documentary","freq:documentary"],["earthquake","freq:earthquake"],["descriptive","freq:descriptive"],["intonation","freq:intonation"],["translator","freq:translator"],["auction","freq:auction"],["lifetime","freq:lifetime"],["amuse","freq:amuse"],["surf","freq:surf"],["opt","freq:opt"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the seven o'clock program about?","o":["A language school","An earthquake","A coin collection","A dog"],"a":1,"why":"a documentary about the great earthquake of 1923（1923年の大地震の記録映画）とある。"},{"q":"Who is the guest on Language Lab?","o":["A farmer","A teacher","A translator","A historian"],"a":2,"why":"Our guest is a translator who has worked at the United Nations（国連で働いた翻訳者）とある。"},{"q":"What can viewers do on the Web site?","o":["Watch the programs later","Buy coins","Send letters","Join an auction"],"a":0,"why":"opt to watch any of these programs later on our Web site（後でウェブサイトで見ることを選べる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0071","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"料理長の開店前の話","text":"Good afternoon, team. We have a full house tonight, so listen carefully. Our special entrée is seafood pasta, and I want it to taste authentic. Fry the garlic slowly in a hot pan, and add the tomatoes only at the end. The bread was specially made for us this morning by the bakery on Oak Street, so serve it warm. Table nine is a birthday party of twelve. They may be noisy, so please seat quiet couples on the other side of the room. One more thing: last night, someone managed to spill soup on a guest's jacket. Carry only two bowls at a time. Let's make this an enjoyable evening for everyone.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。今夜は満席ですので、よく聞いてください。本日の特別な主菜は魚介のパスタで、本場の味に仕上げたいと思います。にんにくは熱したフライパンでゆっくり炒め、トマトは最後に加えてください。パンは今朝、オーク通りのパン屋が当店のために特別に焼いたものですから、温かい状態でお出ししてください。9番テーブルは12人の誕生日会です。にぎやかになるかもしれませんので、静かに過ごしたいお二人連れは部屋の反対側にご案内してください。もう一つ。昨夜、お客様の上着にスープをこぼした人がいました。運ぶのは一度に2皿までにしてください。皆さんにとって楽しい夜にしましょう。","words":[["entrée","freq:entrée"],["pasta","freq:pasta"],["authentic","freq:authentic"],["Fry","freq:fry"],["pan","freq:pan"],["specially","freq:specially"],["bakery","freq:bakery"],["noisy","freq:noisy"],["spill","freq:spill"],["enjoyable","freq:enjoyable"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is tonight's special dish?","o":["Seafood pasta","Tomato soup","Garlic bread","Birthday cake"],"a":0,"why":"Our special entrée is seafood pasta（特別な主菜は魚介のパスタ）とある。"},{"q":"Where should quiet couples be seated?","o":["At table nine","Near the kitchen","Away from the birthday party","By the window"],"a":2,"why":"seat quiet couples on the other side of the room（部屋の反対側に案内する）とある。誕生日会がにぎやかになりそうなため。"},{"q":"What happened last night?","o":["A guest left without paying.","Soup was spilled on a guest.","The bread arrived late.","A party was canceled."],"a":1,"why":"someone managed to spill soup on a guest's jacket（お客様の上着にスープをこぼした）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0072","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"運送会社の運転手への連絡","text":"Good morning, drivers. Here are today's notes from the freight office. Truck four will carry twelve tons of paper to Dayton. Every carton must be tied down before you leave. Truck seven has one parcel marked hazardous. Keep it in the rear compartment, away from the food boxes. Remember that the bridge toll on Route 30 went up this week, so use the company card, not cash. Fuel is now four dollars a gallon, so please drive at a steady speed and write your mileage in the log at the end of the day. Finally, the postal service has changed its closing time to five, so all mail bags must reach the depot by four thirty. Drive safely.","ja":"運転手の皆さん、おはようございます。貨物事務所から今日の連絡です。4号車は紙12トンをデイトンへ運びます。出発前に、段ボール箱はすべて固定してください。7号車には「危険物」と表示された小包が1つあります。食品の箱から離して、後部の区画に置いてください。30号線の橋の通行料が今週値上がりしましたので、現金ではなく会社のカードを使ってください。燃料は現在1ガロン4ドルですので、一定の速度で走り、一日の終わりに走行距離を記録簿に書いてください。最後に、郵便事業の締め切り時刻が5時に変わりました。郵便袋はすべて4時半までに集配所に届けてください。安全運転でお願いします。","words":[["freight","freq:freight"],["tons","freq:ton"],["carton","freq:carton"],["parcel","freq:parcel"],["hazardous","freq:hazardous"],["compartment","freq:compartment"],["toll","freq:toll"],["gallon","freq:gallon"],["mileage","freq:mileage"],["postal","freq:postal"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where should the hazardous parcel be kept?","o":["In the front seat","With the food boxes","At the depot","In the rear compartment"],"a":3,"why":"Keep it in the rear compartment, away from the food boxes（食品の箱から離して後部の区画に）とある。"},{"q":"How should drivers pay the bridge toll?","o":["With the company card","In cash","By phone","At the freight office"],"a":0,"why":"use the company card, not cash（現金ではなく会社のカードを使う）とある。"},{"q":"By when must mail bags reach the depot?","o":["Four o'clock","Four thirty","Five o'clock","The end of the day"],"a":1,"why":"all mail bags must reach the depot by four thirty（4時半までに集配所へ）とある。5時は郵便事業の締め切り時刻。"}]},
{"id":"f-0073","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"総務部からの連絡","text":"Hello, everyone. This is a short reminder from the general affairs team. We are trying to economize this year, and small things add up. First, supplies. Please take only one note pad and one stapler per desk from the supply room, and write what you take on the shared spreadsheet. Second, the copier on the fourth floor needs new toner, which will arrive tomorrow. Until then, please use the one by the restroom. Third, we will streamline cleaning: staff will empty the bins only once a day, so please keep your own desk tidy. Finally, the machines that vend drinks on each floor will be replaced on Friday with models that use half the power.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。総務からの短いお知らせです。今年は経費を節約しようとしており、小さなことも積み重なれば大きくなります。まず、備品についてです。備品室から持ち出すメモ用紙とホチキスは1つの机につき1つずつにして、持ち出した物は共有の表計算シートに記入してください。次に、4階のコピー機は新しいトナーが必要で、明日届きます。それまでは、お手洗いのそばの機械を使ってください。3つ目に、清掃を効率化します。係がごみ箱を空にするのは1日1回だけになりますので、自分の机はきちんと片づけておいてください。最後に、各階の飲み物を販売する機械は、金曜に、消費電力が半分の機種に入れ替えます。","words":[["reminder","freq:reminder"],["economize","freq:economize"],["pad","freq:pad"],["stapler","freq:stapler"],["spreadsheet","freq:spreadsheet"],["toner","freq:toner"],["restroom","freq:restroom"],["streamline","freq:streamline"],["tidy","freq:tidy"],["vend","freq:vend"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should staff do when they take supplies?","o":["Record it on a spreadsheet","Ask their manager","Pay at the supply room","Send an e-mail"],"a":0,"why":"write what you take on the shared spreadsheet（持ち出した物を共有の表計算シートに書く）とある。"},{"q":"Which copier should staff use until tomorrow?","o":["The one on the fourth floor","The one in the supply room","The one near the restroom","The one by the vending machines"],"a":2,"why":"please use the one by the restroom（お手洗いのそばの機械を使う）とある。"},{"q":"What will be replaced on Friday?","o":["The bins","The drink machines","The staplers","The cleaning staff"],"a":1,"why":"The machines that vend drinks ... will be replaced on Friday（飲み物を販売する機械を金曜に入れ替える）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0074","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"上司からの指示","text":"Hi, Kevin. I have read your draft of the annual report, and I would like you to make each correction I marked by Wednesday. First, please shorten the introduction. Three pages is too long. Second, clarify how you reached the profit figure on page ten. I think you forgot to subtract the shipping costs. Third, the evidence for the claim on page twelve is insufficient, so add last year's survey. Do not copy the consultant's words directly. Paraphrase them. Fourth, compile all the tables in an appendix at the back, and ask the design team to improve the graphics. The report is substantially better than last year's, so thank you. Call me if anything is unclear.","ja":"もしもし、ケビン。年次報告書の下書きを読みました。印を付けた訂正を、水曜までにすべて直してください。まず、序文を短くしてください。3ページは長すぎます。次に、10ページの利益の数字をどう出したのかをはっきりさせてください。送料を引くのを忘れているように思います。3つ目に、12ページの主張は根拠が不十分ですので、昨年の調査を加えてください。コンサルタントの言葉をそのまま写してはいけません。言い換えてください。4つ目に、表はすべて巻末の付録にまとめ、図をもっと良くするようデザイン班に頼んでください。報告書は昨年よりかなり良くなっています。ありがとう。分かりにくい点があれば電話してください。","words":[["correction","freq:correction"],["shorten","freq:shorten"],["clarify","freq:clarify"],["subtract","freq:subtract"],["insufficient","freq:insufficient"],["Paraphrase","freq:paraphrase"],["compile","freq:compile"],["appendix","freq:appendix"],["graphics","freq:graphics"],["substantially","freq:substantially"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is wrong with the introduction?","o":["It has errors.","It is too long.","It is missing.","It copies another report."],"a":1,"why":"please shorten the introduction. Three pages is too long（序文は3ページで長すぎる）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker think Kevin forgot to do?","o":["Add last year's survey","Thank the consultant","Send the tables","Take away the shipping costs"],"a":3,"why":"I think you forgot to subtract the shipping costs（送料を引くのを忘れたと思う）とある。subtract を take away と言い換えている。"},{"q":"Where should the tables go?","o":["In an appendix","On page ten","In the introduction","In a separate e-mail"],"a":0,"why":"compile all the tables in an appendix at the back（巻末の付録にまとめる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0075","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"展示会での製品説明","text":"Thank you for stopping at our booth. Let me show you the Lumo, a portable printer that weighs less than a kilogram. It is compatible with any phone or tablet, and you can customize the cover with your company's colors. The Lumo is especially handy for sales staff who need to print a contract in a client's office. During the fair, we are offering an introductory price of ninety-nine dollars. That is thirty percent off. The Lumo has already received favorable reviews in three business magazines, and thanks to that publicity, it is now sold in stores nationwide. Would you like to try it yourself? Just send a photo from your phone.","ja":"当社のブースにお立ち寄りいただきありがとうございます。重さが1キログラムに満たない、持ち運びできるプリンター「ルモ」をご紹介します。どの携帯電話やタブレット端末とも互換性があり、カバーは御社の色に合わせて作ることができます。ルモは、顧客の事務所で契約書を印刷する必要がある営業担当者に、とりわけ便利です。見本市の期間中は、発売記念の価格99ドルでご提供しています。3割引です。ルモはすでにビジネス誌3誌で好意的な評価を受けており、その評判のおかげで、今では全国の店で販売されています。ご自身で試してみませんか。携帯電話から写真を送るだけです。","words":[["booth","freq:booth"],["portable","freq:portable"],["compatible","freq:compatible"],["tablet","freq:tablet"],["customize","freq:customize"],["handy","freq:handy"],["introductory","freq:introductory"],["favorable","freq:favorable"],["publicity","freq:publicity"],["nationwide","freq:nationwide"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the Lumo?","o":["A tablet","A phone cover","A small printer","A business magazine"],"a":2,"why":"the Lumo, a portable printer（持ち運びできるプリンター）とある。"},{"q":"Who is the product especially useful for?","o":["Sales staff","Magazine writers","Store owners","Designers"],"a":0,"why":"especially handy for sales staff who need to print a contract（契約書を印刷する営業担当者に特に便利）とある。"},{"q":"What is offered during the fair?","o":["A free cover","A special low price","A two-year guarantee","A magazine subscription"],"a":1,"why":"an introductory price of ninety-nine dollars. That is thirty percent off（発売記念価格で3割引）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0076","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"保養地の広告","text":"Need a break? Come to Sandy Bay, a seaside resort conveniently located only ninety minutes from the city. Our all-inclusive weekend package covers your room, three meals a day, and every kind of recreation, from tennis to sailing. Start your morning with yoga on the beach, and then relieve your tired muscles at our hot spring spa. On Saturday night, watch a firework show from the pier. Bring a scarf, because the sea wind can be cool. This month, your spouse stays for half price, and children under ten stay free. Rooms are filling quickly for the summer, so call Sandy Bay today and give yourself the rest you deserve.","ja":"ひと休みが必要ですか。サンディ・ベイへお越しください。都心からわずか90分という便利な場所にある、海辺の保養地です。すべて込みの週末プランには、お部屋、1日3回の食事、そしてテニスからヨットまであらゆる娯楽が含まれます。朝は浜辺でのヨガで始め、その後は温泉スパで疲れた筋肉をほぐしてください。土曜の夜には、桟橋から花火をご覧いただけます。海風は冷えることがありますので、スカーフをお持ちください。今月は、配偶者の方が半額で、10歳未満のお子様は無料でご宿泊いただけます。夏のお部屋は急速に埋まっています。今日サンディ・ベイにお電話のうえ、ふさわしい休息をご自身に贈ってください。","words":[["seaside","freq:seaside"],["conveniently","freq:conveniently"],["inclusive","freq:inclusive"],["recreation","freq:recreation"],["yoga","freq:yoga"],["relieve","freq:relieve"],["spa","freq:spa"],["firework","freq:firework"],["scarf","freq:scarf"],["spouse","freq:spouse"]],"qs":[{"q":"How far is Sandy Bay from the city?","o":["Thirty minutes","One hour","Three hours","Ninety minutes"],"a":3,"why":"only ninety minutes from the city（都心から90分）とある。"},{"q":"What does the weekend package include?","o":["Room, meals, and activities","Only the room","Train tickets","A free scarf"],"a":0,"why":"covers your room, three meals a day, and every kind of recreation（部屋・食事・娯楽を含む）とある。"},{"q":"What is offered this month?","o":["Free yoga lessons","A half-price stay for a spouse","A free firework show","A discount for groups of ten"],"a":1,"why":"your spouse stays for half price（配偶者は半額）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0077","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"創業者をたたえる式典","text":"Good evening. Tonight we honor Dr. Elena Ruiz, the founder of the Ruiz Children's Hospital. Forty years ago, she opened a clinic with two rooms and one nurse. Her dedication and creativity turned it into one of the most influential centers of healthcare in the country. She has also helped to fundraise more than ten million dollars for medical research. Many of you know her as a member of the university faculty, where she still teaches every spring. Her old classmate, Dr. Paul Kim, will now say a few words. Later, as a courtesy to our guests from overseas, the forum on children's health will be held in both English and Spanish. Please welcome Dr. Kim.","ja":"こんばんは。今夜は、ルイス小児病院の創設者、エレナ・ルイス博士をたたえます。40年前、博士は2部屋と看護師1人だけの診療所を開きました。博士の献身と創造性が、その診療所を、国内でも有数の影響力を持つ医療の拠点へと変えました。博士は医学研究のために1,000万ドルを超える資金を集めることにも力を尽くしてきました。皆さんの多くは、大学の教授陣の一員としての博士をご存じでしょう。今も毎年春に教えています。ここで、昔の同級生であるポール・キム博士からひと言いただきます。この後、海外からのお客様への配慮として、子どもの健康についての討論会は英語とスペイン語の両方で行います。キム博士をお迎えください。","words":[["founder","freq:founder"],["dedication","freq:dedication"],["creativity","freq:creativity"],["influential","freq:influential"],["healthcare","freq:healthcare"],["fundraise","freq:fundraise"],["faculty","freq:faculty"],["classmate","freq:classmate"],["courtesy","freq:courtesy"],["forum","freq:forum"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did Dr. Ruiz do forty years ago?","o":["She became a professor.","She raised ten million dollars.","She opened a small clinic.","She moved overseas."],"a":2,"why":"she opened a clinic with two rooms and one nurse（2部屋と看護師1人の診療所を開いた）とある。"},{"q":"Who is Dr. Paul Kim?","o":["A former classmate of Dr. Ruiz","The hospital's new director","A guest from overseas","A nurse at the clinic"],"a":0,"why":"Her old classmate, Dr. Paul Kim（昔の同級生のキム博士）とある。"},{"q":"Why will the forum be held in two languages?","o":["The speakers asked for it.","Some guests are from other countries.","It will be shown on television.","The hospital has two branches."],"a":1,"why":"as a courtesy to our guests from overseas（海外からのお客様への配慮として）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0078","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"管理会社の定例会議","text":"Thanks for coming, everyone. I want to talk about complaints at Hillview Apartments. Last month, more than one renter called us repeatedly about the same dishwasher. A repairperson visited three times but could not diagnose the fault, and the tenant is now very dissatisfied. This is a disappointment for all of us. From today, if a machine fails twice, we will replace it instead of repairing it. The maker will discontinue that model anyway. We also urgently need a clear rule for noise problems. When there is a disagreement between neighbors, please visit both sides on the same day and write a short report. Happy tenants stay longer, and that saves us money.","ja":"皆さん、お集まりいただきありがとうございます。ヒルビュー・アパートメンツへの苦情について話したいと思います。先月、同じ食器洗い機のことで、何度も繰り返し電話をかけてきた借り手が1人ではありませんでした。修理工が3回訪問しましたが、故障の原因を突き止められず、その入居者は今、大変不満を抱いています。これは私たち全員にとって残念なことです。今日から、機械が2回故障した場合は、修理ではなく交換することにします。どのみち、製造元はその機種の生産を打ち切ります。騒音の問題についても、明確な決まりが緊急に必要です。隣人どうしで意見が食い違ったときは、同じ日に双方を訪ね、短い報告書を書いてください。満足している入居者は長く住んでくれますし、それが経費の節約になります。","words":[["renter","freq:renter"],["repeatedly","freq:repeatedly"],["dishwasher","freq:dishwasher"],["repairperson","freq:repairperson"],["diagnose","freq:diagnose"],["dissatisfied","freq:dissatisfy"],["disappointment","freq:disappointment"],["discontinue","freq:discontinue"],["urgently","freq:urgently"],["disagreement","freq:disagreement"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was the problem with the dishwasher?","o":["It was too noisy.","It was delivered late.","It was the wrong model.","Its fault could not be found."],"a":3,"why":"could not diagnose the fault（故障の原因を突き止められなかった）とある。"},{"q":"What is the new rule about broken machines?","o":["Replace them after two failures","Repair them three times","Ask the tenant to pay","Call the maker first"],"a":0,"why":"if a machine fails twice, we will replace it instead of repairing it（2回故障したら修理せず交換）とある。"},{"q":"What should staff do when neighbors disagree about noise?","o":["Move one tenant","Visit both sides on the same day","Send a warning letter","Call the police"],"a":1,"why":"please visit both sides on the same day and write a short report（同じ日に双方を訪ねて報告書を書く）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0079","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"銀行の新人研修","text":"Good morning. As a new teller at First Harbor Bank, you are the face of our company. Here are a few basic rules. Be punctual: the doors open at nine, so be at your window by eight forty-five. Greet each customer politely with \"sir\" or \"ma'am.\" Some customers speak with a strong accent, so listen carefully and never hurry them. The waiting area has a rack of newspapers and one business periodical. Please check the placement of the chairs each morning so that the walkway to the advisory desk is clear. If a customer falls asleep in a chair, wake the person gently. And when you count money, do it silently, never aloud. Your trainer will now show you your window.","ja":"おはようございます。ファースト・ハーバー銀行の新しい窓口係として、皆さんは当行の顔です。基本的な決まりをいくつか伝えます。時間を守ってください。扉は9時に開きますので、8時45分までに自分の窓口に着いてください。お客様一人ひとりに「サー」または「マーム」と丁寧にあいさつします。強いなまりで話すお客様もいますので、よく聞き、決して急がせないでください。待合スペースには新聞の棚と、ビジネスの定期刊行物が1誌あります。毎朝、椅子の配置を確かめ、相談窓口への通路をふさがないようにしてください。お客様が椅子で眠ってしまったら、そっと起こしてください。お金を数えるときは、声に出さず、黙って数えます。では、指導員が皆さんの窓口へ案内します。","words":[["teller","freq:teller"],["punctual","freq:punctual"],["ma'am","freq:ma'am"],["accent","freq:accent"],["periodical","freq:periodical"],["placement","freq:placement"],["walkway","freq:walkway"],["advisory","freq:advisory"],["asleep","freq:asleep"],["silently","freq:silently"]],"qs":[{"q":"By what time should tellers be at their windows?","o":["Eight thirty","Nine o'clock","Eight forty-five","Nine fifteen"],"a":2,"why":"be at your window by eight forty-five（8時45分までに窓口に着く）とある。9時は開店時刻。"},{"q":"What should tellers check each morning?","o":["The position of the chairs","The date of the newspapers","The amount of money","The customers' names"],"a":0,"why":"check the placement of the chairs each morning（毎朝椅子の配置を確かめる）とある。"},{"q":"How should tellers count money?","o":["Aloud","Without speaking","With a customer's help","Twice"],"a":1,"why":"do it silently, never aloud（声に出さず黙って）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0080","page":"freq","group":"701〜800","kind":"地域ニュース","text":"Here are three short items from around Mill Valley. First, the drought continues. With humidity at its lowest level in ten years, the city is asking every gardener to water plants only before seven in the morning. Water consumption has already fallen by fifteen percent, which is good news. Ideally, it should fall by twenty. Second, there has been a rumor that the Belle cosmetic factory will close. The plant foreman told us today that this is not true and that forty new workers will be hired. Third, Saturday is clean-up day. Leave old furniture and other junk in front of your house by eight. However, do not put any medicine out. Unused pills should be returned to a pharmacy.","ja":"ミル・バレー各地から、短いニュースを3つお伝えします。まず、干ばつが続いています。湿度がこの10年で最も低くなっており、市は、庭の手入れをする人すべてに、植物への水やりを朝7時前だけにするよう求めています。水の消費量はすでに15パーセント減っており、これはよい知らせです。理想を言えば、20パーセント減らす必要があります。次に、ベル化粧品の工場が閉鎖されるといううわさが流れています。工場の現場監督は今日、これは事実ではなく、新たに40人を雇う予定だと話しました。3つ目に、土曜は清掃の日です。古い家具などの不要品は、8時までに家の前に出してください。ただし、薬は出さないでください。使わなかった錠剤は薬局に返してください。","words":[["drought","freq:drought"],["humidity","freq:humidity"],["gardener","freq:gardener"],["consumption","freq:consumption"],["Ideally","freq:ideally"],["rumor","freq:rumor"],["cosmetic","freq:cosmetic"],["foreman","freq:foreman"],["junk","freq:junk"],["pills","freq:pill"]],"qs":[{"q":"What are gardeners asked to do?","o":["Stop planting flowers","Use less soil","Buy water from the city","Water only early in the morning"],"a":3,"why":"water plants only before seven in the morning（水やりは朝7時前だけ）とある。"},{"q":"What did the foreman say about the factory?","o":["It will not close.","It will move.","It will cut forty jobs.","It was sold."],"a":0,"why":"this is not true and that forty new workers will be hired（閉鎖は事実ではなく40人を新規採用する）とある。"},{"q":"What should residents do with unused pills?","o":["Leave them outside by eight","Take them to a pharmacy","Throw them in the trash","Give them to a neighbor"],"a":1,"why":"Unused pills should be returned to a pharmacy（使わなかった錠剤は薬局に返す）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0081","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"市のイベント案内","text":"This Sunday, the Old Town Antique Market returns to Station Square. More than two hundred sellers will be there, so whether you are a serious collector or just want to browse, you will find something to enjoy. Look for exotic rugs from Central Asia, old paperback novels for one dollar each, and rolls of fabric in every color and stripe. The low prices may tempt you to buy too much, so here is a tip: walk around the whole market once before you spend any money. Choose wisely, and bring your own bag. There is ample parking behind the station, and it is free until noon. The market is open from eight to four.","ja":"今週の日曜、旧市街の骨董市がステーション広場に戻ってきます。200を超える売り手が出店しますので、熱心な収集家の方も、ただ見て回りたいだけの方も、楽しめるものが見つかります。中央アジアの異国風の敷物、1冊1ドルの古い文庫本の小説、あらゆる色としま模様の布地の巻物を探してみてください。値段が安いので、つい買いすぎたくなるかもしれません。そこで一つ助言です。お金を使う前に、一度、市場全体を歩いて回ってください。賢く選び、自分のかばんをお持ちください。駅の裏に十分な広さの駐車場があり、正午まで無料です。骨董市は8時から4時まで開いています。","words":[["Antique","freq:antique"],["collector","freq:collector"],["browse","freq:browse"],["exotic","freq:exotic"],["paperback","freq:paperback"],["fabric","freq:fabric"],["stripe","freq:stripe"],["tempt","freq:tempt"],["wisely","freq:wisely"],["ample","freq:ample"]],"qs":[{"q":"What costs one dollar each?","o":["Paperback novels","Rugs","Rolls of fabric","Shopping bags"],"a":0,"why":"old paperback novels for one dollar each（古い文庫本の小説が1冊1ドル）とある。"},{"q":"What tip does the speaker give?","o":["Arrive before eight","Bring cash only","Look around the whole market before buying","Park in front of the station"],"a":2,"why":"walk around the whole market once before you spend any money（お金を使う前に一度全体を歩いて回る）とある。"},{"q":"What is said about parking?","o":["It is full by noon.","It is free in the morning.","It is far from the square.","It costs one dollar."],"a":1,"why":"it is free until noon（正午まで無料）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0082","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"工事のお知らせ","text":"Good morning. This is a message for people who live and work near Carter Street. On Thursday, a large crane will arrive to lift steel beams for the new library. Trucks will unload the beams between six and nine in the morning, which will disrupt traffic and may cause congestion on nearby roads. Drivers who park on Carter Street must vacate their spaces by Wednesday night. The approximate time needed for the work is three days. A copy of the blueprint and an architectural model of the library can be seen at City Hall. One more thing: a temporary power pole will be put up at the corner. We will send timely updates by text message. Thank you for your patience.","ja":"おはようございます。カーター通りの近くにお住まいの方、お勤めの方へのお知らせです。木曜に、新しい図書館の鉄骨を吊り上げるための大型クレーンが到着します。トラックが朝6時から9時の間に鉄骨を降ろしますので、交通が乱れ、周辺の道路で渋滞が起きるおそれがあります。カーター通りに駐車している方は、水曜の夜までに場所を空けてください。作業に必要な時間は、おおよそ3日です。図書館の設計図の写しと建築模型は、市役所でご覧になれます。もう一点。角に仮設の電柱を立てます。最新の情報は、その都度、時機を逃さずテキストメッセージでお送りします。ご辛抱に感謝します。","words":[["crane","freq:crane"],["unload","freq:unload"],["disrupt","freq:disrupt"],["congestion","freq:congestion"],["vacate","freq:vacate"],["approximate","freq:approximate"],["blueprint","freq:blueprint"],["architectural","freq:architectural"],["pole","freq:pole"],["timely","freq:timely"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is being built?","o":["A library","A parking lot","A city hall","A power station"],"a":0,"why":"to lift steel beams for the new library（新しい図書館の鉄骨を吊り上げる）とある。"},{"q":"What must drivers do by Wednesday night?","o":["Pay a parking fee","Send a text message","Visit City Hall","Move their cars from Carter Street"],"a":3,"why":"must vacate their spaces by Wednesday night（水曜の夜までに駐車場所を空ける）とある。"},{"q":"How long will the work take?","o":["One morning","About three days","One week","Until Wednesday"],"a":1,"why":"The approximate time needed for the work is three days（おおよそ3日）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0083","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"ラジオの料理コーナー","text":"Welcome back to Weekend Kitchen. Summer is here, so today's topic is the perfect barbecue. You do not have to be a professional. Any amateur can do this. First, take the steak out of the cooler thirty minutes before cooking. Cold meat cooks unevenly. Second, spray a little oil on the grill so that the meat does not stick. Third, set a timer for four minutes on each side, and do not keep turning it. While the meat rests, warm a can of bean salad at the edge of the fire. If you are eating in the park, bring a blanket to sit on, and tie a balloon to a tree so that your friends can find you. After the break, we will make a sauce.","ja":"「ウィークエンド・キッチン」に戻りました。夏が来ましたので、今日の話題は完璧なバーベキューです。プロである必要はありません。素人でも誰でもできます。まず、ステーキは焼く30分前に保冷箱から出します。冷たい肉は火の通りにむらが出ます。次に、肉がくっつかないよう、焼き網に油を少し吹きかけます。3つ目に、タイマーを片面4分に合わせ、何度もひっくり返さないことです。肉を休ませている間に、豆のサラダの缶を火の端で温めます。公園で食べるなら、座るための毛布を持っていき、友人が見つけやすいように木に風船を結んでおきましょう。休憩の後は、ソースを作ります。","words":[["barbecue","freq:barbecue"],["amateur","freq:amateur"],["steak","freq:steak"],["cooler","freq:cooler"],["spray","freq:spray"],["grill","freq:grill"],["timer","freq:timer"],["bean","freq:bean"],["blanket","freq:blanket"],["balloon","freq:balloon"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why should the steak be taken out early?","o":["To make it softer","To save time","So that it cooks evenly","So that it can be cut"],"a":2,"why":"Cold meat cooks unevenly（冷たい肉は火の通りにむらが出る）ため、30分前に出すと説明している。"},{"q":"How long should each side be cooked?","o":["Four minutes","Two minutes","Thirty minutes","Until the timer rings twice"],"a":0,"why":"set a timer for four minutes on each side（片面4分）とある。"},{"q":"Why does the speaker suggest tying a balloon to a tree?","o":["To keep birds away","To help friends find the place","To mark the fire","To entertain children"],"a":1,"why":"so that your friends can find you（友人が見つけやすいように）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0084","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"部長会議での話","text":"Thank you all for coming. I want to talk about staff morale. Our last survey was a clear indicator that something is wrong: only half of our junior employees feel that they receive enough guidance from their managers. This is an organizational problem, not a personal one. So here is my strategic plan. First, each manager will meet every team member once a month. Second, we will hire a career counselor who visits twice a week. Third, we will send our most dynamic young staff to the leadership program in May. If we do this, the outlook is good. I believe we can attain a satisfaction score of eighty percent by the end of the year.","ja":"お集まりいただきありがとうございます。従業員の士気についてお話しします。前回の調査は、何かがおかしいことをはっきり示す指標でした。若手社員のうち、上司から十分な指導を受けていると感じているのは半数だけです。これは個人の問題ではなく、組織の問題です。そこで、私の戦略的な計画を示します。まず、各管理職は、月に一度、部下全員と面談します。次に、週2回訪問するキャリア相談員を雇います。3つ目に、最も活動的な若手社員を5月の指導者養成プログラムに送ります。これを実行すれば、見通しは明るいです。年末までに、満足度80パーセントを達成できると信じています。","words":[["morale","freq:morale"],["indicator","freq:indicator"],["junior","freq:junior"],["guidance","freq:guidance"],["organizational","freq:organizational"],["strategic","freq:strategic"],["counselor","freq:counselor"],["dynamic","freq:dynamic"],["outlook","freq:outlook"],["attain","freq:attain"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the survey show?","o":["Staff want higher pay.","Managers work too much.","The company is growing.","Many junior employees lack guidance."],"a":3,"why":"only half of our junior employees feel that they receive enough guidance（十分な指導を受けていると感じる若手は半数だけ）とある。"},{"q":"How often will managers meet each team member?","o":["Once a month","Twice a week","Every day","Once a year"],"a":0,"why":"each manager will meet every team member once a month（月に一度面談）とある。週2回は相談員の訪問。"},{"q":"What goal does the speaker set?","o":["Hiring fifty new staff","A satisfaction score of eighty percent","A new program in May","Fewer meetings"],"a":1,"why":"attain a satisfaction score of eighty percent by the end of the year（年末までに満足度80パーセントを達成）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0085","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"技術サポートの電話","text":"Hello, this is Arun from Skyline, your telecommunication company. I am returning your call about your Internet connection. I am sorry that the problem continues to recur. We have found the cause: a software bug in the router, not a broken circuit in your home. Please do the following. First, disconnect the power cord from the back of the router and wait one minute. Then plug it in again. If the lights turn green, the update has worked. If you feel uncomfortable doing this yourself, I can send an engineer tomorrow morning. Please be cautious with the small white cable, because it breaks easily. Our service is usually very dependable, so we will take ten dollars off your next bill. If you can reproduce the problem, call me.","ja":"もしもし、お客様がご利用の通信会社スカイラインのアルンです。インターネット接続の件で、折り返しお電話しました。問題が繰り返し起きており、申し訳ありません。原因が分かりました。ルーターのソフトウェアの不具合で、ご自宅の回路が壊れているわけではありません。次のようにしてください。まず、ルーターの背面から電源コードを抜き、1分待ちます。それからもう一度差し込みます。ランプが緑になれば、更新は成功です。ご自身で作業するのが不安でしたら、明日の朝、技術者を伺わせます。小さな白いケーブルは壊れやすいので、慎重に扱ってください。当社のサービスは普段とても信頼できるものですので、次回のご請求から10ドルを差し引きます。問題を再現できた場合は、私にお電話ください。","words":[["telecommunication","freq:telecommunication"],["recur","freq:recur"],["bug","freq:bug"],["circuit","freq:circuit"],["disconnect","freq:disconnect"],["cord","freq:cord"],["uncomfortable","freq:uncomfortable"],["cautious","freq:cautious"],["dependable","freq:dependable"],["reproduce","freq:reproduce"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the cause of the problem?","o":["A broken cable","A power cut","A software bug","An unpaid bill"],"a":2,"why":"a software bug in the router, not a broken circuit（ルーターのソフトの不具合で、回路の故障ではない）とある。"},{"q":"What should the customer do first?","o":["Call an engineer","Unplug the power cord","Buy a new router","Replace the white cable"],"a":1,"why":"disconnect the power cord from the back of the router and wait one minute（電源コードを抜いて1分待つ）とある。"},{"q":"What will the company do for the customer?","o":["Reduce the next bill","Send a new router","Cancel the contract","Extend the service for a month"],"a":0,"why":"we will take ten dollars off your next bill（次回の請求から10ドル引く）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0086","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"語学学校の開講あいさつ","text":"Good evening, and welcome to City Night School. Whether you are a teen who wants a high school diploma or an adult who wants to learn something new, you are in the right place. This term, we offer classes in physics, biology, and English at every level, from beginner to advanced. In the English grammar course, we start with points that puzzle many learners, such as the reflexive pronoun. Our teachers avoid easy generalization. We do not say that adults learn slowly. In fact, there is no contradiction between working all day and studying well at night. Each student will be tested individually this week so that we can choose the right class for you.","ja":"こんばんは。シティ夜間学校へようこそ。高校の卒業証書を取りたい十代の方も、新しいことを学びたい大人の方も、ここがふさわしい場所です。今学期は、物理、生物、そして初心者から上級までのあらゆる水準の英語の授業があります。英文法の講座では、再帰代名詞のように、多くの学習者を悩ませる点から始めます。当校の教師は、安易な一般化を避けます。大人は覚えが遅い、などとは言いません。実際、一日中働くことと、夜にしっかり学ぶこととの間に矛盾はありません。今週は、皆さんに合った授業を選べるよう、生徒一人ひとりを個別にテストします。","words":[["teen","freq:teen"],["diploma","freq:diploma"],["physics","freq:physics"],["biology","freq:biology"],["beginner","freq:beginner"],["puzzle","freq:puzzle"],["reflexive","freq:reflexive"],["generalization","freq:generalization"],["contradiction","freq:contradiction"],["individually","freq:individually"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the school for?","o":["Both teenagers and adults","Only high school teachers","Only beginners","University students"],"a":0,"why":"a teen who wants a high school diploma or an adult（十代の人にも大人にも）と述べている。"},{"q":"What will the grammar course begin with?","o":["Easy reading","Points that confuse learners","A physics test","A list of new words"],"a":1,"why":"we start with points that puzzle many learners（多くの学習者を悩ませる点から始める）とある。"},{"q":"Why will students be tested this week?","o":["To earn a diploma","To pay lower fees","To finish the term early","To be placed in the right class"],"a":3,"why":"so that we can choose the right class for you（合った授業を選ぶため）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0087","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"慈善コンサートの開会","text":"Good evening, ladies and gentlemen. I am the chairperson of the Hope Foundation, and it is my pleasure to welcome you to our tenth charitable concert. Tonight, the City Youth Orchestra will play for you. These energetic young musicians are known internationally, and last year they performed in six countries. We are also honored to have the ambassador of Brazil with us. Her advice has been invaluable to our school project there. Every dollar from tonight's tickets will pay for music lessons for children who could not otherwise afford them. A wonderful evening awaits you. Now, please clap as loudly and enthusiastically as you can to welcome the orchestra to the stage.","ja":"皆様、こんばんは。ホープ財団の議長を務めております。第10回の慈善コンサートに皆様をお迎えできることをうれしく思います。今夜は、市の青少年管弦楽団が演奏します。この活気あふれる若い音楽家たちは国際的に知られており、昨年は6か国で演奏しました。また、ブラジル大使をお迎えできたことを光栄に思います。大使の助言は、現地での私たちの学校事業にとって、計り知れないほど貴重でした。今夜のチケットの売上はすべて、そうでなければ受けられない子どもたちの音楽の授業料に充てられます。すばらしい夜が皆様を待っています。では、できるだけ大きく、熱烈な拍手で、楽団を舞台にお迎えください。","words":[["chairperson","freq:chairperson"],["charitable","freq:charitable"],["Orchestra","freq:orchestra"],["energetic","freq:energetic"],["internationally","freq:internationally"],["ambassador","freq:ambassador"],["invaluable","freq:invaluable"],["awaits","freq:await"],["clap","freq:clap"],["enthusiastically","freq:enthusiastically"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the speaker?","o":["A musician","An ambassador","The head of a foundation","A school teacher"],"a":2,"why":"I am the chairperson of the Hope Foundation（ホープ財団の議長）とある。"},{"q":"What is said about the orchestra?","o":["It has played in other countries.","It is from Brazil.","It was formed this year.","It plays only at schools."],"a":0,"why":"known internationally, and last year they performed in six countries（国際的に知られ、昨年は6か国で演奏）とある。"},{"q":"What will the ticket money be used for?","o":["A new concert hall","Music lessons for children","A trip to Brazil","Instruments for the orchestra"],"a":1,"why":"will pay for music lessons for children（子どもたちの音楽の授業料に充てる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0088","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"自動車販売店の広告","text":"Winter has come early, and so has the biggest sale of the year at North Star Motors. After an unusually snowy November, sales of small cars took a dive, so our dealership must clear two hundred vehicles by Friday. Take the Polar X, an environmentally friendly family car with every amenity you could want, including heated seats that absorb the cold in seconds. The price on the window sticker is already low, and this week you will also receive a rebate of one thousand dollars. Still hesitant? Take any car home for a twenty-four-hour test drive, free of charge. North Star Motors, on Highway 7. We are open until nine tonight.","ja":"冬が早く訪れ、ノース・スター・モーターズの年間最大のセールも早くやって来ました。11月は異例の雪が続き、小型車の売れ行きが急に落ち込んだため、当販売店は金曜までに200台を売り切らなければなりません。たとえば「ポーラーX」。環境に優しいファミリーカーで、望みうる快適な設備がすべて備わっており、数秒で冷たさを吸い取る座席ヒーターも付いています。窓の価格表示のシールに書かれた値段がすでに安いうえ、今週は1,000ドルの払い戻しも受けられます。まだ迷っていますか。どの車でも、24時間の試乗のために無料でご自宅へお持ち帰りいただけます。ノース・スター・モーターズは7号線沿いです。今夜は9時まで営業しています。","words":[["unusually","freq:unusually"],["snowy","freq:snowy"],["dive","freq:dive"],["dealership","freq:dealership"],["environmentally","freq:environmentally"],["amenity","freq:amenity"],["absorb","freq:absorb"],["sticker","freq:sticker"],["rebate","freq:rebate"],["hesitant","freq:hesitant"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the sale being held?","o":["A new model has arrived.","The dealership is moving.","It is the store's birthday.","Car sales fell after heavy snow."],"a":3,"why":"After an unusually snowy November, sales of small cars took a dive（雪の多い11月の後、小型車の売れ行きが急落した）とある。"},{"q":"What will buyers receive this week?","o":["A one-thousand-dollar rebate","Free winter tires","A second car at half price","A year of free fuel"],"a":0,"why":"you will also receive a rebate of one thousand dollars（1,000ドルの払い戻し）とある。"},{"q":"What can customers who are unsure do?","o":["Return the car within a month","Take a free one-day test drive","Pay after the winter","Speak to the owner"],"a":1,"why":"Take any car home for a twenty-four-hour test drive, free of charge（24時間の無料試乗）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0089","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"健康セミナーの講演","text":"Thank you for coming to our talk on a healthy lifestyle. Many people believe that only serious illness needs attention. On the contrary, small habitual actions decide how we feel at sixty. Let me give three examples. First, be careful with sugar. Even chewing gum can damage your teeth if you are careless about brushing. Second, have a checkup once a year. Our nurses will administer a simple blood test, and all of our methods conform to national guidelines. Third, clean out your medicine cabinet and dispose of anything past its date. Exercise is likewise important, but that is the topic of next week's talk. Now, does anyone have a question?","ja":"健康的な生活様式についての講演にお越しいただき、ありがとうございます。重い病気にだけ気をつければよいと考える人は多くいます。それどころか、小さな習慣的な行動こそが、60歳のときの体調を決めます。例を3つ挙げます。まず、砂糖に気をつけること。チューインガムでさえ、歯みがきをおろそかにすれば歯を傷めます。次に、年に一度、健康診断を受けること。当院の看護師が簡単な血液検査を実施します。当院の方法はすべて、国の指針に沿っています。3つ目に、薬の戸棚を整理し、期限を過ぎたものは処分すること。運動も同様に大切ですが、それは来週の講演の話題です。では、質問のある方はいらっしゃいますか。","words":[["lifestyle","freq:lifestyle"],["contrary","freq:contrary"],["habitual","freq:habitual"],["gum","freq:gum"],["careless","freq:careless"],["checkup","freq:checkup"],["administer","freq:administer"],["conform","freq:conform"],["dispose","freq:dispose"],["likewise","freq:likewise"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does the speaker say decides how we feel at sixty?","o":["Serious illness","Our family history","Small daily habits","The amount of sleep"],"a":2,"why":"small habitual actions decide how we feel at sixty（小さな習慣的な行動が決める）とある。"},{"q":"How often should people have a checkup?","o":["Once a year","Every month","Every five years","Only when ill"],"a":0,"why":"have a checkup once a year（年に一度）とある。"},{"q":"What will next week's talk be about?","o":["Sugar","Exercise","Medicine","Blood tests"],"a":1,"why":"Exercise is likewise important, but that is the topic of next week's talk（運動は来週の講演の話題）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0090","page":"freq","group":"801〜900","kind":"デザイナーからの留守番電話","text":"Hi, Mr. Brooks. This is Mia Chen, the freelance designer. I am calling about the poster for the Ocean Fair. I have changed the picture of the whale, as you asked, and started the layout anew. A messenger will bring three printed copies to your office this afternoon. I did not staple the pages, so that you can lay them side by side. If you approve, I will send the file to your distributor on Friday. Also, the Chamber of Commerce wants to meet us on Monday at ten. Their office is on the second floor of the Bay Center, just at the top of the escalator. Please convey my thanks to your team for their quick replies. Talk to you soon. Bye.","ja":"もしもし、ブルックスさん。フリーのデザイナーのミア・チェンです。オーシャン・フェアのポスターの件でお電話しました。ご依頼のとおりクジラの絵を変更し、割り付けを改めてやり直しました。本日午後、配達人が印刷した見本3部を事務所にお届けします。並べて見比べられるよう、ページはホチキスで留めていません。ご承認いただければ、金曜にデータを御社の販売代理店へ送ります。また、商工会議所が月曜の10時に私たちと会いたいと言っています。先方の事務所はベイ・センターの2階で、エスカレーターを上がってすぐの所です。素早くお返事をくださったチームの皆様に、私からの感謝をお伝えください。ではまた近いうちに。失礼します。","words":[["freelance","freq:freelance"],["whale","freq:whale"],["anew","freq:anew"],["messenger","freq:messenger"],["staple","freq:staple"],["distributor","freq:distributor"],["Commerce","freq:commerce"],["escalator","freq:escalator"],["convey","freq:convey"],["Bye","freq:bye"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will arrive this afternoon?","o":["A new contract","A photo of a whale","A bill","Printed copies of a poster"],"a":3,"why":"A messenger will bring three printed copies（配達人が印刷した見本3部を届ける）とある。"},{"q":"Why did the speaker not staple the pages?","o":["So that they can be compared side by side","Because she had no stapler","To make them lighter","Because they are not finished"],"a":0,"why":"so that you can lay them side by side（並べて見比べられるように）とある。"},{"q":"Where is Monday's meeting?","o":["At the designer's studio","At an office in the Bay Center","At the distributor's warehouse","At the Ocean Fair"],"a":1,"why":"Their office is on the second floor of the Bay Center（ベイ・センター2階の事務所）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0091","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"人事部の発表","text":"Good morning, everyone. I am pleased to announce that the company will officially introduce flextime on the first of June. Under the new system, you may start work at any time between seven and ten, as long as you work eight hours. Many of you asked for more flexibility, and studies show that it reduces fatigue. Some managers were reluctant at first, and there is one drawback: meetings will be harder to plan. For that reason, it is desirable for everyone to be in the office between ten and three. This modification to our rules will be formally added to the staff handbook next week. Please read it and sign the last page.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。当社は6月1日から、正式にフレックスタイム制を導入することをお知らせします。新しい制度では、8時間働く限り、7時から10時の間のいつでも仕事を始められます。もっと柔軟性がほしいという声が多く寄せられており、調査でも、柔軟な働き方が疲労を減らすことが示されています。当初は気が進まない管理職もいましたし、欠点も一つあります。会議の予定が立てにくくなることです。そのため、10時から3時の間は全員が出社していることが望まれます。この規則の変更は、来週、社員の手引きに正式に加えられます。読んだうえで、最後のページに署名してください。","words":[["officially","freq:officially"],["flextime","freq:flextime"],["flexibility","freq:flexibility"],["fatigue","freq:fatigue"],["reluctant","freq:reluctant"],["drawback","freq:drawback"],["desirable","freq:desirable"],["modification","freq:modification"],["formally","freq:formally"],["handbook","freq:handbook"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will begin on the first of June?","o":["A new training course","A flexible working system","A shorter working week","A new office"],"a":1,"why":"will officially introduce flextime on the first of June（6月1日からフレックスタイム制を導入）とある。"},{"q":"What drawback does the speaker mention?","o":["Planning meetings will be harder.","Pay will be lower.","Staff will be more tired.","Managers will work longer."],"a":0,"why":"there is one drawback: meetings will be harder to plan（会議の予定が立てにくくなる）とある。"},{"q":"What are staff asked to do next week?","o":["Choose their hours","Attend a meeting at ten","Read the handbook and sign it","Talk to their managers"],"a":2,"why":"Please read it and sign the last page（手引きを読んで最後のページに署名）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0092","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"経理部長からの連絡","text":"Hello, this is Irene from accounting. Before the fiscal year ends on March 31, I need your help with three things. First, while checking the Tokyo office accounts, I found a discrepancy of two hundred thousand yen. It seems that a supplier managed to overcharge us for three consecutive months. I have asked them to return the money. Second, please send all requests for reimbursement of travel costs by Friday. Late requests will be paid in April. Third, if you have unused train tickets, check whether they are refundable. The railway will waive its usual fee this month. Finally, the company card is now a debit card, so every payment leaves our account at once.","ja":"もしもし、経理のアイリーンです。会計年度が3月31日に終わる前に、3つのことでご協力をお願いします。まず、東京事務所の帳簿を確認していて、20万円の食い違いを見つけました。ある仕入れ先が、3か月連続で当社に過剰に請求していたようです。先方には返金を求めています。次に、出張費の払い戻しの申請は、すべて金曜までに送ってください。遅れた申請の支払いは4月になります。3つ目に、未使用の乗車券がある場合は、払い戻しができるか確かめてください。鉄道会社は今月、通常の手数料を免除します。最後に、会社のカードは引き落とし式のデビットカードになりましたので、支払いのたびに、すぐに口座からお金が出ていきます。","words":[["fiscal","freq:fiscal"],["discrepancy","freq:discrepancy"],["yen","freq:yen"],["overcharge","freq:overcharge"],["consecutive","freq:consecutive"],["reimbursement","freq:reimbursement"],["unused","freq:unused"],["refundable","freq:refundable"],["waive","freq:waive"],["debit","freq:debit"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the speaker find in the Tokyo accounts?","o":["A difference in the figures","A missing receipt","An unpaid salary","A new supplier"],"a":0,"why":"I found a discrepancy of two hundred thousand yen（20万円の食い違いを見つけた）とある。"},{"q":"By when should travel cost requests be sent?","o":["March 31","April 1","The end of the month","Friday"],"a":3,"why":"send all requests for reimbursement of travel costs by Friday（金曜までに）とある。"},{"q":"What will the railway do this month?","o":["Raise ticket prices","Not charge its usual fee","Stop selling tickets","Send new cards"],"a":1,"why":"The railway will waive its usual fee this month（今月は通常の手数料を免除する）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0093","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"病院の館内放送","text":"Attention, please. This is the hospital safety office. Because of the thunderstorm, the main power line to the building has failed. Fortunately, our backup generator started within ten seconds, and all medical equipment is working normally. However, the heater in the east wing will be off for about an hour. Nurses will bring extra blankets to every occupant of that wing. Please do not use the elevators, and keep each hallway clear, because bags on the floor are a hazard in low light. Thick fog is also expected tonight, so visitors should drive carefully. The storm has damaged a transmission tower nearby, and our radio may not transmit clearly. We will make another announcement in thirty minutes.","ja":"お知らせします。こちらは病院の安全管理室です。雷雨のため、建物への主電源の送電線が止まりました。幸い、予備の発電機が10秒以内に動き出し、医療機器はすべて正常に作動しています。ただし、東棟の暖房は1時間ほど止まります。看護師が、東棟にいらっしゃる方全員に追加の毛布をお持ちします。エレベーターは使わず、廊下には物を置かないでください。薄暗い中では、床に置いたかばんは危険です。今夜は濃い霧も予想されますので、お見舞いの方は気をつけて運転してください。嵐で近くの送信塔が損傷しており、当院の無線がはっきり送信できないおそれがあります。30分後に、もう一度お知らせします。","words":[["thunderstorm","freq:thunderstorm"],["Fortunately","freq:fortunately"],["generator","freq:generator"],["heater","freq:heater"],["occupant","freq:occupant"],["hallway","freq:hallway"],["hazard","freq:hazard"],["fog","freq:fog"],["transmission","freq:transmission"],["transmit","freq:transmit"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened because of the storm?","o":["A window broke.","The elevators stopped forever.","The main power failed.","The hospital was closed."],"a":2,"why":"the main power line to the building has failed（主電源の送電線が止まった）とある。"},{"q":"What will nurses bring to people in the east wing?","o":["Blankets","Hot drinks","Flashlights","Radios"],"a":0,"why":"Nurses will bring extra blankets（追加の毛布を持っていく）とある。暖房が1時間ほど止まるため。"},{"q":"Why should hallways be kept clear?","o":["Doctors need to run.","Bags are dangerous in dim light.","Cleaning is planned.","New beds are arriving."],"a":1,"why":"bags on the floor are a hazard in low light（薄暗い中では床のかばんが危険）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0094","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"店の広告","text":"This weekend only, Home Plus is holding its biggest kitchen and sound sale of the year. Our new deluxe microwave, the Chef 900, is forty dollars off. It is smaller and lighter than last year's model, and it cooks a frozen meal in three minutes. Music lovers should try our cordless headphone sets, sold exclusively at Home Plus. To use your discount, simply insert your loyalty card at the register. Do not have a card yet? You can activate one in the store in less than a minute. Additionally, every customer who spends over one hundred dollars will receive free delivery. Home Plus, on Baker Avenue. We are open from nine to nine.","ja":"今週末限り、ホーム・プラスは、台所用品と音響機器の年間最大のセールを開催します。新しい高級電子レンジ「シェフ900」は40ドル引きです。昨年の機種より小さくて軽く、冷凍食品を3分で調理します。音楽が好きな方は、ホーム・プラスでのみ販売しているコードレスのヘッドホンをお試しください。割引を使うには、レジでお得意様カードを差し込むだけです。まだカードをお持ちでない方は、店内で1分足らずで有効にできます。さらに、100ドルを超えてお買い上げのお客様は全員、配達が無料になります。ホーム・プラスはベーカー通りにあります。9時から9時まで営業しています。","words":[["deluxe","freq:deluxe"],["microwave","freq:microwave"],["lighter","freq:lighter"],["cordless","freq:cordless"],["headphone","freq:headphone"],["exclusively","freq:exclusively"],["insert","freq:insert"],["loyalty","freq:loyalty"],["activate","freq:activate"],["Additionally","freq:additionally"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is said about the Chef 900?","o":["It is larger than the old model.","It is sold only online.","It comes with headphones.","It is smaller and lighter than last year's model."],"a":3,"why":"smaller and lighter than last year's model（昨年の機種より小さくて軽い）とある。"},{"q":"How can customers use the discount?","o":["By inserting a loyalty card","By showing a coupon","By paying in cash","By ordering online"],"a":0,"why":"simply insert your loyalty card at the register（レジでお得意様カードを差し込む）とある。"},{"q":"Who will receive free delivery?","o":["Customers who buy a microwave","Customers who spend over one hundred dollars","New card holders","Customers who come at nine"],"a":1,"why":"every customer who spends over one hundred dollars will receive free delivery（100ドル超の買い物で配達無料）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0095","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"In business news, Gulf Marine announced today that it will downsize its operations in the port of Hallam. The company says it is imperative to cut costs, because its dependence on a single oil refinery has become a risk. Gulf Marine will sell four of the ships in its fleet, including its oldest freighter, and will dispatch the others to ports in Asia. The termination of three hundred jobs will begin in July. A new manager, Mr. David Osei, has been hired to oversee the change. The mayor of Hallam said that the city will suffer economically, and he asked the government for support. Gulf Marine's shares rose two percent after the news.","ja":"経済ニュースです。ガルフ・マリーンは今日、ハラム港での事業を縮小すると発表しました。同社によると、一つの製油所への依存が危険になっているため、費用を削ることが絶対に必要だということです。ガルフ・マリーンは、最も古い貨物船を含め、保有する船団のうち4隻を売却し、残りはアジアの港へ派遣します。300人の雇用の打ち切りは7月に始まります。この変更を監督するため、新しい責任者としてデイビッド・オセイ氏が採用されました。ハラム市長は、市が経済的に打撃を受けると述べ、政府に支援を求めました。この知らせの後、ガルフ・マリーンの株価は2パーセント上がりました。","words":[["downsize","freq:downsize"],["imperative","freq:imperative"],["dependence","freq:dependence"],["refinery","freq:refinery"],["fleet","freq:fleet"],["freighter","freq:freighter"],["dispatch","freq:dispatch"],["termination","freq:termination"],["oversee","freq:oversee"],["economically","freq:economically"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the company cutting costs?","o":["Its ships are too old.","The port is closing.","It relies too much on one refinery.","The government asked it to."],"a":2,"why":"its dependence on a single oil refinery has become a risk（一つの製油所への依存が危険になった）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen in July?","o":["Job cuts will begin.","A new ship will arrive.","The refinery will reopen.","The mayor will resign."],"a":0,"why":"The termination of three hundred jobs will begin in July（300人の雇用の打ち切りが7月に始まる）とある。"},{"q":"What did the mayor do?","o":["He bought shares.","He asked the government for help.","He hired a new manager.","He visited Asia."],"a":1,"why":"he asked the government for support（政府に支援を求めた）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0096","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"町内会の集まり","text":"Thank you for coming to tonight's meeting. I have three items. First, the petition for a new skate park now has six hundred names. Children ride a skateboard on the road in front of the condominium every day, which is dangerous. We will hand the petition to the mayor on Monday. Second, the city will repair the sewer on Mill Road next month, and each homeowner on that street will get a letter this week. Third, there has been a theft at two shops on Main Street. Every local merchant is asked to lock the back door after dark. Finally, our winter coat drive for homeless people starts on Saturday. Please help us publicize it by putting a poster in your window.","ja":"今夜の集まりにお越しいただきありがとうございます。議題は3つあります。まず、新しいスケート場を求める嘆願書は、現在600人の署名が集まっています。子どもたちが毎日、分譲マンションの前の道路でスケートボードに乗っており、危険です。嘆願書は月曜に市長へ手渡します。次に、来月、市がミル通りの下水道を修理します。その通りに家をお持ちの方には、今週、手紙が届きます。3つ目に、メイン通りの2軒の店で盗難がありました。地元の商店主の皆さんには、暗くなったら裏口に鍵をかけるようお願いします。最後に、家のない人たちのための冬のコートの寄付活動が土曜に始まります。窓にポスターを貼って、広く知らせるのにご協力ください。","words":[["petition","freq:petition"],["skate","freq:skate"],["skateboard","freq:skateboard"],["condominium","freq:condominium"],["sewer","freq:sewer"],["homeowner","freq:homeowner"],["theft","freq:theft"],["merchant","freq:merchant"],["homeless","freq:homeless"],["publicize","freq:publicize"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the petition for?","o":["A new skate park","A new road","A sewer repair","More police"],"a":0,"why":"the petition for a new skate park（新しいスケート場を求める嘆願書）とある。"},{"q":"What are merchants asked to do?","o":["Close early","Hire a guard","Sign the petition","Lock their back doors after dark"],"a":3,"why":"lock the back door after dark（暗くなったら裏口に鍵をかける）とある。盗難があったため。"},{"q":"How can residents help the coat drive?","o":["By donating money","By putting up a poster","By writing to the mayor","By visiting the shops"],"a":1,"why":"putting a poster in your window（窓にポスターを貼る）ことで知らせるのに協力してほしいと言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0097","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"送別会でのあいさつ","text":"Good evening, everyone, and welcome to this farewell dinner for Professor Anne Walsh. For twenty-five years, Anne has been our most popular lecturer. Her enthusiasm for history was evident in every class, and she treated each student professionally and kindly. Last month, her nomination for the National Award for Excellence in Teaching received an affirmative vote from every member of the committee. Anne always said that her most meaningful work was her collaboration with local schools, which brought hundreds of children to our museum. Anne, we will miss you. Please come up and accept this small gift from all of us.","ja":"皆さん、こんばんは。アン・ウォルシュ教授の送別の夕食会へようこそ。25年にわたり、アンは私たちの最も人気のある講師でした。歴史に対する彼女の熱意は、どの授業でもはっきり表れており、学生一人ひとりに、専門家らしく、そして親切に接しました。先月、全国優秀教育賞への彼女の推薦は、委員全員から賛成票を得ました。アンはいつも、自分にとって最も意義のある仕事は、地元の学校との協力だったと話していました。その協力によって、何百人もの子どもたちが当博物館を訪れました。アン、寂しくなります。どうぞ前に出て、私たち全員からのささやかな贈り物をお受け取りください。","words":[["farewell","freq:farewell"],["lecturer","freq:lecturer"],["enthusiasm","freq:enthusiasm"],["evident","freq:evident"],["professionally","freq:professionally"],["nomination","freq:nomination"],["Excellence","freq:excellence"],["affirmative","freq:affirmative"],["meaningful","freq:meaningful"],["collaboration","freq:collaboration"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the dinner?","o":["To open a museum","To welcome a new teacher","To say goodbye to a professor","To raise money for schools"],"a":2,"why":"this farewell dinner for Professor Anne Walsh（ウォルシュ教授の送別の夕食会）とある。"},{"q":"What happened last month?","o":["Her award nomination was approved by all members.","She published a book.","She visited local schools.","She joined a committee."],"a":0,"why":"her nomination ... received an affirmative vote from every member（推薦が委員全員から賛成票を得た）とある。"},{"q":"What did Anne say was her most meaningful work?","o":["Writing about history","Working with local schools","Teaching at the museum","Leading the committee"],"a":1,"why":"her most meaningful work was her collaboration with local schools（地元の学校との協力）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0098","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"公民館の催し案内","text":"Hello, and thank you for calling the Westside Community Center. Here are this weekend's events. On Friday night, our outdoor cinema shows a family comedy at seven. Popcorn is free, and a hamburger costs three dollars. On Saturday morning, a local baker will teach you to make bread. Bring five hundred grams of flour and an apron. You will learn how to spread the butter evenly, which is the secret of a soft loaf. On Sunday, our pottery class welcomes any enthusiast aged ten or older. Life here is never dull! All classes are free, but places are limited, so press one to reserve yours now.","ja":"もしもし、ウエストサイド公民館にお電話ありがとうございます。今週末の催しをご案内します。金曜の夜は、屋外映画会で7時から家族向けの喜劇を上映します。ポップコーンは無料で、ハンバーガーは3ドルです。土曜の午前は、地元のパン職人がパンの作り方を教えます。小麦粉500グラムとエプロンをお持ちください。バターを均等に塗る方法を学べます。これが、やわらかいパンの秘密です。日曜の陶芸教室は、10歳以上の熱心な愛好家ならどなたでも歓迎します。ここでの暮らしが退屈になることはありません。教室はすべて無料ですが、定員に限りがありますので、今すぐ1を押してご予約ください。","words":[["cinema","freq:cinema"],["Popcorn","freq:popcorn"],["hamburger","freq:hamburger"],["baker","freq:baker"],["grams","freq:gram"],["flour","freq:flour"],["evenly","freq:evenly"],["pottery","freq:pottery"],["enthusiast","freq:enthusiast"],["dull","freq:dull"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is free on Friday night?","o":["Hamburgers","Movie tickets for adults only","Drinks","Popcorn"],"a":3,"why":"Popcorn is free, and a hamburger costs three dollars（ポップコーンは無料、ハンバーガーは3ドル）とある。"},{"q":"What should people bring to the Saturday class?","o":["Flour and an apron","Butter and eggs","A loaf of bread","Three dollars"],"a":0,"why":"Bring five hundred grams of flour and an apron（小麦粉500グラムとエプロン）とある。"},{"q":"Who can join the pottery class?","o":["Only adults","Anyone ten or older","Only beginners","Members of the center"],"a":1,"why":"welcomes any enthusiast aged ten or older（10歳以上の愛好家なら誰でも）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0099","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"山のロッジの案内","text":"Welcome to Eagle Peak Lodge. Whether you are a serious hiker or a sleepy traveler who needs a rest, we are glad you are here. We have just redecorated every room, and each bed has a new feather pillow. If you plan to go climbing, please stop at the equipment desk. You must wear a helmet on the north trail, and you can rent a complete outfit, including boots and a jacket. Our guides can tailor a route to your level. The sun's rays are strong at this height, so use sunscreen even on cloudy days. After your walk, refresh yourself in the hot bath on the first floor. Please keep the shared kitchen neat for other guests.","ja":"イーグル・ピーク・ロッジへようこそ。本格的にハイキングをする方も、休息が必要な眠たい旅行者の方も、お越しいただきうれしく思います。全室の改装を終えたばかりで、どのベッドにも新しい羽毛の枕をご用意しています。登山を予定している方は、用具の窓口にお立ち寄りください。北の登山道ではヘルメットの着用が必須で、靴や上着を含む装備一式を借りることができます。ガイドが、皆様の水準に合わせて道順を組みます。この標高では太陽の光線が強いので、曇りの日でも日焼け止めを使ってください。歩いた後は、1階の温かいお風呂で元気を取り戻してください。共用の台所は、ほかのお客様のために、きちんと片づけておいてください。","words":[["hiker","freq:hiker"],["sleepy","freq:sleepy"],["redecorated","freq:redecorate"],["pillow","freq:pillow"],["helmet","freq:helmet"],["outfit","freq:outfit"],["tailor","freq:tailor"],["rays","freq:ray"],["refresh","freq:refresh"],["neat","freq:neat"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has the lodge just done?","o":["Opened a new trail","Hired new guides","Redecorated its rooms","Built a kitchen"],"a":2,"why":"We have just redecorated every room（全室の改装を終えたばかり）とある。"},{"q":"What is required on the north trail?","o":["A helmet","A guide","A permit","A map"],"a":0,"why":"You must wear a helmet on the north trail（北の登山道ではヘルメット必須）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about cloudy days?","o":["The trails are closed.","Sunscreen is still needed.","The bath is busier.","Guides are not available."],"a":1,"why":"use sunscreen even on cloudy days（曇りの日でも日焼け止めを使う）とある。太陽の光線が強いため。"}]},
{"id":"f-0100","page":"freq","group":"901〜1000","kind":"動物園のボランティア説明","text":"Good morning, volunteers. Thank you for joining our guide team. Before the gates open, here are a few rules. First, please memorize the main facts on your card. Visitors often misidentify our red pandas as foxes, so be ready to explain. Second, our baby elephant is only three weeks old and still delicate. Do not let anyone speak loudly near her, and never allow food near any cage. Third, phones are a distraction. Please keep yours in your pocket. Fourth, do not inflate balloons in the park, because the noise scares the birds. The animals depend on our reliability, so please arrive on time. At four, we will meet to brainstorm ideas for next month's family day.","ja":"ボランティアの皆さん、おはようございます。ガイドの班に加わっていただきありがとうございます。開門の前に、決まりをいくつか伝えます。まず、カードにある主な事実を暗記してください。来園者はレッサーパンダをキツネと取り違えることがよくありますので、説明できるようにしておいてください。次に、象の赤ちゃんは生後3週間で、まだか弱い状態です。そばで大声で話させないようにし、どのおりの近くにも食べ物を近づけさせないでください。3つ目に、電話は気を散らすものです。ポケットにしまっておいてください。4つ目に、園内で風船を膨らませないでください。音で鳥がおびえます。動物たちは私たちが当てにできる存在であることを頼りにしていますので、時間どおりに来てください。4時に集まって、来月の家族の日の案を出し合います。","words":[["memorize","freq:memorize"],["misidentify","freq:misidentify"],["elephant","freq:elephant"],["delicate","freq:delicate"],["loudly","freq:loudly"],["cage","freq:cage"],["distraction","freq:distraction"],["inflate","freq:inflate"],["reliability","freq:reliability"],["brainstorm","freq:brainstorm"]],"qs":[{"q":"What do visitors often do?","o":["Mistake one animal for another","Feed the elephants","Lose their cards","Arrive late"],"a":0,"why":"Visitors often misidentify our red pandas as foxes（レッサーパンダをキツネと取り違える）とある。"},{"q":"Why should people not speak loudly near the baby elephant?","o":["She is asleep.","She is being filmed.","She is dangerous.","She is very young and delicate."],"a":3,"why":"only three weeks old and still delicate（生後3週間でまだか弱い）ためと説明している。"},{"q":"What will happen at four?","o":["The gates will close.","Volunteers will share ideas.","The birds will be fed.","Balloons will be handed out."],"a":1,"why":"we will meet to brainstorm ideas for next month's family day（集まって案を出し合う）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0101","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"緊急の気象情報","text":"This is an emergency weather report. A hurricane is moving toward the coast and is expected to reach Port Marlow by six tonight. Rainfall of up to three hundred millimeters is probable, and winds will rise sharply after dark. People who live near the river must evacuate now. If you cannot leave your residence, move to an upper floor, not to an underground room. City buses with space for a wheelchair are collecting needy and elderly residents free of charge. Before you go, turn off the gas, and keep a fire extinguisher near the door. Shelters are open at three schools. Stay tuned to this station for updates every fifteen minutes.","ja":"緊急の気象情報です。ハリケーンが沿岸に向かっており、今夜6時までにポート・マーロウに達する見込みです。最大300ミリの降雨の可能性が高く、暗くなってからは風が急激に強まります。川の近くにお住まいの方は、今すぐ避難してください。住居を離れられない場合は、地下の部屋ではなく、上の階へ移動してください。車椅子を載せられる市のバスが、生活に困っている方やお年寄りを無料でお迎えに回っています。出かける前にガスを止め、消火器を玄関の近くに置いてください。避難所は3つの学校に開設されています。この放送局では、15分ごとに最新情報をお伝えします。","words":[["hurricane","freq:hurricane"],["Rainfall","freq:rainfall"],["probable","freq:probable"],["sharply","freq:sharply"],["evacuate","freq:evacuate"],["residence","freq:residence"],["underground","freq:underground"],["wheelchair","freq:wheelchair"],["needy","freq:needy"],["extinguisher","freq:extinguisher"]],"qs":[{"q":"When is the hurricane expected to arrive?","o":["By six tonight","Tomorrow morning","In fifteen minutes","After midnight"],"a":0,"why":"expected to reach Port Marlow by six tonight（今夜6時までに達する見込み）とある。"},{"q":"What should people who cannot leave home do?","o":["Go to the basement","Wait by the river","Go to a higher floor","Call the city bus"],"a":2,"why":"move to an upper floor, not to an underground room（地下ではなく上の階へ移動）とある。"},{"q":"What should people do before leaving?","o":["Open the windows","Turn off the gas","Pack food for three days","Lock the shelters"],"a":1,"why":"Before you go, turn off the gas（出かける前にガスを止める）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0102","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"Good evening. Here is the business news. The furniture chain Homeline filed for bankruptcy this morning, and the layoff of two thousand workers has already begun. An independent auditor found that the company had managed to overpay its top managers by six million dollars while many suppliers remained unpaid. Homeline's share price began to fluctuate wildly last month, when one supplier decided to sue the company. The government says that Homeline was not in compliance with accounting rules and that it will penalize the directors. Customers who have paid for furniture that was not delivered may receive only a partial refund. We will have a full report at ten.","ja":"こんばんは。経済ニュースをお伝えします。家具チェーンのホームラインが今朝、破産を申請し、従業員2,000人の一時解雇がすでに始まっています。独立した監査役の調べで、同社は多くの仕入れ先への支払いを残したまま、経営幹部に600万ドルを払い過ぎていたことが分かりました。ホームラインの株価は、ある仕入れ先が同社を訴えると決めた先月から、激しく変動し始めていました。政府は、ホームラインが会計の規則を守っておらず、取締役を処罰するとしています。代金を払ったのに家具が届いていない顧客は、一部の返金しか受けられない可能性があります。10時に詳しくお伝えします。","words":[["bankruptcy","freq:bankruptcy"],["layoff","freq:layoff"],["auditor","freq:auditor"],["overpay","freq:overpay"],["unpaid","freq:unpaid"],["fluctuate","freq:fluctuate"],["sue","freq:sue"],["compliance","freq:compliance"],["penalize","freq:penalize"],["partial","freq:partial"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the auditor find?","o":["Suppliers were paid twice.","Workers stole furniture.","The stores were unsafe.","Top managers were paid too much."],"a":3,"why":"had managed to overpay its top managers by six million dollars（経営幹部に600万ドルを払い過ぎていた）とある。"},{"q":"When did the share price begin to move wildly?","o":["When a supplier decided to sue","This morning","When the layoffs began","After the audit"],"a":0,"why":"last month, when one supplier decided to sue the company（先月、仕入れ先が訴えると決めたとき）とある。"},{"q":"What may happen to customers who paid for furniture?","o":["They will get a new delivery date.","They may get back only part of their money.","They can choose other items.","They will be paid by the government."],"a":1,"why":"may receive only a partial refund（一部の返金しか受けられないかもしれない）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0103","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"書店でのイベント案内","text":"Good afternoon, shoppers. In ten minutes, on the second floor, the chef Luca Moretti will introduce his new cookbook, Tastes of the Coast. Luca grew up in a fishing village, where seafood is traditionally cooked over an open fire. Today he will prepare a tasty appetizer of grilled shrimp, followed by a pastry made with fresh butter and lemon. The critics have called his cooking superb, and I think you will agree. He will also explain how to choose fish at the market. For example, never buy more than one kilogram at a time. Signed copies are twenty dollars. It is a terrific gift, so please join us upstairs.","ja":"お買い物中の皆様、こんにちは。10分後に2階で、料理人のルカ・モレッティさんが新しい料理本『海辺の味』を紹介します。ルカさんは漁村で育ちました。そこでは伝統的に、魚介類を直火で調理します。今日は、焼いたエビのおいしい前菜と、それに続いて、新鮮なバターとレモンを使った焼き菓子を作ります。評論家は彼の料理を見事だと評しており、皆様もきっと同じ感想を持たれるでしょう。市場での魚の選び方も説明します。たとえば、一度に1キログラムを超えて買ってはいけません。サイン入りの本は20ドルです。すばらしい贈り物になりますので、どうぞ2階へお越しください。","words":[["cookbook","freq:cookbook"],["seafood","freq:seafood"],["traditionally","freq:traditionally"],["tasty","freq:tasty"],["appetizer","freq:appetizer"],["pastry","freq:pastry"],["butter","freq:butter"],["superb","freq:superb"],["kilogram","freq:kilogram"],["terrific","freq:terrific"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will happen in ten minutes?","o":["The store will close.","A cooking class will end.","A chef will present his book.","A fish market will open."],"a":2,"why":"the chef Luca Moretti will introduce his new cookbook（料理人が新しい料理本を紹介する）とある。"},{"q":"Where did Luca grow up?","o":["In a fishing village","In a big city","On a farm","Above a bakery"],"a":0,"why":"Luca grew up in a fishing village（漁村で育った）とある。"},{"q":"How much is a signed copy?","o":["Ten dollars","Twenty dollars","One dollar per kilogram","It is free."],"a":1,"why":"Signed copies are twenty dollars（サイン本は20ドル）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0104","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"音楽祭の案内","text":"Welcome to the opening night of the Lakeside Music Festival. For thirty years, this prestigious event has brought the world's best players to our small town. Tonight, more than two thousand spectators will hear a violin concert by Mina Sato, followed by a drum group from West Africa. Tomorrow is special for another reason: it is a reunion of the festival's first orchestra, whose members last played together in 1995. Children will enjoy the interactive tent, where they can try real instruments. If you cannot stay, our programs are also sent out in stereo on Radio Lake. This festival is a tremendous artistic effort by four hundred volunteers. We hope you find it worthwhile.","ja":"レイクサイド音楽祭の開幕の夜へようこそ。30年にわたり、この名高い催しは、世界最高の演奏家たちを私たちの小さな町に招いてきました。今夜は、2,000人を超える観客が、ミナ・サトウさんのバイオリンの演奏会を聴き、続いて西アフリカの太鼓の楽団を楽しみます。明日は別の理由でも特別です。音楽祭の最初の楽団の再会の日なのです。団員が最後に一緒に演奏したのは1995年でした。お子さんは、本物の楽器を試せる体験型のテントを楽しめます。会場に残れない方のために、番組はラジオ・レイクでステレオ放送もしています。この音楽祭は、400人のボランティアによる、とてつもなく大きな芸術的な取り組みです。価値あるひとときになることを願っています。","words":[["prestigious","freq:prestigious"],["spectators","freq:spectator"],["violin","freq:violin"],["drum","freq:drum"],["reunion","freq:reunion"],["interactive","freq:interactive"],["stereo","freq:stereo"],["tremendous","freq:tremendous"],["artistic","freq:artistic"],["worthwhile","freq:worthwhile"]],"qs":[{"q":"How long has the festival been held?","o":["For five years","Since 1995","For two years","For thirty years"],"a":3,"why":"For thirty years, this prestigious event ...（30年にわたって）とある。"},{"q":"What is special about tomorrow?","o":["The first orchestra will play together again.","Tickets will be free.","A radio station will open.","Children will perform."],"a":0,"why":"it is a reunion of the festival's first orchestra（最初の楽団の再会）とある。"},{"q":"What can children do in the interactive tent?","o":["Meet the players","Try real instruments","Listen to the radio","Draw pictures"],"a":1,"why":"where they can try real instruments（本物の楽器を試せる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0105","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"百貨店の店内放送","text":"Good afternoon, and welcome to Carlton's. Today, our salespeople on the third floor are ready to help you choose business attire for the new season. Our lightweight wool suits are perfect for travel, because they do not wrinkle, even after ten hours in a suitcase. On the first floor, you can personalize a silver necklace or a wooden comb with a name while you wait. It takes only five minutes. And in our home department, every rug and cushion is twenty percent off until Sunday. If you spend more than two hundred dollars, we will deliver your order free of charge. Thank you for shopping at Carlton's.","ja":"こんにちは。カールトンズへようこそ。本日、3階では販売員が、新しい季節の仕事用の服装選びをお手伝いします。当店の軽量のウールのスーツは、スーツケースに10時間入れておいてもしわにならないので、出張にぴったりです。1階では、銀のネックレスや木のくしに、お待ちの間に名前を入れることができます。たった5分でできあがります。また、家庭用品売り場では、敷物とクッションがすべて、日曜まで2割引です。200ドルを超えてお買い上げの場合は、ご注文の品を無料でお届けします。カールトンズをご利用いただきありがとうございます。","words":[["salespeople","freq:salespeople"],["attire","freq:attire"],["lightweight","freq:lightweight"],["wool","freq:wool"],["wrinkle","freq:wrinkle"],["personalize","freq:personalize"],["necklace","freq:necklace"],["comb","freq:comb"],["rug","freq:rug"],["cushion","freq:cushion"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why are the wool suits good for travel?","o":["They are cheap.","They are warm.","They do not wrinkle.","They are easy to wash."],"a":2,"why":"they do not wrinkle, even after ten hours in a suitcase（スーツケースに10時間入れてもしわにならない）とある。"},{"q":"What can customers do on the first floor?","o":["Have a name put on an item","Try on suits","Buy a suitcase","Order a rug"],"a":0,"why":"you can personalize a silver necklace or a wooden comb with a name（ネックレスやくしに名前を入れられる）とある。"},{"q":"Until when are rugs and cushions on sale?","o":["Today only","Sunday","The end of the season","Five o'clock"],"a":1,"why":"twenty percent off until Sunday（日曜まで2割引）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0106","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"フェリーの船内放送","text":"Good afternoon. This is your purser speaking. I would like to reassure you that the short stop we made was not serious. A rope was caught under the ship, and the captain could not steer safely for a few minutes. The problem has been fixed, we are underway again, and normal service will resume at once. We are sorry for the unpleasant noise from the engine room. Please sit comfortably and enjoy the rest of the crossing. We now expect to arrive at four fifteen. Every motorcycle rider should return to the car deck first, in the time slot shown on the ticket. If you need a travel adapter for your phone, the shop on deck two sells them.","ja":"こんにちは。事務長からお知らせします。先ほどの短い停船は深刻なものではありませんので、ご安心ください。船の下に綱が引っかかり、船長が数分の間、安全に舵を取ることができませんでした。問題は解決し、本船は再び航行しており、通常の運航をただちに再開します。機関室からの不快な音につきましては、おわび申し上げます。どうぞ楽にお座りになり、残りの船旅をお楽しみください。到着は4時15分の見込みです。オートバイにお乗りの方は、乗船券に書かれた時間帯に、最初に車両甲板へお戻りください。携帯電話用の旅行用変換器が必要な方は、2階デッキの売店で販売しています。","words":[["purser","freq:purser"],["reassure","freq:reassure"],["steer","freq:steer"],["underway","freq:underway"],["resume","freq:resume"],["unpleasant","freq:unpleasant"],["comfortably","freq:comfortably"],["rider","freq:rider"],["slot","freq:slot"],["adapter","freq:adapter"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did the ship stop?","o":["A rope was caught under it.","The engine failed.","A passenger was ill.","The weather was bad."],"a":0,"why":"A rope was caught under the ship（船の下に綱が引っかかった）とある。"},{"q":"When is the ship now expected to arrive?","o":["At four o'clock","In a few minutes","At two","At four fifteen"],"a":3,"why":"We now expect to arrive at four fifteen（4時15分の見込み）とある。"},{"q":"Who should return to the car deck first?","o":["Truck drivers","Motorcycle riders","Passengers with phones","Families with children"],"a":1,"why":"Every motorcycle rider should return to the car deck first（オートバイに乗る人が最初に戻る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0107","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"病院の新人看護師研修","text":"Good morning, and welcome to the children's ward. Hand hygiene is an integral part of our work, so wash your hands before and after you touch each patient, and wear rubber gloves when you change a bandage. Only a doctor may prescribe medicine. Your job is to check that each child receives the correct dose at the correct time. If you are unsure, it is advisable to ask a senior nurse. Never guess. Every morning, we circulate a list of new patients. Please read it before you start. A pamphlet for parents is kept at the desk. Your familiarity with these rules will grow quickly. For today, simply follow your partner and watch.","ja":"おはようございます。小児病棟へようこそ。手の衛生は私たちの仕事に欠かせない部分です。患者さん一人ひとりに触れる前と後に手を洗い、包帯を替えるときはゴムの手袋を着けてください。薬を処方できるのは医師だけです。皆さんの仕事は、子どもたちがそれぞれ、正しい量を正しい時間に受け取っているかを確かめることです。確信が持てないときは、先輩の看護師に尋ねるのが賢明です。決して推測で動かないでください。毎朝、新しい患者さんの一覧を回覧します。仕事を始める前に読んでください。保護者向けの小冊子は受付に置いてあります。こうした決まりには、すぐに慣れていきます。今日は、組になった相手について回り、見ているだけでかまいません。","words":[["ward","freq:ward"],["hygiene","freq:hygiene"],["integral","freq:integral"],["rubber","freq:rubber"],["prescribe","freq:prescribe"],["dose","freq:dose"],["advisable","freq:advisable"],["circulate","freq:circulate"],["pamphlet","freq:pamphlet"],["familiarity","freq:familiarity"]],"qs":[{"q":"When should nurses wash their hands?","o":["Only in the morning","After reading the list","Before and after touching each patient","When a doctor asks"],"a":2,"why":"wash your hands before and after you touch each patient（患者に触れる前と後に）とある。"},{"q":"What is a nurse's job concerning medicine?","o":["Checking the dose and time","Choosing the medicine","Ordering supplies","Explaining it to parents"],"a":0,"why":"check that each child receives the correct dose at the correct time（正しい量を正しい時間に受け取っているか確かめる）とある。処方できるのは医師だけ。"},{"q":"What should new nurses do today?","o":["Change bandages","Follow a partner and watch","Write a pamphlet","Meet the parents"],"a":1,"why":"simply follow your partner and watch（相手について回って見る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0108","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"資料保管室の作業説明","text":"Thanks for helping with the archive project. Our goal is to scan forty years of company records so that anyone can retrieve a file in seconds. The paper files are in the storeroom on the lower floor, packed in bulk in large boxes. Please carry only one box at a time. When you scan a page, leave a margin of one centimeter on each side, and embed the date in the file name. Accuracy matters more than speed. If you see a flaw in a document, such as a missing page, write it on the yellow sheet. And if anything looks suspicious, for example a contract without a signature, tell me. To expedite the work, we will take turns at the two scanners.","ja":"保管記録の事業に協力してくれてありがとう。目標は、会社の40年分の記録を読み取り、誰でも数秒でファイルを取り出せるようにすることです。紙のファイルは下の階の物置にあり、大きな箱に大量にまとめて詰めてあります。運ぶのは一度に1箱だけにしてください。ページを読み取るときは、両側に1センチメートルの余白を残し、ファイル名に日付を埋め込んでください。速さより正確さが大切です。ページが抜けているなど、書類に不備を見つけたら、黄色の用紙に書いてください。署名のない契約書のように、何か不審なものがあれば、私に知らせてください。作業を早めるため、2台の読み取り機は交代で使います。","words":[["archive","freq:archive"],["retrieve","freq:retrieve"],["storeroom","freq:storeroom"],["bulk","freq:bulk"],["centimeter","freq:centimeter"],["embed","freq:embed"],["Accuracy","freq:accuracy"],["flaw","freq:flaw"],["suspicious","freq:suspicious"],["expedite","freq:expedite"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the goal of the project?","o":["To throw away old files","To move the storeroom","To write a company history","To make records easy to find"],"a":3,"why":"so that anyone can retrieve a file in seconds（誰でも数秒でファイルを取り出せるように）とある。"},{"q":"What should be included in each file name?","o":["The date","The box number","The worker's name","The page count"],"a":0,"why":"embed the date in the file name（ファイル名に日付を埋め込む）とある。"},{"q":"What should workers do if a page is missing?","o":["Scan the next file","Note it on the yellow sheet","Search the storeroom","Call the client"],"a":1,"why":"write it on the yellow sheet（黄色の用紙に書く）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0109","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"市長の記者会見","text":"Thank you all for coming. Today I am announcing a plan that will revolutionize transport in our city. From next April, the city will subsidize electric buses on every route. Old diesel buses pollute our air, and they will be gone within three years. Some prominent business leaders have asked whether the plan will interfere with deliveries downtown. I can give them my assurance that it will not. The relocation of the main bus station to Harbor Street will actually free more road space. I see a similarity with the plan that worked so well in Graz. Each idea has been judged on its merit. This step will signify the start of a cleaner future.","ja":"お集まりいただきありがとうございます。本日、私は、この市の交通を大きく変える計画を発表します。来年4月から、市はすべての路線の電気バスに補助金を出します。古いディーゼルバスは空気を汚しており、3年以内に姿を消します。一部の著名な経済界の指導者から、この計画が中心街の配送の邪魔になるのではないかという質問がありました。そうはならないと保証します。主要なバスターミナルをハーバー通りへ移転することで、むしろ道路の空きが増えます。グラーツでとてもうまくいった計画との類似点があると見ています。どの案も、その価値によって判断しました。この一歩は、よりきれいな未来の始まりを意味することになります。","words":[["revolutionize","freq:revolutionize"],["subsidize","freq:subsidize"],["pollute","freq:pollute"],["prominent","freq:prominent"],["interfere","freq:interfere"],["assurance","freq:assurance"],["relocation","freq:relocation"],["similarity","freq:similarity"],["merit","freq:merit"],["signify","freq:signify"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will the city do from next April?","o":["Build a new road","Close the bus station","Help pay for electric buses","Raise bus fares"],"a":2,"why":"the city will subsidize electric buses on every route（全路線の電気バスに補助金を出す）とある。"},{"q":"What were some business leaders worried about?","o":["Problems with downtown deliveries","Higher taxes","Fewer bus routes","Noise from the station"],"a":0,"why":"whether the plan will interfere with deliveries downtown（中心街の配送の邪魔にならないか）とある。"},{"q":"Where will the main bus station move?","o":["To Graz","To Harbor Street","To the airport","Out of the city"],"a":1,"why":"The relocation of the main bus station to Harbor Street（ハーバー通りへ移転）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0110","page":"freq","group":"1001〜1100","kind":"英会話講座の講義","text":"Welcome back. Today we will practice the contraction, such as \"I'm\" or \"she'll,\" because fluent speakers use it all the time. Listen to these examples. \"She's very athletic and plays volleyball twice a week.\" \"Whoever calls housekeeping will hear a recorded message.\" \"I'd love to visit Canada someday.\" Notice how the short forms make the sentences smoother. Honestly, many learners understand grammar well but speak poorly, simply because they say every word in full. It may feel strange at first, but try it anyhow. For homework, record yourself reading page twelve, and listen for places where you forgot the short form. Now, please repeat after me.","ja":"お帰りなさい。今日は「I'm」や「she'll」のような短縮形を練習します。流暢に話す人はいつも使っているからです。次の例を聞いてください。「彼女はとても運動が得意で、週に2回バレーボールをします。」「客室清掃係に電話した人は誰でも、録音されたメッセージを聞くことになります。」「いつかカナダを訪れてみたいです。」短い形のおかげで、文がなめらかになっていることに注目してください。正直に言うと、文法はよく分かっているのに話すのは下手、という学習者が多いのですが、それは単に、すべての語を省略せずに言うからです。最初は変な感じがするかもしれませんが、とにかく試してみてください。宿題として、12ページを読むところを録音し、短縮形を忘れた箇所を聞いて探してください。では、私の後について繰り返してください。","words":[["contraction","freq:contraction"],["fluent","freq:fluent"],["athletic","freq:athletic"],["volleyball","freq:volleyball"],["Whoever","freq:whoever"],["housekeeping","freq:housekeep"],["someday","freq:someday"],["Honestly","freq:honestly"],["poorly","freq:poorly"],["anyhow","freq:anyhow"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is today's lesson about?","o":["Short forms such as \"I'm\"","Sports vocabulary","Writing letters","Hotel English"],"a":0,"why":"we will practice the contraction, such as \"I'm\" or \"she'll\"（短縮形を練習する）とある。"},{"q":"Why do many learners speak poorly, according to the speaker?","o":["They do not know grammar.","They speak too fast.","They are afraid of mistakes.","They say every word in full."],"a":3,"why":"simply because they say every word in full（すべての語を省略せずに言うから）とある。"},{"q":"What is the homework?","o":["Writing ten sentences","Recording a reading of page twelve","Watching a volleyball game","Calling a hotel"],"a":1,"why":"record yourself reading page twelve（12ページを読むところを録音する）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0111","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"情報システム部の緊急連絡","text":"Attention, all staff. This is the IT department. Early this morning, a hacker tried to enter our network through an old modem in the warehouse. As a result, there was a short outage, and we had to disable remote access for everyone. The system is now operational again, but please follow these steps. First, change your password today. Second, validate your account by entering the code we send to your smartphone. Third, write down the serial number on the back of your laptop and send it to us electronically, using the form on the staff page. We will run a diagnostic test on every machine tonight, so please leave your computer switched on when you go home.","ja":"全従業員にお知らせします。情報システム部です。今朝早く、倉庫にある古いモデムを通じて、ハッカーが当社のネットワークに侵入しようとしました。その結果、短時間の停止が起こり、全員の遠隔接続を無効にせざるを得ませんでした。システムは現在、再び稼働していますが、次の手順に従ってください。まず、今日中にパスワードを変更します。次に、スマートフォンに送られるコードを入力して、アカウントを有効にします。3つ目に、ノートパソコンの裏にある通し番号を書き留め、社員用ページの用紙を使って電子的に送ってください。今夜、すべての機械で診断テストを行いますので、帰宅するときはコンピューターの電源を入れたままにしてください。","words":[["hacker","freq:hacker"],["modem","freq:modem"],["outage","freq:outage"],["disable","freq:disable"],["operational","freq:operational"],["validate","freq:validate"],["smartphone","freq:smartphone"],["serial","freq:serial"],["electronically","freq:electronically"],["diagnostic","freq:diagnostic"]],"qs":[{"q":"What happened this morning?","o":["Someone tried to break into the network.","A laptop was stolen.","The warehouse lost power.","A new system was installed."],"a":0,"why":"a hacker tried to enter our network（ハッカーがネットワークに侵入しようとした）とある。"},{"q":"What should staff do today?","o":["Return their laptops","Buy a new modem","Change their passwords","Work from home"],"a":2,"why":"First, change your password today（今日中にパスワードを変更）とある。"},{"q":"Why should computers be left on tonight?","o":["To receive e-mail","So that a test can be run","To save energy","To back up the warehouse data"],"a":1,"why":"We will run a diagnostic test on every machine tonight（今夜すべての機械で診断テストを行う）ためと説明している。"}]},
{"id":"f-0112","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"宿泊施設の広告","text":"Tired of the city? Plan a weekend getaway at Rosewood Manor, a hundred-year-old house in the quiet countryside of Kent. Wake up to beautiful scenery, enjoy a continental breakfast on the terrace, and spend the day in complete relaxation. Our glass garden house is full of tropical plants, even in winter. In the evening, dance in the grand ballroom, where a band plays every Saturday. You do not need to pack much. Every room has a full set of toiletries, and our doorman will carry your bags. Rosewood Manor is also the perfect place for a company retreat, with meeting rooms for up to forty people. Book this month and save twenty percent.","ja":"都会に疲れましたか。ケントの静かな田園地帯にある、築100年の館「ローズウッド・マナー」で、週末の短い休暇を計画しませんか。美しい景色とともに目を覚まし、テラスでパンとコーヒーの軽い朝食を楽しみ、一日を完全なくつろぎの中で過ごしてください。ガラス張りの庭園の建物は、冬でも熱帯の植物でいっぱいです。夜は、毎週土曜に楽団が演奏する大宴会場で踊りましょう。荷物はあまり必要ありません。全室に洗面用品がひとそろい用意されており、ドアマンがお荷物を運びます。ローズウッド・マナーは、会社の研修合宿にも最適で、40名までの会議室があります。今月ご予約いただくと2割引になります。","words":[["getaway","freq:getaway"],["countryside","freq:countryside"],["scenery","freq:scenery"],["continental","freq:continental"],["relaxation","freq:relaxation"],["tropical","freq:tropical"],["ballroom","freq:ballroom"],["toiletries","freq:toiletry"],["doorman","freq:doorman"],["retreat","freq:retreat"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where is Rosewood Manor?","o":["In the countryside","In a city center","On a tropical island","Near an airport"],"a":0,"why":"in the quiet countryside of Kent（ケントの静かな田園地帯）とある。"},{"q":"What happens every Saturday?","o":["A garden tour is held.","Breakfast is free.","Meetings are held.","A band plays in the ballroom."],"a":3,"why":"the grand ballroom, where a band plays every Saturday（毎週土曜に楽団が演奏する大宴会場）とある。"},{"q":"How can guests save twenty percent?","o":["By staying two nights","By booking this month","By bringing a group of forty","By coming in winter"],"a":1,"why":"Book this month and save twenty percent（今月予約すると2割引）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0113","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"法律事務所の新人研修","text":"Welcome to Hart and Lowe. As a new paralegal, you will mostly work on copyright and trademark cases. Let me explain a few rules. Every letter to a client must be printed on the firm's letterhead and signed by a lawyer. When a client sends a query, we are obliged to reply within two working days. Our rules forbid you to give legal advice yourself, even if the question seems simple. You must also abide by the rule of secrecy: never discuss a case outside the office. Signing the engagement letter will obligate the client to pay our fees, so please check that it is in the file before any work begins. Do you have any questions?","ja":"ハート・アンド・ロウへようこそ。新しい弁護士補助員として、皆さんは主に著作権と商標の案件を担当します。決まりをいくつか説明します。依頼人あての手紙はすべて、事務所名入りの便せんに印刷し、弁護士が署名しなければなりません。依頼人から問い合わせが届いたら、2営業日以内に返事をする義務があります。たとえ質問が簡単に見えても、皆さん自身が法律上の助言をすることは、規則で禁じられています。守秘の決まりにも従わなければなりません。事務所の外で案件について話してはいけません。委任契約書に署名すると、依頼人には当事務所の報酬を支払う義務が生じます。作業を始める前に、それがファイルに入っているかを確かめてください。質問はありますか。","words":[["paralegal","freq:paralegal"],["copyright","freq:copyright"],["trademark","freq:trademark"],["letterhead","freq:letterhead"],["query","freq:query"],["obliged","freq:oblige"],["forbid","freq:forbid"],["abide","freq:abide"],["engagement","freq:engagement"],["obligate","freq:obligate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What kind of cases will the new staff work on?","o":["Tax cases","Family cases","Copyright and trademark cases","Traffic cases"],"a":2,"why":"you will mostly work on copyright and trademark cases（主に著作権と商標の案件）とある。"},{"q":"How soon must the firm reply to a client's question?","o":["Within two working days","On the same day","Within a week","Before the next meeting"],"a":0,"why":"we are obliged to reply within two working days（2営業日以内に返事をする義務がある）とある。"},{"q":"What are paralegals not allowed to do?","o":["Print letters","Give legal advice","Read the files","Talk to lawyers"],"a":1,"why":"Our rules forbid you to give legal advice yourself（自分で法律上の助言をすることは禁じられている）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0114","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"Good evening. In economic news, the government has announced a stimulus plan worth two billion euros. Last year's floods devastated the northern region, and the number of unemployed workers there continues to soar. The money will be used in three ways. First, a new railway line will connect the north with the capital. Second, the automotive industry will receive loans to build electric cars. Third, a training fund will foster new skills among young people. One stockbroker told us that share prices rose as soon as the plan was announced. However, some experts warn that the plan will not help unless factories that closed after the floods open again permanently. We will bring you more tomorrow.","ja":"こんばんは。経済ニュースです。政府は、20億ユーロ規模の景気刺激策を発表しました。昨年の洪水は北部地域に壊滅的な被害を与え、同地域の失業者数は急増し続けています。資金は3つの形で使われます。まず、北部と首都を結ぶ新しい鉄道路線です。次に、自動車産業が電気自動車を製造するための融資を受けます。3つ目に、訓練基金が若者の新しい技能を育てます。ある株式仲買人は、計画が発表されるとすぐに株価が上がったと話しています。ただし、洪水の後に閉鎖した工場が恒久的に再開しない限り、この計画は役に立たないと警告する専門家もいます。詳しくは明日お伝えします。","words":[["stimulus","freq:stimulus"],["euros","freq:euro"],["devastated","freq:devastate"],["unemployed","freq:unemployed"],["soar","freq:soar"],["railway","freq:railway"],["automotive","freq:automotive"],["foster","freq:foster"],["stockbroker","freq:stockbroker"],["permanently","freq:permanently"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the plan needed?","o":["Floods damaged the north.","Share prices fell.","The railway closed.","Car sales dropped."],"a":0,"why":"Last year's floods devastated the northern region（昨年の洪水が北部に壊滅的被害を与えた）とある。"},{"q":"What will the automotive industry receive?","o":["New factories","Tax cuts","Trained workers","Loans to build electric cars"],"a":3,"why":"the automotive industry will receive loans to build electric cars（電気自動車製造のための融資）とある。"},{"q":"What do some experts warn?","o":["The plan costs too much.","Closed factories need to reopen for good.","Young people will leave the north.","Share prices will fall again."],"a":1,"why":"will not help unless factories ... open again permanently（工場が恒久的に再開しない限り役に立たない）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0115","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"劇団からのお知らせ","text":"Hello, and thank you for calling the Northgate Players. We are now holding an audition for our summer show, The Last Circus, a musical based on the biography of the clown Tom Berry. We need twenty actors, four dancers, and volunteers who can sew costumes. The first rehearsal is on June 2. Our designer has just finished a sketch of the stage, and we plan to redesign the lobby as a circus tent to thrill our younger visitors. For the Saturday shows, a sign language interpreter will stand beside the stage. Students of journalism who would like to write about the show are welcome to visit. To book an audition time, press one now.","ja":"もしもし、ノースゲート・プレイヤーズにお電話ありがとうございます。現在、夏の公演『最後のサーカス』のオーディションを行っています。道化師トム・ベリーの伝記をもとにしたミュージカルです。俳優20人、ダンサー4人、そして衣装を縫えるボランティアを募集しています。最初のけいこは6月2日です。デザイナーが舞台の下絵を描き終えたところで、小さなお客様をわくわくさせるため、ロビーをサーカスのテントのように作り直す予定です。土曜の公演では、手話の通訳者が舞台の横に立ちます。公演について記事を書きたい報道専攻の学生の方の見学も歓迎します。オーディションの時間を予約するには、今、1を押してください。","words":[["audition","freq:audition"],["Circus","freq:circus"],["biography","freq:biography"],["sew","freq:sew"],["rehearsal","freq:rehearsal"],["sketch","freq:sketch"],["redesign","freq:redesign"],["thrill","freq:thrill"],["interpreter","freq:interpreter"],["journalism","freq:journalism"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the summer show based on?","o":["A famous film","A children's book","The life of a clown","A circus in June"],"a":2,"why":"a musical based on the biography of the clown Tom Berry（道化師の伝記をもとにしたミュージカル）とある。"},{"q":"What kind of volunteers are needed?","o":["People who can sew","People who can paint","People who can drive","People who can sing"],"a":0,"why":"volunteers who can sew costumes（衣装を縫えるボランティア）とある。"},{"q":"What will be offered at the Saturday shows?","o":["Free tickets for students","Sign language interpreting","A talk by the designer","A visit to the stage"],"a":1,"why":"a sign language interpreter will stand beside the stage（手話の通訳者が舞台の横に立つ）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0116","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"食堂の朝礼","text":"Good morning, team. Two things before we open. First, the menu. Today's specials are a cheeseburger with black pepper sauce and a tuna salad. For dessert, we have vanilla ice cream and a fresh donut. If a customer mentions an allergy, do not guess. Check the red folder, which lists everything in each dish. Second, cleanliness. The health officer comes on Friday. Bacteria grow fast in warm weather, so change every tablecloth after each customer and never put a dropped fork back on the table. It is going to be hot today, and people will be thirsty, so keep the water jugs full. Let's have a good day.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。開店前に2点あります。まず、メニューです。今日のおすすめは、黒こしょうのソースをかけたチーズバーガーと、ツナサラダです。デザートは、バニラアイスクリームと揚げたてのドーナツです。お客様がアレルギーのことを口にされたら、推測で答えないでください。赤いファイルを確認してください。各料理に入っているものがすべて載っています。次に、清潔さについてです。金曜に保健所の担当者が来ます。暖かい時期は細菌がすぐに増えますので、お客様が替わるたびにテーブルクロスを取り替え、落としたフォークは決してテーブルに戻さないでください。今日は暑くなり、皆さんのどが渇きますから、水差しはいつも満たしておいてください。よい一日にしましょう。","words":[["cheeseburger","freq:cheeseburger"],["pepper","freq:pepper"],["tuna","freq:tuna"],["vanilla","freq:vanilla"],["donut","freq:donut"],["allergy","freq:allergy"],["Bacteria","freq:bacteria"],["tablecloth","freq:tablecloth"],["fork","freq:fork"],["thirsty","freq:thirsty"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should staff do if a customer mentions an allergy?","o":["Ask the chef to guess","Suggest the salad","Change the tablecloth","Check the red folder"],"a":3,"why":"Check the red folder, which lists everything in each dish（赤いファイルを確認する）とある。"},{"q":"Who is coming on Friday?","o":["A health officer","A new chef","A food supplier","The owner"],"a":0,"why":"The health officer comes on Friday（金曜に保健所の担当者が来る）とある。"},{"q":"Why should the water jugs be kept full?","o":["The dishwasher is broken.","It will be a hot day.","A large group is coming.","Ice cream is sold out."],"a":1,"why":"It is going to be hot today, and people will be thirsty（今日は暑くてのどが渇く）ためと言っている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0117","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"市の道路情報","text":"This is a traffic update from City Hall. The intersection of King Street and Fifth Avenue will be partially closed from Monday while workers demolish the old bank building. Buses will take an indirect route by way of Park Road, so journeys may take ten minutes longer. Please do not overcrowd the first buses of the morning. Extra ones will run every five minutes. The war monument in the square will be covered to protect it from dust, and a loose roof tile on the station has already been removed. Snow is forecast for Tuesday, and the city will plow main roads first. Our live map uses satellite data and will show every new occurrence within minutes.","ja":"市役所から交通情報をお伝えします。キング通りと5番街の交差点は、作業員が古い銀行の建物を取り壊す間、月曜から一部が通行止めになります。バスはパーク通りを経由する遠回りの経路を通りますので、所要時間が10分ほど長くなることがあります。朝の最初のバスに詰めかけて混雑させないでください。5分おきに増便が走ります。広場の戦争記念碑は、ほこりから守るため覆いをかけます。駅の屋根の緩んだかわらは、すでに取り除きました。火曜は雪の予報で、市は主要な道路から先に除雪します。市のライブ地図は衛星のデータを使っており、新しい出来事を数分以内に表示します。","words":[["intersection","freq:intersection"],["partially","freq:partially"],["demolish","freq:demolish"],["indirect","freq:indirect"],["overcrowd","freq:overcrowd"],["monument","freq:monument"],["tile","freq:tile"],["plow","freq:plow"],["satellite","freq:satellite"],["occurrence","freq:occurrence"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will the intersection be partly closed?","o":["A building is being torn down.","Snow has fallen.","A monument is being built.","A bus broke down."],"a":0,"why":"while workers demolish the old bank building（古い銀行の建物を取り壊す間）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about buses?","o":["They are canceled on Monday.","They are free in the morning.","They will take a longer route.","They will stop at the square."],"a":2,"why":"Buses will take an indirect route（遠回りの経路を通る）ので10分ほど長くかかる、とある。"},{"q":"What will the city do on Tuesday?","o":["Open the bank","Clear snow from main roads first","Remove the monument","Close the station"],"a":1,"why":"the city will plow main roads first（主要な道路から先に除雪する）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0118","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"部長の話","text":"Good morning. Let me begin our departmental meeting with a compliment. You are a hardworking team, and last month's results show it. I especially appreciate your willingness to help the new staff. Now, two requests. First, I would like everyone to take part actively in the Friday training. It is beneficial for all of us, even if some parts feel like repetition. Second, please avoid gossip about the planned merger. Most of what I have heard is irrelevant or simply wrong, and it worries people for no reason. Finally, several of you asked me to reconsider the new desk plan. I have done so, and we will keep the old layout until the summer.","ja":"おはようございます。部門会議を、まず称賛の言葉から始めます。皆さんはよく働くチームで、先月の成績がそれを示しています。新しい社員を進んで助けてくれる姿勢に、特に感謝しています。さて、お願いが2つあります。まず、金曜の研修には、全員が積極的に参加してほしいと思います。繰り返しに感じる部分があっても、私たち全員のためになります。次に、予定されている合併についてのうわさ話は控えてください。私が耳にしたものの大半は、関係のない話か、単に間違っている話で、理由もなく人を不安にさせます。最後に、新しい座席の案を考え直してほしいという声が何人かからありました。考え直した結果、夏までは今の配置のままにします。","words":[["departmental","freq:departmental"],["compliment","freq:compliment"],["hardworking","freq:hardworking"],["willingness","freq:willingness"],["actively","freq:actively"],["beneficial","freq:beneficial"],["repetition","freq:repetition"],["gossip","freq:gossip"],["irrelevant","freq:irrelevant"],["reconsider","freq:reconsider"]],"qs":[{"q":"How does the speaker begin the meeting?","o":["With a warning","With a new rule","With an apology","With praise for the team"],"a":3,"why":"begin our departmental meeting with a compliment（称賛の言葉から始める）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker ask staff to avoid?","o":["Gossip about the merger","Friday training","Helping new staff","Working overtime"],"a":0,"why":"please avoid gossip about the planned merger（合併についてのうわさ話を控える）とある。"},{"q":"What did the speaker decide about the desks?","o":["To buy new ones","To keep the old layout for now","To move them on Friday","To let staff choose"],"a":1,"why":"we will keep the old layout until the summer（夏までは今の配置のまま）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0119","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"キャンプ場の案内","text":"Welcome to Camp Silver Pine. I know that you are impatient to start, but please listen for two minutes. This bus is bound for the lake, where a lifeguard is on duty from nine to five. Do not swim outside those hours. Evenings here are chilly, so wear jeans and a sweater after sunset, and keep a raincoat in your backpack. There are many mosquitoes near the water, so use the spray in your cabin. Each cabin also has a broom. Please sweep the floor every morning. If this is your first night away from home, you may feel a little apprehensive. That is normal, and our staff are here to help. Dinner is at six.","ja":"キャンプ・シルバー・パインへようこそ。早く始めたくて待ちきれないのは分かりますが、2分だけ聞いてください。このバスは湖へ向かいます。湖では9時から5時まで監視員が勤務しています。その時間以外は泳がないでください。ここの夜は肌寒いので、日が沈んだらジーンズとセーターを着て、リュックサックにはレインコートを入れておいてください。水辺には蚊がたくさんいますので、小屋にあるスプレーを使ってください。各小屋にはほうきもあります。毎朝、床を掃いてください。家を離れて過ごす最初の夜という人は、少し不安に感じるかもしれません。それは普通のことですし、スタッフが力になります。夕食は6時です。","words":[["impatient","freq:impatient"],["bound","freq:bound"],["lifeguard","freq:lifeguard"],["chilly","freq:chilly"],["jeans","freq:jeans"],["raincoat","freq:raincoat"],["backpack","freq:backpack"],["mosquitoes","freq:mosquito"],["broom","freq:broom"],["apprehensive","freq:apprehensive"]],"qs":[{"q":"When may campers swim?","o":["At any time","After sunset","Between nine and five","Only before breakfast"],"a":2,"why":"a lifeguard is on duty from nine to five. Do not swim outside those hours（監視員がいる9時から5時の間だけ）とある。"},{"q":"What should campers wear in the evening?","o":["Jeans and a sweater","A swimsuit","A raincoat","Shorts"],"a":0,"why":"wear jeans and a sweater after sunset（日が沈んだらジーンズとセーター）とある。夜は肌寒いため。"},{"q":"What should campers do every morning?","o":["Pack their backpacks","Sweep the cabin floor","Spray the lake","Meet the lifeguard"],"a":1,"why":"Please sweep the floor every morning（毎朝床を掃く）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0120","page":"freq","group":"1101〜1200","kind":"商店街の広告","text":"Looking for a gift that will not empty your wallet? Visit Second Chance, the consignment shop under the stone arc of the Old Bridge. We sell fine things that their owners no longer need, from a gold wristwatch to a diamond ring, at half the usual price. Our owner started the shop out of disgust at how much is thrown away each year. A small piece of jewelry can elevate even a simple outfit. If you are desperate for an idea, our staff will help you choose. Next door, the Bridge Salon offers a haircut for fifteen dollars. And enrollment is now open for our jewelry repair class. A diagram of every step is included in the course book.","ja":"財布が空にならない贈り物をお探しですか。旧橋の石造りのアーチの下にある委託販売の店「セカンド・チャンス」へお越しください。当店では、持ち主がもう必要としなくなった上質な品を、金の腕時計からダイヤモンドの指輪まで、通常の半額で販売しています。店主は、毎年どれほど多くの物が捨てられているかに嫌気がさして、この店を始めました。小さな装身具一つで、簡素な服装さえ引き立ちます。どうしても案が浮かばないときは、店員が選ぶお手伝いをします。隣のブリッジ・サロンでは、15ドルで髪を切ってもらえます。また、宝飾品の修理教室の受講登録が始まりました。教本には、すべての手順の図が載っています。","words":[["consignment","freq:consignment"],["arc","freq:arc"],["wristwatch","freq:wristwatch"],["diamond","freq:diamond"],["disgust","freq:disgust"],["elevate","freq:elevate"],["desperate","freq:desperate"],["Salon","freq:salon"],["enrollment","freq:enrollment"],["diagram","freq:diagram"]],"qs":[{"q":"What does Second Chance sell?","o":["New watches","Used items of good quality","Handmade clothes","Hair products"],"a":1,"why":"We sell fine things that their owners no longer need（持ち主が不要になった上質な品）を売っている。"},{"q":"Why did the owner start the shop?","o":["She disliked waste.","She loved bridges.","She was a jeweler.","She wanted to teach."],"a":0,"why":"out of disgust at how much is thrown away each year（毎年捨てられる物の多さに嫌気がさして）とある。"},{"q":"What is included in the course book?","o":["A discount coupon","A list of prices","A map of the bridge","Diagrams of each step"],"a":3,"why":"A diagram of every step is included in the course book（教本にすべての手順の図が載っている）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0121","page":"freq","group":"1201〜1250","kind":"健康づくり制度の案内","text":"Hello, everyone. I am happy to introduce our new wellness program, which starts next Monday. First, the cafeteria will offer a healthful lunch menu designed by an expert in nutrition, including homemade soup every day. Second, please try to drink at least one liter of water during the daytime. New water stations are on every floor. Third, the company gymnasium will stay open until nine, and you can borrow proper footwear at the desk. For our outdoor walking club, free sunscreen is available at reception. This program is especially useful for staff with chronic back pain, because a trainer will teach simple exercises at noon. Sign up on the staff page today.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。来週の月曜に始まる、新しい健康づくり制度をご紹介します。まず、社員食堂で、栄養の専門家が考えた健康によい昼食メニューを提供します。自家製のスープも毎日付きます。次に、日中に少なくとも1リットルの水を飲むよう心がけてください。各階に新しい給水所があります。3つ目に、会社の体育館は9時まで開いており、適切な履物は受付で借りられます。屋外のウォーキング部のために、受付で日焼け止めを無料で用意しています。この制度は、慢性的な腰痛のある従業員に特に役立ちます。正午に、指導員が簡単な運動を教えるからです。今日、社員用ページから申し込んでください。","words":[["wellness","freq:wellness"],["healthful","freq:healthful"],["nutrition","freq:nutrition"],["homemade","freq:homemade"],["liter","freq:liter"],["daytime","freq:daytime"],["gymnasium","freq:gymnasium"],["footwear","freq:footwear"],["sunscreen","freq:sunscreen"],["chronic","freq:chronic"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will the cafeteria offer?","o":["A healthful lunch menu","Free breakfast","Cooking lessons","Cold drinks only"],"a":0,"why":"the cafeteria will offer a healthful lunch menu（健康によい昼食メニューを提供する）とある。"},{"q":"Until what time will the gymnasium be open?","o":["Noon","Six","Nine","Midnight"],"a":2,"why":"the company gymnasium will stay open until nine（体育館は9時まで開いている）とある。"},{"q":"Who will find the program especially useful?","o":["New employees","Staff with long-term back pain","Members of the walking club","Cafeteria workers"],"a":1,"why":"especially useful for staff with chronic back pain（慢性的な腰痛のある従業員に特に役立つ）とある。chronic を long-term と言い換えている。"}]},
{"id":"f-0122","page":"freq","group":"1201〜1250","kind":"新任役員への説明","text":"Good morning, and welcome to the board. This short induction will explain what we expect of each incoming director. First, please read the company by-law on conflicts of interest. If you own shares in a supplier, you must tell us without hesitation. Second, our code of ethics applies to everyone. Any unauthorized use of company information will violate that code, and the board will act at once. Third, meetings are held on the first Monday of each month. If you are traveling, you may join by videoconference. The timeline for this year's decisions is in your folder. Finally, I hereby confirm that your term begins today and lasts three years.","ja":"おはようございます。取締役会へようこそ。この短い就任研修で、新しく加わる取締役の皆さんに期待することを説明します。まず、利益相反に関する会社の内規をお読みください。仕入れ先の株を持っている場合は、ためらわずに私たちに知らせなければなりません。次に、当社の倫理規定は全員に適用されます。会社の情報を許可なく使うことは、すべてその規定に違反し、取締役会はただちに対処します。3つ目に、会議は毎月第1月曜に開かれます。出張中の場合は、テレビ会議で参加できます。今年の決定事項の予定表は、お手元のファイルにあります。最後に、皆さんの任期が本日始まり、3年間続くことを、ここに確認します。","words":[["induction","freq:induction"],["incoming","freq:incoming"],["by-law","freq:by-law"],["hesitation","freq:hesitation"],["ethics","freq:ethics"],["unauthorized","freq:unauthorized"],["violate","freq:violate"],["videoconference","freq:videoconference"],["timeline","freq:timeline"],["hereby","freq:hereby"]],"qs":[{"q":"What must a director do if they own shares in a supplier?","o":["Sell them","Keep it secret","Leave the board","Inform the board"],"a":3,"why":"you must tell us without hesitation（ためらわずに知らせなければならない）とある。"},{"q":"How can a traveling director attend a meeting?","o":["By videoconference","By sending a letter","By choosing another date","By asking a colleague to vote"],"a":0,"why":"you may join by videoconference（テレビ会議で参加できる）とある。"},{"q":"How long is a director's term?","o":["One year","Three years","One month","Five years"],"a":1,"why":"your term begins today and lasts three years（任期は今日から3年間）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0123","page":"freq","group":"1201〜1250","kind":"学校の用務員への連絡","text":"Good morning. Here is the work list for the summer break. In the science room, every light bulb must be changed, and two of the ceiling fixtures are loose. Please unplug the old refrigerator in the staff room. It is inefficient and unreliable, and a new one arrives on Thursday. The wooden bookcase in the library has begun to deteriorate because of the damp wall, so move the books to the hall and discard any that are badly damaged. Outside, the lawn mower needs a new blade before you cut the sports field. The school inspector will visit in August, and she always looks at cleanliness first. Please finish the floors by the end of July.","ja":"おはようございます。夏休みの作業一覧を伝えます。理科室では、電球をすべて交換しなければならず、天井の照明器具のうち2つが緩んでいます。職員室の古い冷蔵庫のプラグを抜いてください。効率が悪く、当てにもならないので、木曜に新しいものが届きます。図書室の木の本棚は、壁の湿気のせいで傷み始めています。本を講堂へ移し、ひどく傷んだものは処分してください。屋外では、運動場の芝を刈る前に、芝刈り機に新しい刃が必要です。8月に学校の検査官が来ます。彼女はいつも、まず清潔さを見ます。床は7月末までに仕上げてください。","words":[["bulb","freq:bulb"],["fixtures","freq:fixture"],["unplug","freq:unplug"],["inefficient","freq:inefficient"],["unreliable","freq:unreliable"],["bookcase","freq:bookcase"],["deteriorate","freq:deteriorate"],["discard","freq:discard"],["mower","freq:mower"],["cleanliness","freq:cleanliness"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will the old refrigerator be replaced?","o":["It is too small.","It is noisy.","It works poorly.","It was borrowed."],"a":2,"why":"It is inefficient and unreliable（効率が悪く当てにならない）ためと説明している。"},{"q":"What is damaging the bookcase?","o":["A damp wall","Heavy books","Sunlight","Insects"],"a":0,"why":"has begun to deteriorate because of the damp wall（壁の湿気で傷み始めている）とある。"},{"q":"What does the inspector look at first?","o":["The sports field","How clean the school is","The science room","The library books"],"a":1,"why":"she always looks at cleanliness first（いつもまず清潔さを見る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0124","page":"freq","group":"1201〜1250","kind":"テレビ番組の司会","text":"Good evening, and welcome to Star Kitchen, the show where home cooks compete for a dream job. Please cheer for tonight's first contestant, Rosa Lin, a nurse from Portland. Rosa's cooking does not belong to one genre. Her dishes resemble small paintings, and the decoration on each plate takes her an hour. She says that her inspiration is her grandfather, an explorer who brought home recipes from thirty countries. Last year, her cooking blog won wide acclaim. Tonight, she must prepare dinner for six guests, and our judges will watch intently, not only for taste but also for hospitality. Rosa, you have ninety minutes. Your time starts now.","ja":"こんばんは。「スター・キッチン」へようこそ。家庭の料理人が、夢の仕事をかけて競い合う番組です。今夜の最初の出場者、ポートランドの看護師ロサ・リンさんに、どうぞ声援を送ってください。ロサさんの料理は、一つのジャンルに収まりません。料理は小さな絵に似ており、一皿ごとの飾り付けに1時間をかけます。着想の源は、30か国から調理法を持ち帰った探検家の祖父だそうです。昨年、彼女の料理ブログは広く称賛されました。今夜は6人のお客様のために夕食を用意しなければなりません。審査員は、味だけでなく、もてなしについても、じっと見守ります。ロサさん、持ち時間は90分です。今、始まりました。","words":[["cheer","freq:cheer"],["contestant","freq:contestant"],["genre","freq:genre"],["resemble","freq:resemble"],["decoration","freq:decoration"],["inspiration","freq:inspiration"],["explorer","freq:explorer"],["acclaim","freq:acclaim"],["intently","freq:intently"],["hospitality","freq:hospitality"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is Rosa's job?","o":["A painter","A chef","A writer","A nurse"],"a":3,"why":"Rosa Lin, a nurse from Portland（ポートランドの看護師）とある。"},{"q":"Who inspired Rosa's cooking?","o":["Her grandfather","A television judge","A famous chef","Her patients"],"a":0,"why":"her inspiration is her grandfather, an explorer（着想の源は探検家の祖父）とある。"},{"q":"What will the judges look at besides taste?","o":["Speed","Hospitality","Cost","Cleanliness"],"a":1,"why":"not only for taste but also for hospitality（味だけでなくもてなしも）とある。"}]},
{"id":"f-0125","page":"freq","group":"1201〜1250","kind":"試験対策講座の講義","text":"Good morning. Please open your workbook to page thirty. Today's passage is a news story about how the recession changed the car market. Sales of the large sedan fell drastically, while small cars became popular. Question one asks for a factual detail, so find the exact number in the text. Question two is harder. The correct answer is a restatement of the writer's main idea in different words. One complication is that two choices look almost the same. If you change your mind, erase your first mark completely. Reading stories like this every day will broaden your vocabulary. One last thing: please be considerate and keep quiet until everyone has finished.","ja":"おはようございます。練習帳の30ページを開いてください。今日の文章は、不況が自動車市場をどう変えたかについてのニュース記事です。大型のセダンの売れ行きは大幅に落ち込み、一方で小型車が人気になりました。第1問は事実に基づく細かい点を問うものですから、本文から正確な数字を見つけてください。第2問はもっと難しい問題です。正解は、筆者の主旨を別の言葉で言い換えたものです。やっかいなのは、2つの選択肢がほとんど同じに見えることです。考えを変えたときは、最初の印を完全に消してください。こうした記事を毎日読むと、語彙が広がります。最後に一つ。思いやりを持って、全員が終わるまで静かにしていてください。","words":[["workbook","freq:workbook"],["recession","freq:recession"],["sedan","freq:sedan"],["drastically","freq:drastically"],["factual","freq:factual"],["restatement","freq:restatement"],["complication","freq:complication"],["erase","freq:erase"],["broaden","freq:broaden"],["considerate","freq:considerate"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is today's passage about?","o":["A new car design","A reading test","The effect of a recession on car sales","A workbook for drivers"],"a":2,"why":"how the recession changed the car market（不況が自動車市場をどう変えたか）についての記事だとある。"},{"q":"What makes question two difficult?","o":["Two choices look very similar.","The passage is long.","It needs a calculation.","The words are unfamiliar."],"a":0,"why":"two choices look almost the same（2つの選択肢がほとんど同じに見える）とある。"},{"q":"What should students do if they change an answer?","o":["Tell the teacher","Erase the first mark completely","Mark both choices","Start the page again"],"a":1,"why":"erase your first mark completely（最初の印を完全に消す）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0001","page":"colls","group":"会議・話し合い","kind":"留守番電話のメッセージ","text":"Hello, this is Dana from the planning office. I am calling to schedule a meeting about the spring catalog. The session is tentatively scheduled for Thursday at two, and I will book a conference room on the third floor. I know I am asking on short notice, so if you have a prior engagement, please tell me today. Mr. Ito wants every team leader to attend the meeting, and that is why he asked me to call a meeting this week. I will set an agenda and send it this afternoon. Please confirm attendance by e-mail before noon tomorrow. If fewer than five people can come, we will have to postpone the meeting until next week. Thank you.","ja":"もしもし、企画室のデイナです。春のカタログについての会議の予定を入れたくて、お電話しました。会は木曜の2時に仮に予定しており、3階の会議室を私が予約します。急なお願いだと承知していますので、先約がある場合は今日中にお知らせください。伊藤さんはチームリーダー全員に会議へ出席してほしいと考えており、それで今週、会議を招集するよう私に頼みました。議題を決めて、今日の午後にお送りします。明日の正午までに、メールで出席を確認してください。来られる人が5人に満たない場合は、会議を来週に延期しなければなりません。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["schedule a meeting","colls:schedule a meeting"],["tentatively scheduled","colls:tentatively scheduled"],["book a conference room","colls:book a conference room"],["on short notice","colls:on short notice"],["prior engagement","colls:prior engagement"],["attend the meeting","colls:attend a meeting"],["call a meeting","colls:call a meeting"],["set an agenda","colls:set an agenda"],["confirm attendance","colls:confirm attendance"],["postpone the meeting","colls:postpone a meeting"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the meeting about?","o":["A new office","The spring catalog","A staff party","The summer budget"],"a":1,"why":"schedule a meeting about the spring catalog（春のカタログについての会議）とある。"},{"q":"What should listeners do before noon tomorrow?","o":["Confirm that they will attend","Book a room","Write the agenda","Call Mr. Ito"],"a":0,"why":"Please confirm attendance by e-mail before noon tomorrow（明日の正午までに出席を確認）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen if fewer than five people can come?","o":["The meeting will be held online.","Mr. Ito will cancel the catalog.","The room will be changed.","The meeting will be moved to next week."],"a":3,"why":"we will have to postpone the meeting until next week（来週に延期する）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0002","page":"colls","group":"会議・話し合い","kind":"会議の司会の説明","text":"Good afternoon, everyone. Before we start, let me explain how today's session works. Last month we had a heated discussion about the new shift system, and several people left unhappy. Today I want everyone to express an opinion freely. If you strongly disagree with something, say so politely and give a reason. If you would like to raise an issue that is not on the list, please wait until the end. Mr. Tanaka from human resources is here to address a concern many of you have about night shifts, and he will explain the rules in detail. After that, we will break into small groups to exchange ideas. Please take notes, because each group will make a suggestion to management. If anything is unclear, I will ask the speaker to elaborate on a point.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。始める前に、今日の会の進め方を説明します。先月は新しいシフト制度について白熱した議論になり、不満を残したまま帰った人が何人もいました。今日は、全員に自由に意見を述べてほしいと思います。何かに強く反対するときは、丁寧にそう言って、理由を挙げてください。一覧にない問題を提起したい場合は、最後までお待ちください。人事部の田中さんが、夜勤について多くの方が抱いている懸念に対処するために来ており、規則を詳しく説明します。そのあと、小さなグループに分かれて意見を交換します。各グループが経営陣に提案をしますので、メモを取ってください。分かりにくいところがあれば、私が話し手に要点を詳しく述べるよう頼みます。","words":[["heated discussion","colls:heated discussion"],["express an opinion","colls:express an opinion"],["strongly disagree","colls:strongly disagree"],["raise an issue","colls:raise an issue"],["address a concern","colls:address a concern"],["in detail","colls:in detail"],["exchange ideas","colls:exchange ideas"],["take notes","colls:take notes"],["make a suggestion","colls:make a suggestion"],["elaborate on a point","colls:elaborate on a point"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was discussed last month?","o":["Night buses","A new office","The new shift system","Pay rises"],"a":2,"why":"a heated discussion about the new shift system（新しいシフト制度についての白熱した議論）とある。"},{"q":"Why is Mr. Tanaka at the meeting?","o":["To deal with worries about night shifts","To take notes","To lead a small group","To introduce new staff"],"a":0,"why":"to address a concern many of you have about night shifts（夜勤についての懸念に対処するため）とある。"},{"q":"What will each group do?","o":["Vote on the rules","Offer a suggestion to management","Write to Mr. Tanaka","Change the shift list"],"a":1,"why":"each group will make a suggestion to management（各グループが経営陣に提案をする）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0003","page":"colls","group":"会議・話し合い","kind":"社内への報告","text":"Thank you all for waiting. I am pleased to tell you about yesterday's board meeting. As you know, the board had to make a decision about where to build our second factory. It was not easy to reach a consensus. The members spent three hours trying to weigh the options, and at first only half of them were in favor of the northern site. In the end, however, they did come to a conclusion. When the chair decided to take a vote, the northern site was unanimously approved. A unanimous decision is rare for this board, so I think it shows real confidence. The board also agreed to approve a proposal to hire sixty local workers. The plan now needs only final approval from the city, which we expect in June.","ja":"皆さん、お待たせしました。昨日の取締役会についてお伝えできることをうれしく思います。ご存じのとおり、取締役会は第二工場をどこに建てるかについて決定を下さなければなりませんでした。意見の一致に達するのは簡単ではありませんでした。役員たちは3時間かけて選択肢を比べて検討し、最初は北の用地に賛成していたのは半数だけでした。それでも最後には結論に達しました。議長が採決を取ることにしたところ、北の用地が全員一致で承認されました。この取締役会で全員一致の決定は珍しいので、強い自信の表れだと思います。取締役会は、地元の働き手を60人雇うという提案を承認することでも合意しました。計画に必要なのは、あとは市からの最終承認だけで、6月に下りる見込みです。","words":[["make a decision","colls:make a decision"],["reach a consensus","colls:reach a consensus"],["weigh the options","colls:weigh the options"],["in favor of","colls:in favor of"],["come to a conclusion","colls:come to a conclusion"],["take a vote","colls:take a vote"],["unanimously approved","colls:unanimously approved"],["unanimous decision","colls:unanimous decision"],["approve a proposal","colls:approve a proposal"],["final approval","colls:final approval"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did the board decide?","o":["Where to build a factory","When to close a factory","Who will be the chair","How to cut costs"],"a":0,"why":"make a decision about where to build our second factory（第二工場をどこに建てるか）とある。"},{"q":"How many members supported the northern site at first?","o":["None of them","All of them","Half of them","Sixty of them"],"a":2,"why":"at first only half of them were in favor of the northern site（最初は半数だけが賛成）とある。"},{"q":"What is still needed?","o":["A new vote","More workers","A larger site","Approval from the city"],"a":3,"why":"The plan now needs only final approval from the city（あとは市の最終承認だけ）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0004","page":"colls","group":"会議・話し合い","kind":"セミナーの開会のあいさつ","text":"Good morning, and welcome to the Regional Sales Seminar. On behalf of the organizing committee, I would like to make a few opening remarks. First, our staff will distribute handouts at the door, so please take one. It is now my honor to introduce a speaker who needs little introduction. Ms. Helen Cho has trained more than two thousand salespeople. This morning she will give a presentation on winning new customers. She will start with a brief overview of last year's market and then draw attention to three common mistakes. She uses many visual aids, so those at the back may wish to move forward. She will take questions for fifteen minutes at the end. This evening, she will also deliver a speech at our dinner party.","ja":"おはようございます。地域営業セミナーへようこそ。実行委員会を代表して、開会のあいさつを少し申し上げます。まず、係の者が入口で資料を配りますので、1部お取りください。それでは、紹介するまでもない講演者をご紹介します。ヘレン・チョーさんは、これまでに2,000人を超える営業担当者を指導してきました。今朝は、新しい顧客を獲得することについて発表をします。昨年の市場の簡単な概要から始め、そのあと、よくある3つの間違いに注意を向けてもらいます。視覚資料をたくさん使いますので、後ろの席の方は前へ移るとよいかもしれません。最後に15分間、質問を受けます。今晩は、夕食会でも演説をします。","words":[["On behalf of","colls:on behalf of"],["opening remarks","colls:opening remarks"],["distribute handouts","colls:distribute handouts"],["introduce a speaker","colls:introduce a speaker"],["give a presentation","colls:give a presentation"],["brief overview","colls:brief overview"],["draw attention to","colls:draw attention to"],["visual aids","colls:visual aids"],["take questions","colls:take questions"],["deliver a speech","colls:deliver a speech"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where can people get the handouts?","o":["On their seats","At the door","From Ms. Cho","By e-mail"],"a":1,"why":"our staff will distribute handouts at the door（入口で資料を配る）とある。"},{"q":"What is Ms. Cho's presentation about?","o":["Training managers","Using visual aids","Planning a seminar","Winning new customers"],"a":3,"why":"give a presentation on winning new customers（新しい顧客の獲得について発表する）とある。"},{"q":"What will Ms. Cho do this evening?","o":["Give a speech at a dinner","Answer questions","Meet customers","Return home"],"a":0,"why":"she will also deliver a speech at our dinner party（夕食会でも演説をする）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0005","page":"colls","group":"会議・話し合い","kind":"会議の締めくくり","text":"Before we finish, let me briefly summarize today's results. First, the website update is still an unresolved issue, so we must take action this week. I will assign a task to each of you by e-mail, and we need to set a deadline for every item. Second, each team should report on progress at next Monday's session. Kenji, thank you for agreeing to take minutes today. Could you circulate the minutes to all members by the end of the day? Please include the list of tasks. Finally, the client arrives at three, and we need this room for them. If there are no other questions, I would like to adjourn the meeting now. Thank you for your time and your ideas, everyone.","ja":"終わる前に、今日の結果を手短にまとめます。まず、ウェブサイトの更新はまだ未解決の問題ですので、今週中に行動を起こさなければなりません。メールで皆さん一人ひとりに仕事を割り当てますので、すべての項目について締め切りを決める必要があります。次に、各チームは来週月曜の会で進み具合を報告してください。ケンジさん、今日は議事録を取ることを引き受けてくれてありがとう。今日中に、全員に議事録を回覧してもらえますか。仕事の一覧も入れてください。最後に、3時にお客様が到着し、この部屋が必要になります。ほかに質問がなければ、ここで会議を終えたいと思います。皆さん、お時間とご意見をありがとうございました。","words":[["briefly summarize","colls:briefly summarize"],["unresolved issue","colls:unresolved issue"],["take action","colls:take action"],["assign a task","colls:assign a task"],["set a deadline","colls:set a deadline"],["report on progress","colls:report on progress"],["take minutes","colls:take minutes"],["circulate the minutes","colls:circulate the minutes"],["by the end of the day","colls:by the end of the day"],["adjourn the meeting","colls:adjourn a meeting"]],"qs":[{"q":"What problem has not been solved?","o":["The client's visit","The task list","The website update","The room booking"],"a":2,"why":"the website update is still an unresolved issue（ウェブサイトの更新はまだ未解決）とある。"},{"q":"What is Kenji asked to do?","o":["Send the minutes to everyone today","Meet the client","Assign the tasks","Book another room"],"a":0,"why":"Could you circulate the minutes to all members by the end of the day?（今日中に議事録を回覧して）とある。"},{"q":"Why does the speaker want to end the meeting?","o":["The team is tired.","The room is needed for a client.","The deadline has passed.","Kenji has to leave."],"a":1,"why":"the client arrives at three, and we need this room for them（お客様のために部屋が必要）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0006","page":"colls","group":"契約・交渉","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"In business news, Harbor Foods and the supermarket chain FreshWay have finally managed to reach an agreement. The two companies agreed to enter into negotiations in March, when Harbor Foods decided to make an offer to supply all of FreshWay's frozen meals. FreshWay chose to decline the offer at first, saying the prices were too high. Harbor then decided to make a counteroffer with a five percent discount. According to reports, each side had to make a concession: Harbor lowered its prices, and FreshWay promised a three-year contract. FreshWay's president said she was happy to accept the offer because of its favorable terms. Analysts call the result mutually beneficial. It took four months to strike a deal, and deliveries begin in September.","ja":"経済ニュースです。ハーバー・フーズとスーパーのフレッシュウェイが、ついに合意に達しました。両社は3月に交渉に入ることで合意しました。ハーバー・フーズが、フレッシュウェイの冷凍食品をすべて供給するという申し出をすることを決めたときです。フレッシュウェイは当初、価格が高すぎるとして申し出を断りました。そこでハーバーは、5パーセントの値引きを付けた対案を出すことにしました。報道によると、双方が譲歩しなければなりませんでした。ハーバーは価格を下げ、フレッシュウェイは3年契約を約束しました。フレッシュウェイの社長は、有利な条件なので喜んで申し出を受け入れたと述べました。専門家は、この結果を双方に利益のあるものと呼んでいます。取引をまとめるのに4か月かかり、納品は9月に始まります。","words":[["reach an agreement","colls:reach an agreement"],["enter into negotiations","colls:enter into negotiations"],["make an offer","colls:make an offer"],["decline the offer","colls:decline an offer"],["make a counteroffer","colls:make a counteroffer"],["make a concession","colls:make a concession"],["accept the offer","colls:accept an offer"],["favorable terms","colls:favorable terms"],["mutually beneficial","colls:mutually beneficial"],["strike a deal","colls:strike a deal"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did FreshWay refuse the first offer?","o":["The meals were poor.","The contract was too long.","The prices were too high.","Deliveries were too slow."],"a":2,"why":"saying the prices were too high（価格が高すぎると言って）断ったとある。"},{"q":"What did FreshWay promise?","o":["A three-year contract","A five percent discount","A new store","Faster payment"],"a":0,"why":"FreshWay promised a three-year contract（3年契約を約束した）とある。"},{"q":"When will deliveries start?","o":["In March","In four months","Next year","In September"],"a":3,"why":"deliveries begin in September（納品は9月に始まる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0007","page":"colls","group":"契約・交渉","kind":"法務部からの留守番電話","text":"Hi, Marco. This is Jenny Wu from the legal department. I had time to review a contract you sent me, the one with the cleaning company. Before you sign a contract like this, there are two points to change. First, under the terms of section four, they can terminate the contract with only one week's notice. That is too short. Second, they could renew the contract every year without our written consent, and the price could rise. Remember, once both sides sign, this is a binding agreement, and if we breach the contract, we will pay a heavy fee. I can draw up a contract with better conditions by Friday. If the other side refuses, we should get outside legal advice. Call me back at extension 204.","ja":"マルコさん、こんにちは。法務部のジェニー・ウーです。送ってもらった契約書、清掃会社とのものを見直す時間が取れました。このような契約書に署名する前に、変えるべき点が2つあります。1つ目に、第4条の条件のもとでは、先方はわずか1週間前の通知で契約を打ち切ることができます。これは短すぎます。2つ目に、先方は私たちの書面による同意なしに毎年契約を更新でき、価格が上がるおそれがあります。双方が署名すれば、これは拘束力のある合意になり、私たちが契約に違反すれば重い料金を払うことになるのを忘れないでください。金曜までに、もっとよい条件の契約書を作成できます。先方が断るなら、外部の法的な助言を受けるべきです。内線204に折り返してください。","words":[["review a contract","colls:review a contract"],["sign a contract","colls:sign a contract"],["under the terms of","colls:under the terms of"],["terminate the contract","colls:terminate a contract"],["renew the contract","colls:renew a contract"],["written consent","colls:written consent"],["binding agreement","colls:binding agreement"],["breach the contract","colls:breach a contract"],["draw up a contract","colls:draw up a contract"],["legal advice","colls:legal advice"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the contract with?","o":["A law firm","A cleaning company","A bank","A delivery company"],"a":1,"why":"the one with the cleaning company（清掃会社との契約書）とある。"},{"q":"What is wrong with section four?","o":["The notice period is too short.","The price is missing.","The dates are wrong.","It has not been signed."],"a":0,"why":"terminate the contract with only one week's notice. That is too short（1週間前の通知は短すぎる）とある。"},{"q":"What does Jenny offer to do by Friday?","o":["Call the cleaning company","Pay the fee","Write a better contract","Find a lawyer"],"a":2,"why":"I can draw up a contract with better conditions by Friday（金曜までによりよい条件の契約書を作成できる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0008","page":"colls","group":"契約・交渉","kind":"取引先向けの研修","text":"Welcome to the compliance training for new suppliers. Every company that works with us must meet the requirements in this handbook. First, you must comply with regulations on food safety at all times. Second, all work must be done in accordance with our quality standards. Third, you will see confidential information, such as recipes and prices. You must not disclose information of this kind to anyone outside your company. Taking photographs inside our kitchens is strictly prohibited. We expect partners to adhere to the terms of the supply agreement, and we promise to honor a commitment of our own: we always pay within thirty days. If a supplier fails to fulfill an obligation, we may impose a penalty or end the agreement. Now, let's look at page one.","ja":"新しい仕入れ先の皆さん、法令順守の研修へようこそ。当社と仕事をする会社はすべて、この手引きにある要件を満たさなければなりません。まず、食品の安全に関する規則に常に従わなければなりません。次に、すべての作業は当社の品質基準に従って行わなければなりません。3つ目に、皆さんは調理法や価格などの機密情報を目にします。この種の情報を、社外のだれにも開示してはいけません。当社の調理場の中で写真を撮ることは、固く禁じられています。取引先には供給契約の条件を厳守していただきたく、当社も自らの約束を守ることをお約束します。支払いは必ず30日以内に行います。仕入れ先が義務を果たさない場合、当社は罰則を科すか、契約を終えることがあります。では、1ページを見ましょう。","words":[["meet the requirements","colls:meet the requirements"],["comply with regulations","colls:comply with regulations"],["in accordance with","colls:in accordance with"],["confidential information","colls:confidential information"],["disclose information","colls:disclose information"],["strictly prohibited","colls:strictly prohibited"],["adhere to the terms","colls:adhere to the terms"],["honor a commitment","colls:honor a commitment"],["fulfill an obligation","colls:fulfill an obligation"],["impose a penalty","colls:impose a penalty"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the training for?","o":["New suppliers","New cooks","Customers","Safety inspectors"],"a":0,"why":"the compliance training for new suppliers（新しい仕入れ先向けの研修）とある。"},{"q":"What is not allowed in the kitchens?","o":["Eating","Talking","Wearing shoes","Taking photographs"],"a":3,"why":"Taking photographs inside our kitchens is strictly prohibited（調理場での撮影は固く禁じられている）とある。"},{"q":"What does the company promise?","o":["To raise prices","To pay within thirty days","To share its recipes","To visit every supplier"],"a":1,"why":"we always pay within thirty days（必ず30日以内に支払う）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0009","page":"colls","group":"契約・交渉","kind":"社長から社員への話","text":"Good morning. Today I have important news. After a year of talks, we will announce a merger this afternoon: Nordic Paper will merge with a rival, Lund Packaging. Five years ago, the two firms started working together in Poland, and those close ties helped us build a relationship of trust. Last year we decided to form a partnership for shipping as well. A full merger is the next step in this strategic alliance. Nordic Paper will hold a majority stake of sixty percent in the new firm. Some of you may worry about your jobs. Let me be clear: we do not plan to cut staff. In fact, we want to expand operations in Asia and may acquire a company there next year. In the long run, this change will make all of us stronger.","ja":"おはようございます。今日は大切なお知らせがあります。1年にわたる話し合いの末、今日の午後、合併を発表します。ノルディック・ペーパーは、競合相手のルンド・パッケージングと合併します。5年前、両社はポーランドで協力を始め、その緊密な関係のおかげで信頼の関係を築くことができました。昨年は、輸送でも提携を結ぶことを決めました。完全な合併は、この戦略的な提携の次の一歩です。ノルディック・ペーパーは、新会社の60パーセントという過半数の株式を持ちます。仕事について心配する方もいるでしょう。はっきり申し上げます。人員を減らす予定はありません。それどころか、アジアで事業を拡大したいと考えており、来年はそこで会社を買収するかもしれません。長い目で見れば、この変化は私たち全員を強くします。","words":[["announce a merger","colls:announce a merger"],["merge with a rival","colls:merge with a rival"],["close ties","colls:close ties"],["build a relationship","colls:build a relationship"],["form a partnership","colls:form a partnership"],["strategic alliance","colls:strategic alliance"],["majority stake","colls:majority stake"],["expand operations","colls:expand operations"],["acquire a company","colls:acquire a company"],["In the long run","colls:in the long run"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will be announced this afternoon?","o":["A new product","A factory closing","A merger","A price cut"],"a":2,"why":"we will announce a merger this afternoon（今日の午後、合併を発表する）とある。"},{"q":"What did the two firms do five years ago?","o":["Started working together in Poland","Opened an office in Asia","Cut their staff","Bought a shipping firm"],"a":0,"why":"the two firms started working together in Poland（ポーランドで協力を始めた）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about jobs?","o":["Many will move to Asia.","Sixty percent will change.","New staff will be hired at once.","There is no plan to cut staff."],"a":3,"why":"we do not plan to cut staff（人員を減らす予定はない）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0010","page":"colls","group":"契約・交渉","kind":"地域のニュース","text":"This is the local news. The city has decided to award a contract for the new bridge to Delta Construction. Six firms chose to bid on a project worth forty million dollars, and each had to submit a bid by June first. Delta was not the lowest bidder, but the city said its safety record was the best. Rival firm Stone Works, which expected to win a contract this year, is angry. Its president says the process was unfair and that the firm may take legal action. She plans to file a lawsuit next week and seek compensation for its costs. The mayor said he hopes to settle a dispute like this out of court. Work on the bridge is expected to start in the fall.","ja":"地域のニュースです。市は、新しい橋の契約をデルタ建設に発注することを決めました。4,000万ドル相当の事業に6社が入札することを選び、各社は6月1日までに入札しなければなりませんでした。デルタは最も安い金額を出した入札者ではありませんでしたが、市は、同社の安全面の実績が最もよかったと述べました。今年こそ契約を勝ち取ると見込んでいた競合のストーン・ワークスは怒っています。同社の社長は、手続きが不公平だったとし、法的措置を取るかもしれないと述べています。来週訴訟を起こし、かかった費用の補償を求める考えです。市長は、このような紛争は法廷の外で解決したいと述べました。橋の工事は秋に始まる見込みです。","words":[["award a contract","colls:award a contract"],["bid on a project","colls:bid on a project"],["submit a bid","colls:submit a bid"],["lowest bidder","colls:lowest bidder"],["win a contract","colls:win a contract"],["take legal action","colls:take legal action"],["file a lawsuit","colls:file a lawsuit"],["seek compensation","colls:seek compensation"],["settle a dispute","colls:settle a dispute"],["out of court","colls:out of court"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did the city choose Delta Construction?","o":["Its price was the lowest.","Its safety record was the best.","It is a local firm.","It finished first."],"a":1,"why":"the city said its safety record was the best（安全面の実績が最もよかった）とある。"},{"q":"What does the president of Stone Works plan to do?","o":["File a lawsuit","Build another bridge","Meet the mayor","Lower its price"],"a":0,"why":"She plans to file a lawsuit next week（来週訴訟を起こす考え）とある。"},{"q":"When will work on the bridge begin?","o":["On June first","Next week","In the fall","Next year"],"a":2,"why":"Work on the bridge is expected to start in the fall（秋に始まる見込み）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0011","page":"colls","group":"注文・配送","kind":"電話の自動音声","text":"Thank you for calling Parker Office Supply. To place an order, press one. Please note that customers who buy in bulk receive a ten percent discount, and a large order of over fifty boxes is delivered free. If you would like to request a quote for your company, press two, and we will send a price list upon request. To confirm an order or cancel an order you have already made, press three and have your order number ready. New business customers must complete a form on our website before we can process an order. We are sorry, but our printer paper in size A3 is currently unavailable. We expect more next week. To speak with our staff, please stay on the line.","ja":"パーカー事務用品にお電話ありがとうございます。注文するには1を押してください。まとめて購入するお客様には10パーセントの割引があり、50箱を超える大量の注文は無料で配達します。会社用に見積もりを依頼したい場合は2を押してください。ご要望があれば価格表をお送りします。すでにした注文を確認する、または注文を取り消すには3を押し、注文番号をご用意ください。新しい法人のお客様は、当社が注文を処理する前に、ウェブサイトで用紙に記入していただく必要があります。申し訳ありませんが、A3サイズの印刷用紙は現在手に入りません。来週、入荷する見込みです。係の者と話すには、そのままお待ちください。","words":[["place an order","colls:place an order"],["in bulk","colls:in bulk"],["large order","colls:large order"],["request a quote","colls:request a quote"],["upon request","colls:upon request"],["confirm an order","colls:confirm an order"],["cancel an order","colls:cancel an order"],["complete a form","colls:complete a form"],["process an order","colls:process an order"],["currently unavailable","colls:currently unavailable"]],"qs":[{"q":"What do customers who buy large amounts receive?","o":["A free gift","A discount","A catalog","Faster service"],"a":1,"why":"customers who buy in bulk receive a ten percent discount（まとめ買いには10パーセントの割引）とある。"},{"q":"What must new business customers do first?","o":["Complete a form on the website","Visit the store","Pay in advance","Call a manager"],"a":0,"why":"New business customers must complete a form on our website（ウェブサイトで用紙に記入する）とある。"},{"q":"What is not available now?","o":["Price lists","Delivery","Order numbers","A3 printer paper"],"a":3,"why":"our printer paper in size A3 is currently unavailable（A3の印刷用紙は現在手に入らない）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0012","page":"colls","group":"注文・配送","kind":"開店前の打ち合わせ","text":"Good morning, team. Before we open, here are today's jobs. First, we need to take inventory in the garden section this morning. Yesterday several customers asked for the blue watering cans, and we could not tell them whether they were in stock. Please check availability on the computer before you answer. The large plant pots are out of stock, and forty are on back order until Friday. Summer chairs are in limited supply, so each customer may buy only four. We have sufficient stock of soil, so please restock the shelves near the entrance. Also, we always run low on supplies such as paper bags on weekends, so use them carefully. Finally, gloves are readily available in aisle six if you need a pair.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。開店の前に、今日の仕事を伝えます。まず、今朝は園芸売り場の在庫を調べる必要があります。昨日、何人ものお客様から青いじょうろについて聞かれましたが、在庫があるかどうか答えられませんでした。答える前に、コンピューターで在庫を確認してください。大きな植木鉢は在庫切れで、40個が金曜まで入荷待ちです。夏用のいすは供給量が限られているので、お一人4脚までとします。土は十分な在庫がありますので、入口近くの棚に商品を補充してください。また、週末にはいつも紙袋などの備品が残り少なくなりますので、大事に使ってください。最後に、手袋が必要な人は、6番通路ですぐ手に入ります。","words":[["take inventory","colls:take inventory"],["in stock","colls:in stock"],["check availability","colls:check availability"],["out of stock","colls:out of stock"],["on back order","colls:on back order"],["limited supply","colls:limited supply"],["sufficient stock","colls:sufficient stock"],["restock the shelves","colls:restock the shelves"],["run low on supplies","colls:run low on supplies"],["readily available","colls:readily available"]],"qs":[{"q":"What should staff do before answering customers about an item?","o":["Ask the manager","Look in the storeroom","Check the computer","Call the supplier"],"a":2,"why":"Please check availability on the computer before you answer（答える前にコンピューターで確認）とある。"},{"q":"How many summer chairs may one customer buy?","o":["Four","Six","Forty","As many as they like"],"a":0,"why":"each customer may buy only four（お一人4脚まで）とある。"},{"q":"What often runs low on weekends?","o":["Soil","Paper bags","Gloves","Plant pots"],"a":1,"why":"we always run low on supplies such as paper bags on weekends（週末は紙袋などが残り少なくなる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0013","page":"colls","group":"注文・配送","kind":"取引先への留守番電話","text":"Hello, Ms. Rivera. This is Tom from Bright Home Lighting, returning your call. We will ship your order this afternoon. Because the lamps are fragile items, we pack each one in a special box. You asked whether we could expedite the shipment for your store opening. Yes, we can use next-day delivery at no extra charge, since your order qualifies for free shipping. Once the boxes are in transit, I will e-mail you a number so that you can track the shipment online. The driver should deliver the package before noon tomorrow. Someone must be there to sign for the package, so please tell your staff. If nobody is available, call me at 555-0142, and we will choose another time.","ja":"リベラ様、こんにちは。ブライト・ホーム照明のトムです。折り返しお電話しました。ご注文の品は今日の午後に発送します。ランプは壊れやすい品物ですので、1つずつ専用の箱に入れます。お店の開店に合わせて発送を早められるか、とのお尋ねでした。はい、ご注文は送料無料の対象ですので、追加料金なしで翌日配達を使えます。箱が輸送中になりましたら、オンラインで荷物を追跡できるよう、番号をメールでお送りします。運転手は明日の正午までに荷物を配達するはずです。荷物の受け取りに署名する方がその場にいる必要がありますので、お店の方にお伝えください。どなたもいらっしゃらない場合は、555-0142までお電話ください。別の時間を決めましょう。","words":[["ship your order","colls:ship an order"],["fragile items","colls:fragile items"],["expedite the shipment","colls:expedite a shipment"],["next-day delivery","colls:next-day delivery"],["at no extra charge","colls:at no extra charge"],["free shipping","colls:free shipping"],["in transit","colls:in transit"],["track the shipment","colls:track a shipment"],["deliver the package","colls:deliver a package"],["sign for the package","colls:sign for a package"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why does Ms. Rivera want the order quickly?","o":["Her store is opening.","Her lamps broke.","She is moving.","She is going on a trip."],"a":0,"why":"expedite the shipment for your store opening（開店に合わせて発送を早める）とある。"},{"q":"What will Tom send by e-mail?","o":["A bill","A photo of the lamps","A list of drivers","A tracking number"],"a":3,"why":"I will e-mail you a number so that you can track the shipment online（追跡用の番号をメールで送る）とある。"},{"q":"What must someone do when the driver arrives?","o":["Pay a fee","Open the boxes","Sign for the package","Call Tom"],"a":2,"why":"Someone must be there to sign for the package（受け取りに署名する人が必要）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0014","page":"colls","group":"注文・配送","kind":"返品についての案内","text":"Thank you for shopping at Kitchen Corner. Here is some information about our return policy. When you receive a shipment from us, please inspect the contents on the same day. If you find damaged goods or a defective product, call us within seven days, and we will issue a refund or send a new one. You may also return an item simply because you changed your mind. In that case, it must be unused, in good condition, and in its original packaging. We give a full refund within thirty days of purchase; after that, you can only exchange an item for another of the same price. Please keep your receipt, because we cannot help you without it. For more details, visit our website.","ja":"キッチン・コーナーをご利用いただき、ありがとうございます。返品の決まりについてご案内します。当店から荷物を受け取ったら、その日のうちに中身を点検してください。破損した商品や欠陥品を見つけた場合は、7日以内にお電話ください。返金するか、新しいものをお送りします。気が変わったというだけの理由でも、商品を返品できます。その場合は、未使用で、よい状態で、元の包装に入っていなければなりません。購入から30日以内なら全額返金します。それを過ぎると、同じ価格の別の商品と交換することしかできません。レシートがないと対応できませんので、取っておいてください。詳しくは、当店のウェブサイトをご覧ください。","words":[["receive a shipment","colls:receive a shipment"],["inspect the contents","colls:inspect the contents"],["damaged goods","colls:damaged goods"],["defective product","colls:defective product"],["issue a refund","colls:issue a refund"],["return an item","colls:return an item"],["in good condition","colls:in good condition"],["original packaging","colls:original packaging"],["full refund","colls:full refund"],["exchange an item","colls:exchange an item"]],"qs":[{"q":"When should customers check what is in the box?","o":["Within seven days","On the day it arrives","Within thirty days","Before paying"],"a":1,"why":"please inspect the contents on the same day（その日のうちに中身を点検）とある。"},{"q":"What is required when returning an item after a change of mind?","o":["It must be in its original packaging.","It must be damaged.","It must be a gift.","It must be expensive."],"a":0,"why":"it must be unused, in good condition, and in its original packaging（未使用・よい状態・元の包装）とある。"},{"q":"What can customers do after thirty days?","o":["Get a full refund","Get half the price back","Nothing at all","Exchange the item"],"a":3,"why":"after that, you can only exchange an item（それ以降は交換のみ）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0015","page":"colls","group":"注文・配送","kind":"倉庫での連絡","text":"Listen up, everyone. As you know, we are three days behind schedule. The storm last week made it impossible to unload cargo at the port, and that continues to cause a delay here. Two ships arrive tonight, and each incoming shipment is for the furniture factory. I need the night team to stack boxes in area C so that the morning team can load a truck every thirty minutes. Our customers expect their goods to be promptly delivered, and at this time of year we must work hard to meet demand. One more thing. The company that makes our plastic wrap has been late four times, so we will switch suppliers next month. We have found a reliable supplier in the city. Thanks for your hard work.","ja":"皆さん、聞いてください。ご存じのとおり、私たちは予定より3日遅れています。先週の嵐で港では貨物を降ろすことができず、それがここでも遅れを引き起こし続けています。今夜、船が2隻着き、これから届く荷物はどちらも家具工場向けです。朝の班が30分ごとにトラックに荷を積めるよう、夜の班にはC区画に箱を積み重ねてもらう必要があります。お客様は商品が速やかに配達されることを期待しており、この時期は需要を満たすために懸命に働かなければなりません。もう一つ。包装用フィルムを作っている会社は4回も遅れたので、来月、仕入れ先を替えます。市内に信頼できる仕入れ先を見つけました。いつも頑張ってくれてありがとう。","words":[["behind schedule","colls:behind schedule"],["unload cargo","colls:unload cargo"],["cause a delay","colls:cause a delay"],["incoming shipment","colls:incoming shipment"],["stack boxes","colls:stack boxes"],["load a truck","colls:load a truck"],["promptly delivered","colls:promptly delivered"],["meet demand","colls:meet demand"],["switch suppliers","colls:switch suppliers"],["reliable supplier","colls:reliable supplier"]],"qs":[{"q":"What caused the problem at the port?","o":["A strike","A broken crane","A storm","A lack of staff"],"a":2,"why":"The storm last week made it impossible to unload cargo（先週の嵐で貨物を降ろせなかった）とある。"},{"q":"What should the night team do?","o":["Stack boxes in area C","Drive the trucks","Call the factory","Unload the ships"],"a":0,"why":"I need the night team to stack boxes in area C（夜の班はC区画に箱を積む）とある。"},{"q":"Why will the company change its plastic wrap supplier?","o":["The price went up.","The supplier was late several times.","The quality was poor.","The supplier closed."],"a":1,"why":"has been late four times, so we will switch suppliers（4回遅れたので仕入れ先を替える）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0016","page":"colls","group":"支払い・経理","kind":"水道局からの留守番電話","text":"This is a message from City Water Service for Mr. Alan Brooks. Our records show an outstanding balance of eighty-two dollars on your account. Last month we had to issue an invoice a second time, but we have not received an answer. An overdue payment like this is usually easy to fix. You can make a payment by phone, online, or at any post office, and you do not have to pay a bill of this size in full at once. If you settle the account by June tenth, we will waive a fee of ten dollars that we normally add for late payment. After that date, we must charge a fee every week. To avoid problems in the future, many customers choose to pay three months in advance. Thank you.","ja":"市水道局から、アラン・ブルックス様へのお知らせです。当局の記録では、お客様の口座に82ドルの未払いの残高があります。先月、請求書を二度発行しなければなりませんでしたが、お返事をいただいていません。このような期限を過ぎた支払いは、たいてい簡単に解決できます。電話、オンライン、またはどの郵便局でも支払いをすることができ、この金額の請求書を一度に全額で支払う必要はありません。6月10日までに勘定を清算していただければ、遅れた支払いに通常加える10ドルの料金を免除します。その日を過ぎると、毎週、料金を請求しなければなりません。今後の問題を避けるため、多くのお客様が3か月分を前もって支払うことを選んでいます。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["outstanding balance","colls:outstanding balance"],["issue an invoice","colls:issue an invoice"],["overdue payment","colls:overdue payment"],["make a payment","colls:make a payment"],["pay a bill","colls:pay a bill"],["in full","colls:in full"],["settle the account","colls:settle an account"],["waive a fee","colls:waive a fee"],["charge a fee","colls:charge a fee"],["in advance","colls:in advance"]],"qs":[{"q":"How much does Mr. Brooks owe?","o":["Ten dollars","Eighty-two dollars","Sixty dollars","One hundred dollars"],"a":1,"why":"an outstanding balance of eighty-two dollars（82ドルの未払いの残高）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen if he pays by June tenth?","o":["The late fee will not be charged.","He will get a discount on water.","His account will be closed.","He will receive a new invoice."],"a":0,"why":"we will waive a fee of ten dollars（10ドルの料金を免除する）とある。"},{"q":"What do many customers do to avoid problems?","o":["Pay at the post office","Call every week","Use less water","Pay three months ahead"],"a":3,"why":"many customers choose to pay three months in advance（3か月分を前もって支払う）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0017","page":"colls","group":"支払い・経理","kind":"部内会議での説明","text":"Thanks for coming. I want to talk about the budget for the office move. We asked three companies to estimate the cost, and the cheapest price was still higher than we planned. As you know, we are working with a tight budget this year, and we cannot exceed the budget the board approved. If we go over budget, the difference will come from our training money. So here is my plan to cut costs. First, we will pack the small items ourselves. Second, we will reduce expenses by moving on a weekday. Third, I will allocate funds for new desks only where they are really needed. I have also kept five thousand dollars to cover the cost of any unexpected expenses. If we are careful, we can stay within budget.","ja":"お集まりいただきありがとうございます。事務所の引っ越しの予算についてお話しします。3社に費用を見積もるよう頼みましたが、最も安い金額でも、計画より高いものでした。ご存じのとおり、今年は厳しい予算でやりくりしており、取締役会が承認した予算を超えることはできません。予算を超えた場合、その差額は研修費から出すことになります。そこで、経費を削る私の案です。1つ目に、小さな物は自分たちで荷造りします。2つ目に、平日に引っ越すことで支出を減らします。3つ目に、新しい机のための資金は、本当に必要なところにだけ割り当てます。また、予想外の出費の費用をまかなうために、5,000ドルを取ってあります。気をつければ、予算内に収まります。","words":[["estimate the cost","colls:estimate the cost"],["tight budget","colls:tight budget"],["exceed the budget","colls:exceed the budget"],["over budget","colls:over budget"],["cut costs","colls:cut costs"],["reduce expenses","colls:reduce expenses"],["allocate funds","colls:allocate funds"],["cover the cost","colls:cover the cost"],["unexpected expenses","colls:unexpected expenses"],["within budget","colls:within budget"]],"qs":[{"q":"What is the budget for?","o":["An office move","A training course","New computers","A company party"],"a":0,"why":"the budget for the office move（事務所の引っ越しの予算）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen if the team spends too much?","o":["The move will be canceled.","The board will pay more.","Money will be taken from training.","Staff will pay themselves."],"a":2,"why":"the difference will come from our training money（差額は研修費から出す）とある。"},{"q":"How will the team save money on the moving day?","o":["By hiring students","By moving on a weekday","By moving at night","By using one truck"],"a":1,"why":"we will reduce expenses by moving on a weekday（平日に引っ越して支出を減らす）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0018","page":"colls","group":"支払い・経理","kind":"経理担当からの説明","text":"Hello, everyone. I am Priya from accounting, and I will explain how we reimburse employees for business travel. When you return from a trip, please submit receipts within ten days. You can only claim expenses for hotels, transport, and meals with clients. Please keep a record of each taxi ride, because drivers do not always give receipts. We transfer money to your bank account on a monthly basis, together with your salary. If you need to withdraw cash abroad, use the company card, and the amount will be automatically deducted from your travel budget. You will see every payment on your monthly statement. One more thing: if a client pays you directly, do not deposit a check yourself. Bring it to our office on the second floor.","ja":"皆さん、こんにちは。経理のプリヤです。出張について、従業員に払い戻す方法を説明します。出張から戻ったら、10日以内に領収書を提出してください。経費を請求できるのは、ホテル、交通、顧客との食事だけです。運転手がいつも領収書をくれるとは限りませんので、タクシーに乗るたびに記録をつけてください。お金は月単位で、給料と一緒に皆さんの銀行口座に振り込みます。海外で現金を引き出す必要があるときは会社のカードを使ってください。その金額は出張の予算から自動的に差し引かれます。すべての支払いは、月ごとの明細書で確認できます。もう一つ。顧客から直接支払いを受けた場合、自分で小切手を入金しないでください。2階の私たちの部屋まで持ってきてください。","words":[["reimburse employees","colls:reimburse employees"],["submit receipts","colls:submit receipts"],["claim expenses","colls:claim expenses"],["keep a record","colls:keep a record"],["transfer money","colls:transfer money"],["on a monthly basis","colls:on a monthly basis"],["withdraw cash","colls:withdraw cash"],["automatically deducted","colls:automatically deducted"],["monthly statement","colls:monthly statement"],["deposit a check","colls:deposit a check"]],"qs":[{"q":"When must receipts be handed in?","o":["Before the trip","On the last day of the month","With the salary","Within ten days of returning"],"a":3,"why":"please submit receipts within ten days（10日以内に領収書を提出）とある。"},{"q":"Why should employees write down taxi rides?","o":["Drivers may not give receipts.","Taxis are not allowed.","The company card cannot be used.","Clients pay for taxis."],"a":0,"why":"because drivers do not always give receipts（運転手が領収書をくれるとは限らない）とある。"},{"q":"What should an employee do with a check from a client?","o":["Send it back","Bring it to the accounting office","Put it in the bank","Keep it until the next trip"],"a":1,"why":"Bring it to our office on the second floor（2階の経理の部屋へ持ってくる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0019","page":"colls","group":"支払い・経理","kind":"経済ニュース","text":"Now for the business report. Sunrise Hotels will report earnings tomorrow, and investors are hopeful. Two years ago, the chain was in the red and continued to suffer a loss every quarter. Last year, however, it began to make a profit again, helped by steady growth in foreign visitors. Its new airport hotels now generate revenue of two million dollars a month. Analysts expect the company to announce record profits tomorrow. If so, its share price could rise sharply. The news is not as good for rival chain Grand Stay. After a sharp decline in business travel, its sales are expected to fall slightly for the third time this year. We will bring you both results tomorrow evening.","ja":"続いて経済の話題です。サンライズ・ホテルズは明日、決算を発表し、投資家は期待しています。2年前、同社は赤字で、四半期ごとに損失を出し続けていました。しかし昨年は、外国からの訪問者の着実な成長に助けられ、再び利益を上げ始めました。新しい空港ホテルは今、月に200万ドルの収益を生んでいます。専門家は、同社が明日、記録的な利益を発表すると見ています。そうなれば、株価は急に上がるかもしれません。競合のグランド・ステイにとっては、あまりよい知らせではありません。出張の急激な減少を受けて、同社の売上は今年3度目となるわずかな下落が見込まれています。両社の結果は、明日の夜にお伝えします。","words":[["report earnings","colls:report earnings"],["in the red","colls:in the red"],["suffer a loss","colls:suffer a loss"],["make a profit","colls:make a profit"],["steady growth","colls:steady growth"],["generate revenue","colls:generate revenue"],["record profits","colls:record profits"],["rise sharply","colls:rise sharply"],["sharp decline","colls:sharp decline"],["fall slightly","colls:fall slightly"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was true of Sunrise Hotels two years ago?","o":["It opened airport hotels.","It bought Grand Stay.","It was losing money.","It had record profits."],"a":2,"why":"the chain was in the red and continued to suffer a loss（赤字で損失を出し続けていた）とある。"},{"q":"What helped Sunrise Hotels recover?","o":["More foreign visitors","Lower prices","A new president","Business travel"],"a":0,"why":"helped by steady growth in foreign visitors（外国からの訪問者の着実な成長に助けられた）とある。"},{"q":"What is expected for Grand Stay?","o":["A sharp rise in sales","A new hotel","A change of name","A small fall in sales"],"a":3,"why":"its sales are expected to fall slightly（売上はわずかに下がる見込み）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0020","page":"colls","group":"支払い・経理","kind":"ラジオ番組の対談","text":"Welcome back to Small Business Today. My guest, Laura Kim, started a bakery ten years ago. Laura, how did you raise funds at the start? Well, the first thing I did was open an account for the business, separate from my own. Then I decided to take out a loan of thirty thousand dollars. I wanted to invest in equipment, especially a good oven. That oven was a sound investment, and I still use it. In the third year, we had financial difficulties, and I could hardly balance the books. So I asked an accountant to conduct an audit. She found that we were wasting flour and butter. After that, I was able to repay the loan in two years. My advice is simple: before you make an investment, ask an expert.","ja":"「スモール・ビジネス・トゥデイ」に戻りました。ゲストのローラ・キムさんは、10年前にパン屋を始めました。ローラさん、最初はどうやって資金を集めたのですか。ええ、最初にしたのは、自分のものとは別に、店のための口座を開くことでした。それから、3万ドルのローンを組むことにしました。設備、特によいオーブンに投資したかったのです。あのオーブンは堅実な投資で、今も使っています。3年目に財政難になり、帳簿の帳尻を合わせるのがやっとでした。そこで、会計士に監査を行うよう頼みました。彼女は、私たちが小麦粉とバターを無駄にしていることを見つけました。そのあとは、2年でローンを返済することができました。私の助言は簡単です。投資する前に、専門家に聞いてください。","words":[["raise funds","colls:raise funds"],["open an account","colls:open an account"],["take out a loan","colls:take out a loan"],["invest in equipment","colls:invest in equipment"],["sound investment","colls:sound investment"],["financial difficulties","colls:financial difficulties"],["balance the books","colls:balance the books"],["conduct an audit","colls:conduct an audit"],["repay the loan","colls:repay a loan"],["make an investment","colls:make an investment"]],"qs":[{"q":"What did Laura want to buy with the loan?","o":["A shop","A good oven","A delivery van","Flour and butter"],"a":1,"why":"I wanted to invest in equipment, especially a good oven（設備、特によいオーブンに投資したかった）とある。"},{"q":"What did the accountant discover?","o":["The bakery was wasting ingredients.","The loan was too large.","The oven was broken.","Prices were too low."],"a":0,"why":"She found that we were wasting flour and butter（小麦粉とバターを無駄にしていた）とある。"},{"q":"What does Laura advise?","o":["Borrowing less money","Buying cheap equipment","Asking an expert before investing","Opening two accounts"],"a":2,"why":"before you make an investment, ask an expert（投資する前に専門家に聞く）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0021","page":"colls","group":"人事・採用","kind":"ラジオの求人広告","text":"Are you looking for a new challenge? Green Valley Hospital is planning to recruit new staff for its kitchen. We need to fill a vacancy for a head cook, and this is a full-time position with weekends off. A qualified candidate will have at least three years of relevant experience in a large kitchen. If you would like to apply for a position like this, please submit a resume through our website by May fifteenth. We will conduct an interview with each person on our short list in the last week of May. The successful applicant will start work on July first. We welcome highly qualified cooks of any age. For more information, call our personnel office at 555-0177.","ja":"新しい挑戦をお探しですか。グリーン・バレー病院は、調理場の新しい職員を募集する予定です。料理長の欠員を埋める必要があり、これは週末が休みの常勤の職です。適任の候補者とは、大きな調理場で少なくとも3年の関連する経験がある方です。このような職に応募したい方は、5月15日までに当院のウェブサイトから履歴書を提出してください。5月の最後の週に、候補に残った方一人ひとりと面接を行います。採用された応募者は、7月1日に仕事を始めます。年齢を問わず、能力の十分な料理人を歓迎します。詳しくは、人事課 555-0177 までお電話ください。","words":[["recruit new staff","colls:recruit new staff"],["fill a vacancy","colls:fill a vacancy"],["full-time position","colls:full-time position"],["qualified candidate","colls:qualified candidate"],["relevant experience","colls:relevant experience"],["apply for a position","colls:apply for a position"],["submit a resume","colls:submit a resume"],["conduct an interview","colls:conduct an interview"],["successful applicant","colls:successful applicant"],["highly qualified","colls:highly qualified"]],"qs":[{"q":"What job is being advertised?","o":["A nurse","A head cook","A driver","An office clerk"],"a":1,"why":"fill a vacancy for a head cook（料理長の欠員を埋める）とある。"},{"q":"How should people apply?","o":["Through the website","By visiting the hospital","By phone","By mail"],"a":0,"why":"please submit a resume through our website（ウェブサイトから履歴書を提出）とある。"},{"q":"When will the new employee start?","o":["On May fifteenth","In the last week of May","On July first","Next weekend"],"a":2,"why":"The successful applicant will start work on July first（7月1日に仕事を始める）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0022","page":"colls","group":"人事・採用","kind":"新入社員へのあいさつ","text":"Good morning, and welcome. I am glad that all twelve of you decided to accept a position with us. To join a company of this size can be confusing, so let me explain your first month. Every new hire will undergo training for two weeks. The first week is in the classroom. The second week is hands-on training in the store, because the best way to acquire skills is on the job. Each of you will report to a supervisor, who will provide guidance and answer your questions. Do not worry about mistakes, because that is how you gain experience. Lunch is free in the staff cafeteria during training. Now, please open your handbook to page three.","ja":"おはようございます。ようこそ。12人全員が当社の職を引き受けると決めてくれたことを、うれしく思います。これほどの規模の会社に入社すると戸惑うこともありますので、最初の1か月について説明します。新入社員は全員、2週間の研修を受けます。1週目は教室です。2週目は店舗での実地研修です。技能を身につける一番の方法は、仕事をしながら学ぶことだからです。皆さんはそれぞれ上司の下で働き、その上司が指導し、質問に答えます。間違いを心配しないでください。そうやって経験を積むのですから。研修中、社員食堂の昼食は無料です。では、手引きの3ページを開いてください。","words":[["accept a position","colls:accept a position"],["join a company","colls:join a company"],["new hire","colls:new hire"],["undergo training","colls:undergo training"],["hands-on training","colls:hands-on training"],["acquire skills","colls:acquire skills"],["on the job","colls:on the job"],["report to a supervisor","colls:report to a supervisor"],["provide guidance","colls:provide guidance"],["gain experience","colls:gain experience"]],"qs":[{"q":"How long is the training?","o":["One week","One month","Three days","Two weeks"],"a":3,"why":"Every new hire will undergo training for two weeks（2週間の研修を受ける）とある。"},{"q":"Where does the second week take place?","o":["In the store","In the classroom","At head office","Online"],"a":0,"why":"The second week is hands-on training in the store（2週目は店舗での実地研修）とある。"},{"q":"What is free during training?","o":["Uniforms","Lunch","Parking","Handbooks"],"a":1,"why":"Lunch is free in the staff cafeteria during training（研修中は社員食堂の昼食が無料）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0023","page":"colls","group":"人事・採用","kind":"年末の部長の話","text":"Before the holidays, I would like to say a few words about this year. In January, I asked each of you to set a goal, and most of you managed to exceed expectations. Sales in our area grew by twelve percent, which is an outstanding performance. Because of that, everyone on this team will get an annual bonus in December. Next week, I will meet each of you to evaluate performance. I will give you constructive feedback, and I hope you will give me some, too. Two members worked especially hard to earn a promotion: from April, Dana and Luis will assume responsibility for our new office. They will also receive a raise. It is a pleasure to lead such a highly motivated team.","ja":"休みに入る前に、今年について少しお話しします。1月に、皆さん一人ひとりに目標を立てるようお願いしましたが、ほとんどの人が期待を上回ることができました。私たちの地域の売上は12パーセント伸びました。すばらしい業績です。そのため、このチームの全員が12月に年に一度の賞与を受け取ります。来週は、業績を評価するために、一人ずつ面談します。私から建設的な意見を伝えますので、皆さんからも私にいただければと思います。2人のメンバーは、昇進を勝ち取るために特によく働きました。4月から、デイナさんとルイスさんが新しい事務所の責任を負います。2人は昇給も受けます。これほど意欲の高いチームを率いることができて、うれしく思います。","words":[["set a goal","colls:set a goal"],["exceed expectations","colls:exceed expectations"],["outstanding performance","colls:outstanding performance"],["annual bonus","colls:annual bonus"],["evaluate performance","colls:evaluate performance"],["constructive feedback","colls:constructive feedback"],["earn a promotion","colls:earn a promotion"],["assume responsibility","colls:assume responsibility"],["receive a raise","colls:receive a raise"],["highly motivated","colls:highly motivated"]],"qs":[{"q":"By how much did sales grow?","o":["Two percent","Ten percent","Twelve percent","Twenty percent"],"a":2,"why":"Sales in our area grew by twelve percent（売上は12パーセント伸びた）とある。"},{"q":"What will the speaker do next week?","o":["Meet each member of the team","Open a new office","Pay the bonus","Take a holiday"],"a":0,"why":"Next week, I will meet each of you to evaluate performance（来週、一人ずつ面談して業績を評価する）とある。"},{"q":"What will Dana and Luis do from April?","o":["Join another company","Train new staff","Set new goals","Take charge of a new office"],"a":3,"why":"Dana and Luis will assume responsibility for our new office（新しい事務所の責任を負う）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0024","page":"colls","group":"人事・採用","kind":"人事部からのお知らせ","text":"Attention, all staff. Starting next month, we are introducing flexible hours. You may begin work at any time between seven and ten. Staff in the sales office may also work remotely two days a week. We know that many of you have a heavy workload and often work overtime. We hope the new system helps. The rules for paid leave are also changing. To take a day off, simply request leave on the staff website three days before. You no longer need a paper form. While you are on leave, a co-worker will check your e-mail. In the call center, at least five people must be on duty at all times, so please find someone to cover a shift before you make a request.","ja":"職員の皆さんにお知らせします。来月から、柔軟な勤務時間を取り入れます。7時から10時の間なら、いつ仕事を始めてもかまいません。営業所の職員は、週に2日、会社から離れた場所で働くこともできます。多くの方が多い仕事量を抱え、たびたび残業していることは承知しています。新しい制度が助けになればと思います。有給休暇の決まりも変わります。1日休みを取るには、3日前に職員用のウェブサイトで休暇を申請するだけです。紙の用紙はもう要りません。休暇中は、同僚があなたのメールを確認します。コールセンターでは、常に少なくとも5人が勤務中でなければなりませんので、申請する前に、勤務を代わる人を見つけてください。","words":[["flexible hours","colls:flexible hours"],["work remotely","colls:work remotely"],["heavy workload","colls:heavy workload"],["work overtime","colls:work overtime"],["paid leave","colls:paid leave"],["take a day off","colls:take a day off"],["request leave","colls:request leave"],["on leave","colls:on leave"],["on duty","colls:on duty"],["cover a shift","colls:cover a shift"]],"qs":[{"q":"When will the new system begin?","o":["Next month","Next week","Tomorrow","Next year"],"a":0,"why":"Starting next month, we are introducing flexible hours（来月から）とある。"},{"q":"How should staff ask for a day off?","o":["By filling in a paper form","By telling a co-worker","By using the staff website","By calling the call center"],"a":2,"why":"simply request leave on the staff website（職員用のウェブサイトで申請する）とある。"},{"q":"What must call center staff do before asking for leave?","o":["Work overtime","Find someone to take their shift","Check their e-mail","Finish all their calls"],"a":1,"why":"please find someone to cover a shift before you make a request（申請の前に勤務を代わる人を見つける）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0025","page":"colls","group":"人事・採用","kind":"経営陣についての社内連絡","text":"I have some news about our management team. As many of you know, Mr. Ogawa will step down as president in March. After forty years, he has decided to take early retirement and spend more time with his family. The board will appoint a successor next week. In other news, Ms. Rao, who is in charge of our Osaka factory, will transfer to a branch in Singapore. Her newly appointed replacement, Mr. Bell, will be the immediate supervisor of the production team. I also want to answer a rumor. We do not plan to cut jobs. Only one person chose to submit a resignation this year. Finally, please join us at a farewell party for Mr. Ogawa on March twentieth.","ja":"経営陣についてお知らせがあります。多くの方がご存じのとおり、小川さんは3月に社長を退きます。40年勤めた末、早期退職して、家族と過ごす時間を増やすことに決めました。取締役会は来週、後任を任命します。別の話題です。大阪工場を担当しているラオさんが、シンガポールの支店に異動します。新しく任命された後任のベルさんが、製造チームの直属の上司になります。うわさにもお答えしておきます。人員を削減する予定はありません。今年、辞表を出すことを選んだのは1人だけです。最後に、3月20日の小川さんの送別会に、ぜひご参加ください。","words":[["step down as president","colls:step down as president"],["take early retirement","colls:take early retirement"],["appoint a successor","colls:appoint a successor"],["in charge of","colls:in charge of"],["transfer to a branch","colls:transfer to a branch"],["newly appointed","colls:newly appointed"],["immediate supervisor","colls:immediate supervisor"],["cut jobs","colls:cut jobs"],["submit a resignation","colls:submit a resignation"],["farewell party","colls:farewell party"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is Mr. Ogawa leaving?","o":["He is moving to Singapore.","He is taking early retirement.","He was asked to leave.","He is starting a company."],"a":1,"why":"he has decided to take early retirement（早期退職することに決めた）とある。"},{"q":"Where will Ms. Rao work next?","o":["In Osaka","At head office","In the production team","In Singapore"],"a":3,"why":"will transfer to a branch in Singapore（シンガポールの支店に異動する）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about jobs?","o":["There is no plan to cut them.","Many people have resigned.","Forty jobs will be added.","The factory will close."],"a":0,"why":"We do not plan to cut jobs（人員を削減する予定はない）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0026","page":"colls","group":"営業・マーケティング","kind":"新製品の発表会","text":"Good afternoon, and thank you for joining us. Today we launch a product that we have worked on for three years: the AquaPure bottle. Last year we decided to conduct a survey of two thousand hikers. The answers showed a growing demand for a bottle that cleans river water. Filters are already widely used at home, but there was nothing light enough on the market for long walks. That gave us a chance to meet customer needs and enter a market where we had never sold anything. Our competitive edge is weight: the bottle weighs only two hundred grams. We believe every hiker is a potential customer, and we hope the low price will attract customers who have never bought our goods before. Now, let me show you how it works.","ja":"こんにちは。ご参加ありがとうございます。本日、私たちは3年かけて取り組んできた製品を発売します。アクアピュア・ボトルです。昨年、私たちは2,000人のハイカーを対象に調査を行うことにしました。その回答から、川の水をきれいにするボトルへの高まる需要が分かりました。浄水フィルターは家庭ではすでに広く使われていますが、長い山歩きに持っていけるほど軽いものは市場に出ていませんでした。それが、顧客の要望に応え、これまで何も売ったことのない市場に参入する機会になりました。当社の競争上の強みは重さです。このボトルはわずか200グラムです。ハイカーは全員が見込み客だと考えており、安い価格が、これまで当社の商品を買ったことのない客を引きつけることを期待しています。では、使い方をお見せします。","words":[["launch a product","colls:launch a product"],["conduct a survey","colls:conduct a survey"],["growing demand","colls:growing demand"],["widely used","colls:widely used"],["on the market","colls:on the market"],["meet customer needs","colls:meet customer needs"],["enter a market","colls:enter a market"],["competitive edge","colls:competitive edge"],["potential customer","colls:potential customer"],["attract customers","colls:attract customers"]],"qs":[{"q":"Who answered the survey?","o":["Shop owners","Students","Hikers","Engineers"],"a":2,"why":"conduct a survey of two thousand hikers（2,000人のハイカーを対象にした調査）とある。"},{"q":"What is special about the bottle?","o":["Its color","Its size","Its long history","Its light weight"],"a":3,"why":"Our competitive edge is weight: the bottle weighs only two hundred grams（強みは重さで、わずか200グラム）とある。"},{"q":"What will the speaker do next?","o":["Show how the bottle works","Announce the price","Answer questions","Introduce a hiker"],"a":0,"why":"Now, let me show you how it works（使い方をお見せします）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0027","page":"colls","group":"営業・マーケティング","kind":"販売促進の会議","text":"Let's move on to the plan for our new ice cream. As you know, our budget is small, so it will not be a heavily advertised product. We cannot run an advertisement on television. Instead, we will promote the product in three cheaper ways. First, students will distribute flyers at five train stations in July. Second, the cup has an eye-catching design, so people will share photos online. That will help us reach an audience under thirty and raise awareness without paying for it. Third, we will send free samples to two hundred loyal customers. Good news travels by word of mouth, and it took us years to build a reputation for quality, so the taste must be perfect. Any questions so far?","ja":"新しいアイスクリームの計画に移りましょう。ご存じのとおり予算が少ないので、大々的に宣伝された製品にはなりません。テレビに広告を出すことはできません。その代わり、もっと安い3つの方法で製品を宣伝します。1つ目に、7月に学生が5つの駅でちらしを配ります。2つ目に、カップは人目を引くデザインなので、人々がオンラインで写真を共有してくれるでしょう。それで、お金をかけずに30歳未満の人たちに届き、認知度を高めることができます。3つ目に、200人の常連客に無料の試供品を送ります。よい評判は口コミで広まります。品質の評判を築くのに何年もかかったのですから、味は完璧でなければなりません。ここまでで質問はありますか。","words":[["heavily advertised","colls:heavily advertised"],["run an advertisement","colls:run an advertisement"],["promote the product","colls:promote a product"],["distribute flyers","colls:distribute flyers"],["eye-catching design","colls:eye-catching design"],["reach an audience","colls:reach an audience"],["raise awareness","colls:raise awareness"],["loyal customers","colls:loyal customers"],["by word of mouth","colls:by word of mouth"],["build a reputation","colls:build a reputation"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will there be no television advertisement?","o":["The budget is small.","The product is not ready.","Television is too slow.","The rules do not allow it."],"a":0,"why":"our budget is small（予算が少ない）ので、テレビに広告を出せないとある。"},{"q":"Where will flyers be handed out?","o":["At schools","In supermarkets","At train stations","At a festival"],"a":2,"why":"students will distribute flyers at five train stations（5つの駅でちらしを配る）とある。"},{"q":"Who will receive free samples?","o":["Students","Two hundred loyal customers","Station staff","People under thirty"],"a":1,"why":"we will send free samples to two hundred loyal customers（200人の常連客に試供品を送る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0028","page":"colls","group":"営業・マーケティング","kind":"店内放送","text":"Attention, shoppers. Welcome to Maxwell's Department Store. To celebrate our fiftieth birthday, we will hold a sale on every floor this weekend. All winter coats are on sale, and selected boots are at half price. On the third floor, we offer a discount of twenty percent on kitchen goods for a limited time, from now until six o'clock. Do not miss our special offer on bed sheets: buy two and get one free. You can also redeem a coupon from today's newspaper at any cash desk. At Maxwell's, we promise competitive prices all year. When our costs fall, we lower prices, and we have not had to raise prices on children's clothing for three years. Thank you for shopping with us.","ja":"お買い物中の皆さまにお知らせします。マクスウェル百貨店へようこそ。創業50周年を祝って、今週末は全フロアでセールを開きます。冬のコートはすべて特売で、一部のブーツは半額です。3階では、今から6時までの期間限定で、台所用品を20パーセント割引します。シーツの特別提供もお見逃しなく。2枚買うと1枚が無料になります。今日の新聞のクーポンも、どの会計でもお使いいただけます。マクスウェルは、一年を通して他社に負けない価格をお約束します。経費が下がれば値下げしますし、子ども服はこの3年間、値上げせずに済んでいます。ご利用ありがとうございます。","words":[["hold a sale","colls:hold a sale"],["on sale","colls:on sale"],["at half price","colls:at half price"],["offer a discount","colls:offer a discount"],["for a limited time","colls:for a limited time"],["special offer","colls:special offer"],["redeem a coupon","colls:redeem a coupon"],["competitive prices","colls:competitive prices"],["lower prices","colls:lower prices"],["raise prices","colls:raise prices"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the store having a sale?","o":["It is closing.","Winter is over.","A new floor has opened.","It is fifty years old."],"a":3,"why":"To celebrate our fiftieth birthday（創業50周年を祝って）とある。"},{"q":"Until when is the kitchen goods discount available?","o":["Until noon","Until Sunday","Until six o'clock","Until next week"],"a":2,"why":"from now until six o'clock（今から6時まで）とある。"},{"q":"Where can shoppers find a coupon?","o":["In today's newspaper","On the third floor","On the website","At the entrance"],"a":0,"why":"redeem a coupon from today's newspaper（今日の新聞のクーポン）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0029","page":"colls","group":"営業・マーケティング","kind":"営業チームの朝礼","text":"Good morning, team. We have two weeks left to meet a target of five hundred units this quarter, and we are at four hundred and ten. Here is how we can boost sales. The new printer continues to sell well, so start with existing customers who bought the old model. Call them today. Second, each of you should visit a client at least twice this week. Do not just make a sales pitch. Bring the machine and give a demonstration, because people buy what they can touch. Maria did that on Monday with a prospective client, a law firm, and managed to secure an order for thirty units in one hour. If you need my help to close a deal, call me at any time. Let's finish strong.","ja":"皆さん、おはようございます。今四半期の500台という目標を達成するまで、残り2週間です。今は410台です。売上を伸ばす方法をお伝えします。新しいプリンターはよく売れ続けていますので、まずは古い型を買った既存の顧客から始めてください。今日、電話をかけてください。次に、各自、今週は少なくとも2回、顧客を訪問してください。売り込みをするだけではいけません。機械を持っていって実演をしてください。人は手で触れられるものを買うからです。マリアさんは月曜に、見込みのある顧客である法律事務所でそうして、1時間で30台の注文を取りつけました。取引を成立させるのに私の助けが必要なら、いつでも電話してください。最後まで頑張りましょう。","words":[["meet a target","colls:meet a target"],["boost sales","colls:boost sales"],["sell well","colls:sell well"],["existing customers","colls:existing customers"],["visit a client","colls:visit a client"],["make a sales pitch","colls:make a sales pitch"],["give a demonstration","colls:give a demonstration"],["prospective client","colls:prospective client"],["secure an order","colls:secure an order"],["close a deal","colls:close a deal"]],"qs":[{"q":"How many units has the team sold so far?","o":["Thirty","Ninety","Five hundred","Four hundred and ten"],"a":3,"why":"we are at four hundred and ten（今は410台）とある。"},{"q":"Who should the team call first?","o":["People who bought the old model","Law firms","New companies","The factory"],"a":0,"why":"start with existing customers who bought the old model（古い型を買った既存の顧客から始める）とある。"},{"q":"What did Maria do on Monday?","o":["She trained new staff.","She repaired a printer.","She got an order for thirty units.","She met the manager."],"a":2,"why":"managed to secure an order for thirty units in one hour（1時間で30台の注文を取りつけた）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0030","page":"colls","group":"営業・マーケティング","kind":"ラジオの市場解説","text":"In today's market report, we look at the coffee business. Three large chains still dominate the market, but they now face competition from small local shops. When we analyze the data from the last five years, we can identify a trend: customers are willing to pay more for quality. The number of small shops is rapidly growing, especially near universities. Because of this fierce competition, the leading brand, Bean House, cut two hundred jobs last spring. To stay ahead of the competition, it is now looking at the overseas market and plans to open a branch in Seoul in May. Will the plan work? We will ask an expert right after the break, so please stay with us.","ja":"今日の市場解説では、コーヒー業界を取り上げます。今も3つの大手チェーンが市場を支配していますが、小さな地元の店との競争に直面しています。過去5年間のデータを分析すると、ある傾向を見つけることができます。客は品質のためなら、より多く払ってもよいと考えているのです。小さな店の数は、特に大学の近くで急成長しています。この激しい競争のため、最大手のブランドであるビーン・ハウスは、昨年の春に200人を削減しました。競争相手の先を行くため、同社は今、海外市場に目を向けており、5月にソウルに支店を開く予定です。この計画はうまくいくでしょうか。このあとすぐ専門家に聞きますので、そのままお聞きください。","words":[["dominate the market","colls:dominate the market"],["face competition","colls:face competition"],["analyze the data","colls:analyze the data"],["identify a trend","colls:identify a trend"],["rapidly growing","colls:rapidly growing"],["fierce competition","colls:fierce competition"],["leading brand","colls:leading brand"],["stay ahead of the competition","colls:stay ahead of the competition"],["overseas market","colls:overseas market"],["open a branch","colls:open a branch"]],"qs":[{"q":"What trend does the speaker describe?","o":["People drink less coffee.","Customers pay more for quality.","Prices are falling.","Chains are opening near universities."],"a":1,"why":"customers are willing to pay more for quality（品質のためならより多く払う）とある。"},{"q":"What did Bean House do last spring?","o":["It opened in Seoul.","It bought small shops.","It raised its prices.","It cut two hundred jobs."],"a":3,"why":"Bean House, cut two hundred jobs last spring（昨年の春に200人を削減した）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen after the break?","o":["Music will be played.","The weather will be given.","An expert will be interviewed.","Listeners will call in."],"a":2,"why":"We will ask an expert right after the break（このあとすぐ専門家に聞く）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0031","page":"colls","group":"顧客対応","kind":"受付係への研修","text":"Welcome to your first day at the reception desk. Let me explain how we handle calls. Always answer the phone within three rings and give your name. When customers make an inquiry about prices, you may answer it yourself. For other questions, transfer a call to the right department. Never leave a caller on hold for more than one minute. If the person they want is out, offer to take a message, and write down the name and number. Some callers prefer to leave a message on voice mail. Tell them that our staff will return a call the same day. If a caller asks for further information, send our catalog by e-mail. We try to respond to an inquiry within two hours. Finally, when an important client is on the line, tell the manager at once.","ja":"受付での初日へようこそ。電話の扱い方を説明します。電話には必ず呼び出し音3回以内に出て、名前を名乗ってください。お客様が価格について問い合わせをしたときは、自分で答えてかまいません。ほかの質問については、担当の部署に電話を転送してください。電話の相手を1分以上、保留で待たせてはいけません。相手が話したい人が外出中なら、伝言を受けることを申し出て、名前と番号を書き留めてください。留守番電話に伝言を残すほうを好む方もいます。その場合は、当社の者がその日のうちに折り返し電話すると伝えてください。さらに詳しい情報を求められたら、カタログをメールで送ってください。問い合わせには2時間以内に答えるよう努めています。最後に、大切な顧客が電話に出ているときは、すぐに部長に知らせてください。","words":[["answer the phone","colls:answer the phone"],["make an inquiry","colls:make an inquiry"],["transfer a call","colls:transfer a call"],["on hold","colls:on hold"],["take a message","colls:take a message"],["leave a message","colls:leave a message"],["return a call","colls:return a call"],["further information","colls:further information"],["respond to an inquiry","colls:respond to an inquiry"],["on the line","colls:on the line"]],"qs":[{"q":"How quickly should staff answer the phone?","o":["Within one minute","Within two hours","At once","Within three rings"],"a":3,"why":"Always answer the phone within three rings（必ず呼び出し音3回以内に出る）とある。"},{"q":"What kind of question may receptionists answer themselves?","o":["Questions about prices","Questions about repairs","Questions about jobs","Questions about managers"],"a":0,"why":"When customers make an inquiry about prices, you may answer it yourself（価格の問い合わせは自分で答えてよい）とある。"},{"q":"What should staff send to callers who want more details?","o":["A price list by mail","A message to the manager","The catalog by e-mail","A voice mail"],"a":2,"why":"send our catalog by e-mail（カタログをメールで送る）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0032","page":"colls","group":"顧客対応","kind":"ホテルからのおわびの電話","text":"Hello, Mr. Grant. This is Susan Lee, the manager of Riverside Hotel. I am calling about your stay last weekend. I understand that you had to make a complaint because your room was not ready until six o'clock. First, I would like to offer an apology. We never want to cause inconvenience to our guests, and I deeply regret what happened on your wedding anniversary. We accept responsibility for the mistake. Our new booking system had failed, and my staff did not know how to resolve a problem like that. I never want a guest to leave as a dissatisfied customer. We have now trained every clerk to handle a complaint quickly. Please accept my sincere apology, together with a free night on your next visit. Once again, I apologize for the delay.","ja":"グラント様、こんにちは。リバーサイド・ホテルの支配人、スーザン・リーです。先週末のご宿泊の件でお電話しています。お部屋が6時まで用意できず、苦情を言わなければならなかったと承知しています。まず、おわびしたいと思います。私どもはお客様に不便をかけることを決して望んでおらず、結婚記念日に起きたことを深く遺憾に思います。この間違いの責任は私どもにあると認めます。新しい予約システムが故障し、係の者はそのような問題を解決する方法を知りませんでした。お客様に、不満を持つ客としてお帰りいただきたくはありません。現在は、すべての係が苦情にすばやく対応できるよう研修を済ませています。次回のご宿泊の無料1泊とともに、心からのおわびをお受け取りください。あらためて、遅れをおわびします。","words":[["make a complaint","colls:make a complaint"],["offer an apology","colls:offer an apology"],["cause inconvenience","colls:cause inconvenience"],["deeply regret","colls:deeply regret"],["accept responsibility","colls:accept responsibility"],["resolve a problem","colls:resolve a problem"],["dissatisfied customer","colls:dissatisfied customer"],["handle a complaint","colls:handle a complaint"],["sincere apology","colls:sincere apology"],["apologize for the delay","colls:apologize for the delay"]],"qs":[{"q":"What was Mr. Grant's problem?","o":["His room was noisy.","His bill was wrong.","His room was not ready on time.","His booking was lost."],"a":2,"why":"your room was not ready until six o'clock（部屋が6時まで用意できなかった）とある。"},{"q":"What caused the mistake?","o":["A lack of rooms","A failure of the booking system","A wedding party","A new manager"],"a":1,"why":"Our new booking system had failed（新しい予約システムが故障した）とある。"},{"q":"What does the manager offer?","o":["A refund","A larger room","A free dinner","A free night"],"a":3,"why":"together with a free night on your next visit（次回の無料1泊とともに）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0033","page":"colls","group":"顧客対応","kind":"修理窓口からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, this is Mark from Polar Appliances, calling for Ms. Ito. You contacted us yesterday to request a repair for your refrigerator. I checked our records, and the machine is still under warranty, so the work will be free of charge. From what you told us, it is hard to diagnose a problem like this by phone. It may be a faulty part in the door, or the machine may not have been properly installed. We would like to send a technician to your home. He can replace a part on the same day if necessary. I can schedule an appointment for Thursday morning or Friday afternoon. Also, I am sorry that our website was out of order yesterday. Please call me back at 555-0164.","ja":"もしもし、ポーラー電器のマークです。伊藤様にお電話しています。昨日、冷蔵庫の修理を依頼するためにご連絡をいただきました。記録を調べたところ、製品はまだ保証期間中ですので、作業は無料です。伺ったお話からすると、このような問題の原因を電話で突き止めるのは難しいです。ドアの不良部品かもしれませんし、製品が正しく取り付けられていなかったのかもしれません。ご自宅に技術者を派遣したいと思います。必要なら、その日のうちに部品を交換できます。木曜の午前か金曜の午後に予約を入れることができます。また、昨日は当社のウェブサイトが故障しており、申し訳ありませんでした。555-0164 まで折り返しお電話ください。","words":[["request a repair","colls:request a repair"],["under warranty","colls:under warranty"],["free of charge","colls:free of charge"],["diagnose a problem","colls:diagnose a problem"],["faulty part","colls:faulty part"],["properly installed","colls:properly installed"],["send a technician","colls:send a technician"],["replace a part","colls:replace a part"],["schedule an appointment","colls:schedule an appointment"],["out of order","colls:out of order"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why will the repair cost nothing?","o":["The refrigerator is under warranty.","Ms. Ito is a new customer.","The shop made a mistake.","The part is cheap."],"a":0,"why":"the machine is still under warranty, so the work will be free of charge（保証期間中なので無料）とある。"},{"q":"What does Mark want to do?","o":["Send a new refrigerator","Explain the repair by phone","Send a technician to her home","Visit the shop"],"a":2,"why":"We would like to send a technician to your home（ご自宅に技術者を派遣したい）とある。"},{"q":"What was wrong yesterday?","o":["The phone line","The delivery truck","The warranty card","The company's website"],"a":3,"why":"our website was out of order yesterday（昨日はウェブサイトが故障していた）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0034","page":"colls","group":"顧客対応","kind":"レンタカー会社の自動音声","text":"Thank you for calling Lakeside Car Rental. You are a valued customer, and we greatly appreciate your business. Our goal is to provide a service that will meet expectations every time. To help us improve the quality of our work, we would like you to complete a survey after this call. It has only four questions and takes one minute. We welcome feedback of any kind, good or bad. If you received excellent service from one of our staff today, please tell us his or her name. You can also leave a review on our website. Customers who do so receive ten percent off their next rental. And if you were happy with us, we hope you will highly recommend us to your friends. To begin the survey, press one.","ja":"レイクサイド・レンタカーにお電話ありがとうございます。あなたは大切なお客様であり、ご利用に大いに感謝しています。私たちの目標は、毎回期待に応えるサービスを提供することです。仕事の質を高めるため、この電話のあとでアンケートに答えていただければと思います。質問は4つだけで、1分で終わります。よいものでも悪いものでも、どのようなご意見も歓迎します。今日、当社の者からすばらしいサービスを受けた場合は、その者の名前をお知らせください。当社のウェブサイトにレビューを書くこともできます。書いてくださったお客様は、次回のご利用が10パーセント引きになります。そして、ご満足いただけたなら、お友達に当社を強く勧めていただければ幸いです。アンケートを始めるには、1を押してください。","words":[["valued customer","colls:valued customer"],["greatly appreciate","colls:greatly appreciate"],["provide a service","colls:provide a service"],["meet expectations","colls:meet expectations"],["improve the quality","colls:improve the quality"],["complete a survey","colls:complete a survey"],["welcome feedback","colls:welcome feedback"],["excellent service","colls:excellent service"],["leave a review","colls:leave a review"],["highly recommend","colls:highly recommend"]],"qs":[{"q":"How long does the survey take?","o":["Four minutes","One minute","Ten minutes","Half an hour"],"a":1,"why":"It has only four questions and takes one minute（質問は4つだけで1分）とある。"},{"q":"What do customers who write a review receive?","o":["A free rental","A gift card","A discount on their next rental","A larger car"],"a":2,"why":"receive ten percent off their next rental（次回が10パーセント引き）とある。"},{"q":"How can callers start the survey?","o":["By pressing one","By staying on the line","By visiting the website","By calling again"],"a":0,"why":"To begin the survey, press one（始めるには1を押す）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0035","page":"colls","group":"顧客対応","kind":"図書館のオンラインサービスの案内","text":"Welcome to the City Library's online service. To use it, you first need to create an account. Go to our website, type your card number, and enter a password of at least eight letters. If you have moved, please update personal information such as your address at the same time. With an account, you can borrow e-books at any time, day or night. You can also sign up for a newsletter about new books and events, and you will receive a notification when a book you want is ready. Remember to renew your membership every two years. To do this, you must come to the desk and show identification. If you subscribe to a service such as our monthly magazine box, you can cancel the subscription online with one click.","ja":"市立図書館のオンラインサービスへようこそ。利用するには、まずアカウントを作る必要があります。当館のウェブサイトで、カード番号を打ち込み、8文字以上のパスワードを入力してください。引っ越した方は、同時に住所などの個人情報を更新してください。アカウントがあれば、昼でも夜でも、いつでも電子書籍を借りられます。新しい本や催しについてのメールマガジンに登録することもでき、読みたい本の用意ができると通知を受け取れます。2年ごとに会員資格を更新するのを忘れないでください。そのためには、窓口に来て身分証を見せなければなりません。月ごとの雑誌ボックスなどのサービスに加入している場合は、オンラインで1回クリックするだけで解約できます。","words":[["create an account","colls:create an account"],["enter a password","colls:enter a password"],["update personal information","colls:update personal information"],["at any time","colls:at any time"],["sign up for a newsletter","colls:sign up for a newsletter"],["receive a notification","colls:receive a notification"],["renew your membership","colls:renew a membership"],["show identification","colls:show identification"],["subscribe to a service","colls:subscribe to a service"],["cancel the subscription","colls:cancel a subscription"]],"qs":[{"q":"How long must the password be?","o":["Four letters","Six letters","Ten letters","At least eight letters"],"a":3,"why":"enter a password of at least eight letters（8文字以上のパスワード）とある。"},{"q":"When will users receive a notification?","o":["When a book they want is ready","When the library closes","When they move","Every two years"],"a":0,"why":"you will receive a notification when a book you want is ready（読みたい本の用意ができたとき）とある。"},{"q":"What is needed to renew a membership?","o":["A password","A fee","Showing identification at the desk","A newsletter"],"a":2,"why":"you must come to the desk and show identification（窓口で身分証を見せる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0036","page":"colls","group":"出張・移動","kind":"旅行会社からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, Mr. Novak. This is Erin from Blue Sky Travel. You asked me to book a flight to Vancouver for June tenth. I am sorry, but the direct flight on that day is fully booked, because June is peak season. I was able to reserve a seat on the morning flight through Seattle, but I can hold it only until five today. Please call me to confirm the reservation. If I do not hear from you, I will have to cancel the reservation tonight. I can also make a reservation at the Harbor Hotel for you. Finally, would you like to rent a car at the airport, or shall I arrange transportation to the hotel? A shuttle costs only twenty dollars. My number is 555-0193. Thank you.","ja":"ノバク様、こんにちは。ブルー・スカイ旅行のエリンです。6月10日のバンクーバー行きの飛行機を予約するようご依頼いただきました。申し訳ありませんが、6月は繁忙期のため、その日の直行便は予約でいっぱいです。シアトル経由の午前の便の席を予約することはできましたが、押さえておけるのは今日の5時までです。予約を確認するため、お電話ください。ご連絡がなければ、今夜、予約を取り消さなければなりません。ハーバー・ホテルの予約も私のほうでできます。最後に、空港で車を借りますか。それとも、ホテルまでの交通手段を手配しましょうか。シャトルはわずか20ドルです。私の番号は 555-0193 です。よろしくお願いします。","words":[["book a flight","colls:book a flight"],["direct flight","colls:direct flight"],["fully booked","colls:fully booked"],["peak season","colls:peak season"],["reserve a seat","colls:reserve a seat"],["confirm the reservation","colls:confirm a reservation"],["cancel the reservation","colls:cancel a reservation"],["make a reservation","colls:make a reservation"],["rent a car","colls:rent a car"],["arrange transportation","colls:arrange transportation"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the direct flight not available?","o":["It was canceled.","The weather is bad.","It is fully booked.","It leaves too early."],"a":2,"why":"the direct flight on that day is fully booked（その日の直行便は予約でいっぱい）とある。"},{"q":"Until when can Erin hold the seat?","o":["Until five today","Until tomorrow morning","Until June tenth","Until tonight at nine"],"a":0,"why":"I can hold it only until five today（押さえておけるのは今日の5時まで）とある。"},{"q":"How much does the shuttle cost?","o":["Five dollars","Ten dollars","Fifty dollars","Twenty dollars"],"a":3,"why":"A shuttle costs only twenty dollars（シャトルは20ドル）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0037","page":"colls","group":"出張・移動","kind":"空港の搭乗案内","text":"Attention, passengers on Pacific Air flight 208 to Honolulu. We are sorry for the delayed flight. The aircraft has now arrived, and you may board the plane in ten minutes at gate fourteen. Please present a passport and boarding pass at the gate. Each passenger may bring one small bag on board. If your bag does not fit in the overhead compartment, our staff will check a bag for you at the gate. Passengers who still need to go through security should hurry, because we do not want anyone to miss a flight today. If you are hoping to catch a flight to Maui after you land, our staff in Honolulu will help you. Once you are seated, please fasten your seat belt at once. Thank you.","ja":"パシフィック航空208便ホノルル行きをご利用のお客様にご案内します。便が遅れており、申し訳ありません。機体が到着しましたので、10分後に14番ゲートで飛行機にお乗りいただけます。ゲートでパスポートと搭乗券を提示してください。お一人につき、小さなかばんを1つ機内に持ち込めます。かばんが頭上の荷物入れに入らない場合は、係の者がゲートでかばんをお預かりします。まだ保安検査を通る必要のあるお客様は、お急ぎください。今日はどなたにも飛行機に乗り遅れてほしくありません。到着後にマウイ行きの便に乗る予定の方は、ホノルルの係の者がお手伝いします。席に着いたら、すぐにシートベルトを締めてください。ありがとうございます。","words":[["delayed flight","colls:delayed flight"],["board the plane","colls:board a plane"],["present a passport","colls:present a passport"],["on board","colls:on board"],["overhead compartment","colls:overhead compartment"],["check a bag","colls:check a bag"],["go through security","colls:go through security"],["miss a flight","colls:miss a flight"],["catch a flight","colls:catch a flight"],["fasten your seat belt","colls:fasten a seat belt"]],"qs":[{"q":"When can passengers begin boarding?","o":["In ten minutes","In one hour","At once","After the next announcement"],"a":0,"why":"you may board the plane in ten minutes（10分後に乗れる）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen to a bag that is too large for the overhead compartment?","o":["It will be left behind.","It will be put under the seat.","The passenger will pay a fee.","Staff will check it at the gate."],"a":3,"why":"our staff will check a bag for you at the gate（係がゲートで預かる）とある。"},{"q":"Who will get help in Honolulu?","o":["Passengers with large bags","Passengers without passports","Passengers going on to Maui","Passengers who are late"],"a":2,"why":"If you are hoping to catch a flight to Maui after you land, our staff in Honolulu will help you（マウイ行きに乗り継ぐ人を手伝う）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0038","page":"colls","group":"出張・移動","kind":"ラジオの交通情報","text":"Good morning. This is the seven o'clock traffic report. There is heavy traffic on Highway 9 after an accident near the bridge, and drivers must take a detour through Mill Road. To avoid traffic downtown, we suggest an alternate route along the river. The trains, however, are running on time. If you need to get to the airport, catch a train from Central Station, where the express train leaves every fifteen minutes. Remember that the city marathon starts at nine, so it will be hard to take a taxi in the center this morning. The stadium is within walking distance of Park Station, and police officers will give directions to visitors. We will be back with another report in thirty minutes.","ja":"おはようございます。7時の交通情報です。橋の近くで事故があり、9号線はひどい渋滞です。車の方は、ミル通りを通って回り道をしなければなりません。中心部の渋滞を避けるには、川沿いの別の道をお勧めします。一方、電車は時間どおりに動いています。空港へ行く必要のある方は、中央駅から電車に乗ってください。急行列車が15分おきに出ています。市民マラソンが9時に始まりますので、今朝は中心部でタクシーに乗るのは難しいでしょう。競技場は公園駅から歩いて行ける距離にあり、警察官が来場者に道を教えます。30分後に、また交通情報をお伝えします。","words":[["heavy traffic","colls:heavy traffic"],["take a detour","colls:take a detour"],["avoid traffic","colls:avoid traffic"],["alternate route","colls:alternate route"],["on time","colls:on time"],["catch a train","colls:catch a train"],["express train","colls:express train"],["take a taxi","colls:take a taxi"],["within walking distance","colls:within walking distance"],["give directions","colls:give directions"]],"qs":[{"q":"What caused the traffic on Highway 9?","o":["Road work","An accident","The marathon","Bad weather"],"a":1,"why":"after an accident near the bridge（橋の近くの事故のあと）とある。"},{"q":"How often does the express train leave?","o":["Every five minutes","Every thirty minutes","Every hour","Every fifteen minutes"],"a":3,"why":"the express train leaves every fifteen minutes（急行列車は15分おき）とある。"},{"q":"Why will taxis be hard to find this morning?","o":["A marathon is being held.","Drivers are on strike.","The trains have stopped.","The airport is closed."],"a":0,"why":"the city marathon starts at nine（市民マラソンが9時に始まる）ためとある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0039","page":"colls","group":"出張・移動","kind":"ホテルの受付での案内","text":"Good evening, Ms. Carter, and welcome. I am sorry you had to wait to check into the hotel after such a long flight. I have good news. Because we had a vacant room on the top floor, we decided to upgrade your room at no extra cost. It is a spacious room with a scenic view of the harbor. A complimentary breakfast is served from six thirty in the restaurant beside the lobby. If you have an early meeting, you can request a wake-up call by pressing zero. Our hotel is conveniently located, only five minutes from the convention center. If you decide to extend your stay, just tell us by ten in the morning. And after you check out, we can store luggage for you until the evening. Here is your key.","ja":"カーター様、こんばんは。ようこそ。長いフライトのあとで、ホテルにチェックインするのにお待たせしてしまい、申し訳ありません。よいお知らせがあります。最上階に空室がありましたので、追加の費用なしでお部屋を上の等級に変えることにしました。港のよい眺めが楽しめる広い部屋です。無料の朝食は、ロビーの隣のレストランで6時半からご用意しています。朝早い会議がある場合は、0を押してモーニングコールを頼むことができます。当ホテルは便利な場所にあり、会議場までわずか5分です。滞在を延ばすことにした場合は、午前10時までにお知らせください。チェックアウトのあとも、夕方まで荷物をお預かりできます。こちらが鍵です。","words":[["check into the hotel","colls:check into a hotel"],["vacant room","colls:vacant room"],["upgrade your room","colls:upgrade a room"],["spacious room","colls:spacious room"],["scenic view","colls:scenic view"],["complimentary breakfast","colls:complimentary breakfast"],["request a wake-up call","colls:request a wake-up call"],["conveniently located","colls:conveniently located"],["extend your stay","colls:extend a stay"],["store luggage","colls:store luggage"]],"qs":[{"q":"What good news does the clerk give?","o":["Breakfast is free today.","The flight was refunded.","The room has been upgraded.","The meeting was moved."],"a":2,"why":"we decided to upgrade your room at no extra cost（追加の費用なしで部屋を上の等級に変えた）とある。"},{"q":"How can a guest ask for a wake-up call?","o":["By pressing zero","By visiting the desk","By calling the restaurant","By filling in a card"],"a":0,"why":"you can request a wake-up call by pressing zero（0を押して頼める）とある。"},{"q":"How far is the convention center?","o":["Thirty minutes away","Next door","Ten minutes away","Five minutes away"],"a":3,"why":"only five minutes from the convention center（会議場までわずか5分）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0040","page":"colls","group":"出張・移動","kind":"見本市の案内放送","text":"Welcome to the Asia Food Industry Fair. Many of you have come a long way on business, so here is some useful information. If you plan to attend a conference session this afternoon, please note that Room B is now Room D. You can still register for a workshop on packaging at the desk. Tomorrow at ten, visitors can tour a facility where noodles are made, and buses leave from the main gate. We know you are on a tight schedule, but please join the dinner tonight. It is a good chance to exchange business cards. The city is proud to host an event of this size. If you need to exchange money or plan an itinerary for sightseeing, visit the tourist desk in the lobby. Finally, the hall will open ahead of schedule tomorrow, at eight thirty.","ja":"アジア食品産業見本市へようこそ。多くの方が仕事で遠くからお越しですので、役に立つ情報をお伝えします。今日の午後、会議の部に出席する予定の方は、B室がD室に変わったことにご注意ください。包装についての講習会には、今も受付で申し込むことができます。明日の10時には、めんを作っている施設を見学できます。バスは正門から出ます。詰まった予定でお過ごしとは存じますが、今夜の夕食会にぜひご参加ください。名刺を交換するよい機会です。市は、これほどの規模の催しを主催できることを誇りに思っています。両替する、あるいは観光の旅程を立てる必要がある方は、ロビーの観光案内所へどうぞ。最後に、会場は明日、予定より早く8時半に開きます。","words":[["on business","colls:on business"],["attend a conference","colls:attend a conference"],["register for a workshop","colls:register for a workshop"],["tour a facility","colls:tour a facility"],["tight schedule","colls:tight schedule"],["exchange business cards","colls:exchange business cards"],["host an event","colls:host an event"],["exchange money","colls:exchange money"],["plan an itinerary","colls:plan an itinerary"],["ahead of schedule","colls:ahead of schedule"]],"qs":[{"q":"What has changed about this afternoon's session?","o":["The time","The room","The speaker","The topic"],"a":1,"why":"Room B is now Room D（B室がD室に変わった）とある。"},{"q":"What can visitors do tomorrow at ten?","o":["Join a dinner","Take a city tour","See where noodles are made","Attend a packaging class"],"a":2,"why":"visitors can tour a facility where noodles are made（めんを作っている施設を見学できる）とある。"},{"q":"Where can visitors change money?","o":["At the main gate","At the bank next door","At the registration desk","At the tourist desk in the lobby"],"a":3,"why":"visit the tourist desk in the lobby（ロビーの観光案内所へ）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0041","page":"colls","group":"生産・品質・設備","kind":"工場見学の案内","text":"Welcome to the Sunwell bicycle factory. This plant has been in operation since 1988. In those days, workers had to assemble parts by hand, and we made fifty bicycles a day. Today the line is almost fully automated, and mass production allows us to make nine hundred. On your left, you can see the staff who operate machinery that paints the frames. Last year we managed to streamline a process in this area, and painting now takes half the time. Because spring is coming, we must increase production, and the factory is running at full capacity. We have to meet a deadline for a large order from Germany next week. We only halt production twice a year, for cleaning. Now, please follow me to the testing room.","ja":"サンウェル自転車工場へようこそ。この工場は1988年から稼働しています。当時は、働き手が手で部品を組み立てなければならず、1日に50台を作っていました。今では製造ラインはほぼ完全に自動化されており、大量生産のおかげで900台を作ることができます。左手に、フレームを塗装する機械を操作する人たちが見えます。昨年、この区画の工程を効率化することができ、塗装にかかる時間は半分になりました。春が近いので生産を増やさなければならず、工場はフル稼働しています。来週、ドイツからの大量の注文の締め切りに間に合わせなければなりません。生産を止めるのは、清掃のための年に2回だけです。では、試験室へご案内します。","words":[["in operation","colls:in operation"],["assemble parts","colls:assemble parts"],["fully automated","colls:fully automated"],["mass production","colls:mass production"],["operate machinery","colls:operate machinery"],["streamline a process","colls:streamline a process"],["increase production","colls:increase production"],["at full capacity","colls:at full capacity"],["meet a deadline","colls:meet a deadline"],["halt production","colls:halt production"]],"qs":[{"q":"How many bicycles does the factory make a day now?","o":["Fifty","Five hundred","Nine hundred","Nineteen hundred"],"a":2,"why":"mass production allows us to make nine hundred（大量生産で900台を作れる）とある。"},{"q":"What changed in the painting area last year?","o":["Painting became twice as fast.","New colors were added.","More staff were hired.","The machines were removed."],"a":0,"why":"painting now takes half the time（塗装にかかる時間が半分になった）とある。"},{"q":"Why does the factory stop production twice a year?","o":["For holidays","For training","For repairs","For cleaning"],"a":3,"why":"We only halt production twice a year, for cleaning（清掃のために年2回だけ止める）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0042","page":"colls","group":"生産・品質・設備","kind":"品質管理の打ち合わせ","text":"Good morning. I called this meeting because of a problem with the K-20 kettle. As you know, we have high standards, and every kettle is thoroughly tested before it leaves the plant. However, last week a customer found a minor flaw in the handle. It is not dangerous, but if we fail to detect a defect like this, we may have to recall a product one day, and that would cost millions. So, from today, two people will inspect each product instead of one. We will also conduct a test on the handles every hour. On Friday, there will be a thorough inspection of the whole line. Every item must meet the standard set by the government. I am counting on all of you to help us maintain quality.","ja":"おはようございます。K-20型のやかんに問題があったので、この会議を開きました。ご存じのとおり、当社には高い基準があり、やかんはすべて、工場を出る前に徹底的に試験されています。ところが先週、あるお客様が取っ手に小さな欠点を見つけました。危険なものではありませんが、このような欠陥を見つけることができなければ、いつか製品を回収しなければならなくなるかもしれず、そうなれば何百万もの費用がかかります。そこで今日から、製品を検査する人を1人から2人にします。また、取っ手については1時間ごとに試験を行います。金曜には、製造ライン全体の徹底した検査をします。すべての品物は、政府が定めた基準を満たさなければなりません。品質を保つために、皆さんの力を頼りにしています。","words":[["high standards","colls:high standards"],["thoroughly tested","colls:thoroughly tested"],["minor flaw","colls:minor flaw"],["detect a defect","colls:detect a defect"],["recall a product","colls:recall a product"],["inspect each product","colls:inspect a product"],["conduct a test","colls:conduct a test"],["thorough inspection","colls:thorough inspection"],["meet the standard","colls:meet a standard"],["maintain quality","colls:maintain quality"]],"qs":[{"q":"Where was the flaw found?","o":["In the lid","In the handle","In the box","In the cord"],"a":1,"why":"a customer found a minor flaw in the handle（取っ手に小さな欠点を見つけた）とある。"},{"q":"What will change from today?","o":["Each product will be checked by two people.","The kettle will be redesigned.","Production will stop.","Prices will rise."],"a":0,"why":"two people will inspect each product instead of one（検査する人を1人から2人にする）とある。"},{"q":"What will happen on Friday?","o":["A customer will visit.","The government will set a new rule.","The whole line will be inspected.","The kettles will be recalled."],"a":2,"why":"On Friday, there will be a thorough inspection of the whole line（金曜にライン全体の徹底した検査）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0043","page":"colls","group":"生産・品質・設備","kind":"見学者への安全説明","text":"Before you enter the plant, please listen to these safety rules. First, you must wear protective gear, including a helmet and glasses, at all times. Second, some rooms contain hazardous materials. These rooms are clearly marked with red signs, and visitors may not enter. Third, please follow safety procedures when you walk near the machines, and stay inside the yellow lines. These simple rules help us prevent an accident. In case of emergency, you will hear a loud bell. Walk to the nearest emergency exit, and do not use the elevator. We take precautions every day, but if you are hurt, even slightly, please report an injury to your guide immediately. Thank you for your cooperation. Let's begin the tour.","ja":"工場に入る前に、次の安全の決まりをお聞きください。まず、ヘルメットと眼鏡を含む保護具を、常に身に着けなければなりません。次に、危険物が置いてある部屋があります。これらの部屋は赤い標識ではっきり表示されており、見学の方は入れません。3つ目に、機械の近くを歩くときは安全手順に従い、黄色い線の内側にいてください。こうした簡単な決まりが、事故を防ぐのに役立ちます。緊急の場合には、大きなベルが鳴ります。最も近い非常口まで歩き、エレベーターは使わないでください。私たちは毎日予防措置を取っていますが、少しでもけがをしたら、すぐに案内係にけがを報告してください。ご協力ありがとうございます。では、見学を始めましょう。","words":[["protective gear","colls:protective gear"],["at all times","colls:at all times"],["hazardous materials","colls:hazardous materials"],["clearly marked","colls:clearly marked"],["follow safety procedures","colls:follow safety procedures"],["prevent an accident","colls:prevent an accident"],["In case of emergency","colls:in case of emergency"],["emergency exit","colls:emergency exit"],["take precautions","colls:take precautions"],["report an injury","colls:report an injury"]],"qs":[{"q":"How are the rooms with hazardous materials marked?","o":["With yellow lines","With a bell","With locked doors","With red signs"],"a":3,"why":"These rooms are clearly marked with red signs（赤い標識ではっきり表示されている）とある。"},{"q":"What should visitors do in an emergency?","o":["Walk to the nearest emergency exit","Take the elevator","Wait for the guide","Stay inside the yellow lines"],"a":0,"why":"Walk to the nearest emergency exit, and do not use the elevator（最も近い非常口まで歩く）とある。"},{"q":"What should visitors do if they are hurt?","o":["Leave the plant","Call an ambulance","Tell their guide at once","Go to the office"],"a":2,"why":"please report an injury to your guide immediately（すぐに案内係に報告する）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0044","page":"colls","group":"生産・品質・設備","kind":"建物の管理室からのお知らせ","text":"This is an announcement from the building office. This Saturday, our engineers will perform maintenance on the heating system. This is routine maintenance, but it will affect several services. The east elevators will be out of service from eight until noon, and the parking garage will be temporarily closed. The engineers will also fix a leak in the third-floor kitchen and install equipment to replace the outdated equipment in the lobby. The new lights will help us save energy. The electricity will be turned off at nine, and we expect to restore power by ten. If a technical problem causes a delay, we will tell you by e-mail. We are sorry for the trouble, and we thank you for your patience.","ja":"建物の管理室からお知らせします。今週の土曜、技術者が暖房設備の保守作業を行います。これは定期的な保守ですが、いくつかのサービスに影響が出ます。東側のエレベーターは8時から正午まで使用できず、駐車場は一時的に閉鎖されます。技術者は、3階の給湯室の水漏れを直し、ロビーの古くなった設備に代わる設備も取り付けます。新しい照明は、エネルギーを節約するのに役立ちます。電気は9時に止まり、10時までに電力を復旧させる見込みです。技術的な問題で遅れが出る場合は、メールでお知らせします。ご迷惑をおかけして申し訳ありません。ご理解に感謝します。","words":[["perform maintenance","colls:perform maintenance"],["routine maintenance","colls:routine maintenance"],["out of service","colls:out of service"],["temporarily closed","colls:temporarily closed"],["fix a leak","colls:fix a leak"],["install equipment","colls:install equipment"],["outdated equipment","colls:outdated equipment"],["save energy","colls:save energy"],["restore power","colls:restore power"],["technical problem","colls:technical problem"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will be worked on this Saturday?","o":["The roof","The heating system","The front doors","The phone lines"],"a":1,"why":"perform maintenance on the heating system（暖房設備の保守作業）とある。"},{"q":"How long will the electricity be off?","o":["All day","Four hours","Ten minutes","About one hour"],"a":3,"why":"turned off at nine, and we expect to restore power by ten（9時に止まり10時までに復旧）とある。"},{"q":"How will people learn about a delay?","o":["By e-mail","By a notice in the lobby","By phone","By a second announcement"],"a":0,"why":"we will tell you by e-mail（メールで知らせる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0045","page":"colls","group":"生産・品質・設備","kind":"地域のニュース","text":"In local news, the new city library is now under construction beside the river. The city decided not to renovate a building from the 1960s, because repairs would have cost too much. It took six months to obtain a permit, but the work is now on schedule. The builders plan to complete construction by next April. The mayor says the library will be environmentally friendly. It will use renewable energy from the sun, and rainwater will be collected for the garden. To reduce waste, the builders will recycle materials from the old building, including bricks and wood. The mayor said that the city wants to show children how to protect the environment. The old library will stay open until March.","ja":"地域のニュースです。新しい市立図書館が今、川のそばで建設中です。市は、1960年代の建物を改装することはしないと決めました。修理に費用がかかりすぎるためです。許可を得るのに6か月かかりましたが、工事は今、予定どおりに進んでいます。建設会社は、来年の4月までに工事を完了する予定です。市長は、図書館は環境にやさしいものになると述べています。太陽による再生可能エネルギーを使い、雨水を集めて庭に使います。ごみを減らすため、建設会社はれんがや木材など、古い建物の資材を再利用します。市長は、環境を守る方法を子どもたちに示したいと述べました。古い図書館は3月まで開いています。","words":[["under construction","colls:under construction"],["renovate a building","colls:renovate a building"],["obtain a permit","colls:obtain a permit"],["on schedule","colls:on schedule"],["complete construction","colls:complete construction"],["environmentally friendly","colls:environmentally friendly"],["renewable energy","colls:renewable energy"],["reduce waste","colls:reduce waste"],["recycle materials","colls:recycle materials"],["protect the environment","colls:protect the environment"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why did the city choose not to renovate the old building?","o":["It was too small.","It was too far from the river.","Repairs would have cost too much.","The permit was refused."],"a":2,"why":"because repairs would have cost too much（修理に費用がかかりすぎる）とある。"},{"q":"When is construction expected to end?","o":["In six months","By March","In the 1960s","By next April"],"a":3,"why":"complete construction by next April（来年の4月までに工事を完了する）とある。"},{"q":"What will be reused from the old building?","o":["Books and shelves","Bricks and wood","Windows","Solar panels"],"a":1,"why":"recycle materials from the old building, including bricks and wood（れんがや木材など古い建物の資材を再利用）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0046","page":"colls","group":"日常業務・連絡","kind":"同僚への留守番電話","text":"Hi, Paul. It's Nina. I am sorry about yesterday. I meant to send an e-mail only to you, but it went to the whole department by mistake, before the sales summary was finished. Please ignore it. I spent this morning trying to revise the draft, and the new version is much shorter. I will attach a file to my next message. Could you proofread the document by three o'clock? I need to file a report with the head office today. After you check it, please forward a message from me to Ms. Abe, because I do not have her new address. Also, make a copy of the final version and keep it for future reference. If you find a serious problem, do not write back. Come and tell me in person. I am in room 402.","ja":"ポール、ニナです。昨日はごめんなさい。あなただけにメールを送るつもりでしたが、売上のまとめが仕上がる前に、間違って部署全体に届いてしまいました。あれは無視してください。今朝は下書きを修正するのに時間をかけ、新しい版はずっと短くなりました。次のメールにファイルを添付します。3時までに書類を校正してもらえますか。今日、本社に報告書を提出する必要があるのです。確認が済んだら、私からの伝言を阿部さんに転送してください。彼女の新しいアドレスを知らないので。それと、最終版のコピーを取って、今後の参考のために取っておいてください。重大な問題を見つけたら、返信はしないでください。直接会って教えてください。私は402号室にいます。","words":[["send an e-mail","colls:send an e-mail"],["by mistake","colls:by mistake"],["revise the draft","colls:revise a draft"],["attach a file","colls:attach a file"],["proofread the document","colls:proofread a document"],["file a report","colls:file a report"],["forward a message","colls:forward a message"],["make a copy","colls:make a copy"],["for future reference","colls:for future reference"],["in person","colls:in person"]],"qs":[{"q":"What mistake did Nina make?","o":["She lost a file.","She missed a meeting.","She sent an e-mail to the whole department.","She forgot Ms. Abe's address."],"a":2,"why":"it went to the whole department by mistake（間違って部署全体に届いた）とある。"},{"q":"What does Nina ask Paul to do by three o'clock?","o":["Proofread the document","Call the head office","Write the summary","Find room 402"],"a":0,"why":"Could you proofread the document by three o'clock?（3時までに書類を校正して）とある。"},{"q":"What should Paul do if he finds a serious problem?","o":["Send an e-mail","Call Ms. Abe","Make another copy","Tell Nina in person"],"a":3,"why":"Come and tell me in person（直接会って教えて）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0047","page":"colls","group":"日常業務・連絡","kind":"歯科医院からの留守番電話","text":"Hello, this is a message for Ms. Elena Park from Dr. Shaw's dental office. You called to make an appointment for a cleaning, and we gave you Monday at four. Unfortunately, Dr. Shaw must attend a meeting that day, so we need to reschedule an appointment or two, including yours. We know you have a busy schedule, and we are sorry to change things at the last minute. We have openings on Tuesday and Thursday morning. To save time, you can choose a new time on our website. Please contact us at your earliest convenience so that we can set a date. Your health is our top priority. If you cannot keep an appointment in the future, please tell us one day before. We will make arrangements for another visit.","ja":"もしもし、ショー歯科医院から、エレナ・パーク様への伝言です。歯のクリーニングの予約をするためにお電話をいただき、月曜の4時をご案内しました。あいにく、その日はショー先生が会議に出なければならず、パーク様の分を含めて、予約を1つ2つ変更する必要があります。忙しい予定でお過ごしのことと存じます。間際になっての変更で申し訳ありません。火曜と木曜の午前に空きがあります。時間を節約するには、当院のウェブサイトで新しい時間を選ぶこともできます。日取りを決められるよう、ご都合がつき次第ご連絡ください。パーク様の健康が、私たちの最優先事項です。今後、予約どおりに来られないときは、1日前までにお知らせください。別の日の来院を手配します。","words":[["make an appointment","colls:make an appointment"],["reschedule an appointment","colls:reschedule an appointment"],["busy schedule","colls:busy schedule"],["at the last minute","colls:at the last minute"],["save time","colls:save time"],["at your earliest convenience","colls:at your earliest convenience"],["set a date","colls:set a date"],["top priority","colls:top priority"],["keep an appointment","colls:keep an appointment"],["make arrangements","colls:make arrangements"]],"qs":[{"q":"Why must the appointment be changed?","o":["The office will be closed.","Dr. Shaw has a meeting.","Ms. Park is busy.","The website is down."],"a":1,"why":"Dr. Shaw must attend a meeting that day（その日はショー先生が会議に出る）とある。"},{"q":"When are there openings?","o":["On Monday at four","Every afternoon","On Friday evening","On Tuesday and Thursday morning"],"a":3,"why":"We have openings on Tuesday and Thursday morning（火曜と木曜の午前に空きがある）とある。"},{"q":"What should patients do if they cannot come?","o":["Tell the office one day before","Send a friend","Pay a fee","Visit the website"],"a":0,"why":"please tell us one day before（1日前までに知らせる）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0048","page":"colls","group":"日常業務・連絡","kind":"共同企画の説明","text":"Thank you all for coming. As you know, this year our office will work closely with the Madrid team on the new travel app. It is a joint effort, so each of you will collaborate with colleagues you have never met. Please share information openly, even when the news is bad. Each of you will play a role, with designers here and engineers there. The time difference is hard, so please make an effort to answer messages within a day. If someone in Madrid needs to ask a favor, try to lend a hand, and they will do the same for you. We have already begun to make progress on the design. One last thing. This project is long, so do not forget to take a break when you need one.","ja":"皆さん、お集まりいただきありがとうございます。ご存じのとおり、今年、私たちの事務所は新しい旅行アプリについて、マドリードのチームと緊密に協力して働きます。これは共同の取り組みですので、皆さんはそれぞれ、会ったことのない同僚と協力することになります。悪い知らせのときでも、情報を率直に共有してください。デザイナーはこちら、技術者は向こうというように、一人ひとりが役割を果たします。時差は大変ですが、1日以内に連絡に返事をするよう努力してください。マドリードのだれかが頼み事をしてきたら、手を貸すようにしてください。向こうも同じようにしてくれます。デザインについては、すでに前進し始めています。最後に一つ。この企画は長いので、必要なときは休憩するのを忘れないでください。","words":[["work closely","colls:work closely"],["joint effort","colls:joint effort"],["collaborate with colleagues","colls:collaborate with colleagues"],["share information","colls:share information"],["play a role","colls:play a role"],["make an effort","colls:make an effort"],["ask a favor","colls:ask a favor"],["lend a hand","colls:lend a hand"],["make progress","colls:make progress"],["take a break","colls:take a break"]],"qs":[{"q":"What will the two teams make together?","o":["A travel app","A website for designers","A guidebook","A training course"],"a":0,"why":"on the new travel app（新しい旅行アプリについて）とある。"},{"q":"How quickly should staff answer messages?","o":["Within an hour","Within a week","Within a day","At once"],"a":2,"why":"make an effort to answer messages within a day（1日以内に返事をするよう努力する）とある。"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about the design?","o":["It is finished.","It has not started.","It will be done in Madrid.","Progress has already begun."],"a":3,"why":"We have already begun to make progress on the design（デザインはすでに前進し始めている）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0049","page":"colls","group":"日常業務・連絡","kind":"駐車場についての社内放送","text":"Good afternoon. I would like to make an announcement about parking. After long talks, the company and the staff committee have come to an agreement. We will introduce a policy of shared parking, and the new rules take effect on May first. From that day, spaces near the entrance are for visitors only. We have also decided to enter into an agreement with the garage across the street, so staff can park there for free. That contract will go into effect on the same day. Guards will enforce a rule against parking on the grass, but they will make an exception for delivery trucks. The north gate will stay closed until further notice. Our company has worked hard to earn a reputation as a good neighbor, so please drive slowly.","ja":"こんにちは。駐車について発表します。長い話し合いの末、会社と職員委員会は合意に達しました。駐車場を共同で使う方針を導入し、新しい決まりは5月1日に実施されます。その日から、入口近くの区画は来客専用になります。また、通りの向かいの駐車場と契約を結ぶことも決めましたので、職員はそこに無料でとめられます。その契約も同じ日に発効します。警備員は、芝生の上にとめてはいけないという規則を守らせますが、配達のトラックには例外を認めます。北門は、追って知らせがあるまで閉めたままにします。当社は、よい隣人としての評判を得るために努力してきましたので、ゆっくり運転してください。","words":[["make an announcement","colls:make an announcement"],["come to an agreement","colls:come to an agreement"],["introduce a policy","colls:introduce a policy"],["take effect","colls:take effect"],["enter into an agreement","colls:enter into an agreement"],["go into effect","colls:go into effect"],["enforce a rule","colls:enforce a rule"],["make an exception","colls:make an exception"],["until further notice","colls:until further notice"],["earn a reputation","colls:earn a reputation"]],"qs":[{"q":"When do the new rules begin?","o":["Today","On May first","Next week","After the north gate opens"],"a":1,"why":"the new rules take effect on May first（新しい決まりは5月1日に実施）とある。"},{"q":"Where can staff park for free?","o":["Near the entrance","On the grass","In the garage across the street","By the north gate"],"a":2,"why":"the garage across the street, so staff can park there for free（向かいの駐車場に無料でとめられる）とある。"},{"q":"Who may park on the grass?","o":["Delivery trucks","Visitors","Guards","Nobody at all"],"a":0,"why":"they will make an exception for delivery trucks（配達のトラックには例外を認める）とある。"}]},
{"id":"c-0050","page":"colls","group":"日常業務・連絡","kind":"創業記念式典のあいさつ","text":"Good evening, everyone. Tonight we celebrate an anniversary, because our company is thirty years old. First, I want to express gratitude to the people who made this possible. Five years ago, we set out to become the top bakery chain in the region. This year we managed to achieve a goal that once seemed impossible, and now we can all reap the rewards. Last month, our bread managed to win an award at the national fair, which was a great success for us. Much of the credit goes to Mr. Kato. He continues to make a contribution every day, and when we needed to drum up support for the new kitchen, he spoke to every manager. He even helped to organize an event like tonight's. In recognition of his thirty years of service, please welcome Mr. Kato to the stage.","ja":"皆さん、こんばんは。今夜は記念日を祝います。当社が30周年を迎えたからです。まず、これを可能にしてくださった方々に感謝を表したいと思います。5年前、私たちは地域で一番のパン屋チェーンになることを目指しました。今年、かつては不可能に思えた目標を達成することができ、今、全員が成果を得ることができます。先月は、当社のパンが全国見本市で賞を取ることができ、私たちにとって大成功でした。その功績の多くは加藤さんのものです。加藤さんは毎日貢献し続けており、新しい調理場への支持を集める必要があったときは、すべての部長に話をしてくれました。今夜のような催しを企画するのも手伝ってくれました。30年の勤続をたたえて、加藤さんを壇上にお迎えください。","words":[["celebrate an anniversary","colls:celebrate an anniversary"],["express gratitude","colls:express gratitude"],["achieve a goal","colls:achieve a goal"],["reap the rewards","colls:reap the rewards"],["win an award","colls:win an award"],["great success","colls:great success"],["make a contribution","colls:make a contribution"],["drum up support","colls:drum up support"],["organize an event","colls:organize an event"],["In recognition of","colls:in recognition of"]],"qs":[{"q":"How old is the company?","o":["Five years","Ten years","Fifty years","Thirty years"],"a":3,"why":"our company is thirty years old（当社は30周年）とある。"},{"q":"What happened last month?","o":["A new kitchen opened.","The bread won an award.","Mr. Kato retired.","A new store opened."],"a":1,"why":"our bread managed to win an award at the national fair（全国見本市で賞を取った）とある。"},{"q":"How did Mr. Kato help with the new kitchen?","o":["He paid for it.","He designed it.","He spoke to every manager.","He cooked in it."],"a":2,"why":"when we needed to drum up support for the new kitchen, he spoke to every manager（支持を集めるためにすべての部長に話した）とある。"}]}
];
